{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T00:49:26.709229", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Retrieve action mapping from the environment for robustness\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map[\"UP\"]\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map[\"DOWN\"]\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map[\"LEFT\"]\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map[\"RIGHT\"]\n  ACTION_USE = action_map[\"USE\"]\n\n  # Get the integer ID for the target primitive.\n  # Use .lower() to match internal cookbook naming conventions.\n  # The __getitem__ method of Index returns None if the item is not found.\n  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive.lower()]\n  if primitive_id is None:\n    # If the primitive name is not recognized, it cannot be collected.\n    return []\n\n  # Crucial check: If the target primitive is not an item that can be picked up,\n  # there's no valid sequence of \"collect\" actions.\n  if primitive_id not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  # Get current state details from the environment's internal CraftState\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  start_pos = current_state.pos  # Agent's current (x, y) position\n  grid = current_state.grid      # The full grid layout (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  \n  # Extract grid dimensions\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Define obstacle kinds: these are entities that block movement.\n  # A cell is an obstacle if it contains any of these `non_grabbable` items.\n  obstacle_kind_ids = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # Define possible movements: (delta_x, delta_y, action_index)\n  # These correspond to changes in grid coordinates and the action to perform it.\n  move_actions = [\n      (0, -1, ACTION_UP),    # North: (x, y-1)\n      (0, 1, ACTION_DOWN),   # South: (x, y+1)\n      (-1, 0, ACTION_LEFT),  # West:  (x-1, y)\n      (1, 0, ACTION_RIGHT)   # East:  (x+1, y)\n  ]\n\n  # Initialize Breadth-First Search (BFS)\n  # Queue stores (current_position_tuple, list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])])\n  # Set to keep track of visited grid cells to prevent cycles and redundant exploration\n  visited = {start_pos}\n\n  # BFS loop to find the shortest path\n  while queue:\n    current_pos, path_so_far = queue.popleft()\n    cx, cy = current_pos\n\n    # If the current cell contains the desired primitive, we've found our target.\n    # The path to this cell plus a 'USE' action is the solution.\n    # `grid[cx, cy, primitive_id] > 0` checks if the item is present (e.g., 1 for one-hot).\n    if grid[cx, cy, primitive_id] > 0:\n      return path_so_far + [ACTION_USE]\n\n    # Explore all four neighboring cells (up, down, left, right)\n    for dx, dy, action_move in move_actions:\n      nx, ny = cx + dx, cy + dy  # Calculate neighbor's coordinates\n      next_pos = (nx, ny)\n\n      # 1. Check if the neighbor is within the grid boundaries\n      if not (0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height):\n        continue\n\n      # 2. Check if this neighbor cell has already been visited during the BFS\n      if next_pos in visited:\n        continue\n\n      # 3. Check if the neighbor cell is blocked by an impassable object.\n      # Iterate through all known obstacle kinds; if any is present in the cell, it's blocked.\n      is_blocked = False\n      for obstacle_id in obstacle_kind_ids:\n        if grid[nx, ny, obstacle_id] > 0:\n          is_blocked = True\n          break\n      \n      if is_blocked:\n        continue # Cannot move to this cell if it's blocked\n\n      # If the neighbor is valid (within bounds, unvisited, and traversable),\n      # add it to the queue with the updated path and mark it as visited.\n      visited.add(next_pos)\n      queue.append((next_pos, path_so_far + [action_move]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and the primitive was never found (queue became empty),\n  # it means the primitive is not reachable from the current position.\n  return []", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T00:49:27.830295", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map[\"UP\"]\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map[\"DOWN\"]\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map[\"LEFT\"]\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map[\"RIGHT\"]\n  ACTION_USE = action_map[\"USE\"]\n\n  # 1. Get the integer ID for the target primitive.\n  # Use .lower() to match the keys in the cookbook's index.\n  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive.lower()]\n  if primitive_id is None:\n    # If the primitive name is not recognized, it cannot be collected.\n    return []\n\n  # 2. Crucial check: If the target primitive is not an item that can be grabbed/collected,\n  # there's no sequence of actions to \"collect\" it.\n  if primitive_id not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  # 3. Get current state details from the environment\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  start_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's current (x, y) integer position\n  grid = current_state.grid # The full grid layout: (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  \n  # Get grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT)\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # 4. Define obstacle kinds: A cell is considered an obstacle if it contains\n  # ANY item from the `non_grabbable_indices` set.\n  obstacle_kind_ids = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # 5. Define possible movements (change in x, change in y, corresponding action)\n  # (dx, dy) maps to (column_change, row_change) for grid[x, y]\n  move_actions = [\n      (0, -1, ACTION_UP),    # Move North (decreases y, i.e., row index)\n      (0, 1, ACTION_DOWN),   # Move South (increases y)\n      (-1, 0, ACTION_LEFT),  # Move West (decreases x, i.e., column index)\n      (1, 0, ACTION_RIGHT)   # Move East (increases x)\n  ]\n\n  # 6. Initialize Breadth-First Search (BFS)\n  # Queue stores tuples: ((x, y), [actions_to_reach_here])\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])])\n  # Set to keep track of visited grid cells ((x, y) tuples) to avoid cycles and redundant work\n  visited = {start_pos}\n\n  # 7. BFS loop to find the shortest path to the primitive\n  while queue:\n    current_pos, path_so_far = queue.popleft()\n    cx, cy = current_pos\n\n    # Check if the current cell (cx, cy) contains the desired primitive.\n    # `grid[cx, cy, primitive_id] > 0` indicates presence (e.g., 1 for 1-hot encoding).\n    if grid[cx, cy, primitive_id] > 0:\n      # If the primitive is at the current cell, and it's grabbable (checked upfront),\n      # we've found the shortest path to it. Append ACTION_USE to collect it.\n      return path_so_far + [ACTION_USE]\n\n    # Explore neighboring cells\n    for dx, dy, action_move in move_actions:\n      nx, ny = cx + dx, cy + dy # Calculate neighbor's coordinates\n      next_pos = (nx, ny)\n\n      # Check 1: Is the neighbor within grid boundaries?\n      if not (0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height):\n        continue\n\n      # Check 2: Has the neighbor already been visited?\n      if next_pos in visited:\n        continue\n\n      # Check 3: Is the neighbor cell an obstacle?\n      # A cell is an obstacle if it contains any object that is in the `non_grabbable_indices` set.\n      is_obstacle_cell = False\n      for obstacle_id in obstacle_kind_ids:\n        if grid[nx, ny, obstacle_id] > 0: # If this obstacle is present in the cell\n          is_obstacle_cell = True\n          break\n      \n      if is_obstacle_cell:\n        continue # Skip this move if it leads to an impassable object\n\n      # If the neighbor is valid (within bounds, not visited, and traversable),\n      # add it to the queue with its path and mark it as visited.\n      visited.add(next_pos)\n      queue.append((next_pos, path_so_far + [action_move]))\n\n  # 8. If the BFS completes and the primitive was not found anywhere accessible on the grid,\n  # return an empty list, indicating that it cannot be collected from the current state.\n  return []", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T00:51:09.922285", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  initial_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's initial position (col, row)\n  initial_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's initial direction (0:N, 1:E, 2:S, 3:W)\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape # Grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n\n  # Get the integer index for the primitive (lowercase for consistency)\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive.lower())\n\n  # Check for uncollectible primitive (boundary)\n  if primitive_idx == env.world.cookbook.index.index(\"boundary\"):\n      return []\n\n  # Get action mappings\n  ACTION_MAP = env.action_specs()\n  ACTIONS = {\n      \"DOWN\": ACTION_MAP[\"DOWN\"],\n      \"UP\": ACTION_MAP[\"UP\"],\n      \"LEFT\": ACTION_MAP[\"LEFT\"],\n      \"RIGHT\": ACTION_MAP[\"RIGHT\"],\n      \"USE\": ACTION_MAP[\"USE\"]\n  }\n\n  # Define (d_col, d_row) deltas for each move action AND the resulting direction.\n  # When an agent moves, its direction attribute updates to match the direction of movement.\n  # Format: (action_index: (delta_col, delta_row, new_direction_after_move))\n  MOVE_ACTION_DATA = {\n      ACTIONS[\"UP\"]: (0, -1, 0),    # Move North (Up), face North (dir 0)\n      ACTIONS[\"DOWN\"]: (0, 1, 2),   # Move South (Down), face South (dir 2)\n      ACTIONS[\"LEFT\"]: (-1, 0, 3),  # Move West (Left), face West (dir 3)\n      ACTIONS[\"RIGHT\"]: (1, 0, 1)   # Move East (Right), face East (dir 1)\n  }\n\n  # Define (d_col, d_row) deltas for each cardinal direction.\n  # This is used to calculate the coordinates of the cell directly in front of the agent.\n  # dir: 0=N, 1=E, 2=S, 3=W\n  DIR_TO_DELTA = {\n      0: (0, -1),  # North (Up)\n      1: (1, 0),   # East (Right)\n      2: (0, 1),   # South (Down)\n      3: (-1, 0)   # West (Left)\n  }\n\n  # Determine the type of primitive to collect and its collection method\n  is_primitive_workshop = (primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices)\n  is_primitive_grabbable_or_water_stone = (\n      primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices or\n      primitive_idx == env.world.water_index or\n      primitive_idx == env.world.stone_index\n  )\n\n  # Define entities that generally block movement (non-grabbables)\n  # This includes boundaries, workshops, water, stone.\n  blocking_kinds = set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices)\n\n  # Helper function to check if a cell (r_c, r_r) is traversable by the agent.\n  # The `target_prim_idx` is needed to handle special cases like water/stone.\n  def is_traversable(r_c, r_r, target_prim_idx):\n      # Check grid boundaries\n      if not (0 <= r_c < grid_width and 0 <= r_r < grid_height):\n          return False\n\n      # Check for blocking entities in the cell\n      for k_idx in blocking_kinds:\n          if grid[r_c, r_r, k_idx] > 0: # If this cell contains a potentially blocking item\n              # Special case: If the blocking item is water or stone AND it is the primitive we are trying to collect,\n              # then we *can* move onto it (to then USE it).\n              if k_idx == target_prim_idx and (k_idx == env.world.water_index or k_idx == env.world.stone_index):\n                  continue # It's okay to move onto this specific blocking item.\n              else:\n                  return False # It's a true blocking item (boundary, workshop, or water/stone not being targeted).\n      return True # No blocking entities found in this cell (or special case handled).\n\n  # Breadth-First Search (BFS) setup\n  # Queue stores elements as: (((current_col, current_row), current_direction), list_of_actions_to_reach_this_state)\n  queue = collections.deque([(((initial_pos[0], initial_pos[1]), initial_dir), [])])\n  # Visited set stores ((col, row), direction) tuples to avoid redundant exploration and cycles.\n  visited = set([((initial_pos[0], initial_pos[1]), initial_dir)])\n\n  while queue:\n      # Dequeue the current state and path\n      ((current_c, current_r), current_dir), path_actions = queue.popleft()\n\n      # --- Check if the goal (primitive collection condition) is met for the current state ---\n      if is_primitive_workshop:\n          # For workshops, the agent needs to be adjacent to a workshop (in a traversable spot).\n          # The agent's current position (current_c, current_r) must be a valid, traversable spot.\n          if is_traversable(current_c, current_r, primitive_idx):\n              # Check all 8 neighboring cells (including the agent's current cell, though a workshop would block movement there)\n              for dc_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n                  for dr_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n                      px, py = current_c + dc_adj, current_r + dr_adj # Potential primitive location\n                      \n                      # Ensure potential primitive location is within bounds and contains the workshop\n                      if (0 <= px < grid_width and 0 <= py < grid_height) and grid[px, py, primitive_idx] > 0:\n                          # Agent is at (current_c, current_r) which is adjacent to (px, py) containing the workshop.\n                          # This path is valid for \"collecting\" (i.e., reaching) a workshop.\n                          return path_actions\n      elif is_primitive_grabbable_or_water_stone:\n          # For grabbables (like wood) or special non-grabbables (water, stone),\n          # the agent needs to be positioned and oriented such that 'USE' will hit the primitive.\n          front_dc, front_dr = DIR_TO_DELTA[current_dir]\n          front_c, front_r = current_c + front_dc, current_r + front_dr\n\n          # Ensure the cell in front is within grid boundaries and contains the desired primitive\n          if (0 <= front_c < grid_width and 0 <= front_r < grid_height) and grid[front_c, front_r, primitive_idx] > 0:\n              # Goal reached: primitive is in front, and agent can USE.\n              return path_actions + [ACTIONS[\"USE\"]]\n\n      # --- Explore neighboring states by trying all possible movement actions ---\n      for action, (dc_move, dr_move, new_dir) in MOVE_ACTION_DATA.items():\n          next_c, next_r = current_c + dc_move, current_r + dr_move\n          next_state_tuple = ((next_c, next_r), new_dir) # The new state includes updated position AND direction\n\n          # If the next state (position and direction) has not been visited, AND the next cell is traversable:\n          if next_state_tuple not in visited and is_traversable(next_c, next_r, primitive_idx):\n              visited.add(next_state_tuple)\n              queue.append((next_state_tuple, path_actions + [action]))\n\n  # If the queue is exhausted and no path was found, return an empty list.\n  return []", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T00:51:11.071772", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Use .lower() to ensure case-insensitive matching for primitive names\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive.lower()] \n  \n  # Get action mappings from the environment\n  actions_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTIONS = {\n      \"UP\": actions_map[\"UP\"],\n      \"DOWN\": actions_map[\"DOWN\"],\n      \"LEFT\": actions_map[\"LEFT\"],\n      \"RIGHT\": actions_map[\"RIGHT\"],\n      \"USE\": actions_map[\"USE\"]\n  }\n\n  # Define movement actions and their effects: (dc, dr, new_direction)\n  # When an agent moves, its direction attribute updates to match the direction of movement.\n  # (action_index: (delta_col, delta_row, new_direction_after_move))\n  MOVE_ACTION_DATA = {\n      ACTIONS[\"UP\"]: (0, -1, 0),    # Move North (Up), face North (dir 0)\n      ACTIONS[\"RIGHT\"]: (1, 0, 1),  # Move East (Right), face East (dir 1)\n      ACTIONS[\"DOWN\"]: (0, 1, 2),   # Move South (Down), face South (dir 2)\n      ACTIONS[\"LEFT\"]: (-1, 0, 3)   # Move West (Left), face West (dir 3)\n  }\n\n  # Define (d_col, d_row) deltas for each cardinal direction.\n  # This is used to calculate the coordinates of the cell directly in front of the agent.\n  # dir: 0=N, 1=E, 2=S, 3=W\n  DIR_TO_DELTA = {\n      0: (0, -1),  # North (Up): (dc, dr)\n      1: (1, 0),   # East (Right): (dc, dr)\n      2: (0, 1),   # South (Down): (dc, dr)\n      3: (-1, 0)   # West (Left): (dc, dr)\n  }\n\n  # Get current state information\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  initial_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's initial position (col, row)\n  initial_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's initial direction (0:N, 1:E, 2:S, 3:W)\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Identify entities that block movement.\n  # In CraftWorld, typically `non_grabbable_indices` block movement onto their square.\n  blocking_entities_indices = set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices)\n  \n  # Special case: 'boundary' primitive cannot be collected or traversed\n  if primitive_idx == env.world.cookbook.index['boundary']:\n      return []\n\n  # Breadth-First Search (BFS) setup\n  # Queue stores elements as: ((current_position=(col, row), current_direction), list_of_actions_to_reach_this_state)\n  queue = collections.deque([((initial_pos, initial_dir), [])])\n  \n  # Visited set stores ((col, row), direction) tuples to avoid redundant exploration and cycles.\n  visited = {((initial_pos, initial_dir))}\n\n  best_path = None # To store the shortest sequence of actions found\n\n  while queue:\n      # Dequeue the current state and path\n      ((current_c, current_r), current_dir), path_actions = queue.popleft()\n\n      # --- Goal Check: Is the agent positioned and oriented to 'USE' the primitive? ---\n      # The 'USE' action in CraftState typically acts on the cell directly in front of the agent.\n      front_dc, front_dr = DIR_TO_DELTA[current_dir]\n      front_c, front_r = current_c + front_dc, current_r + front_dr\n\n      # Check if the cell in front is within grid boundaries and contains the desired primitive\n      if (0 <= front_c < grid_width and 0 <= front_r < grid_height and\n              grid[front_c, front_r, primitive_idx] > 0):\n          # Goal reached: Agent is adjacent to the primitive and facing it.\n          best_path = path_actions + [ACTIONS[\"USE\"]]\n          break # Found the shortest path, exit BFS\n\n      # --- Explore neighboring states by trying all possible movement actions ---\n      for action, (dc_move, dr_move, new_dir) in MOVE_ACTION_DATA.items():\n          next_c, next_r = current_c + dc_move, current_r + dr_move\n          next_pos = (next_c, next_r)\n          next_state_key = (next_pos, new_dir) # A state in BFS includes position AND direction\n\n          # 1. Bounds Check: Is the next position within the grid?\n          if not (0 <= next_c < grid_width and 0 <= next_r < grid_height):\n              continue\n\n          # 2. Visited Check: Has this exact (position, direction) state been visited before?\n          if next_state_key in visited:\n              continue\n\n          # 3. Traversability Check: Is the next position blocked by any non-grabbable entity?\n          is_blocked = False\n          for k_idx in blocking_entities_indices:\n              if grid[next_c, next_r, k_idx] > 0:\n                  is_blocked = True\n                  break\n          if is_blocked:\n              continue # Cannot move into a blocked cell\n\n          # If all checks pass, add the new state to the queue and mark as visited\n          visited.add(next_state_key)\n          queue.append((next_state_key, path_actions + [action]))\n\n  # Return the found path, or an empty list if no path could be found (BFS queue exhausted)\n  return best_path if best_path is not None else []", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T00:52:07.987736", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1` (based on the provided `collect_v0` function, which is the most advanced example).\"\"\"\n  actions = []\n  \n  current_state = env._current_state \n  grid = current_state.grid\n  current_pos = current_state.pos\n  \n  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Retrieve action mapping from the environment for robustness\n  _action_specs = env.action_specs()\n  DOWN = _action_specs['DOWN']\n  UP = _action_specs['UP']\n  LEFT = _action_specs['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = _action_specs['RIGHT']\n  USE = _action_specs['USE']\n\n  DELTAS = {\n      UP: (-1, 0),\n      DOWN: (1, 0),\n      LEFT: (0, -1),\n      RIGHT: (0, 1)\n  }\n\n  # V2 Improvement: Ensure the primitive is actually grabbable.\n  # If not grabbable, no actions can collect it.\n  if primitive_id not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  # 1. Check if the agent is already next to the primitive\n  # This is the fastest path if applicable.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_id):\n      actions.append(USE)\n      return actions\n\n  # 2. Find all locations of the target primitive on the grid\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for r in range(WIDTH):\n      for c in range(HEIGHT):\n          if grid[r, c, primitive_id] == 1:\n              primitive_locations.append((r, c))\n\n  # If no primitive instances are found, there's nothing to collect.\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      return []\n\n  # 3. Pre-compute all valid \"target use positions\".\n  # A \"target use position\" is a grid cell from which the agent can apply 'USE'\n  # to collect the desired primitive. This cell must be adjacent to a primitive\n  # location AND must be traversable by the agent.\n  target_use_positions = set()\n  for pr, pc in primitive_locations:\n      # Check all 4 cardinal neighbors of the primitive location\n      for dr, dc in DELTAS.values(): \n          adj_r, adj_c = pr + dr, pc + dc\n\n          # Ensure the adjacent cell is within grid boundaries\n          if not (0 <= adj_r < WIDTH and 0 <= adj_c < HEIGHT):\n              continue\n\n          # Ensure the adjacent cell is traversable. An agent must be able to\n          # stand on this cell. Traversable cells do not contain non-grabbable items.\n          is_traversable = True\n          for i_kind in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n              if grid[adj_r, adj_c, i_kind] == 1: \n                  is_traversable = False\n                  break \n          \n          if is_traversable:\n              target_use_positions.add((adj_r, adj_c))\n    \n  # If there are no traversable spots from which to use the primitive, it's uncollectable.\n  if not target_use_positions:\n      return []\n\n  # 4. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path\n  #    to any of the pre-computed `target_use_positions`.\n  q = collections.deque([(current_pos, [])]) \n  visited = {current_pos} \n\n  target_adj_pos_path = None # To store the path to the closest target use position\n\n  while q:\n      (r, c), path = q.popleft()\n\n      # If the current BFS node is one of our target use positions, we've found\n      # the shortest path to a spot from which we can collect.\n      if (r, c) in target_use_positions:\n          target_adj_pos_path = path \n          break \n\n      # Explore valid neighboring cells (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT) from the current position.\n      for action_dir, (dr, dc) in DELTAS.items():\n          nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc \n\n          # Check 1: Ensure the new position is within the grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= nr < WIDTH and 0 <= nc < HEIGHT):\n              continue\n          \n          # Check 2: Ensure the new position is traversable (not an obstacle).\n          # This is the same traversability check as for target_use_positions.\n          is_traversable = True\n          for i_kind in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n              if grid[nr, nc, i_kind] == 1: \n                  is_traversable = False\n                  break \n          \n          if not is_traversable:\n              continue \n          \n          # Check 3: If this neighbor has not been visited yet, add it to the queue.\n          if (nr, nc) not in visited:\n              visited.add((nr, nc))\n              q.append(((nr, nc), path + [action_dir]))\n    \n  # 5. Construct the final sequence of actions.\n  # If a path to a valid collection spot was found, append the USE action.\n  if target_adj_pos_path is not None:\n      actions.extend(target_adj_pos_path)\n      actions.append(USE) \n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T00:52:09.190602", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions = []\n  \n  current_state = env._current_state \n  grid = current_state.grid\n  current_pos = current_state.pos\n  \n  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Retrieve action mapping from the environment for robustness\n  _action_specs = env.action_specs()\n  DOWN = _action_specs['DOWN']\n  UP = _action_specs['UP']\n  LEFT = _action_specs['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = _action_specs['RIGHT']\n  USE = _action_specs['USE']\n\n  DELTAS = {\n      UP: (-1, 0),\n      DOWN: (1, 0),\n      LEFT: (0, -1),\n      RIGHT: (0, 1)\n  }\n\n  # V2 Improvement: Ensure the primitive is actually grabbable.\n  if primitive_id not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  # 1. Check if the agent is already next to the primitive\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_id):\n      actions.append(USE)\n      return actions\n\n  # 2. Find all locations of the target primitive on the grid\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for r in range(WIDTH):\n      for c in range(HEIGHT):\n          if grid[r, c, primitive_id] == 1:\n              primitive_locations.append((r, c))\n\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      return []\n\n  # V2 Improvement: Pre-compute all valid \"target use positions\".\n  # A \"target use position\" is a grid cell from which the agent can apply 'USE'\n  # to collect the desired primitive. This cell must be adjacent to a primitive\n  # location AND must be traversable by the agent.\n  target_use_positions = set()\n  for pr, pc in primitive_locations:\n      for dr, dc in DELTAS.values(): # Iterate through all 4 cardinal directions\n          adj_r, adj_c = pr + dr, pc + dc\n\n          # Ensure the adjacent cell is within grid boundaries\n          if not (0 <= adj_r < WIDTH and 0 <= adj_c < HEIGHT):\n              continue\n\n          # Ensure the adjacent cell is traversable (not an obstacle).\n          # An agent must be able to stand on this cell to use a primitive next to it.\n          is_traversable = True\n          for i_kind in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n              if grid[adj_r, adj_c, i_kind] == 1: # If this cell contains a non-grabbable item\n                  is_traversable = False\n                  break # This neighbor is an obstacle\n          \n          if is_traversable:\n              target_use_positions.add((adj_r, adj_c))\n    \n  # If there are no traversable spots from which to use the primitive, it's uncollectable.\n  if not target_use_positions:\n      return []\n\n  # 3. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path\n  #    to any of the pre-computed `target_use_positions`.\n  q = collections.deque([(current_pos, [])]) \n  visited = {current_pos} \n\n  path_to_target_use_pos = None \n\n  while q:\n      (r, c), path = q.popleft()\n\n      # Directly check if the current BFS node (r, c) is one of our pre-computed target positions.\n      if (r, c) in target_use_positions:\n          path_to_target_use_pos = path \n          break \n\n      # Explore valid neighboring cells from the current position (r, c).\n      for action_dir, (dr, dc) in DELTAS.items():\n          nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc \n\n          # Check 1: Ensure the new position is within the grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= nr < WIDTH and 0 <= nc < HEIGHT):\n              continue\n          \n          # Check 2: Ensure the new position is traversable (not an obstacle).\n          is_traversable = True\n          for i_kind in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n              if grid[nr, nc, i_kind] == 1: \n                  is_traversable = False\n                  break \n          \n          if not is_traversable:\n              continue \n          \n          # Check 3: If this neighbor has not been visited yet, add it to the queue.\n          if (nr, nc) not in visited:\n              visited.add((nr, nc))\n              q.append(((nr, nc), path + [action_dir]))\n    \n  # 4. Construct the final sequence of actions.\n  if path_to_target_use_pos is not None:\n      actions.extend(path_to_target_use_pos)\n      actions.append(USE) \n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T00:53:34.464658", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  initial_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's initial position (col, row)\n  initial_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's initial direction (0:N, 1:E, 2:S, 3:W)\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape # Grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n\n  # Get the integer index for the primitive (lowercase for consistency)\n  try:\n    primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive.lower())\n  except KeyError:\n    # If the primitive name is not found, it's not a valid primitive to collect.\n    return []\n\n  # Get action mappings\n  ACTION_MAP = env.action_specs()\n  ACTIONS = {\n      \"DOWN\": ACTION_MAP[\"DOWN\"],\n      \"UP\": ACTION_MAP[\"UP\"],\n      \"LEFT\": ACTION_MAP[\"LEFT\"],\n      \"RIGHT\": ACTION_MAP[\"RIGHT\"],\n      \"USE\": ACTION_MAP[\"USE\"]\n  }\n\n  # Define (d_col, d_row) deltas for each move action AND the resulting direction.\n  # When an agent moves, its direction attribute updates to match the direction of movement.\n  # Format: (action_index: (delta_col, delta_row, new_direction_after_move))\n  MOVE_ACTION_DATA = {\n      ACTIONS[\"UP\"]: (0, -1, 0),    # Move North (Up), face North (dir 0)\n      ACTIONS[\"DOWN\"]: (0, 1, 2),   # Move South (Down), face South (dir 2)\n      ACTIONS[\"LEFT\"]: (-1, 0, 3),  # Move West (Left), face West (dir 3)\n      ACTIONS[\"RIGHT\"]: (1, 0, 1)   # Move East (Right), face East (dir 1)\n  }\n\n  # Define (d_col, d_row) deltas for each cardinal direction.\n  # This is used to calculate the coordinates of the cell directly in front of the agent.\n  # dir: 0=N, 1=E, 2=S, 3=W\n  DIR_TO_DELTA = {\n      0: (0, -1),  # North (Up): (dc, dr)\n      1: (1, 0),   # East (Right): (dc, dr)\n      2: (0, 1),   # South (Down): (dc, dr)\n      3: (-1, 0)   # West (Left): (dc, dr)\n  }\n\n  # Get boundary index for obstacle checking. Boundaries are typically impassable.\n  try:\n      boundary_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(\"boundary\")\n  except KeyError:\n      # If 'boundary' isn't in the index, assume no boundary obstacles for movement\n      # or that they are not explicitly indexed. Set to a value that won't match a real kind.\n      boundary_idx = -1 \n\n  # If the primitive itself is the boundary, it's not something we can \"collect\" by interaction.\n  if primitive_idx == boundary_idx:\n      return []\n\n  # Breadth-First Search (BFS) setup\n  # Queue stores elements as: ((current_position=(col, row), current_direction), list_of_actions_to_reach_this_state)\n  queue = collections.deque([((initial_pos, initial_dir), [])])\n  # Visited set stores ((col, row), direction) tuples to avoid redundant exploration and cycles.\n  visited = {(initial_pos, initial_dir)}\n\n  best_path = None # To store the shortest sequence of actions found\n\n  while queue:\n      # Dequeue the current state and path\n      ((current_c, current_r), current_dir), path_actions = queue.popleft()\n\n      # --- Check if the goal (primitive collection condition) is met for the current state ---\n      # The 'USE' action operates on the cell directly in front of the agent.\n      front_dc, front_dr = DIR_TO_DELTA[current_dir]\n      front_c, front_r = current_c + front_dc, current_r + front_dr\n\n      # Ensure the cell in front is within grid boundaries\n      if (0 <= front_c < grid_width and 0 <= front_r < grid_height):\n          # Check if the desired primitive is located in the cell directly in front\n          if grid[front_c, front_r, primitive_idx] > 0:\n              # Goal reached: The agent is positioned and oriented correctly to 'USE' the primitive.\n              # This path leads to the primitive being in front, ready to be \"used\" (collected/interacted with).\n              best_path = path_actions + [ACTIONS[\"USE\"]]\n              break # Found the shortest path, exit BFS (since BFS finds shortest path first)\n\n      # --- Explore neighboring states by trying all possible movement actions ---\n      for action, (dc_move, dr_move, new_dir) in MOVE_ACTION_DATA.items():\n          next_c, next_r = current_c + dc_move, current_r + dr_move\n          next_pos = (next_c, next_r)\n          next_state = (next_pos, new_dir) # The new state includes the updated position AND direction\n\n          # Check if the next position is within grid boundaries\n          if not (0 <= next_c < grid_width and 0 <= next_r < grid_height):\n              continue\n\n          # Check if the next position is blocked by a 'boundary' (impassable terrain)\n          # This check is only performed if `boundary_idx` was successfully found.\n          if boundary_idx != -1 and grid[next_c, next_r, boundary_idx] > 0:\n              continue\n\n          # If the state (position and direction) has not been visited, add it to the queue\n          if next_state not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_state)\n              queue.append((next_state, path_actions + [action]))\n\n  # Return the found path, or an empty list if no path could be found (BFS queue exhausted)\n  return best_path if best_path is not None else []", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T00:53:35.597285", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  initial_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's initial position (col, row)\n  initial_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's initial direction (0:N, 1:E, 2:S, 3:W)\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape # Grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n\n  # Get action mappings\n  ACTION_MAP = env.action_specs()\n  ACTIONS = {\n      \"DOWN\": ACTION_MAP[\"DOWN\"],\n      \"UP\": ACTION_MAP[\"UP\"],\n      \"LEFT\": ACTION_MAP[\"LEFT\"],\n      \"RIGHT\": ACTION_MAP[\"RIGHT\"],\n      \"USE\": ACTION_MAP[\"USE\"]\n  }\n\n  # Define (d_col, d_row) deltas for each move action AND the resulting direction.\n  # When an agent moves, its direction attribute updates to match the direction of movement.\n  # Format: (action_index: (delta_col, delta_row, new_direction_after_move))\n  MOVE_ACTION_DATA = {\n      ACTIONS[\"UP\"]: (0, -1, 0),    # Move North (Up), face North (dir 0)\n      ACTIONS[\"DOWN\"]: (0, 1, 2),   # Move South (Down), face South (dir 2)\n      ACTIONS[\"LEFT\"]: (-1, 0, 3),  # Move West (Left), face West (dir 3)\n      ACTIONS[\"RIGHT\"]: (1, 0, 1)   # Move East (Right), face East (dir 1)\n  }\n\n  # Define (d_col, d_row) deltas for each cardinal direction.\n  # This is used to calculate the coordinates of the cell directly in front of the agent.\n  # dir: 0=N, 1=E, 2=S, 3=W\n  DIR_TO_DELTA = {\n      0: (0, -1),  # North (Up): (dc, dr)\n      1: (1, 0),   # East (Right): (dc, dr)\n      2: (0, 1),   # South (Down): (dc, dr)\n      3: (-1, 0)   # West (Left): (dc, dr)\n  }\n\n  # Get the integer index for the primitive (lowercase for consistency with cookbook index)\n  try:\n    primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive.lower())\n  except KeyError:\n    # If the primitive name is not found, it's uncollectable by this function.\n    return []\n\n  # Get boundary index for obstacle checking. Boundaries are impassable.\n  boundary_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(\"boundary\")\n\n  # --- Categorize the primitive type for collection logic ---\n  # If the primitive itself is a boundary, it cannot be collected or traversed.\n  if primitive_idx == boundary_idx:\n      return []\n\n  is_grabbable_item = (primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices)\n  is_water_or_stone = (primitive_idx == env.world.water_index or primitive_idx == env.world.stone_index)\n  is_workshop = (primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices)\n\n  requires_facing_and_use = is_grabbable_item or is_water_or_stone\n  requires_adjacency = is_workshop\n\n  # If the primitive is not a known collectable type, return empty path.\n  if not (requires_facing_and_use or requires_adjacency):\n      return []\n\n  # --- Pre-compute all valid target agent states (position, direction) for collection ---\n  target_agent_states = set() # Stores ((col, row), direction) tuples\n\n  # Find all instances of the primitive on the grid using numpy's argwhere\n  primitive_locations_on_grid = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, primitive_idx] > 0)\n  \n  for prim_c, prim_r in primitive_locations_on_grid:\n      if requires_facing_and_use:\n          # For primitives requiring 'USE' (e.g., WOOD, WATER, STONE), agent must be facing the primitive.\n          # This means the primitive is in the cell *in front* of the agent.\n          # If primitive is at (prim_c, prim_r) and agent is facing direction 'd',\n          # then agent's position (agent_c, agent_r) must be (prim_c - dc_front, prim_r - dr_front).\n          for d in range(4): # Iterate through all 4 possible agent directions\n              dc_front, dr_front = DIR_TO_DELTA[d]\n              agent_c, agent_r = prim_c - dc_front, prim_r - dr_front\n\n              # Check if the calculated agent position is within grid bounds\n              if (0 <= agent_c < grid_width and 0 <= agent_r < grid_height):\n                  # Check if the agent's potential position is not a boundary\n                  if grid[agent_c, agent_r, boundary_idx] == 0:\n                      target_agent_states.add(((agent_c, agent_r), d))\n\n      elif requires_adjacency:\n          # For workshops, agent needs to be in any adjacent (8-directional) traversable cell.\n          # Agent's direction doesn't specifically matter for *being* adjacent to a workshop,\n          # but the BFS state needs a direction, so we consider all 4.\n          for dc_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n              for dr_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n                  if dc_adj == 0 and dr_adj == 0: # Skip the primitive's own cell itself\n                      continue\n                  agent_c, agent_r = prim_c + dc_adj, prim_r + dr_adj\n\n                  # Check if the calculated agent position is within grid bounds\n                  if (0 <= agent_c < grid_width and 0 <= agent_r < grid_height):\n                      # Check if the agent's potential position is not a boundary\n                      if grid[agent_c, agent_r, boundary_idx] == 0:\n                          for d in range(4): # All directions are valid for an adjacent position\n                              target_agent_states.add(((agent_c, agent_r), d))\n  \n  # If no valid target states are found (e.g., primitive is surrounded by boundaries, or not on map)\n  if not target_agent_states:\n      return []\n\n  # --- Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path to any target state ---\n  # Queue stores elements as: ((current_position=(col, row), current_direction), list_of_actions_to_reach_this_state)\n  queue = collections.deque([((initial_pos, initial_dir), [])])\n  # Visited set stores ((col, row), direction) tuples to avoid redundant exploration and cycles.\n  visited = {(initial_pos, initial_dir)}\n\n  best_path_to_target = None # To store the shortest sequence of actions found to reach any target state\n\n  while queue:\n      # Dequeue the current state and path\n      ((current_c, current_r), current_dir), path_actions = queue.popleft()\n\n      # If the current state is one of our pre-computed target states, we've found the shortest path.\n      if ((current_c, current_r), current_dir) in target_agent_states:\n          best_path_to_target = path_actions\n          break # Found the shortest path, exit BFS\n\n      # --- Explore neighboring states by trying all possible movement actions ---\n      for action, (dc_move, dr_move, new_dir) in MOVE_ACTION_DATA.items():\n          next_c, next_r = current_c + dc_move, current_r + dr_move\n          next_pos = (next_c, next_r)\n          next_state = (next_pos, new_dir) # The new state includes the updated position AND direction\n\n          # Check if the next position is within grid boundaries\n          if not (0 <= next_c < grid_width and 0 <= next_r < grid_height):\n              continue\n\n          # Check if the next position is blocked by a 'boundary' (impassable terrain)\n          if grid[next_c, next_r, boundary_idx] > 0:\n              continue\n\n          # If the state (position and direction) has not been visited, add it to the queue\n          if next_state not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_state)\n              queue.append((next_state, path_actions + [action]))\n\n  # --- Construct the final action sequence based on the shortest path found ---\n  if best_path_to_target is None:\n      return [] # No path found to any target collection position.\n  \n  if requires_facing_and_use:\n      # For grabbable items/water/stone, append the 'USE' action after reaching the target state.\n      return best_path_to_target + [ACTIONS[\"USE\"]]\n  else: # implies requires_adjacency (for workshops)\n      # For workshops, just reaching an adjacent position is sufficient; no 'USE' action here from collect.\n      return best_path_to_target", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T00:54:18.150758", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1`.\"\"\"\n  actions = []\n\n  # 1. Get Action Mappings and Primitive Index\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT, USE = action_map['UP'], action_map['DOWN'], action_map['LEFT'], action_map['RIGHT'], action_map['USE']\n\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Get current state information\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  start_dir = current_state.dir # Initial direction of the agent\n  global_grid = current_state.grid\n  W, H, _ = global_grid.shape\n  inventory = current_state.inventory # Check agent's current inventory\n\n  # Optimization: If the primitive is already in the inventory, no actions are needed.\n  if inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # Determine if the primitive is grabbable (can be walked on and picked up)\n  # or non-grabbable (requires being adjacent and USE action, e.g., mining stone/water, using workshop).\n  primitive_is_grabbable = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n\n  # Map DMLab action values to (dr, dc) movement deltas AND CraftState.dir values.\n  # CraftState.dir: 0=South (DOWN), 1=North (UP), 2=West (LEFT), 3=East (RIGHT).\n  # The agent's direction updates to match the last movement action.\n  action_to_move_and_dir = {\n      UP: ((-1, 0), 1),    # Move UP, new direction is North (1)\n      DOWN: ((1, 0), 0),   # Move DOWN, new direction is South (0)\n      LEFT: ((0, -1), 2),  # Move LEFT, new direction is West (2)\n      RIGHT: ((0, 1), 3)   # Move RIGHT, new direction is East (3)\n  }\n\n  # Map CraftState.dir values to (dr, dc) deltas for the cell \"in front\" of the agent.\n  # This is crucial for determining where the USE action will apply.\n  dir_to_fwd_delta = {\n      0: (1, 0),  # Facing South, cell in front is (row+1, col)\n      1: (-1, 0), # Facing North, cell in front is (row-1, col)\n      2: (0, -1), # Facing West, cell in front is (row, col-1)\n      3: (0, 1)   # Facing East, cell in front is (row, col+1)\n  }\n\n  # Obstacle indices: cells that cannot be stepped onto (e.g., Water, Stone, Workshops).\n  # The `CraftState.step` method prevents movement into any cell containing a non-grabbable item.\n  obstacle_indices = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  def is_valid_move(r, c):\n      \"\"\"Checks if (r, c) is within grid bounds and doesn't contain any non-grabbable obstacles.\"\"\"\n      if not (0 <= r < W and 0 <= c < H):\n          return False\n      # A cell is an obstacle if it contains *any* non-grabbable item.\n      # Agent can walk onto grabbable items (e.g., WOOD, IRON), but not non-grabbable ones.\n      if any(global_grid[r, c, obs_idx] == 1 for obs_idx in obstacle_indices):\n          return False\n      return True\n  \n  # BFS Queue: Stores tuples of ( (current_position (r,c), current_direction (int)), path_so_far (list of actions) )\n  queue = collections.deque([(((start_pos), start_dir), [])])\n  \n  # Visited set: Stores (position (r,c), direction (int)) tuples to avoid redundant exploration.\n  # The direction is included because it affects the outcome of a 'USE' action.\n  visited = {(start_pos, start_dir)}\n\n  path_to_target = None # This will store the sequence of actions to reach the target state.\n  \n  while queue:\n      ((r, c), current_dir_val), path_so_far = queue.popleft()\n\n      # Check if the current state (position and direction) satisfies the collection goal.\n      if primitive_is_grabbable:\n          # For grabbable items (e.g., WOOD, IRON), the agent needs to be on the same cell\n          # as the primitive to collect it. The item is collected automatically when stepping on it.\n          if global_grid[r, c, primitive_idx] == 1:\n              path_to_target = path_so_far\n              break # Found the shortest path to a cell containing the grabbable item.\n      else:\n          # For non-grabbable items (e.g., STONE, WATER, WORKSHOP), the agent must be\n          # adjacent to the primitive AND facing it to use the 'USE' action.\n          fwd_dr, fwd_dc = dir_to_fwd_delta[current_dir_val]\n          target_r, target_c = r + fwd_dr, c + fwd_dc\n\n          # Check if the cell directly in front contains the primitive.\n          if 0 <= target_r < W and 0 <= target_c < H and global_grid[target_r, target_c, primitive_idx] == 1:\n              path_to_target = path_so_far\n              break # Found the shortest path ending in the correct position and direction to use the primitive.\n\n      # Explore neighbors by applying movement actions.\n      for action_val, (move_delta, new_dir_val) in action_to_move_and_dir.items():\n          dr, dc = move_delta\n          next_r, next_c = r + dr, c + dc\n          next_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n          next_state_tuple = (next_pos, new_dir_val)\n\n          # Only proceed if the next position is valid (within bounds and not an obstacle)\n          # and this (position, direction) state has not been visited before.\n          if is_valid_move(next_r, next_c) and next_state_tuple not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_state_tuple)\n              queue.append((next_state_tuple, path_so_far + [action_val]))\n  \n  if path_to_target is not None:\n      if not primitive_is_grabbable:\n          # If the primitive is non-grabbable, the 'USE' action is required after reaching the target position/direction.\n          actions = path_to_target + [USE]\n      else:\n          # If the primitive is grabbable, simply reaching the target cell is sufficient for collection.\n          actions = path_to_target\n  # If path_to_target remains None, 'actions' stays an empty list, indicating the primitive is unreachable.\n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T00:54:19.455859", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions = []\n\n  # 1. Get Action Mappings and Primitive Index\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT, USE = action_map['UP'], action_map['DOWN'], action_map['LEFT'], action_map['RIGHT'], action_map['USE']\n\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Get current state information\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  start_dir = current_state.dir # Initial direction of the agent\n  global_grid = current_state.grid\n  W, H, _ = global_grid.shape\n\n  # Determine if the primitive is grabbable (can be walked on and picked up)\n  # or non-grabbable (requires being adjacent and USE action, e.g., mining stone/water, using workshop).\n  primitive_is_grabbable = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n\n  # Map DMLab action values to (dr, dc) movement deltas AND CraftState.dir values.\n  # CraftState.dir: 0=South (DOWN), 1=North (UP), 2=West (LEFT), 3=East (RIGHT).\n  # The agent's direction updates to match the last movement action.\n  action_to_move_and_dir = {\n      UP: ((-1, 0), 1),    # Move UP, new direction is North (1)\n      DOWN: ((1, 0), 0),   # Move DOWN, new direction is South (0)\n      LEFT: ((0, -1), 2),  # Move LEFT, new direction is West (2)\n      RIGHT: ((0, 1), 3)   # Move RIGHT, new direction is East (3)\n  }\n\n  # Map CraftState.dir values to (dr, dc) deltas for the cell \"in front\" of the agent.\n  # This is crucial for determining where the USE action will apply.\n  dir_to_fwd_delta = {\n      0: (1, 0),  # Facing South, cell in front is (row+1, col)\n      1: (-1, 0), # Facing North, cell in front is (row-1, col)\n      2: (0, -1), # Facing West, cell in front is (row, col-1)\n      3: (0, 1)   # Facing East, cell in front is (row, col+1)\n  }\n\n  # Obstacle indices: cells that cannot be stepped onto (e.g., Water, Stone, Workshops).\n  # The `CraftState.step` method prevents movement into any cell containing a non-grabbable item.\n  obstacle_indices = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  def is_valid_move(r, c):\n      \"\"\"Checks if (r, c) is within grid bounds and doesn't contain any non-grabbable obstacles.\"\"\"\n      if not (0 <= r < W and 0 <= c < H):\n          return False\n      # A cell is an obstacle if it contains *any* non-grabbable item.\n      # Agent can walk onto grabbable items (e.g., WOOD, IRON), but not non-grabbable ones.\n      if any(global_grid[r, c, obs_idx] == 1 for obs_idx in obstacle_indices):\n          return False\n      return True\n  \n  # BFS Queue: Stores tuples of ( (current_position (r,c), current_direction (int)), path_so_far (list of actions) )\n  queue = collections.deque([(((start_pos), start_dir), [])])\n  \n  # Visited set: Stores (position (r,c), direction (int)) tuples to avoid redundant exploration.\n  visited = {(start_pos, start_dir)}\n\n  path_to_target = None # This will store the sequence of actions to reach the target state.\n  \n  while queue:\n      ((r, c), current_dir_val), path_so_far = queue.popleft()\n\n      # Check if the current state (position and direction) satisfies the collection goal.\n      if primitive_is_grabbable:\n          # For grabbable items (e.g., WOOD, IRON), the agent needs to be on the same cell\n          # as the primitive to collect it.\n          if global_grid[r, c, primitive_idx] == 1:\n              path_to_target = path_so_far\n              break # Found the shortest path to a cell containing the grabbable item.\n      else:\n          # For non-grabbable items (e.g., STONE, WATER, WORKSHOP), the agent must be\n          # adjacent to the primitive AND facing it to use the 'USE' action.\n          fwd_dr, fwd_dc = dir_to_fwd_delta[current_dir_val]\n          target_r, target_c = r + fwd_dr, c + fwd_dc\n\n          # Check if the cell directly in front contains the primitive.\n          if 0 <= target_r < W and 0 <= target_c < H and global_grid[target_r, target_c, primitive_idx] == 1:\n              path_to_target = path_so_far\n              break # Found the shortest path ending in the correct position and direction to use the primitive.\n\n      # Explore neighbors by applying movement actions.\n      for action_val, (move_delta, new_dir_val) in action_to_move_and_dir.items():\n          dr, dc = move_delta\n          next_r, next_c = r + dr, c + dc\n          next_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n          next_state_tuple = (next_pos, new_dir_val)\n\n          # Only proceed if the next position is valid (within bounds and not an obstacle)\n          # and this (position, direction) state has not been visited before.\n          if is_valid_move(next_r, next_c) and next_state_tuple not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_state_tuple)\n              queue.append((next_state_tuple, path_so_far + [action_val]))\n  \n  if path_to_target:\n      # If a path was found, append the USE action at the end to perform the collection.\n      actions = path_to_target + [USE]\n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T00:55:26.134312", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  UP = action_map['UP']\n  LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  current_pos = current_state.pos\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Helper function to check if a cell is within bounds and not an obstacle\n  def _is_traversable(x, y):\n      if not (0 <= x < grid_width and 0 <= y < grid_height):\n          return False\n      for obs_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n          if grid[x, y, obs_idx] > 0:\n              return False\n      return True\n\n  if primitive_idx not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n      # If the item is not grabbable (e.g., WATER, WORKSHOP), it cannot be collected.\n      return []\n\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n      # If the agent is already in the 3x3 neighborhood of the primitive, just use it.\n      return [USE]\n\n  # Find all grid locations where the primitive exists\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for x in range(grid_width):\n      for y in range(grid_height):\n          if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n              primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      # Primitive not found anywhere on the map\n      return []\n\n  # Define possible movement deltas (cardinal movements)\n  move_deltas = {\n      (0, -1): UP,\n      (0, 1): DOWN,\n      (-1, 0): LEFT,\n      (1, 0): RIGHT\n  }\n\n  # Determine all possible target cells for the BFS.\n  # These are cells where the agent can stand such that the primitive_idx is in its 3x3 neighborhood.\n  # This aligns with the `current_state.next_to()` method's definition.\n  target_cells_for_use = set()\n  for px, py in primitive_locations:\n      # Iterate through the 3x3 neighborhood (including diagonals) around the primitive location\n      for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n          for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n              nx, ny = px + dx, py + dy\n              \n              if _is_traversable(nx, ny):\n                  target_cells_for_use.add((nx, ny))\n  \n  # If no traversable target cells can be found, the primitive is unreachable\n  if not target_cells_for_use:\n      return []\n\n  # Perform a Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path\n  # Queue stores tuples: ((current_x, current_y), list_of_actions_taken)\n  queue = collections.deque([(current_pos, [])])\n  visited = {current_pos} # Keep track of visited coordinates to avoid loops\n  found_path = None\n\n  while queue:\n      (x, y), path = queue.popleft()\n\n      # If the current cell is one of our target cells, we've found a path.\n      # The BFS ensures this is the shortest path.\n      if (x, y) in target_cells_for_use:\n          found_path = path\n          break\n\n      # Explore neighboring cells (cardinal movements only)\n      for (dx, dy), action_to_take in move_deltas.items():\n          nx, ny = x + dx, y + dy\n          \n          if _is_traversable(nx, ny) and (nx, ny) not in visited:\n              visited.add((nx, ny))\n              queue.append(((nx, ny), path + [action_to_take]))\n\n  # If a path was found, append the USE action to collect the primitive\n  if found_path is None:\n      # No path could be found to any cell from which the primitive can be collected\n      return []\n  else:\n      # Path found, now perform the USE action\n      return found_path + [USE]", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T00:55:27.338620", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  UP = action_map['UP']\n  LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  current_pos = current_state.pos\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Determine if the primitive is an item that can be \"collected\" or interacted with\n  # via the USE action. This includes items that can be picked up (grabbable)\n  # and static interactable objects like workshops.\n  is_grabbable = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n  \n  if not (is_grabbable or is_workshop):\n      # If the primitive is neither grabbable nor a workshop, it's not a target\n      # for the 'collect' action (e.g., BOUNDARY, WATER, STONE, if not mineable).\n      return []\n\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n      # If the agent is already in the 3x3 neighborhood of the primitive, just use it.\n      return [USE]\n\n  # Find all grid locations where the primitive exists\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for x in range(grid_width):\n      for y in range(grid_height):\n          if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n              primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      # Primitive not found anywhere on the map\n      return []\n\n  # Define possible movement deltas (cardinal movements)\n  move_deltas = {\n      (0, -1): UP,\n      (0, 1): DOWN,\n      (-1, 0): LEFT,\n      (1, 0): RIGHT\n  }\n\n  # Define \"impassable\" terrain for pathfinding.\n  # We assume that entities listed in `cookbook.environment` are generally obstacles,\n  # but workshops (which are also in `environment` and `non_grabbable_indices`)\n  # are typically points you can walk onto/through to interact or pass.\n  # So, `impassable_for_movement_kinds` are environment entities *excluding* workshops.\n  impassable_for_movement_kinds = set()\n  for env_idx in env.world.cookbook.environment:\n      if env_idx not in env.world.workshop_indices:\n          impassable_for_movement_kinds.add(env_idx)\n  \n  # Perform a Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path\n  # Queue stores tuples: ((current_x, current_y), list_of_actions_taken)\n  queue = collections.deque([(current_pos, [])])\n  visited = {current_pos} # Keep track of visited coordinates to avoid loops\n  found_path = None\n\n  # Determine all possible target cells for the BFS.\n  # These are cells where the agent can stand such that the primitive_idx is in its 3x3 neighborhood.\n  target_cells_for_use = set()\n  for px, py in primitive_locations:\n      for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n          for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n              nx, ny = px + dx, py + dy\n\n              # Check if the potential target cell is within grid bounds\n              if 0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height:\n                  # Check if the potential target cell is traversable\n                  is_traversable_target_cell = True\n                  # Iterate through all entity kinds that might be present at (nx, ny)\n                  for k_idx in range(grid.shape[2]): \n                      if grid[nx, ny, k_idx] > 0 and k_idx in impassable_for_movement_kinds:\n                          is_traversable_target_cell = False\n                          break\n                  \n                  if is_traversable_target_cell:\n                      target_cells_for_use.add((nx, ny))\n  \n  # If no traversable target cells can be found, the primitive is unreachable\n  if not target_cells_for_use:\n      return []\n\n  while queue:\n      (x, y), path = queue.popleft()\n\n      # If the current cell is one of our target cells, we've found a path.\n      # The BFS ensures this is the shortest path.\n      if (x, y) in target_cells_for_use:\n          found_path = path\n          break\n\n      # Explore neighboring cells (cardinal movements only)\n      for (dx, dy), action_to_take in move_deltas.items():\n          nx, ny = x + dx, y + dy\n\n          # Check bounds for the new cell\n          if 0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height:\n              # Check if the new cell (nx, ny) is traversable (not an obstacle)\n              is_traversable = True\n              # Iterate through all entity kinds that might be present at (nx, ny)\n              for k_idx in range(grid.shape[2]): \n                  if grid[nx, ny, k_idx] > 0 and k_idx in impassable_for_movement_kinds:\n                      is_traversable = False\n                      break\n              \n              # If traversable and not yet visited, add to queue\n              if is_traversable and (nx, ny) not in visited:\n                  visited.add((nx, ny))\n                  queue.append(((nx, ny), path + [action_to_take]))\n\n  # If a path was found, append the USE action to collect/interact with the primitive\n  if found_path is None:\n      # No path could be found to any cell from which the primitive can be collected\n      return []\n  else:\n      # Path found, now perform the USE action\n      return found_path + [USE]", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T00:56:44.129217", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions_list = []\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  initial_grid = current_state.grid # The grid state at the start of collection\n  initial_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's starting (row, col)\n  initial_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's starting direction (0:R, 1:U, 2:L, 3:D)\n\n  # Get the integer ID for the target primitive from the cookbook index\n  primitive_id = current_state.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = initial_grid.shape # Get grid dimensions\n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment's action specifications\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION = action_map['UP']\n  TURN_LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  TURN_RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define changes in (row, col) for each direction when moving forward\n  DIR_TO_DRDC = {\n      0: (0, 1),   # Facing RIGHT (0), moves in positive column (c+1)\n      1: (-1, 0),  # Facing UP (1), moves in negative row (r-1)\n      2: (0, -1),  # Facing LEFT (2), moves in negative column (c-1)\n      3: (1, 0)    # Facing DOWN (3), moves in positive row (r+1)\n  }\n\n  # Define how agent's direction changes for left/right turns\n  TURN_LEFT_MAP = {0: 1, 1: 2, 2: 3, 3: 0}  # R(0)->U(1)->L(2)->D(3)->R(0)\n  TURN_RIGHT_MAP = {0: 3, 1: 0, 2: 1, 3: 2} # R(0)->D(3)->L(2)->U(1)->R(0)\n\n  # Get indices of entities that block movement (e.g., BOUNDARY, WATER, WORKSHOP_X)\n  non_walkable_kinds_indices = current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # BFS initialization: Queue stores ( (current_pos_tuple, current_dir_int), list_of_actions_to_reach_here )\n  queue = collections.deque([((initial_pos, initial_dir), [])])\n  # Visited set stores (position, direction) tuples to prevent cycles and redundant exploration\n  visited = {(initial_pos, initial_dir)}\n\n  target_path = None # This will store the action sequence if a target state is found\n\n  while queue:\n      (current_pos, current_dir), path_actions = queue.popleft()\n      r, c = current_pos\n\n      # 1. Goal Check: Is the primitive directly in front of the agent in the current state?\n      # Calculate the coordinates of the cell directly in front of the agent\n      front_dr, front_dc = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n      front_r, front_c = r + front_dr, c + front_dc\n      \n      # Check if the \"front\" cell is within grid bounds\n      if (0 <= front_r < WIDTH and 0 <= front_c < HEIGHT):\n          # If the primitive exists in that front cell, we've reached a collectable state\n          if initial_grid[front_r, front_c, primitive_id] > 0:\n              target_path = path_actions # The actions to get to this (pos, dir) state\n              break # Found the path, exit BFS\n\n      # 2. Explore possible next actions: Move Forward, Turn Left, Turn Right\n      \n      # Try Move Forward\n      move_dr, move_dc = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir] # Dr,Dc for moving forward\n      next_r, next_c = r + move_dr, c + move_dc\n      next_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n      next_dir = current_dir # Direction does not change when moving forward\n\n      # Check if the next position is within bounds and this (position, direction) state hasn't been visited\n      if (0 <= next_r < WIDTH and 0 <= next_c < HEIGHT and\n          (next_pos, next_dir) not in visited):\n          \n          # Check if the next position is walkable\n          is_walkable = True\n          # Agent cannot walk onto non-grabbable/blocking entities\n          for kind_idx in non_walkable_kinds_indices:\n              if initial_grid[next_r, next_c, kind_idx] > 0:\n                  is_walkable = False\n                  break\n          # Agent also cannot walk onto the primitive itself to collect it; it must be adjacent\n          if is_walkable and initial_grid[next_r, next_c, primitive_id] > 0:\n              is_walkable = False\n\n          if is_walkable:\n              visited.add((next_pos, next_dir))\n              queue.append(((next_pos, next_dir), path_actions + [MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION]))\n\n      # Try Turn Left\n      next_dir_left = TURN_LEFT_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Turning does not change position, only direction\n      if ((current_pos, next_dir_left) not in visited):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_left))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_left), path_actions + [TURN_LEFT_ACTION]))\n\n      # Try Turn Right\n      next_dir_right = TURN_RIGHT_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Turning does not change position, only direction\n      if ((current_pos, next_dir_right) not in visited):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_right))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_right), path_actions + [TURN_RIGHT_ACTION]))\n\n  # If a path was successfully found to a state where the primitive is in front,\n  # append the USE action to complete the collection.\n  if target_path is not None:\n      actions_list.extend(target_path)\n      actions_list.append(USE_ACTION)\n\n  return actions_list", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T00:56:45.441639", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Returns a list of actions to find and collect the primitive in the passed env.\n    \n    This function implements a Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest\n    sequence of actions (movements and turns) that brings the agent to a position\n    where the specified primitive can be collected using the 'USE' action.\n    It assumes the 'USE' action collects the item directly in front of the agent.\n\n    Args:\n        env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab object representing the current simulation environment.\n        primitive (str): The name of the primitive resource to collect (e.g., \"WOOD\", \"STONE\").\n\n    Returns:\n        List[int]: A sequence of action indices (integers) to execute to collect the primitive.\n                   Returns an empty list if the primitive is unreachable.\n  \"\"\"\n  actions_list = []\n  current_state = env._current_state # Get the current state of the environment\n  initial_grid = current_state.grid # The grid layout at the start of this collection attempt\n  initial_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's starting position (row, column) tuple\n  initial_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's starting direction (0:RIGHT, 1:UP, 2:LEFT, 3:DOWN)\n\n  # Get the integer ID for the target primitive from the cookbook index\n  try:\n      primitive_id = current_state.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n      # If the primitive name is not found, it's uncollectable by this method.\n      return []\n\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = initial_grid.shape # Dimensions of the grid\n\n  # Map human-readable action names to their integer indices as understood by the environment\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION = action_map['UP']   # Assuming 'UP' corresponds to moving forward\n  TURN_LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  TURN_RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define changes in (row, column) for each facing direction when moving forward\n  # This mapping is crucial for calculating new positions after a 'MOVE_FORWARD' action.\n  DIR_TO_DRDC = {\n      0: (0, 1),   # Facing RIGHT: +1 to column (move right)\n      1: (-1, 0),  # Facing UP: -1 to row (move up)\n      2: (0, -1),  # Facing LEFT: -1 to column (move left)\n      3: (1, 0)    # Facing DOWN: +1 to row (move down)\n  }\n\n  # Define how agent's direction changes when turning left or right\n  TURN_LEFT_MAP = {0: 1, 1: 2, 2: 3, 3: 0}   # R (0) -> U (1) -> L (2) -> D (3) -> R (0)\n  TURN_RIGHT_MAP = {0: 3, 1: 0, 2: 1, 3: 2} # R (0) -> D (3) -> L (2) -> U (1) -> R (0)\n\n  # Get indices of entities that block agent movement (e.g., boundaries, water, workshops)\n  non_walkable_kinds_indices = current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # BFS setup:\n  # Queue stores tuples: ((current_position_tuple, current_direction_int), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here)\n  queue = collections.deque([((initial_pos, initial_dir), [])])\n  # Visited set stores (position_tuple, direction_int) to prevent redundant exploration and cycles.\n  visited = {(initial_pos, initial_dir)}\n\n  target_path = None # This will store the action sequence once the target state is found.\n\n  while queue:\n      (current_pos, current_dir), path_actions = queue.popleft()\n      r, c = current_pos # Current row and column of the agent\n\n      # 1. Check if the current state is a goal state:\n      # A goal state is one where the primitive is directly in front of the agent,\n      # allowing the 'USE' action to collect it.\n      \n      # Calculate coordinates of the cell directly in front of the agent\n      front_dr, front_dc = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n      front_r, front_c = r + front_dr, c + front_dc\n      \n      # Check if the cell in front is within grid boundaries\n      if (0 <= front_r < WIDTH and 0 <= front_c < HEIGHT):\n          # Check if the primitive is present in the cell directly in front\n          if initial_grid[front_r, front_c, primitive_id] > 0:\n              target_path = path_actions # Found path to the desired position+direction\n              break # Exit BFS as the shortest path is found\n\n      # 2. Explore possible next actions from the current state: Move Forward, Turn Left, Turn Right\n      \n      # Try Move Forward action:\n      next_r_move, next_c_move = r + front_dr, c + front_dc # Position after moving forward\n      next_pos_move = (next_r_move, next_c_move)\n      next_dir_move = current_dir # Direction remains unchanged after moving forward\n\n      # Check if next position is within grid boundaries and if this (position, direction) state\n      # has not been visited to avoid redundant paths and infinite loops.\n      if (0 <= next_r_move < WIDTH and 0 <= next_c_move < HEIGHT and\n          (next_pos_move, next_dir_move) not in visited):\n          \n          is_walkable = True\n          # A cell is walkable if it's not occupied by any non-walkable entity (boundary, water, workshop etc.).\n          for kind_idx in non_walkable_kinds_indices:\n              if initial_grid[next_r_move, next_c_move, kind_idx] > 0:\n                  is_walkable = False\n                  break\n          # Crucially, the agent cannot walk *onto* the primitive itself; it must be adjacent to use it.\n          if initial_grid[next_r_move, next_c_move, primitive_id] > 0:\n              is_walkable = False\n\n          if is_walkable:\n              visited.add((next_pos_move, next_dir_move))\n              queue.append(((next_pos_move, next_dir_move), path_actions + [MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION]))\n\n      # Try Turn Left action:\n      next_dir_left = TURN_LEFT_MAP[current_dir] # New direction after turning left\n      # Turning does not change the agent's position.\n      if ((current_pos, next_dir_left) not in visited):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_left))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_left), path_actions + [TURN_LEFT_ACTION]))\n\n      # Try Turn Right action:\n      next_dir_right = TURN_RIGHT_MAP[current_dir] # New direction after turning right\n      # Turning does not change the agent's position.\n      if ((current_pos, next_dir_right) not in visited):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_right))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_right), path_actions + [TURN_RIGHT_ACTION]))\n\n  # If a path to a collectible position (where the primitive is directly in front) was found,\n  # append the 'USE' action to the sequence to actually collect it.\n  if target_path is not None:\n      actions_list.extend(target_path)\n      actions_list.append(USE_ACTION)\n\n  return actions_list", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T00:57:34.819823", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Get the integer index for the primitive\n  cookbook_index = env.world.cookbook.index\n  try:\n    primitive_idx = cookbook_index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    # Primitive name not found in the cookbook, cannot collect\n    return []\n\n  # Check if primitive is already in inventory. If so, no collection is needed.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # Ensure the target primitive is something that can be 'collected' (i.e., it's grabbable).\n  # 'collect' implies adding to inventory via a 'USE' action. Non-grabbable items cannot be collected this way.\n  if primitive_idx not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n      # This primitive cannot be collected via a simple 'USE' action after reaching it.\n      return []\n\n  # Define non-traversable indices. These are grid cells the agent cannot move onto.\n  # We consider any non-grabbable entity that is NOT a workshop as a movement barrier.\n  # Workshops are typically locations where the agent can stand to interact.\n  non_traversable_indices = set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices) - set(env.world.workshop_indices)\n  \n  # Get action mappings (e.g., DOWN->0, UP->1, LEFT->2, RIGHT->3, USE->4) from the environment.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n  \n  # Define valid movement directions and their corresponding actions.\n  # (dx, dy) tuples represent changes in (x, y) coordinates for a move.\n  moves = {\n      action_map['DOWN']: (0, 1),\n      action_map['UP']: (0, -1),\n      action_map['LEFT']: (-1, 0),\n      action_map['RIGHT']: (1, 0),\n  }\n\n  # BFS initialization for pathfinding.\n  # The queue stores tuples of (current_position, list_of_actions_to_reach_this_position).\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])])\n  # The visited set stores positions to avoid cycles and redundant path explorations.\n  visited = {start_pos}\n\n  while queue:\n    current_pos, path_actions = queue.popleft()\n    cx, cy = current_pos\n\n    # Create a temporary CraftState instance for the current position to leverage its `next_to` method.\n    # This method efficiently checks if the primitive is in the 3x3 neighborhood.\n    # Only `pos` changes; other state attributes are taken from the actual current state as they are static for pathfinding.\n    temp_state_for_check = craft.CraftState(\n        scenario=current_state.scenario,\n        grid=grid,\n        pos=current_pos,\n        dir=current_state.dir,\n        inventory=current_state.inventory\n    )\n    \n    # Check if the primitive is within the 3x3 neighborhood of the current position.\n    # If it is, we've found a location from which the primitive can be 'USE'd.\n    if temp_state_for_check.next_to(primitive_idx):\n      # Append the 'USE' action and return the complete sequence of actions.\n      return path_actions + [USE_ACTION]\n\n    # Explore valid, unvisited, and traversable neighboring positions.\n    for action_id, (dx_move, dy_move) in moves.items():\n      next_x, next_y = cx + dx_move, cy + dy_move\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # 1. Check if the next position is out of grid bounds.\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue \n\n      # 2. Check if the next position has already been visited during BFS.\n      if next_pos in visited:\n        continue\n\n      # 3. Check traversability: Determine if the agent can move into `next_pos`.\n      # A cell is blocked if it contains any 'kind' that is in our `non_traversable_indices`.\n      is_blocked = False\n      for kind_idx in non_traversable_indices:\n          if grid[next_x, next_y, kind_idx] == 1:\n              is_blocked = True\n              break\n      if is_blocked:\n        continue # Cannot move into a blocked cell.\n\n      # If all checks pass (within bounds, not visited, not an obstacle),\n      # add the new position to the visited set and the queue.\n      visited.add(next_pos)\n      queue.append((next_pos, path_actions + [action_id]))\n\n  # If the BFS queue becomes empty and no path to the primitive was found,\n  # the primitive is unreachable from the current state.\n  return []", "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T00:57:36.027844", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # 1. Get the integer index for the primitive.\n  cookbook_index = env.world.cookbook.index\n  try:\n    primitive_idx = cookbook_index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    # Primitive name not found in the cookbook, cannot collect it.\n    return []\n\n  # 2. Check if primitive is already in inventory.\n  # If we already have it, no need to collect more.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # 3. Ensure the target primitive is actually something we can 'collect'.\n  # 'Collect' implies picking something up and adding it to inventory via a 'USE' action.\n  # This typically only applies to grabbable items. Non-grabbable items (like WATER or WORKSHOPS)\n  # cannot be \"collected\" into inventory in this manner.\n  if primitive_idx not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  # 4. Define non-traversable indices.\n  # We assume that any non-grabbable entity that is NOT a workshop is a barrier to movement.\n  # Workshops are special locations the agent can typically stand on or pass through.\n  non_traversable_indices = set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices) - set(env.world.workshop_indices)\n  \n  # 5. Get action mappings from the environment's action specifications.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n  \n  # Define valid movement directions and their corresponding actions and (dx, dy) offsets.\n  # (dx, dy) tuples represent changes in (x, y) coordinates for movements.\n  # Using the action_map ensures robustness to numerical action ID changes.\n  moves = {\n      action_map['DOWN']: (0, 1),   # (dx, dy) for moving down (increasing y)\n      action_map['UP']: (0, -1),    # (dx, dy) for moving up (decreasing y)\n      action_map['LEFT']: (-1, 0),  # (dx, dy) for moving left (decreasing x)\n      action_map['RIGHT']: (1, 0),  # (dx, dy) for moving right (increasing x)\n  }\n\n  # 6. BFS initialization for pathfinding.\n  # The queue stores tuples of (current_position, list_of_actions_to_reach_this_position).\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])])\n  # The visited set stores positions to avoid cycles and redundant path explorations.\n  visited = {start_pos}\n\n  # 7. BFS Loop.\n  while queue:\n    current_pos, path_actions = queue.popleft()\n    cx, cy = current_pos\n\n    # 7.1. Check for Goal Condition: Is the primitive within the 3x3 neighborhood of current_pos?\n    # This simulates `CraftState.next_to(primitive_idx)` behavior, indicating if a 'USE' action\n    # from `current_pos` could interact with (collect) the primitive.\n    is_adjacent_or_on_primitive = False\n    for dx_adj in range(-1, 2):  # Iterate through offsets for the 3x3 grid around current_pos\n      for dy_adj in range(-1, 2):\n        nx_adj, ny_adj = cx + dx_adj, cy + dy_adj\n        \n        # Check if the adjacent/on-primitive cell is within grid boundaries.\n        if 0 <= nx_adj < grid_width and 0 <= ny_adj < grid_height:\n          # Check if this cell contains the desired primitive.\n          # The grid stores one-hot encoding for each kind, so 1 indicates presence.\n          if grid[nx_adj, ny_adj, primitive_idx] == 1:\n            is_adjacent_or_on_primitive = True\n            break # Found the primitive, no need to check further in this neighborhood\n      if is_adjacent_or_on_primitive:\n        break # Found the primitive, no need to check further in this neighborhood\n\n    if is_adjacent_or_on_primitive:\n      # If the primitive is within 'USE' range, append the 'USE' action and return the complete path.\n      return path_actions + [USE_ACTION]\n\n    # 7.2. Explore valid, unvisited, and traversable neighboring positions.\n    for action_id, (dx_move, dy_move) in moves.items():\n      next_x, next_y = cx + dx_move, cy + dy_move\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # Check 1: Is the next position out of grid bounds?\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue \n\n      # Check 2: Has the next position already been visited during BFS?\n      if next_pos in visited:\n        continue\n\n      # Check 3: Is the cell at `next_pos` blocked by a non-traversable entity?\n      # A cell is blocked if it contains any 'kind' that is in our `non_traversable_indices`.\n      is_blocked = False\n      for kind_idx in non_traversable_indices:\n          if grid[next_x, next_y, kind_idx] == 1:\n              is_blocked = True\n              break # Found a blocking entity, no need to check other kinds on this tile.\n      if is_blocked:\n        continue # Cannot move into a blocked cell.\n\n      # If all checks pass (within bounds, not visited, not blocked),\n      # add the new position to the visited set and the queue.\n      visited.add(next_pos)\n      queue.append((next_pos, path_actions + [action_id]))\n\n  # 8. If the BFS queue becomes empty and no path to the primitive was found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable from the current state under these rules.\n  return []", "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T00:58:25.948652", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions_list = []\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  initial_grid = current_state.grid\n  initial_pos = current_state.pos # tuple (r, c)\n  initial_dir = current_state.dir # int (0-3), 0:RIGHT, 1:UP, 2:LEFT, 3:DOWN\n\n  primitive_id = current_state.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = initial_grid.shape\n\n  # === Improvement for v2: Ensure the primitive is actually grabbable ===\n  # If the primitive cannot be picked up into inventory (e.g., it's a terrain feature, water, or a workshop),\n  # return an empty list immediately as it's not \"collectible\".\n  if primitive_id in current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  # Map DSL movement/turn actions to their integer indices from action_specs\n  MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION = action_map['UP']\n  TURN_LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  TURN_RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Direction mapping: (dr, dc) for agent's facing direction (0:R, 1:U, 2:L, 3:D)\n  DIR_TO_DRDC = {\n      0: (0, 1),   # Facing RIGHT, move in positive column direction (c)\n      1: (-1, 0),  # Facing UP, move in negative row direction (r)\n      2: (0, -1),  # Facing LEFT, move in negative column direction (c)\n      3: (1, 0)    # Facing DOWN, move in positive row direction (r)\n  }\n\n  # Map for turning left/right, updating the agent's direction (0-3)\n  TURN_LEFT_MAP = {0: 1, 1: 2, 2: 3, 3: 0}\n  TURN_RIGHT_MAP = {0: 3, 1: 0, 2: 1, 3: 2}\n\n  # Get indices of non-grabbable items that block movement (e.g., BOUNDARY, WATER, WORKSHOP_X)\n  non_walkable_kinds_indices = current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # Optimization: If the primitive is already collectible from the current position, just use it.\n  # The `next_to` method checks the 3x3 neighborhood around the agent's position.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_id):\n      return [USE_ACTION]\n\n  # BFS state: ((row, col), direction), path_actions\n  # Queue stores ( (current_pos_tuple, current_dir_int), list_of_actions_to_reach_here )\n  queue = collections.deque([((initial_pos, initial_dir), [])])\n  # Visited set stores (current_pos_tuple, current_dir_int) to avoid cycles and redundant paths\n  visited = {(initial_pos, initial_dir)}\n\n  target_path = None # Stores the action list to reach the target state\n\n  while queue:\n      (current_pos, current_dir), path_actions = queue.popleft()\n      r, c = current_pos\n\n      # Check if the current position (r, c) is suitable for collecting the primitive.\n      # This means the primitive must be in the 3x3 neighborhood of (r, c).\n      found_collectable_position = False\n      for dr_check in [-1, 0, 1]:\n          for dc_check in [-1, 0, 1]:\n              check_r, check_c = r + dr_check, c + dc_check\n              # Ensure the checked cell is within grid bounds\n              if (0 <= check_r < WIDTH and 0 <= check_c < HEIGHT and\n                  initial_grid[check_r, check_c, primitive_id] > 0):\n                  found_collectable_position = True\n                  break # Found the primitive in the neighborhood\n          if found_collectable_position:\n              break\n\n      if found_collectable_position:\n          target_path = path_actions\n          break # Path to a position from which the primitive can be collected is found\n\n      # Explore possible next actions: Move Forward, Turn Left, Turn Right\n      \n      # Try Move Forward\n      move_dr, move_dc = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n      next_r, next_c = r + move_dr, c + move_dc\n      next_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n      next_dir = current_dir # Moving forward does not change facing direction\n\n      # Check if next_pos is within bounds and this (position, direction) state hasn't been visited\n      if (0 <= next_r < WIDTH and 0 <= next_c < HEIGHT and\n          (next_pos, next_dir) not in visited):\n          \n          is_walkable = True\n          # A cell is walkable if it doesn't contain any non-grabbable entity (e.g., boundary, water, workshops).\n          for kind_idx in non_walkable_kinds_indices:\n              if initial_grid[next_r, next_c, kind_idx] > 0:\n                  is_walkable = False\n                  break\n\n          if is_walkable:\n              visited.add((next_pos, next_dir))\n              queue.append(((next_pos, next_dir), path_actions + [MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION]))\n\n      # Try Turn Left\n      next_dir_left = TURN_LEFT_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Turning does not change position, only direction.\n      if ((current_pos, next_dir_left) not in visited):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_left))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_left), path_actions + [TURN_LEFT_ACTION]))\n\n      # Try Turn Right\n      next_dir_right = TURN_RIGHT_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Turning does not change position, only direction.\n      if ((current_pos, next_dir_right) not in visited):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_right))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_right), path_actions + [TURN_RIGHT_ACTION]))\n\n  # If a path was found to a collectable position, append the USE action\n  if target_path is not None:\n      actions_list.extend(target_path)\n      actions_list.append(USE_ACTION)\n\n  return actions_list", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T00:58:27.079348", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions_list = []\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  initial_grid = current_state.grid\n  initial_pos = current_state.pos # tuple (r, c)\n  initial_dir = current_state.dir # int (0-3), 0:RIGHT, 1:UP, 2:LEFT, 3:DOWN\n\n  primitive_id = current_state.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = initial_grid.shape\n\n  # === Improvement for v2: Ensure the primitive is actually grabbable ===\n  # The 'collect' function implies picking up an item into inventory.\n  # If the primitive is an entity that cannot be picked up (e.g., WORKSHOP, WATER, BOUNDARY,\n  # or specific environmental \"STONE\" that is not a collectible resource),\n  # it cannot be \"collected\". In such cases, return an empty list immediately.\n  # The `grabbable_indices` is the authoritative source for what can be picked up.\n  if primitive_id not in current_state.world.grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  # Map DSL movement/turn actions to their integer indices from action_specs\n  MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION = action_map['UP'] # Often used for 'move forward'\n  TURN_LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  TURN_RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Direction mapping: (dr, dc) for agent's facing direction (0:R, 1:U, 2:L, 3:D)\n  DIR_TO_DRDC = {\n      0: (0, 1),   # Facing RIGHT, move in positive column direction (c)\n      1: (-1, 0),  # Facing UP, move in negative row direction (r)\n      2: (0, -1),  # Facing LEFT, move in negative column direction (c)\n      3: (1, 0)    # Facing DOWN, move in positive row direction (r)\n  }\n\n  # Map for turning left/right, updating the agent's direction (0-3)\n  TURN_LEFT_MAP = {0: 1, 1: 2, 2: 3, 3: 0}\n  TURN_RIGHT_MAP = {0: 3, 1: 0, 2: 1, 3: 2}\n\n  # Get indices of non-grabbable items that block movement (e.g., BOUNDARY, WATER, WORKSHOP_X).\n  # These are truly obstacles that the agent cannot walk through.\n  non_walkable_kinds_indices = current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # Optimization: If the primitive is already collectible from the current position, just use it.\n  # The `next_to` method checks the 3x3 neighborhood around the agent's position.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_id):\n      return [USE_ACTION]\n\n  # BFS state: ((row, col), direction), path_actions\n  # Queue stores ( (current_pos_tuple, current_dir_int), list_of_actions_to_reach_here )\n  queue = collections.deque([((initial_pos, initial_dir), [])])\n  # Visited set stores (current_pos_tuple, current_dir_int) to avoid cycles and redundant paths\n  visited = {(initial_pos, initial_dir)}\n\n  target_path = None # Stores the action list to reach the target state\n\n  while queue:\n      (current_pos, current_dir), path_actions = queue.popleft()\n      r, c = current_pos\n\n      # Check if the current position (r, c) is suitable for collecting the primitive.\n      # This means the primitive must be in the 3x3 neighborhood of (r, c).\n      found_collectable_position = False\n      for dr_check in [-1, 0, 1]:\n          for dc_check in [-1, 0, 1]:\n              check_r, check_c = r + dr_check, c + dc_check\n              # Ensure the checked cell is within grid bounds\n              if (0 <= check_r < WIDTH and 0 <= check_c < HEIGHT and\n                  initial_grid[check_r, check_c, primitive_id] > 0):\n                  found_collectable_position = True\n                  break # Found the primitive in the neighborhood\n          if found_collectable_position:\n              break\n\n      if found_collectable_position:\n          target_path = path_actions\n          break # Path to a position from which the primitive can be collected is found\n\n      # Explore possible next actions: Move Forward, Turn Left, Turn Right\n      \n      # Try Move Forward\n      move_dr, move_dc = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n      next_r, next_c = r + move_dr, c + move_dc\n      next_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n      next_dir = current_dir # Moving forward does not change facing direction\n\n      # Check if next_pos is within bounds and this (position, direction) state hasn't been visited\n      if (0 <= next_r < WIDTH and 0 <= next_c < HEIGHT and\n          (next_pos, next_dir) not in visited):\n          \n          is_walkable = True\n          # A cell is walkable if it doesn't contain any non-grabbable entity (e.g., boundary, water, workshops).\n          # These are typically non-walkable and should block movement.\n          for kind_idx in non_walkable_kinds_indices:\n              if initial_grid[next_r, next_c, kind_idx] > 0:\n                  is_walkable = False\n                  break\n          \n          # As in collect_v1, we do NOT check if the primitive itself blocks movement here.\n          # The agent can walk onto a cell containing a collectible primitive (e.g., grass, wood).\n\n          if is_walkable:\n              visited.add((next_pos, next_dir))\n              queue.append(((next_pos, next_dir), path_actions + [MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION]))\n\n      # Try Turn Left\n      next_dir_left = TURN_LEFT_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Turning does not change position, only direction.\n      if ((current_pos, next_dir_left) not in visited):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_left))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_left), path_actions + [TURN_LEFT_ACTION]))\n\n      # Try Turn Right\n      next_dir_right = TURN_RIGHT_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Turning does not change position, only direction.\n      if ((current_pos, next_dir_right) not in visited):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_right))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_right), path_actions + [TURN_RIGHT_ACTION]))\n\n  # If a path was found to a collectable position, append the USE action\n  if target_path is not None:\n      actions_list.extend(target_path)\n      actions_list.append(USE_ACTION)\n\n  return actions_list", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T00:59:17.258032", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions = []\n  \n  # Get the current state directly for grid and position information\n  current_state = env._current_state \n  grid = current_state.grid\n  current_pos = current_state.pos\n  \n  # Get the integer ID of the primitive from the cookbook index.\n  # This provides the numerical representation of the primitive in the grid and inventory.\n  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Retrieve action mapping from the environment for robustness.\n  # This ensures the action integers (e.g., UP, DOWN) correspond to the environment's\n  # current mapping, making the code resilient to changes in action definitions.\n  _action_specs = env.action_specs()\n  DOWN = _action_specs['DOWN']\n  UP = _action_specs['UP']\n  LEFT = _action_specs['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = _action_specs['RIGHT']\n  USE = _action_specs['USE']\n\n  # Define movement deltas for convenience for the 4 cardinal directions.\n  # Maps action indices to their corresponding (row_change, col_change).\n  DELTAS = {\n      UP: (-1, 0),\n      DOWN: (1, 0),\n      LEFT: (0, -1),\n      RIGHT: (0, 1)\n  }\n\n  # 1. Immediate check: If the agent is already next to (or on) the primitive,\n  #    a single 'USE' action is sufficient to collect it.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_id):\n      actions.append(USE)\n      return actions\n\n  # 2. Find all locations of the target primitive on the grid.\n  #    This helps in identifying potential targets for the pathfinding algorithm.\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for r in range(WIDTH):\n      for c in range(HEIGHT):\n          # If the primitive_id occupies this cell (indicated by a 1 in its grid layer).\n          if grid[r, c, primitive_id] == 1:\n              primitive_locations.append((r, c))\n\n  # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the grid, it cannot be collected.\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      return []\n\n  # 3. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path\n  #    to a cell adjacent to any primitive location.\n  # The queue stores tuples: ((current_row, current_col), [list_of_actions_to_reach_here]).\n  q = collections.deque([(current_pos, [])]) \n  # The visited set keeps track of positions already explored to avoid cycles and redundant paths.\n  visited = {current_pos} \n\n  # This variable will store the shortest path found to an adjacent cell.\n  target_adj_pos_path = None \n\n  while q:\n      (r, c), path = q.popleft()\n\n      # Check if the current position (r, c) is adjacent to any of the primitive locations.\n      # \"Adjacent\" means a Manhattan distance of 1 (horizontally or vertically).\n      # From such a position, the 'USE' action can be applied to collect the primitive.\n      for pr, pc in primitive_locations:\n          if abs(r - pr) + abs(c - pc) == 1: \n              target_adj_pos_path = path # Found the shortest path to an adjacent cell.\n              break # Break from this inner loop as we've found our target path.\n      \n      if target_adj_pos_path is not None:\n          break # Exit the BFS loop once the shortest path to an adjacent cell has been found.\n\n      # Explore valid neighboring cells (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT).\n      for action_dir, (dr, dc) in DELTAS.items():\n          nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc # Calculate the new potential position.\n\n          # Check bounds: Ensure the new position is within the grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= nr < WIDTH and 0 <= nc < HEIGHT):\n              continue\n          \n          # Check traversability:\n          # A cell is considered non-traversable if it contains any item\n          # whose kind index is in the world's `non_grabbable_indices` set.\n          # These typically represent obstacles like 'BOUNDARY', 'WATER', or 'WORKSHOP' structures.\n          is_traversable = not any(grid[nr, nc, i_kind] == 1 \n                                   for i_kind in env.world.non_grabbable_indices)\n          \n          if not is_traversable:\n              continue # Skip this neighbor if it's an obstacle.\n          \n          # If the neighbor has not been visited, add it to the queue to explore later.\n          if (nr, nc) not in visited:\n              visited.add((nr, nc)) # Mark as visited.\n              new_path = path + [action_dir] # Extend the current path with the action taken.\n              q.append(((nr, nc), new_path)) # Add the new state and path to the queue.\n    \n  # 4. If a path to an adjacent cell was found during BFS,\n  #    extend the actions list with this path and then append a 'USE' action.\n  #    The 'USE' action will collect the primitive from the adjacent cell.\n  if target_adj_pos_path is not None:\n      actions.extend(target_adj_pos_path)\n      actions.append(USE) # Perform 'USE' action once adjacent to the primitive.\n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T00:59:18.450925", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions = []\n  \n  current_state = env._current_state \n  grid = current_state.grid\n  current_pos = current_state.pos\n  \n  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Retrieve action mapping from the environment for robustness\n  _action_specs = env.action_specs()\n  DOWN = _action_specs['DOWN']\n  UP = _action_specs['UP']\n  LEFT = _action_specs['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = _action_specs['RIGHT']\n  USE = _action_specs['USE']\n\n  # Define movement deltas for convenience for the 4 cardinal directions\n  DELTAS = {\n      UP: (-1, 0),\n      DOWN: (1, 0),\n      LEFT: (0, -1),\n      RIGHT: (0, 1)\n  }\n\n  # Pre-compute a traversability map: True if cell is an obstacle (non-traversable).\n  # This avoids repeated checks for non-grabbable items at each step of the BFS.\n  is_obstacle_map = np.zeros((WIDTH, HEIGHT), dtype=bool)\n  for r in range(WIDTH):\n      for c in range(HEIGHT):\n          # A cell is an obstacle if any non-grabbable item (e.g., BOUNDARY, WATER)\n          # is present at that grid location.\n          is_obstacle_map[r, c] = any(grid[r, c, i_kind] == 1 \n                                      for i_kind in env.world.non_grabbable_indices)\n\n  # 1. Immediate check: If the agent is already next to the primitive, just use it.\n  # This handles cases where the primitive is directly collectible from the current position.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_id):\n      actions.append(USE)\n      return actions\n\n  # 2. Find all locations of the target primitive on the grid.\n  # This is necessary to define the targets for our pathfinding algorithm.\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for r in range(WIDTH):\n      for c in range(HEIGHT):\n          if grid[r, c, primitive_id] == 1:\n              primitive_locations.append((r, c))\n\n  # If no primitive of the specified kind is found on the grid, return an empty list\n  # as it cannot be collected.\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      return []\n\n  # 3. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path\n  #    to a cell that is adjacent to any of the primitive locations.\n  # The queue stores tuples: ((current_row, current_col), [list_of_actions_to_reach_here]).\n  q = collections.deque([(current_pos, [])]) \n  # The visited set keeps track of positions already explored to avoid cycles and redundant paths.\n  visited = {current_pos} \n\n  # This variable will store the shortest path found to an adjacent cell.\n  target_adj_pos_path = None \n\n  while q:\n      (r, c), path = q.popleft()\n\n      # Check if the current BFS node (r, c) is adjacent to any of the primitive locations.\n      # \"Adjacent\" means a Manhattan distance of 1 (horizontally or vertically).\n      # If so, we've found the shortest path to a collectible spot.\n      for pr, pc in primitive_locations:\n          if abs(r - pr) + abs(c - pc) == 1: \n              target_adj_pos_path = path # Store the path found.\n              break # Exit inner loop, as we've found an adjacent primitive.\n      \n      if target_adj_pos_path is not None:\n          break # Exit the BFS loop, as the shortest path is found.\n\n      # Explore valid neighboring cells (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT).\n      for action_dir, (dr, dc) in DELTAS.items():\n          nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc # Calculate the coordinates of the potential new position.\n\n          # Check 1: Ensure the new position is within the grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= nr < WIDTH and 0 <= nc < HEIGHT):\n              continue\n          \n          # Check 2: Use the pre-computed obstacle map to determine traversability.\n          # If the cell is marked as an obstacle, it cannot be moved onto.\n          if is_obstacle_map[nr, nc]:\n              continue\n          \n          # Check 3: If this neighbor has not been visited yet, add it to the queue.\n          if (nr, nc) not in visited:\n              visited.add((nr, nc)) # Mark as visited.\n              new_path = path + [action_dir] # Extend the current path with the action taken.\n              q.append(((nr, nc), new_path)) # Add the new state to the queue for further exploration.\n    \n  # 4. Construct the final sequence of actions.\n  # If a path to an adjacent cell was found during BFS,\n  # extend the actions list with this path and then append a 'USE' action\n  # to collect the primitive.\n  if target_adj_pos_path is not None:\n      actions.extend(target_adj_pos_path)\n      actions.append(USE) # Perform 'USE' action once adjacent to the primitive.\n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T01:00:09.506823", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Returns a list of actions to find and collect the primitive in the passed env.\n    This version correctly distinguishes between grabbable and non-grabbable items\n    to determine the required final agent position and orientation for collection.\n    \n    Args:\n        env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab object.\n        primitive (str): The name of the primitive to collect.\n\n    Returns:\n        List[int]: A sequence of action indices to execute (moves + final USE).\n  \"\"\"\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  # Map action names to their integer IDs for clarity and robust lookup.\n  UP = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Get numerical ID for the target primitive from the cookbook's index.\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  try:\n      primitive_id = cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n  except KeyError:\n      # If the primitive name is not recognized by the cookbook, it cannot be collected.\n      return []\n\n  # Get the current state of the agent and environment from the CraftLab wrapper.\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's current (row, col) position\n  start_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's current facing direction (0:N, 1:E, 2:S, 3:W)\n\n  # Grid dimensions are WIDTH (rows) x HEIGHT (columns).\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Define IDs of terrain types that the agent cannot walk through or onto.\n  # These are \"boundary\" (walls), \"water\", and typically \"stone\" (if it acts as a solid block).\n  impassable_terrain_ids = {\n      cookbook.index.index(\"boundary\"),\n      env.world.water_index,\n      env.world.stone_index # Assuming stone is a solid obstacle to walking\n  }\n\n  # Helper function to check if a given grid cell (r, c) is a valid location\n  # for the agent to stand on.\n  def is_valid_walk_pos(r, c):\n    # Check if the position is within the grid boundaries.\n    if not (0 <= r < WIDTH and 0 <= c < HEIGHT):\n      return False\n    # Check if the cell contains any impassable terrain.\n    # If the grid layer for any impassable ID has a value > 0, it means it's present.\n    for impassable_id in impassable_terrain_ids:\n        if grid[r, c, impassable_id] > 0:\n            return False # This cell is blocked.\n    return True\n\n  # Determine if the target primitive is 'grabbable'. Grabbable items can be collected\n  # by standing *on the same cell* and using 'USE'. Non-grabbable items (like a workbench,\n  # or a stone block to mine) require the agent to be *adjacent* and *facing* the item.\n  is_grabbable = primitive_id in env.world.grabbable_indices\n\n  # Pre-scan the grid to find all occurrences of the target primitive.\n  primitive_locations = [] # List of (row, col) tuples where the primitive is located.\n  for r in range(WIDTH):\n      for c in range(HEIGHT):\n          if grid[r, c, primitive_id] > 0:\n              primitive_locations.append((r, c))\n\n  # If no instances of the primitive are found on the grid, it's impossible to collect.\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      return []\n\n  # Define movement deltas (dr, dc) for each action and the resulting agent direction.\n  # The agent's direction updates to match the direction of movement.\n  move_deltas = {\n      UP: (-1, 0), # Moving UP changes row by -1\n      DOWN: (1, 0), # Moving DOWN changes row by +1\n      LEFT: (0, -1), # Moving LEFT changes col by -1\n      RIGHT: (0, 1) # Moving RIGHT changes col by +1\n  }\n\n  # Map action IDs to the DMLab-style direction ID (0:UP/North, 1:RIGHT/East, 2:DOWN/South, 3:LEFT/West).\n  # This is the direction the agent will face after performing that move action.\n  action_to_direction_map = {\n      UP: 0,    # Agent faces North after moving UP\n      RIGHT: 1, # Agent faces East after moving RIGHT\n      DOWN: 2,  # Agent faces South after moving DOWN\n      LEFT: 3,  # Agent faces West after moving LEFT\n  }\n\n  # Map DMLab direction ID to the (dr, dc) delta that represents looking in that direction.\n  # This is used for non-grabbable items, where the agent needs to face the item.\n  dir_to_look_delta = {\n      0: (-1, 0), # North (UP)\n      1: (0, 1),  # East (RIGHT)\n      2: (1, 0),  # South (DOWN)\n      3: (0, -1)  # West (LEFT)\n  }\n\n  # --- Define Target Goal States for BFS ---\n  # These are (agent_row, agent_col, agent_direction) tuples from which a single 'USE'\n  # action will successfully collect the primitive.\n  target_use_states = set()\n  for prim_r, prim_c in primitive_locations:\n      if is_grabbable:\n          # For grabbable items, the agent must be on the same cell as the item.\n          if is_valid_walk_pos(prim_r, prim_c):\n              # Agent's direction usually doesn't matter when picking up grabbable items on the same cell.\n              # We consider all 4 directions as valid initial directions before USE.\n              for d_id in action_to_direction_map.values(): # Iterate through all possible DMLab direction IDs\n                  target_use_states.add((prim_r, prim_c, d_id))\n      else:\n          # For non-grabbable items, the agent must be adjacent to the item AND facing it.\n          for facing_dir_id, (dr_look, dc_look) in dir_to_look_delta.items():\n              # Calculate the required agent position (ar, ac) such that if the agent\n              # is at (ar, ac) and faces `facing_dir_id`, it will be looking at (prim_r, prim_c).\n              # The item is at (agent_r + dr_look, agent_c + dc_look).\n              # So, agent_pos = (prim_r - dr_look, prim_c - dc_look).\n              agent_r, agent_c = prim_r - dr_look, prim_c - dc_look\n              \n              # Check if this calculated agent position is valid to stand on.\n              if is_valid_walk_pos(agent_r, agent_c):\n                  target_use_states.add((agent_r, agent_c, facing_dir_id))\n\n  # If no valid target states can be reached (e.g., primitive is in an unreachable location),\n  # it's impossible to collect this primitive.\n  if not target_use_states:\n      return []\n\n  # --- Breadth-First Search (BFS) Implementation ---\n  # Queue stores tuples: ((current_row, current_col), current_direction, list_of_actions_taken_so_far)\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_pos, start_dir, [])])\n  # Visited set stores (position, direction) pairs to avoid redundant exploration and cycles.\n  visited = {(start_pos, start_dir)}\n\n  while queue:\n    (r, c), current_dir, path = queue.popleft()\n\n    # Check if the current state is a goal state (i.e., we are in a position and\n    # facing the correct direction to use 'USE' and collect the item).\n    if (r, c, current_dir) in target_use_states:\n        return path + [USE] # Append the final USE action and return the complete path.\n\n    # Explore possible next states by trying all movement actions.\n    for action, (dr_move, dc_move) in move_deltas.items():\n      next_r, next_c = r + dr_move, c + dc_move\n      next_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n      \n      # The agent's facing direction updates to the direction of the movement.\n      next_dir = action_to_direction_map[action]\n\n      # Only add to queue if the next position is valid to walk on and this exact\n      # (position, direction) state has not been visited before.\n      if is_valid_walk_pos(next_r, next_c) and (next_pos, next_dir) not in visited:\n        visited.add((next_pos, next_dir))\n        queue.append((next_pos, next_dir, path + [action]))\n\n  # If the BFS queue becomes empty and no path to a target state was found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable from the current state.\n  return []", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T01:00:10.641099", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Get relevant IDs from the environment's world and cookbook\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  try:\n      primitive_id = cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n  except KeyError:\n      # If the primitive name is not recognized, return an empty list of actions.\n      return []\n\n  # Get the current state information\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  start_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's current facing direction\n\n  # Grid dimensions (WIDTH is first dimension, HEIGHT is second)\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Define IDs of entities that are considered strictly impassable for agent movement.\n  # Agent cannot walk onto these cells.\n  impassable_terrain_ids = {\n      cookbook.index.index(\"boundary\"),\n      env.world.water_index,\n      env.world.stone_index # Assuming stone also blocks movement onto its cell\n  }\n\n  # Helper function to check if a position (r, c) is valid for the agent to stand on.\n  # This means it must be within grid bounds and not contain any impassable terrain.\n  def is_valid_walk_pos(r, c):\n    # Check if the position is within the grid boundaries.\n    if not (0 <= r < WIDTH and 0 <= c < HEIGHT):\n      return False\n    # Check if the cell at (r, c) contains any of the defined impassable terrain types.\n    for impassable_id in impassable_terrain_ids:\n        if grid[r, c, impassable_id] > 0:\n            return False # This cell contains an impassable block\n    return True\n\n  # Determine if the primitive itself is grabbable (can be picked up by standing on its cell and using USE).\n  is_grabbable = primitive_id in env.world.grabbable_indices\n\n  # Pre-compute all locations on the grid where the target primitive exists.\n  primitive_locations = [] # List of (row, col) tuples\n  for r in range(WIDTH):\n      for c in range(HEIGHT):\n          if grid[r, c, primitive_id] > 0:\n              primitive_locations.append((r, c))\n\n  # If there are no instances of the primitive found on the grid, it's impossible to collect.\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      return []\n\n  # Define possible movement deltas (dr, dc) and their corresponding action IDs.\n  move_deltas = {\n      UP: (-1, 0), # Moving UP changes row by -1\n      DOWN: (1, 0), # Moving DOWN changes row by +1\n      LEFT: (0, -1), # Moving LEFT changes col by -1\n      RIGHT: (0, 1) # Moving RIGHT changes col by +1\n  }\n\n  # Map action IDs to the resulting agent direction ID after performing that move.\n  # DMLab-style directions: 0:UP, 1:RIGHT, 2:DOWN, 3:LEFT\n  action_to_direction_map = {\n      UP: 0,\n      RIGHT: 1, # Note: Moving Right changes direction to Right\n      DOWN: 2,\n      LEFT: 3,\n  }\n\n  # Map direction ID to the (dr, dc) delta that points to the cell *in front of* the agent.\n  # This is used for non-grabbable items where the agent must face the item.\n  dir_to_look_delta = {\n      0: (-1, 0), # UP (looking North)\n      1: (0, 1),  # RIGHT (looking East)\n      2: (1, 0),  # DOWN (looking South)\n      3: (0, -1)  # LEFT (looking West)\n  }\n\n  # Pre-compute all valid (agent_pos_r, agent_pos_c, agent_direction_id) states\n  # from which a single 'USE' action would successfully collect the primitive.\n  target_use_states = set()\n  for pr, pc in primitive_locations: # Iterate through each primitive instance location\n      if is_grabbable:\n          # If the item is grabbable, the agent needs to stand on the same cell (pr, pc).\n          # The agent's direction does not typically matter for picking up grabbable items.\n          if is_valid_walk_pos(pr, pc): # Ensure agent can actually walk onto this cell.\n              # Add all 4 possible agent directions, as any direction works when standing on a grabbable item.\n              for d_id in action_to_direction_map.values():\n                  target_use_states.add(((pr, pc), d_id))\n      else:\n          # If the item is non-grabbable (e.g., stone, workshop), the agent must be\n          # adjacent to it and facing it to 'USE' it.\n          for facing_dir_id, (dr_look, dc_look) in dir_to_look_delta.items():\n              # Calculate the required agent position (ar, ac) such that if the agent\n              # is at (ar, ac) and faces `facing_dir_id`, it will be looking at (pr, pc).\n              # (ar + dr_look, ac + dc_look) = (pr, pc)  => (ar, ac) = (pr - dr_look, pc - dc_look)\n              ar, ac = pr - dr_look, pc - dc_look\n              \n              # Check if this calculated agent position is valid to stand on.\n              if is_valid_walk_pos(ar, ac):\n                  target_use_states.add(((ar, ac), facing_dir_id))\n\n  # If no valid target states can be identified, then the primitive is uncollectable.\n  if not target_use_states:\n      return []\n\n  # Initialize BFS: State is (current_position (r,c), current_direction (int), path_of_actions (list)).\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_pos, start_dir, [])])\n  # Keep track of visited (position, direction) pairs to prevent cycles and find shortest path.\n  visited = {(start_pos, start_dir)}\n\n  while queue:\n    (r, c), current_dir, path = queue.popleft()\n\n    # --- Goal Check ---\n    # If the current agent state (position and direction) is one from which 'USE' would succeed,\n    # we have found the shortest path to collect the primitive.\n    if ((r, c), current_dir) in target_use_states:\n        return path + [USE] # Append the final USE action and return the complete path.\n\n    # --- Explore Neighbors (Movement Actions) ---\n    # For each possible movement action (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT).\n    for action, (dr, dc) in move_deltas.items():\n      next_r, next_c = r + dr, c + dc\n      next_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n      \n      # When the agent moves, its facing direction updates to the direction of movement.\n      next_dir = action_to_direction_map[action] \n\n      # Only explore this new state if the next position is walkable and this\n      # (position, direction) state has not been visited before.\n      if is_valid_walk_pos(next_r, next_c) and (next_pos, next_dir) not in visited:\n        visited.add((next_pos, next_dir))\n        # Add the new state to the queue, appending the current action to the path.\n        queue.append((next_pos, next_dir, path + [action]))\n\n  # If the BFS queue becomes empty and no path to a collectable primitive was found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable or doesn't exist in a collectable state.\n  return []", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T01:01:15.327480", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions_list = []\n  current_state = env._current_state # Get the current state of the environment\n  initial_grid = current_state.grid # The grid layout at the start of this collection attempt\n  initial_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's starting position (row, column) tuple\n  initial_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's starting direction (0:RIGHT, 1:UP, 2:LEFT, 3:DOWN)\n\n  # Get the integer ID for the target primitive from the cookbook index\n  try:\n      primitive_id = current_state.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n      # If the primitive name is not found, it's uncollectable by this method.\n      return []\n\n  # IMPORTANT IMPROVEMENT FOR V2:\n  # Check if the primitive is actually grabbable. 'collect' implies picking up an item.\n  # If the primitive is a non-grabbable entity (like a workshop, water, or non-collectible stone),\n  # it cannot be 'collected' into inventory.\n  if primitive_id not in current_state.world.grabbable_indices:\n      # For instance, workshops, water, or specific environmental stone types are non-grabbable.\n      # If the goal is a workshop, it's used by standing next to it and 'USE', not 'collected'.\n      # This function's purpose is to *collect* a primitive.\n      return []\n\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = initial_grid.shape # Dimensions of the grid\n\n  # Map human-readable action names to their integer indices\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION = action_map['UP']   # Assuming 'UP' corresponds to moving forward\n  TURN_LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  TURN_RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define changes in (row, column) for each facing direction when moving forward\n  # This is crucial for calculating new positions after a 'MOVE_FORWARD' action.\n  DIR_TO_DRDC = {\n      0: (0, 1),   # Facing RIGHT: +1 to column (move right)\n      1: (-1, 0),  # Facing UP: -1 to row (move up)\n      2: (0, -1),  # Facing LEFT: -1 to column (move left)\n      3: (1, 0)    # Facing DOWN: +1 to row (move down)\n  }\n\n  # Define how agent's direction changes when turning left or right\n  TURN_LEFT_MAP = {0: 1, 1: 2, 2: 3, 3: 0}   # R (0) -> U (1) -> L (2) -> D (3) -> R (0)\n  TURN_RIGHT_MAP = {0: 3, 1: 0, 2: 1, 3: 2} # R (0) -> D (3) -> L (2) -> U (1) -> R (0)\n\n  # Get indices of entities that block agent movement (e.g., boundaries, water, workshops).\n  # These are truly obstacles the agent cannot walk through.\n  non_walkable_kinds_indices = current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # BFS setup:\n  # Queue stores tuples: ((current_position_tuple, current_direction_int), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here)\n  queue = collections.deque([((initial_pos, initial_dir), [])])\n  # Visited set stores (position_tuple, direction_int) to prevent redundant exploration and cycles.\n  visited = {(initial_pos, initial_dir)}\n\n  target_path = None # This will store the action sequence once the target state is found.\n\n  while queue:\n      (current_pos, current_dir), path_actions = queue.popleft()\n      r, c = current_pos # Current row and column of the agent\n\n      # 1. Check if the current state is a goal state:\n      # A goal state for 'collect' means the primitive is directly in front of the agent,\n      # allowing the 'USE' action to pick it up. This assumes 'USE' is directional.\n      \n      # Calculate coordinates of the cell directly in front of the agent\n      front_dr, front_dc = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n      front_r, front_c = r + front_dr, c + front_dc\n      \n      # Check if the cell in front is within grid boundaries\n      if (0 <= front_r < WIDTH and 0 <= front_c < HEIGHT):\n          # Check if the primitive is present in the cell directly in front\n          if initial_grid[front_r, front_c, primitive_id] > 0:\n              target_path = path_actions # Found path to the desired position+direction\n              break # Exit BFS as the shortest path is found\n\n      # 2. Explore possible next actions from the current state: Move Forward, Turn Left, Turn Right\n      \n      # Try Move Forward action:\n      next_r_move, next_c_move = r + front_dr, c + front_dc # Position after moving forward\n      next_pos_move = (next_r_move, next_c_move)\n      next_dir_move = current_dir # Direction remains unchanged after moving forward\n\n      # Check if next position is within grid boundaries and if this (position, direction) state\n      # has not been visited to prevent redundant paths and infinite loops.\n      if (0 <= next_r_move < WIDTH and 0 <= next_c_move < HEIGHT and\n          (next_pos_move, next_dir_move) not in visited):\n          \n          is_walkable = True\n          # A cell is walkable if it's not occupied by any non-walkable entity (boundary, water, workshop etc.).\n          # This check uses `non_grabbable_indices` which typically define obstacles.\n          for kind_idx in non_walkable_kinds_indices:\n              if initial_grid[next_r_move, next_c_move, kind_idx] > 0:\n                  is_walkable = False\n                  break\n          \n          # IMPROVEMENT FOR V2: Unlike V0, do NOT consider cells containing the primitive itself as non-walkable.\n          # If the primitive is grabbable (checked at the start), agents can typically walk *over* it\n          # on the ground and then use the 'USE' action when adjacent/facing.\n\n          if is_walkable:\n              visited.add((next_pos_move, next_dir_move))\n              queue.append(((next_pos_move, next_dir_move), path_actions + [MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION]))\n\n      # Try Turn Left action:\n      next_dir_left = TURN_LEFT_MAP[current_dir] # New direction after turning left\n      # Turning does not change the agent's position.\n      if ((current_pos, next_dir_left) not in visited):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_left))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_left), path_actions + [TURN_LEFT_ACTION]))\n\n      # Try Turn Right action:\n      next_dir_right = TURN_RIGHT_MAP[current_dir] # New direction after turning right\n      # Turning does not change the agent's position.\n      if ((current_pos, next_dir_right) not in visited):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_right))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_right), path_actions + [TURN_RIGHT_ACTION]))\n\n  # If a path to a collectible position (where the primitive is directly in front) was found,\n  # append the 'USE' action to the sequence to actually collect it.\n  if target_path is not None:\n      actions_list.extend(target_path)\n      actions_list.append(USE_ACTION)", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T01:01:16.573043", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions_list = []\n  current_state = env._current_state # Get the current state of the environment\n  initial_grid = current_state.grid # The grid layout at the start of this collection attempt\n  initial_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's starting position (row, column) tuple\n  initial_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's starting direction (0:RIGHT, 1:UP, 2:LEFT, 3:DOWN)\n\n  # Get the integer ID for the target primitive from the cookbook index\n  try:\n      primitive_id = current_state.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n      # If the primitive name is not found, it's uncollectable by this method.\n      return []\n\n  # === Key Improvement for v2: Ensure the primitive is actually grabbable ===\n  # The 'collect' function implies picking up an item into inventory.\n  # If the primitive is not in the `grabbable_indices` set (e.g., WORKSHOP, WATER, BOUNDARY,\n  # or environmental STONE), it cannot be \"collected\" into inventory.\n  # In such cases, there is no valid sequence of actions to collect it.\n  if primitive_id not in current_state.world.grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = initial_grid.shape # Dimensions of the grid\n\n  # Map human-readable action names to their integer indices as understood by the environment\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION = action_map['UP']   # Assuming 'UP' corresponds to moving forward\n  TURN_LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  TURN_RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define changes in (row, column) for each facing direction when moving forward\n  # This mapping is crucial for calculating new positions after a 'MOVE_FORWARD' action.\n  DIR_TO_DRDC = {\n      0: (0, 1),   # Facing RIGHT: +1 to column (move right)\n      1: (-1, 0),  # Facing UP: -1 to row (move up)\n      2: (0, -1),  # Facing LEFT: -1 to column (move left)\n      3: (1, 0)    # Facing DOWN: +1 to row (move down)\n  }\n\n  # Define how agent's direction changes when turning left or right\n  TURN_LEFT_MAP = {0: 1, 1: 2, 2: 3, 3: 0}   # R (0) -> U (1) -> L (2) -> D (3) -> R (0)\n  TURN_RIGHT_MAP = {0: 3, 1: 0, 2: 1, 3: 2} # R (0) -> D (3) -> L (2) -> U (1) -> R (0)\n\n  # Get indices of entities that block agent movement (e.g., boundaries, water, workshops)\n  # These are considered \"non-walkable\" for BFS pathfinding\n  non_walkable_kinds_indices = current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # BFS setup:\n  # Queue stores tuples: ((current_position_tuple, current_direction_int), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here)\n  queue = collections.deque([((initial_pos, initial_dir), [])])\n  # Visited set stores (position_tuple, direction_int) to prevent redundant exploration and cycles.\n  visited = {(initial_pos, initial_dir)}\n\n  target_path = None # This will store the action sequence once the target state is found.\n\n  while queue:\n      (current_pos, current_dir), path_actions = queue.popleft()\n      r, c = current_pos # Current row and column of the agent\n\n      # 1. Check if the current state is a goal state:\n      # A goal state for collection is one where the primitive is directly in front of the agent,\n      # allowing the 'USE' action to succeed.\n      \n      # Calculate coordinates of the cell directly in front of the agent\n      front_dr, front_dc = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n      front_r, front_c = r + front_dr, c + front_dc\n      \n      # Check if the cell in front is within grid boundaries\n      if (0 <= front_r < WIDTH and 0 <= front_c < HEIGHT):\n          # Check if the primitive is present in the cell directly in front\n          if initial_grid[front_r, front_c, primitive_id] > 0:\n              target_path = path_actions # Found path to the desired position+direction\n              break # Exit BFS as the shortest path is found\n\n      # 2. Explore possible next actions from the current state: Move Forward, Turn Left, Turn Right\n      \n      # Try Move Forward action:\n      next_r_move, next_c_move = r + front_dr, c + front_dc # Position after moving forward\n      next_pos_move = (next_r_move, next_c_move)\n      next_dir_move = current_dir # Direction remains unchanged after moving forward\n\n      # Check if next position is within grid boundaries and if this (position, direction) state\n      # has not been visited to avoid redundant paths and infinite loops.\n      if (0 <= next_r_move < WIDTH and 0 <= next_c_move < HEIGHT and\n          (next_pos_move, next_dir_move) not in visited):\n          \n          is_walkable = True\n          # A cell is walkable if it's not occupied by any non-walkable entity (e.g., boundary, water, workshops).\n          for kind_idx in non_walkable_kinds_indices:\n              if initial_grid[next_r_move, next_c_move, kind_idx] > 0:\n                  is_walkable = False\n                  break\n          # Crucially, the agent typically cannot walk *onto* the primitive itself if it's the target;\n          # it needs to be adjacent to use it.\n          if initial_grid[next_r_move, next_c_move, primitive_id] > 0:\n              is_walkable = False\n\n          if is_walkable:\n              visited.add((next_pos_move, next_dir_move))\n              queue.append(((next_pos_move, next_dir_move), path_actions + [MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION]))\n\n      # Try Turn Left action:\n      next_dir_left = TURN_LEFT_MAP[current_dir] # New direction after turning left\n      # Turning does not change the agent's position.\n      if ((current_pos, next_dir_left) not in visited):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_left))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_left), path_actions + [TURN_LEFT_ACTION]))\n\n      # Try Turn Right action:\n      next_dir_right = TURN_RIGHT_MAP[current_dir] # New direction after turning right\n      # Turning does not change the agent's position.\n      if ((current_pos, next_dir_right) not in visited):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_right))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_right), path_actions + [TURN_RIGHT_ACTION]))\n\n  # If a path to a collectible position (where the primitive is directly in front) was found,\n  # append the 'USE' action to the sequence to actually collect it.\n  if target_path is not None:\n      actions_list.extend(target_path)\n      actions_list.append(USE_ACTION)\n\n  return actions_list", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T01:01:54.792449", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions = []\n  \n  # Retrieve the current state from the environment\n  current_state = env._current_state \n  grid = current_state.grid\n  current_pos = current_state.pos\n  \n  # Get the integer ID of the primitive from the environment's cookbook index.\n  # Using .index.index(name) ensures it handles new names by assigning them an ID if needed,\n  # but for existing names, it simply retrieves the ID.\n  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment's action specifications.\n  # This makes the code more robust to changes in action integer values.\n  ACTION_MAP = env.action_specs()\n  DOWN = ACTION_MAP['DOWN']\n  UP = ACTION_MAP['UP']\n  LEFT = ACTION_MAP['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = ACTION_MAP['RIGHT']\n  USE = ACTION_MAP['USE']\n\n  # Define movement deltas (row_change, col_change) corresponding to actions.\n  # Note: In numpy arrays for grid, row increases downwards, col increases rightwards.\n  DELTAS = {\n      UP: (-1, 0),   # Move up decreases the row index\n      DOWN: (1, 0),  # Move down increases the row index\n      LEFT: (0, -1), # Move left decreases the column index\n      RIGHT: (0, 1)  # Move right increases the column index\n  }\n\n  # First, check if the specified primitive is actually a \"collectible\" item.\n  # Collectible primitives are those that can be picked up, as opposed to\n  # environmental features like water, boundaries, or workshops.\n  if primitive_id not in env.world.cookbook.primitives:\n      # If it's not a primitive that can be collected, return an empty list of actions.\n      return []\n\n  # Get grid dimensions for boundary checks.\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Check if the agent is already adjacent to or on the same cell as the primitive.\n  # CraftState.next_to checks the 3x3 neighborhood around the agent's position.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_id):\n      # If so, a single 'USE' action is sufficient to collect it.\n      actions.append(USE)\n      return actions\n\n  # Find all grid locations where the target primitive is present.\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for r in range(WIDTH):\n      for c in range(HEIGHT):\n          # The grid stores items using one-hot encoding at the depth dimension.\n          # If grid[r, c, primitive_id] is 1, the primitive is at (r,c).\n          if grid[r, c, primitive_id] == 1:\n              primitive_locations.append((r, c))\n\n  # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the grid, there's nothing to collect.\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      return []\n\n  # Use Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path from the agent's\n  # current position to any cell that is *adjacent* to a primitive location.\n  # The queue stores tuples: ((current_row, current_col), [list_of_actions_to_reach_this_pos]).\n  q = collections.deque([(current_pos, [])]) \n  visited = {current_pos} # Keep track of visited positions to prevent infinite loops and redundant exploration.\n\n  target_adjacent_path = None # Stores the path to the closest cell adjacent to a primitive.\n\n  while q:\n      (r, c), path = q.popleft()\n\n      # Check if the current cell (r, c) is adjacent (Manhattan distance 1)\n      # to any of the located primitive items.\n      is_adjacent_to_primitive = False\n      for pr, pc in primitive_locations:\n          if abs(r - pr) + abs(c - pc) == 1: \n              target_adjacent_path = path # This path leads to a cell from which we can 'USE' the primitive.\n              is_adjacent_to_primitive = True\n              break # Found the shortest path to an adjacent cell, so we can stop BFS.\n      \n      if is_adjacent_to_primitive:\n          break # Exit the BFS loop, as the optimal path has been found.\n\n      # Explore valid neighboring cells.\n      for action_dir, (dr, dc) in DELTAS.items():\n          nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc # Calculate the new potential position.\n\n          # Boundary check: Ensure the new position is within the grid limits.\n          if not (0 <= nr < WIDTH and 0 <= nc < HEIGHT):\n              continue\n          \n          # Traversability check: Ensure the new position is not an obstacle.\n          # Obstacles are defined as non-grabbable items (e.g., boundaries, water, workshops).\n          is_traversable = True\n          for i_kind in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n              # If the new cell contains any non-grabbable item, it's an obstacle.\n              if grid[nr, nc, i_kind] == 1: \n                  is_traversable = False\n                  break \n          \n          if not is_traversable:\n              continue # Skip this neighbor if it's an obstacle.\n          \n          # If the neighbor position has not been visited, add it to the queue\n          # with the updated path.\n          if (nr, nc) not in visited:\n              visited.add((nr, nc))\n              new_path = path + [action_dir]\n              q.append(((nr, nc), new_path))\n    \n  # If a path to an adjacent cell was found, append the necessary actions.\n  if target_adjacent_path is not None:\n      actions.extend(target_adjacent_path) # Add movement actions.\n      actions.append(USE) # Add the 'USE' action to collect the primitive.\n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T01:01:55.972765", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions = []\n  \n  current_state = env._current_state \n  grid = current_state.grid\n  current_pos = current_state.pos\n  \n  # Get action mappings from the environment's action_specs\n  ACTION_MAP = env.action_specs()\n  UP = ACTION_MAP['UP']\n  DOWN = ACTION_MAP['DOWN']\n  LEFT = ACTION_MAP['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = ACTION_MAP['RIGHT']\n  USE = ACTION_MAP['USE']\n\n  # Get the integer ID of the primitive from the cookbook index\n  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Validate that the requested 'primitive' is indeed a collectible primitive item.\n  # If it's an environment entity (like a boundary or workshop), it cannot be 'collected'.\n  if primitive_id not in env.world.cookbook.primitives:\n      return []\n\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Define movement deltas corresponding to actions\n  DELTAS = {\n      UP: (-1, 0),  # (dr, dc) for moving UP (decreases row index)\n      DOWN: (1, 0), # (dr, dc) for moving DOWN (increases row index)\n      LEFT: (0, -1), # (dr, dc) for moving LEFT (decreases col index)\n      RIGHT: (0, 1) # (dr, dc) for moving RIGHT (increases col index)\n  }\n\n  # 1. Immediate check: If the agent is already next to the primitive, just 'USE' it.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_id):\n      actions.append(USE)\n      return actions\n\n  # 2. Find all grid locations where the target primitive exists.\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for r in range(WIDTH):\n      for c in range(HEIGHT):\n          # Check if the primitive_id layer at (r, c) has a value of 1 (present)\n          if grid[r, c, primitive_id] == 1:\n              primitive_locations.append((r, c))\n\n  # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the grid, it's unreachable.\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      return []\n\n  # 3. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path\n  #    to a cell that is adjacent to any of the primitive locations.\n  # Queue stores tuples: ((current_row, current_col), [list_of_actions_to_reach_here])\n  q = collections.deque([(current_pos, [])]) \n  visited = {current_pos} # Keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles and redundant paths\n\n  target_adjacent_path = None # Will store the action sequence to reach an adjacent cell\n\n  while q:\n      (r, c), path_so_far = q.popleft()\n\n      # Check if the current cell (r, c) is adjacent to any of the primitive's locations.\n      # Adjacency is defined by Manhattan distance of 1 (up, down, left, or right).\n      for pr, pc in primitive_locations:\n          if abs(r - pr) + abs(c - pc) == 1:\n              target_adjacent_path = path_so_far # This path gets us adjacent to the primitive\n              break # Found the shortest path to an adjacent cell, can stop BFS\n      \n      if target_adjacent_path is not None:\n          break # Exit BFS loop as the goal is met\n\n      # Explore valid neighboring cells\n      for action_dir, (dr, dc) in DELTAS.items():\n          nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc # Calculate new potential position\n\n          # Boundary check: Ensure the new position is within grid limits\n          if not (0 <= nr < WIDTH and 0 <= nc < HEIGHT):\n              continue\n          \n          # Traversability check: Ensure the new position is not occupied by a non-grabbable item.\n          # Non-grabbable items include walls, water, and workshops, which block movement.\n          is_traversable = True\n          for kind_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n              if grid[nr, nc, kind_idx] == 1: # If this cell contains a non-grabbable item\n                  is_traversable = False\n                  break # This neighbor is an obstacle, cannot move here\n          \n          if not is_traversable:\n              continue # Skip this neighbor if it's an obstacle\n          \n          # If the neighbor has not been visited, add it to the queue for exploration\n          if (nr, nc) not in visited:\n              visited.add((nr, nc))\n              new_path = path_so_far + [action_dir]\n              q.append(((nr, nc), new_path))\n    \n  # 4. Construct the final action sequence\n  if target_adjacent_path is not None:\n      actions.extend(target_adjacent_path)\n      actions.append(USE) # Once adjacent, use the item to collect it\n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T01:02:57.359020", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  current_pos = current_state.pos\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # 1. Map the primitive string name to its integer index using the cookbook.\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  try:\n    primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    # If the primitive name is not recognized in the cookbook, it's an invalid target.\n    return []\n\n  # 2. Categorize the primitive type based on CraftWorld and Cookbook definitions.\n  #    This determines how the agent interacts with it (e.g., picks up, uses tool, or just reaches).\n  is_grabbable_item = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop_location = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n  # A \"defined primitive resource\" is an item listed in the cookbook's `primitives` set,\n  # implying it's a basic resource, whether grabbable or requiring a 'USE' action (like mining).\n  is_defined_primitive_resource = primitive_idx in cookbook.primitives\n\n  # 3. Early exit for environmental features that are not intended to be \"collected\"\n  #    by this DSL command (e.g., BOUNDARY walls, or WATER if it's not a resource).\n  #    If it's non-grabbable, and not a workshop, and not a defined primitive resource,\n  #    it's likely an impassable, uncollectible environmental obstacle.\n  if (primitive_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices and not is_workshop_location) and not is_defined_primitive_resource:\n      return []\n\n  # 4. Helper function to determine if a specific grid cell (r, c) is traversable by the agent.\n  def is_traversable(r: int, c: int) -> bool:\n      # Check if coordinates are within the grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= r < grid_width and 0 <= c < grid_height):\n          return False\n      \n      # Water is generally considered an impassable obstacle.\n      if grid[r, c, env.world.water_index] == 1:\n          return False\n\n      # Check for other non-grabbable entities that block movement.\n      # Workshops are special: they are non-grabbable but are traversable for the agent.\n      # Other non-grabbable entities (like BOUNDARY, or STONE if it acts as a block) are obstacles.\n      # We check all kinds present at the cell.\n      kinds_at_cell = np.where(grid[r, c] == 1)[0]\n      for kind_at_cell_idx in kinds_at_cell:\n          if kind_at_cell_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices and \\\n             kind_at_cell_idx not in env.world.workshop_indices:\n              return False # This cell contains an unpassable obstacle.\n      return True\n\n  # 5. Locate all instances of the target primitive on the current grid.\n  primitive_grid_locations = []\n  for r in range(grid_width):\n    for c in range(grid_height):\n      if grid[r, c, primitive_idx] == 1:\n        primitive_grid_locations.append((r, c))\n\n  if not primitive_grid_locations:\n    # The primitive does not exist anywhere on the current map.\n    return []\n\n  # 6. Determine \"collectible spots\": these are traversable grid cells where the agent\n  #    can stand to be able to collect/interact with the primitive.\n  #    For most items, this means being in the 3x3 neighborhood.\n  collectible_spots = set()\n  # Offsets for a 3x3 neighborhood (including the center cell (0,0)).\n  NEIGHBORHOOD_OFFSETS = [\n      (dr, dc) for dr in [-1, 0, 1] for dc in [-1, 0, 1]\n  ]\n\n  for pr, pc in primitive_grid_locations:\n    for dr, dc in NEIGHBORHOOD_OFFSETS:\n      nr, nc = pr + dr, pc + dc\n      # A potential collectible spot must be traversable by the agent.\n      if is_traversable(nr, nc):\n        collectible_spots.add((nr, nc))\n  \n  if not collectible_spots:\n    # No reachable (traversable) spots identified where the agent can stand to collect the primitive.\n    return []\n\n  # 7. Define mappings for cardinal directions to action constants for pathfinding.\n  ACTION_UP, ACTION_DOWN, ACTION_LEFT, ACTION_RIGHT, ACTION_USE = (\n      craft.UP, craft.DOWN, craft.LEFT, craft.RIGHT, craft.USE\n  )\n  ACTION_MAP = {\n      (-1, 0): ACTION_UP,   # North (row -1, col 0)\n      (1, 0): ACTION_DOWN,  # South (row +1, col 0)\n      (0, -1): ACTION_LEFT, # West (row 0, col -1)\n      (0, 1): ACTION_RIGHT  # East (row 0, col +1)\n  }\n  CARDINAL_DIRECTIONS = [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]\n\n  # 8. Immediate collection check: If the agent is already in a position to collect the primitive.\n  #    'next_to' means within the 3x3 neighborhood of the agent's current position.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n    # If it's a grabbable item or a primitive resource that requires a 'USE' action (like mining stone),\n    # just perform 'USE' and return.\n    if is_grabbable_item or (is_defined_primitive_resource and not is_workshop_location): \n      return [ACTION_USE]\n    # If it's a workshop, being 'next_to' (which includes standing on it if traversable) is sufficient.\n    # No further 'USE' action is needed to \"collect\" (i.e., be present at) a workshop.\n    elif is_workshop_location:\n        return []\n\n  # 9. Perform a Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path from the agent's\n  #    current position to any of the identified collectible spots.\n  q = collections.deque([(current_pos, [])]) # Queue stores (current_position, path_taken_actions)\n  visited = {current_pos} # Set to keep track of visited grid cells to prevent cycles and redundant exploration.\n  path_found = None # Will store the shortest sequence of actions found.\n\n  while q:\n    (r, c), current_path = q.popleft()\n\n    # If the current position is one of our target collectible spots, we have found the shortest path.\n    if (r, c) in collectible_spots:\n      path_found = current_path\n      break\n\n    # Explore all four cardinal neighbors (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT).\n    for dr, dc in CARDINAL_DIRECTIONS:\n      next_r, next_c = r + dr, c + dc\n      \n      if (next_r, next_c) not in visited: # Only explore if this cell hasn't been visited yet.\n        if is_traversable(next_r, next_c): # Only explore if the cell is traversable.\n          visited.add((next_r, next_c))\n          q.append(((next_r, next_c), current_path + [ACTION_MAP[(dr, dc)]]))\n\n  # 10. Construct the final sequence of actions if a path was found.\n  final_actions = []\n  if path_found:\n    final_actions.extend(path_found)\n    # After moving to the collectible spot, append the 'USE' action if necessary.\n    # 'USE' is needed for grabbable items and defined primitive resources (like mining stone/wood),\n    # but not for workshops (where simply reaching the location is the 'collection').\n    if is_grabbable_item or (is_defined_primitive_resource and not is_workshop_location):\n      final_actions.append(ACTION_USE) \n  \n  return final_actions", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T01:02:58.604146", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions = []\n\n  # Get current state and grid dimensions\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  agent_pos = current_state.pos\n  grid_height, grid_width, _ = grid.shape # grid.shape is (height, width, n_kinds)\n\n  # 1. Get Primitive Index from the cookbook.\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  try:\n    primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    # Primitive name not found in the cookbook index.\n    return []\n\n  # 2. Categorize the primitive's properties based on the world configuration.\n  is_grabbable_item = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop_location = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n  # A \"defined primitive resource\" means it's a resource (like wood, stone) that might\n  # need to be \"used\" (e.g., mined, chopped), even if not directly \"grabbable\".\n  is_defined_primitive_resource = primitive_idx in cookbook.primitives\n\n  # Early exit for truly uncollectible/uninteractable environmental features.\n  # This includes things like 'BOUNDARY'. If a non-grabbable item is not a workshop\n  # and not a defined primitive resource (which implies interaction), it's considered uncollectible.\n  if (primitive_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices and not is_workshop_location) and not is_defined_primitive_resource:\n      return []\n\n  # 3. Helper function: Determine if a grid cell (r, c) is traversable by the agent.\n  def is_traversable(r, c):\n      # Check if coordinates are within grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= r < grid_height and 0 <= c < grid_width):\n          return False\n\n      # Check for water, which is generally non-passable.\n      if grid[r, c, env.world.water_index] == 1:\n          return False\n\n      # Check for other blocking obstacles. A cell is blocked if it contains any\n      # non-grabbable entity that is *not* a workshop. Workshops are traversable.\n      cell_contents_indices = np.where(grid[r, c] == 1)[0]\n      for kind_idx_in_cell in cell_contents_indices:\n          if kind_idx_in_cell in env.world.non_grabbable_indices and \\\n             kind_idx_in_cell not in env.world.workshop_indices:\n              return False # This cell contains an unpassable obstacle.\n      return True\n\n  # 4. Find all locations on the grid where the target primitive exists.\n  # Using numpy.where is efficient.\n  primitive_rows, primitive_cols = np.where(grid[:, :, primitive_idx] == 1)\n  primitive_grid_locations = list(zip(primitive_rows, primitive_cols))\n\n  if not primitive_grid_locations:\n    # The primitive does not exist anywhere on the current map.\n    return []\n\n  # 5. Identify all \"collectible spots\": these are traversable cells where the agent\n  # can stand to be 'next to' or 'on' one of the target primitive instances.\n  # The `CraftState.next_to` method checks the 3x3 neighborhood (including the agent's current cell).\n  collectible_spots = set()\n  \n  # Offsets for a 3x3 neighborhood including the center (0,0)\n  NEIGHBORHOOD_OFFSETS = [\n      (dr, dc) for dr in [-1, 0, 1] for dc in [-1, 0, 1]\n  ]\n\n  for pr, pc in primitive_grid_locations:\n    for dr, dc in NEIGHBORHOOD_OFFSETS:\n      nr, nc = pr + dr, pc + dc\n      \n      # If this potential standing spot is traversable, it's a valid \"collectible spot\".\n      if is_traversable(nr, nc):\n        collectible_spots.add((nr, nc))\n\n  if not collectible_spots:\n    # No reachable (traversable) spots identified where the agent can effectively\n    # interact with the primitive.\n    return []\n\n  # 6. Define mappings for cardinal directions to action constants for pathfinding.\n  ACTION_MAP = {\n      (-1, 0): craft.UP,\n      (1, 0): craft.DOWN,\n      (0, -1): craft.LEFT,\n      (0, 1): craft.RIGHT\n  }\n  CARDINAL_DIRECTIONS = [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]\n  \n  # 7. Immediate Collection Check: If the agent is already in a position to interact\n  # with the primitive (i.e., next to it or on a workshop spot), perform immediate action if needed.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n    # If it's a grabbable item or a defined resource that requires 'USE' (e.g., mining stone),\n    # and it's not a workshop, then apply USE.\n    if is_grabbable_item or (is_defined_primitive_resource and not is_workshop_location):\n      actions.append(craft.USE)\n      return actions\n    # If it's a workshop, being 'next_to' (or on) is sufficient, no 'USE' action is needed.\n    # The 'collect' action for a workshop effectively means reaching it.\n    elif is_workshop_location:\n      return [] # Already \"collected\" by being present.\n\n  # 8. Perform a Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path from the agent's\n  # current position to any of the identified collectible spots.\n  q = collections.deque([(agent_pos, [])]) # Queue stores (current_position, path_taken_actions)\n  visited = {agent_pos} # Set to keep track of visited grid cells to prevent cycles.\n  path_to_collect_spot = None # Will store the shortest sequence of actions found.\n\n  while q:\n    (r, c), current_path = q.popleft()\n\n    # If the current position is one of our target collectible spots, we found the shortest path.\n    if (r, c) in collectible_spots:\n      path_to_collect_spot = current_path\n      break\n\n    # Explore cardinal neighbors (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT).\n    for dr, dc in CARDINAL_DIRECTIONS:\n      next_r, next_c = r + dr, c + dc\n      \n      if (next_r, next_c) not in visited:\n        if is_traversable(next_r, next_c):\n          visited.add((next_r, next_c))\n          q.append(((next_r, next_c), current_path + [ACTION_MAP[(dr, dc)]]))\n\n  # 9. Construct the final sequence of actions if a path was found.\n  if path_to_collect_spot:\n    actions.extend(path_to_collect_spot)\n    # After moving to the collectible spot, perform the 'USE' action if required.\n    # 'USE' is needed for grabbable items or other defined primitive resources that are not workshops.\n    if is_grabbable_item or (is_defined_primitive_resource and not is_workshop_location):\n      actions.append(craft.USE)\n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T01:04:18.819607", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  DOWN_ACTION = action_map[\"DOWN\"]\n  UP_ACTION = action_map[\"UP\"]\n  LEFT_ACTION = action_map[\"LEFT\"]\n  RIGHT_ACTION = action_map[\"RIGHT\"]\n  USE_ACTION = action_map[\"USE\"]\n\n  # Get the integer ID for the target primitive from the cookbook index.\n  # This ID is used to identify the primitive within the grid and inventory.\n  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Get current state details from the environment.\n  # This includes the agent's current position and the layout of the grid.\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Determine if the target primitive is a grabbable item (e.g., WOOD, IRON).\n  # Grabbable items can be picked up and added to the inventory using USE_ACTION.\n  # Non-grabbable items (e.g., WATER, WORKSHOP) are typically environmental features\n  # that are \"collected\" by simply reaching their location.\n  grabbable_ids_set = set(env.world.grabbable_indices)\n  is_grabbable_primitive = (primitive_id in grabbable_ids_set)\n\n  # Identify obstacle kinds. These are non-grabbable entities that the agent\n  # cannot typically pass through, unless the obstacle itself is the target\n  # primitive (e.g., moving onto a 'WATER' tile if 'WATER' is the target).\n  obstacle_kinds_ids = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # Define possible movement actions and their corresponding (dx, dy) changes.\n  move_actions = {\n      UP_ACTION: (0, -1),\n      DOWN_ACTION: (0, 1),\n      LEFT_ACTION: (-1, 0),\n      RIGHT_ACTION: (1, 0),\n  }\n\n  # Initialize Breadth-First Search (BFS) for pathfinding.\n  # The queue stores tuples of (current_position, path_taken_so_far_as_action_list).\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])])\n  # The 'visited' set keeps track of explored positions to prevent cycles\n  # and redundant exploration, ensuring the shortest path is found.\n  visited = {start_pos}\n\n  # BFS loop to find the shortest path to the primitive.\n  while queue:\n    current_pos, path_so_far = queue.popleft()\n    cx, cy = current_pos\n\n    # Check if the target primitive is located at the current position.\n    if grid[cx, cy, primitive_id] > 0:\n      # If the primitive is grabbable, append a USE_ACTION to pick it up.\n      # The agent is now on the tile with the primitive. The assumption is that\n      # USE_ACTION picks up items from the current tile.\n      if is_grabbable_primitive:\n        return path_so_far + [USE_ACTION]\n      else:\n        # If it's a non-grabbable environmental feature, \"collecting\" it\n        # simply means reaching its location. No USE_ACTION is needed.\n        return path_so_far\n\n    # Explore neighboring cells (possible next moves).\n    for action, (dx, dy) in move_actions.items():\n      nx, ny = cx + dx, cy + dy\n      next_pos = (nx, ny)\n\n      # 1. Boundary check: Ensure the next position is within the grid limits.\n      if not (0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height):\n        continue\n\n      # 2. Visited check: Avoid revisiting already explored positions.\n      if next_pos in visited:\n        continue\n\n      # 3. Obstacle check: Determine if the next position contains an obstacle.\n      # A cell is considered an obstacle if it contains any non-grabbable item\n      # that is *not* the primitive we are currently trying to collect.\n      # This allows the agent to move onto the target primitive's tile even if\n      # it's generally considered non-grabbable (e.g., a workshop).\n      is_obstacle_cell = False\n      for kind_id in obstacle_kinds_ids:\n        if kind_id != primitive_id and grid[nx, ny, kind_id] > 0:\n          is_obstacle_cell = True\n          break\n      \n      if is_obstacle_cell:\n        continue # Skip this move if it leads to an impassable obstacle.\n\n      # If the move is valid (within bounds, not visited, not an obstacle),\n      # add the next position to the visited set and enqueue it with the\n      # updated path.\n      visited.add(next_pos)\n      queue.append((next_pos, path_so_far + [action]))\n\n  # If the BFS queue becomes empty and no path to the primitive was found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable from the current position.\n  return []", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T01:04:20.204902", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  DOWN_ACTION = action_map[\"DOWN\"]\n  UP_ACTION = action_map[\"UP\"]\n  LEFT_ACTION = action_map[\"LEFT\"]\n  RIGHT_ACTION = action_map[\"RIGHT\"]\n  USE_ACTION = action_map[\"USE\"]\n\n  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  start_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's starting direction (0=N, 1=E, 2=S, 3=W)\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  grabbable_ids_set = set(env.world.grabbable_indices)\n  is_grabbable_primitive = (primitive_id in grabbable_ids_set)\n\n  # Non-grabbable indices typically represent impassable terrain or fixed environmental features.\n  obstacle_kinds_ids = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # Define possible moves and their corresponding (dx, dy) and resulting agent direction.\n  # CraftState.dir: 0=N (Up), 1=E (Right), 2=S (Down), 3=W (Left)\n  move_actions_info = {\n      UP_ACTION: (0, -1, 0),    # (dx, dy, new_dir)\n      DOWN_ACTION: (0, 1, 2),\n      LEFT_ACTION: (-1, 0, 3),\n      RIGHT_ACTION: (1, 0, 1),\n  }\n\n  # Map directions (0-3) to their corresponding (dx, dy) offsets for checking the cell in front.\n  direction_to_offset = {\n      0: (0, -1),  # North (Up)\n      1: (1, 0),   # East (Right)\n      2: (0, 1),   # South (Down)\n      3: (-1, 0),  # West (Left)\n  }\n\n  # BFS state: (current_position, current_direction, path_taken_so_far_as_action_list)\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_pos, start_dir, [])])\n  # Visited set: (position, direction) to avoid cycles and redundant exploration.\n  visited = {(start_pos, start_dir)}\n\n  while queue:\n    (cx, cy), current_dir, path_so_far = queue.popleft()\n\n    # --- Goal Check ---\n    if is_grabbable_primitive:\n      # For grabbable items (e.g., WOOD, IRON), we assume USE_ACTION acts on the cell *in front* of the agent.\n      # So, the goal is to reach a position where the primitive is in the agent's current facing direction.\n      dir_dx, dir_dy = direction_to_offset[current_dir]\n      target_px, target_py = cx + dir_dx, cy + dir_dy\n\n      # Check if the cell in front is within bounds and contains the target primitive\n      if (0 <= target_px < grid_width and 0 <= target_py < grid_height and\n          grid[target_px, target_py, primitive_id] > 0):\n        return path_so_far + [USE_ACTION]\n    else:\n      # For non-grabbable items (e.g., WORKSHOP, WATER), \"collecting\" means simply reaching their cell.\n      if grid[cx, cy, primitive_id] > 0:\n        return path_so_far\n\n    # --- Explore Neighbors ---\n    for action, (dx, dy, next_dir) in move_actions_info.items():\n      nx, ny = cx + dx, cy + dy\n      next_pos = (nx, ny)\n      \n      # Check if the next position is within grid boundaries\n      if not (0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height):\n        continue\n\n      # Check if this (position, direction) state has already been visited\n      if (next_pos, next_dir) in visited:\n        continue\n\n      # Determine if the next position is an obstacle based on the primitive type.\n      is_obstacle_cell = False\n      if is_grabbable_primitive:\n        # If we are looking for a grabbable item (e.g., WOOD) and USE_ACTION is directional,\n        # we generally don't want to path *onto* the item itself, but rather to a cell adjacent to it.\n        # Thus, the grabbable primitive's cell itself is treated as an obstacle for movement.\n        if grid[nx, ny, primitive_id] > 0:\n          is_obstacle_cell = True\n        else:\n          # Also check for any other general non-grabbable obstacles (e.g., WATER, STONE)\n          # that are not the primitive we are trying to collect.\n          for kind_id in obstacle_kinds_ids:\n            if grid[nx, ny, kind_id] > 0: # Is there any non-grabbable thing here?\n              is_obstacle_cell = True\n              break\n      else:\n        # If we are looking for a non-grabbable item (e.g., WORKSHOP, WATER),\n        # we *can* move onto its tile to \"collect\" it.\n        # Obstacles are other non-grabbable entities that are NOT the target primitive.\n        for kind_id in obstacle_kinds_ids:\n          if kind_id != primitive_id and grid[nx, ny, kind_id] > 0:\n            is_obstacle_cell = True\n            break\n      \n      if is_obstacle_cell:\n        continue # Skip this move if it leads to an obstacle\n\n      # If the move is valid (within bounds, not visited, not an obstacle), add the new state to the queue\n      visited.add((next_pos, next_dir))\n      queue.append((next_pos, next_dir, path_so_far + [action]))\n\n  # If the queue becomes empty and no path to the primitive was found, return an empty list\n  return []", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T01:05:18.963029", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  initial_pos_c, initial_pos_r = current_state.pos # Agent's initial position (col, row)\n  initial_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's initial direction (0:N, 1:E, 2:S, 3:W)\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape # Grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n\n  # Get the integer index for the primitive.\n  # Convert to lowercase as names are often stored this way in the index.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive.lower())\n\n  # Handle special case: 'boundary' is not collectable.\n  if primitive_idx == env.world.cookbook.index.index(\"boundary\"):\n      return []\n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment's action specifications.\n  ACTION_MAP = env.action_specs()\n  ACTIONS = {\n      \"DOWN\": ACTION_MAP[\"DOWN\"],\n      \"UP\": ACTION_MAP[\"UP\"],\n      \"LEFT\": ACTION_MAP[\"LEFT\"],\n      \"RIGHT\": ACTION_MAP[\"RIGHT\"],\n      \"USE\": ACTION_MAP[\"USE\"]\n  }\n\n  # Define movement data: (action_index: (delta_col, delta_row, new_direction_after_move))\n  # This mapping helps in updating the agent's state correctly after a move action.\n  MOVE_ACTION_DATA = {\n      ACTIONS[\"UP\"]: (0, -1, 0),    # Move North (Up), face North (dir 0)\n      ACTIONS[\"DOWN\"]: (0, 1, 2),   # Move South (Down), face South (dir 2)\n      ACTIONS[\"LEFT\"]: (-1, 0, 3),  # Move West (Left), face West (dir 3)\n      ACTIONS[\"RIGHT\"]: (1, 0, 1)   # Move East (Right), face East (dir 1)\n  }\n\n  # Define direction-to-delta mapping for determining the cell directly in front of the agent.\n  # dir: 0=N, 1=E, 2=S, 3=W corresponds to (col_delta, row_delta)\n  DIR_TO_DELTA = {\n      0: (0, -1),  # North (Up): no change in col, row decreases\n      1: (1, 0),   # East (Right): col increases, no change in row\n      2: (0, 1),   # South (Down): no change in col, row increases\n      3: (-1, 0)   # West (Left): col decreases, no change in row\n  }\n\n  # Categorize the primitive based on its collection mechanism.\n  # 1. Workshops: require adjacency, no 'USE' action.\n  is_primitive_workshop = (primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices)\n  # 2. Grabbables (e.g., WOOD) or special non-grabbables (WATER, STONE):\n  #    Require being in front of and using 'USE' action.\n  is_primitive_grabbable_or_water_stone = (\n      primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices or\n      primitive_idx == env.world.water_index or\n      primitive_idx == env.world.stone_index\n  )\n\n  # Define a set of entity kinds that generally block agent movement.\n  # This includes boundaries, workshops, and water/stone (unless they are the target itself).\n  blocking_kinds = set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices)\n\n  def is_traversable(check_c, check_r, target_prim_idx):\n      \"\"\"\n      Helper function to determine if a cell at (check_c, check_r) is traversable.\n      A cell is traversable if it's within grid bounds and does not contain blocking entities.\n      Special handling for water/stone: if they are the target, the agent *can* move onto them.\n      \"\"\"\n      # Check grid boundaries\n      if not (0 <= check_c < grid_width and 0 <= check_r < grid_height):\n          return False\n\n      # Check for blocking entities in the cell.\n      for k_idx in blocking_kinds:\n          if grid[check_c, check_r, k_idx] > 0: # If this cell contains a potentially blocking item\n              # Special case: If the blocking item is water or stone AND it is the primitive\n              # we are currently trying to collect, then we *can* move onto it.\n              if k_idx == target_prim_idx and (k_idx == env.world.water_index or k_idx == env.world.stone_index):\n                  continue # It's okay to move onto this specific blocking item.\n              else:\n                  # Otherwise, it's a true blocking item (e.g., boundary, workshop, or\n                  # water/stone that is not the target), so the cell is not traversable.\n                  return False\n      return True # No blocking entities found, or special case handled.\n\n  # Breadth-First Search (BFS) setup\n  # Queue stores tuples: (((current_col, current_row), current_direction), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_this_state)\n  queue = collections.deque([(((initial_pos_c, initial_pos_r), initial_dir), [])])\n  # Visited set stores ((col, row), direction) tuples to avoid cycles and redundant computations.\n  visited = set([((initial_pos_c, initial_pos_r), initial_dir)])\n\n  while queue:\n      # Dequeue the current state and the path to reach it.\n      ((current_c, current_r), current_dir), path_actions = queue.popleft()\n\n      # --- Check if the current state satisfies the collection condition for the primitive ---\n      if is_primitive_workshop:\n          # For workshops, the agent needs to be at a traversable position adjacent to a workshop.\n          # The agent doesn't \"use\" a workshop to collect it in this context; just reaching it suffices.\n          if is_traversable(current_c, current_r, primitive_idx): # Agent is at a valid, traversable spot\n              # Check the 3x3 neighborhood (including current cell) for the workshop.\n              for dc_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n                  for dr_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n                      # Calculate potential workshop location\n                      px, py = current_c + dc_adj, current_r + dr_adj\n                      \n                      # Ensure location is within bounds and contains the primitive (workshop)\n                      if (0 <= px < grid_width and 0 <= py < grid_height) and grid[px, py, primitive_idx] > 0:\n                          # Agent is at (current_c, current_r) which is adjacent to (px, py) containing the workshop.\n                          # This means the workshop is 'collected' by reaching an adjacent spot.\n                          return path_actions\n      elif is_primitive_grabbable_or_water_stone:\n          # For grabbable items or special non-grabbables like water/stone,\n          # the agent needs to be positioned and oriented such that a 'USE' action will collect the item.\n          # This means the item must be in the cell directly in front of the agent.\n          front_dc, front_dr = DIR_TO_DELTA[current_dir]\n          front_c, front_r = current_c + front_dc, current_r + front_dr\n\n          # Check if the cell directly in front is within grid boundaries and contains the primitive.\n          if (0 <= front_c < grid_width and 0 <= front_r < grid_height) and grid[front_c, front_r, primitive_idx] > 0:\n              # Goal reached: the primitive is directly in front, so a 'USE' action will collect it.\n              return path_actions + [ACTIONS[\"USE\"]]\n\n      # --- Explore neighboring states by trying all possible movement actions ---\n      for action, (dc_move, dr_move, new_dir) in MOVE_ACTION_DATA.items():\n          next_c, next_r = current_c + dc_move, current_r + dr_move\n          next_state_tuple = ((next_c, next_r), new_dir) # The new state includes updated position AND direction\n\n          # If the next state (position and direction) has not been visited,\n          # AND the next cell is traversable (considering the target primitive's rules):\n          if next_state_tuple not in visited and is_traversable(next_c, next_r, primitive_idx):\n              visited.add(next_state_tuple)\n              queue.append((next_state_tuple, path_actions + [action]))\n\n  # If the queue is exhausted and no path to collect the primitive was found, return an empty list.\n  return []", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T01:05:20.123953", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  initial_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's initial position (col, row)\n  initial_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's initial direction (0:N, 1:E, 2:S, 3:W)\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape # Grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n\n  # Get the integer index for the primitive (lowercase for consistency)\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive.lower())\n\n  # Check for uncollectible primitive (boundary)\n  if primitive_idx == env.world.cookbook.index.index(\"boundary\"):\n      return []\n\n  # Get action mappings\n  ACTION_MAP = env.action_specs()\n  ACTIONS = {\n      \"DOWN\": ACTION_MAP[\"DOWN\"],\n      \"UP\": ACTION_MAP[\"UP\"],\n      \"LEFT\": ACTION_MAP[\"LEFT\"],\n      \"RIGHT\": ACTION_MAP[\"RIGHT\"],\n      \"USE\": ACTION_MAP[\"USE\"]\n  }\n\n  # Define (d_col, d_row) deltas for each move action AND the resulting direction.\n  # When an agent moves, its direction attribute updates to match the direction of movement.\n  # Format: (action_index: (delta_col, delta_row, new_direction_after_move))\n  MOVE_ACTION_DATA = {\n      ACTIONS[\"UP\"]: (0, -1, 0),    # Move North (Up), face North (dir 0)\n      ACTIONS[\"DOWN\"]: (0, 1, 2),   # Move South (Down), face South (dir 2)\n      ACTIONS[\"LEFT\"]: (-1, 0, 3),  # Move West (Left), face West (dir 3)\n      ACTIONS[\"RIGHT\"]: (1, 0, 1)   # Move East (Right), face East (dir 1)\n  }\n\n  # Define (d_col, d_row) deltas for each cardinal direction.\n  # This is used to calculate the coordinates of the cell directly in front of the agent.\n  # dir: 0=N, 1=E, 2=S, 3=W\n  DIR_TO_DELTA = {\n      0: (0, -1),  # North (Up)\n      1: (1, 0),   # East (Right)\n      2: (0, 1),   # South (Down)\n      3: (-1, 0)   # West (Left)\n  }\n\n  # Determine the type of primitive to collect and its collection method\n  is_primitive_workshop = (primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices)\n  is_primitive_grabbable_or_water_stone = (\n      primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices or\n      primitive_idx == env.world.water_index or\n      primitive_idx == env.world.stone_index\n  )\n\n  # Define entities that generally block movement (non-grabbables)\n  # This includes boundaries, workshops, water, stone.\n  blocking_kinds = set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices)\n\n  # Helper function to check if a cell (r_c, r_r) is traversable by the agent.\n  # The `target_prim_idx` is needed to handle special cases like water/stone.\n  def is_traversable(r_c, r_r, target_prim_idx):\n      # Check grid boundaries\n      if not (0 <= r_c < grid_width and 0 <= r_r < grid_height):\n          return False\n\n      # Check for blocking entities in the cell\n      for k_idx in blocking_kinds:\n          if grid[r_c, r_r, k_idx] > 0: # If this cell contains a potentially blocking item\n              # Special case: If the blocking item is water or stone AND it is the primitive we are trying to collect,\n              # then we *can* move onto it (to then USE it).\n              if k_idx == target_prim_idx and (k_idx == env.world.water_index or k_idx == env.world.stone_index):\n                  continue # It's okay to move onto this specific blocking item.\n              else:\n                  return False # It's a true blocking item (boundary, workshop, or water/stone not being targeted).\n      return True # No blocking entities found in this cell (or special case handled).\n\n  # Breadth-First Search (BFS) setup\n  # Queue stores elements as: (((current_col, current_row), current_direction), list_of_actions_to_reach_this_state)\n  queue = collections.deque([(((initial_pos[0], initial_pos[1]), initial_dir), [])])\n  # Visited set stores ((col, row), direction) tuples to avoid redundant exploration and cycles.\n  visited = set([((initial_pos[0], initial_pos[1]), initial_dir)])\n\n  while queue:\n      # Dequeue the current state and path\n      ((current_c, current_r), current_dir), path_actions = queue.popleft()\n\n      # --- Check if the goal (primitive collection condition) is met for the current state ---\n      if is_primitive_workshop:\n          # For workshops, the agent needs to be adjacent to a workshop (in a traversable spot).\n          # The agent's current position (current_c, current_r) must be a valid, traversable spot.\n          if is_traversable(current_c, current_r, primitive_idx):\n              # Check all 8 neighboring cells (including the agent's current cell, though a workshop would block movement there)\n              for dc_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n                  for dr_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n                      px, py = current_c + dc_adj, current_r + dr_adj # Potential primitive location\n                      \n                      # Ensure potential primitive location is within bounds and contains the workshop\n                      if (0 <= px < grid_width and 0 <= py < grid_height) and grid[px, py, primitive_idx] > 0:\n                          # Agent is at (current_c, current_r) which is adjacent to (px, py) containing the workshop.\n                          # This path is valid for \"collecting\" (i.e., reaching) a workshop.\n                          return path_actions\n      elif is_primitive_grabbable_or_water_stone:\n          # For grabbables (like wood) or special non-grabbables (water, stone),\n          # the agent needs to be positioned and oriented such that 'USE' will hit the primitive.\n          front_dc, front_dr = DIR_TO_DELTA[current_dir]\n          front_c, front_r = current_c + front_dc, current_r + front_dr\n\n          # Ensure the cell in front is within grid boundaries and contains the desired primitive\n          if (0 <= front_c < grid_width and 0 <= front_r < grid_height) and grid[front_c, front_r, primitive_idx] > 0:\n              # Goal reached: primitive is in front, and agent can USE.\n              return path_actions + [ACTIONS[\"USE\"]]\n\n      # --- Explore neighboring states by trying all possible movement actions ---\n      for action, (dc_move, dr_move, new_dir) in MOVE_ACTION_DATA.items():\n          next_c, next_r = current_c + dc_move, current_r + dr_move\n          next_state_tuple = ((next_c, next_r), new_dir) # The new state includes updated position AND direction\n\n          # If the next state (position and direction) has not been visited, AND the next cell is traversable:\n          if next_state_tuple not in visited and is_traversable(next_c, next_r, primitive_idx):\n              visited.add(next_state_tuple)\n              queue.append((next_state_tuple, path_actions + [action]))\n\n  # If the queue is exhausted and no path was found, return an empty list.\n  return []", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T01:06:36.866651", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  state = env._current_state\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  \n  # Get primitive index\n  try:\n    prim_idx = cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n  except ValueError: # If primitive string is not known to the cookbook\n    return []\n\n  # Define action mappings and related constants\n  ACTION_MAP = env.action_specs()\n  UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT, USE = ACTION_MAP[\"UP\"], ACTION_MAP[\"DOWN\"], ACTION_MAP[\"LEFT\"], ACTION_MAP[\"RIGHT\"], ACTION_MAP[\"USE\"]\n\n  # Map (dx, dy) to movement action index\n  # Assuming (row, col) coordinates, UP decreases row, DOWN increases row, etc.\n  DELTAS_BY_ACTION = {\n      UP: (-1, 0), \n      DOWN: (1, 0),\n      LEFT: (0, -1),\n      RIGHT: (0, 1)\n  }\n  \n  # Map internal direction index (0:N, 1:S, 2:W, 3:E) to (dx, dy)\n  # This mapping is crucial for determining what's \"in front\" of the agent.\n  DIR_TO_DELTA = {\n      0: (-1, 0), # North (UP)\n      1: (1, 0),  # South (DOWN)\n      2: (0, -1), # West (LEFT)\n      3: (0, 1)   # East (RIGHT)\n  }\n  \n  # Map (dx, dy) to direction index (used to determine agent's new facing direction after moving)\n  DELTA_TO_DIR = {v: k for k, v in DIR_TO_DELTA.items()}\n\n  # Grid dimensions\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = state.grid.shape\n\n  # Specific indices for obstacle checking and primitive type classification\n  boundary_idx = None\n  if \"BOUNDARY\" in cookbook.index.contents:\n    boundary_idx = cookbook.index.index(\"BOUNDARY\")\n\n  water_idx = None\n  if \"WATER\" in cookbook.index.contents:\n    water_idx = cookbook.index.index(\"WATER\")\n\n  bridge_idx = None\n  if \"BRIDGE\" in cookbook.index.contents:\n    bridge_idx = cookbook.index.index(\"BRIDGE\")\n\n  is_grabbable = prim_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_non_grabbable = prim_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices # e.g., WORKSHOP, WATER, BOUNDARY\n\n  # 1. Initial check: If the primitive is grabbable and already in inventory, no actions needed.\n  if is_grabbable and state.inventory[prim_idx] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # 2. Initial check: If the primitive is non-grabbable and we are already on its tile, no actions needed.\n  # This implies \"collecting\" a non-grabbable means reaching its location (e.g., entering a workshop).\n  if is_non_grabbable and state.grid[state.pos[0], state.pos[1], prim_idx] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # BFS setup\n  start_pos = state.pos\n  start_dir = state.dir\n  \n  # Queue stores ( (current_x, current_y, current_direction), list_of_actions_to_reach_this_state )\n  q = collections.deque([((start_pos[0], start_pos[1], start_dir), [])])\n  \n  # Visited set stores (x, y, direction) to avoid cycles and redundant exploration paths\n  visited = {(start_pos[0], start_pos[1], start_dir)}\n\n  while q:\n    ((curr_x, curr_y, curr_dir), path_so_far) = q.popleft()\n\n    # Goal Check: Have we reached a state where the primitive is \"collected\"?\n    if is_grabbable:\n        # For grabbable items, \"collected\" means being adjacent and performing a USE action.\n        # Check if the primitive is directly in front of the agent from the current (pos, dir).\n        front_dx, front_dy = DIR_TO_DELTA[curr_dir]\n        target_cell_x, target_cell_y = curr_x + front_dx, curr_y + front_dy\n\n        if 0 <= target_cell_x < WIDTH and 0 <= target_cell_y < HEIGHT:\n            if state.grid[target_cell_x, target_cell_y, prim_idx] > 0:\n                # Found the primitive in front. Add USE action and return the path.\n                final_actions = list(path_so_far)\n                final_actions.append(USE)\n                return final_actions\n    elif is_non_grabbable:\n        # For non-grabbable primitives, \"collect\" typically means reaching or being on the location.\n        # Check if the agent is currently ON the primitive's location.\n        if state.grid[curr_x, curr_y, prim_idx] > 0:\n            # We are at the location of the non-grabbable primitive. No USE action needed.\n            return list(path_so_far)\n\n    # Explore neighbors by considering possible movement actions (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT)\n    for action_taken, (move_dx, move_dy) in DELTAS_BY_ACTION.items():\n      next_x, next_y = curr_x + move_dx, curr_y + move_dy\n      \n      # The agent's direction after moving will be the direction of the movement itself.\n      next_dir = DELTA_TO_DIR[(move_dx, move_dy)] \n\n      # Check bounds for the next position\n      if not (0 <= next_x < WIDTH and 0 <= next_y < HEIGHT):\n        continue\n\n      # Obstacle Check: Determine if the next cell is traversable.\n      is_blocked = False\n      \n      # Cannot move onto a BOUNDARY tile.\n      if boundary_idx is not None and state.grid[next_x, next_y, boundary_idx] > 0:\n          is_blocked = True\n      \n      # Cannot move onto a WATER tile unless agent has a BRIDGE.\n      if not is_blocked and water_idx is not None and state.grid[next_x, next_y, water_idx] > 0:\n          if bridge_idx is None or state.inventory[bridge_idx] == 0:\n              is_blocked = True\n      \n      if is_blocked:\n        continue # Skip this path, as it leads to an impassable cell.\n\n      # Check if this (position, direction) state has been visited to avoid cycles and re-exploring.\n      if (next_x, next_y, next_dir) not in visited:\n        visited.add((next_x, next_y, next_dir))\n        q.append(((next_x, next_y, next_dir), path_so_far + [action_taken]))\n\n  # If the queue is exhausted and no path to collect the primitive was found\n  return []", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T01:06:38.096244", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Retrieve necessary information\n  state = env._current_state\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  \n  # Get primitive index safely\n  try:\n    prim_idx = cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n  except ValueError:\n    return [] # Primitive string not known in the cookbook\n\n  # Define action mappings\n  ACTION_MAP = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_USE = ACTION_MAP['USE']\n\n  # Grid dimensions\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = state.grid.shape\n  current_pos = state.pos # (row, col)\n\n  # Define movement deltas and corresponding actions\n  # Maps (delta_row, delta_col) to the action that performs this movement\n  MOVES = {\n      (-1, 0): ACTION_MAP['UP'],\n      (1, 0): ACTION_MAP['DOWN'],\n      (0, -1): ACTION_MAP['LEFT'],\n      (0, 1): ACTION_MAP['RIGHT']\n  }\n\n  # Map direction index (0:N, 1:S, 2:W, 3:E) to (dr, dc) for calculating facing cell\n  DIR_TO_FACING_DELTA = {\n      0: (-1, 0), # North (UP)\n      1: (1, 0),  # South (DOWN)\n      2: (0, -1), # West (LEFT)\n      3: (0, 1)   # East (Right)\n  }\n  \n  # Map (dr, dc) of movement to resulting agent direction index\n  # When the agent moves, its direction updates to face the direction of movement.\n  MOVE_DELTA_TO_DIR = {v: k for k, v in DIR_TO_FACING_DELTA.items()}\n\n  # Check if primitive is already in inventory (only applicable to grabbable items)\n  if prim_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices and state.inventory[prim_idx] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # Identify movement blockers\n  # Start with non-grabbable items. Workshops are generally traversable.\n  # BOUNDARY is usually also in non_grabbable_indices and should definitely be a blocker.\n  # Water is special-cased.\n  movement_blockers = set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices) - set(env.world.workshop_indices)\n  \n  water_idx = None\n  try:\n      water_idx = cookbook.index.index(\"WATER\")\n  except ValueError: pass\n\n  bridge_idx = None\n  try:\n      bridge_idx = cookbook.index.index(\"BRIDGE\")\n  except ValueError: pass\n\n  # BFS setup\n  # Queue stores ( (row, col, current_dir), list_of_actions_to_reach_this_state )\n  queue = collections.deque([((current_pos[0], current_pos[1], state.dir), [])])\n  \n  # Visited set stores (row, col, current_dir) to avoid cycles and redundant paths\n  visited = {(current_pos[0], current_pos[1], state.dir)}\n\n  while queue:\n      (curr_r, curr_c, curr_dir), path_so_far = queue.popleft()\n\n      # --- Goal Check: Is the primitive in the cell directly in front of the agent? ---\n      facing_dr, facing_dc = DIR_TO_FACING_DELTA[curr_dir]\n      target_r, target_c = curr_r + facing_dr, curr_c + facing_dc\n\n      # Check if the target cell is within grid bounds\n      if 0 <= target_r < WIDTH and 0 <= target_c < HEIGHT:\n          # Check if the primitive exists in the target cell\n          if state.grid[target_r, target_c, prim_idx] > 0:\n              final_actions = list(path_so_far)\n              \n              # If the primitive is grabbable, a 'USE' action is required to collect it.\n              # Otherwise (non-grabbable like WORKSHOP, WATER), reaching the position\n              # where it is in front is considered \"collected\" (no USE needed).\n              if prim_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n                  final_actions.append(ACTION_USE)\n              return final_actions\n\n      # --- Explore Neighbors (Movement Actions) ---\n      for (move_dr, move_dc), action_val in MOVES.items():\n          next_r, next_c = curr_r + move_dr, curr_c + move_dc\n          # After moving, the agent's direction is updated to face the direction of movement\n          next_dir = MOVE_DELTA_TO_DIR[(move_dr, move_dc)] \n\n          # Check if the next position is within grid boundaries\n          if not (0 <= next_r < WIDTH and 0 <= next_c < HEIGHT):\n              continue\n\n          # Check for blockages at the `next_r, next_c` cell\n          is_blocked = False\n          \n          # Get indices of all items present in the next cell\n          # np.where returns a tuple, [0] gets the actual array of indices.\n          kinds_at_next_cell = np.where(state.grid[next_r, next_c, :] > 0)[0]\n          \n          for kind_id in kinds_at_next_cell:\n              if kind_id == water_idx:\n                  # If it's water and we don't have a bridge, it's blocked.\n                  # If bridge_idx is None, it means BRIDGE item doesn't exist in this game, so it's always blocked.\n                  if bridge_idx is None or state.inventory[bridge_idx] == 0:\n                      is_blocked = True\n                      break\n              elif kind_id in movement_blockers:\n                  # This covers BOUNDARY and other non-traversable non-grabbables.\n                  is_blocked = True\n                  break\n          \n          if is_blocked:\n              continue\n\n          # If not blocked and this (position, direction) state has not been visited, add to queue\n          if (next_r, next_c, next_dir) not in visited:\n              visited.add((next_r, next_c, next_dir))\n              queue.append(((next_r, next_c, next_dir), path_so_far + [action_val]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes without finding a path to the primitive\n  return []", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T01:07:57.045382", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions = []\n\n  # 1. Get Action Mappings and Primitive Index\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  # Map action names to their integer indices\n  UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT, USE = action_map['UP'], action_map['DOWN'], action_map['LEFT'], action_map['RIGHT'], action_map['USE']\n\n  # Get the integer index for the target primitive from the cookbook\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Get current state information from the environment's internal state\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  start_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's current (row, col)\n  global_grid = current_state.grid # The full grid layout\n  W, H, N_KINDS = global_grid.shape # Grid dimensions (Width, Height, Number of Kinds)\n\n  # Determine properties of the target primitive\n  primitive_is_grabbable = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  primitive_is_workshop = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n\n  # Define movement deltas for BFS exploration based on action values\n  move_deltas = {\n      UP: (-1, 0),  # Row decreases for UP\n      DOWN: (1, 0),   # Row increases for DOWN\n      LEFT: (0, -1),  # Column decreases for LEFT\n      RIGHT: (0, 1)   # Column increases for RIGHT\n  }\n\n  def is_valid_move(r, c):\n      \"\"\"\n      Checks if the given (row, col) is within grid bounds and traversable.\n      A cell is traversable if it does not contain a non-grabbable item,\n      UNLESS that non-grabbable item IS the target primitive AND\n      the target primitive is a workshop (allowing movement onto it).\n      \"\"\"\n      # Check bounds\n      if not (0 <= r < W and 0 <= c < H):\n          return False\n      \n      # Iterate through all kinds present in the cell (r, c)\n      for k_idx in range(N_KINDS):\n          if global_grid[r, c, k_idx] == 1: # If this kind is present in the cell\n              if k_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n                  # This cell contains a non-grabbable item.\n                  # Is it an exception (a workshop we want to step on)?\n                  # We can step on workshops if they are our target primitive.\n                  if not (k_idx == primitive_idx and primitive_is_workshop):\n                      # It's a non-grabbable obstacle that is NOT our target workshop.\n                      return False\n      return True\n\n  def is_adjacent_to_kind(r, c, kind_idx):\n      \"\"\"\n      Checks if any cell in the 3x3 neighborhood (including diagonals) around (r, c)\n      contains the specified `kind_idx`.\n      This is used for non-grabbable primitives (like STONE, WATER) where interaction\n      happens from an adjacent cell.\n      \"\"\"\n      for dr in [-1, 0, 1]:\n          for dc in [-1, 0, 1]:\n              # Skip the current cell (r,c) itself; only check neighbors\n              if dr == 0 and dc == 0:\n                  continue \n              nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n              # Check bounds and if the kind is present in the neighboring cell\n              if 0 <= nr < W and 0 <= nc < H and global_grid[nr, nc, kind_idx] == 1:\n                  return True\n      return False\n  \n  # Initialize BFS structures\n  # queue stores (current_position (r,c), path_so_far (list of actions))\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])])\n  # visited set stores (r, c) tuples to avoid cycles and re-processing\n  visited = {start_pos} \n\n  path_to_target = None # This will store the sequence of actions to reach the target area\n\n  # BFS Loop\n  while queue:\n      (r, c), path_so_far = queue.popleft()\n\n      # Determine if the current position (r, c) is a valid \"actionable\" location\n      # for the target primitive.\n      is_current_pos_actionable = False\n      if primitive_is_workshop or primitive_is_grabbable:\n          # For workshops OR grabbable items, the agent must be ON the cell\n          # containing the primitive itself to collect/interact.\n          if global_grid[r, c, primitive_idx] == 1:\n              is_current_pos_actionable = True\n      else: # This covers non-grabbable items that are NOT workshops (e.g., STONE, WATER)\n          # For these, the agent must be ADJACENT to the primitive to interact (USE) with it.\n          if is_adjacent_to_kind(r, c, primitive_idx):\n              is_current_pos_actionable = True\n\n      if is_current_pos_actionable:\n          # Found the shortest path to an actionable location.\n          path_to_target = path_so_far\n          break \n\n      # Explore neighbors: Add valid, unvisited adjacent cells to the queue\n      for action_val, (dr, dc) in move_deltas.items():\n          next_r, next_c = r + dr, c + dc\n          next_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n\n          if is_valid_move(next_r, next_c) and next_pos not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_pos)\n              queue.append((next_pos, path_so_far + [action_val]))\n  \n  # If a path was found, construct the final action sequence\n  if path_to_target is not None:\n      # Append the USE action at the end to collect or interact with the primitive.\n      # The problem context implies that USE will be effective once the agent is in the\n      # correct relative position (on the primitive for grabbable/workshop, adjacent for others).\n      actions = path_to_target + [USE]\n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T01:07:58.304810", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions = []\n\n  # 1. Get Action Mappings and Primitive Index\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT, USE = action_map['UP'], action_map['DOWN'], action_map['LEFT'], action_map['RIGHT'], action_map['USE']\n\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  global_grid = current_state.grid\n  W, H, _ = global_grid.shape\n\n  # 2. Categorize the target primitive for specific collection logic\n  is_grabbable = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n  is_water_or_stone = (primitive_idx == env.world.water_index or primitive_idx == env.world.stone_index)\n\n  # Define movement deltas for BFS exploration\n  move_deltas = {\n      UP: (-1, 0),\n      DOWN: (1, 0),\n      LEFT: (0, -1),\n      RIGHT: (0, 1)\n  }\n\n  # Get the index for the 'BOUNDARY' entity, which is always an impassable obstacle\n  # Assuming 'BOUNDARY' is always in the cookbook index.\n  boundary_idx = env.world.cookbook.index['BOUNDARY'] \n\n  def is_traversable(r, c):\n      \"\"\"\n      Checks if the given (row, col) is within grid bounds and\n      is a cell the agent can legally move onto.\n      \"\"\"\n      # Check bounds\n      if not (0 <= r < W and 0 <= c < H):\n          return False\n\n      # Check for obstacles present at (r, c)\n      # An item acts as an obstacle if it's non-grabbable AND it's NOT the target workshop\n      # (because we explicitly want to path to and occupy workshops).\n      for k_idx in env.world.cookbook.kinds: # Iterate through all possible kinds\n          if global_grid[r, c, k_idx] == 1: # If this kind is present at (r, c)\n              # If it's the BOUNDARY, it's always an obstacle.\n              if k_idx == boundary_idx:\n                  return False\n              \n              # If it's any other non-grabbable entity:\n              if k_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n                  # If it's the target primitive and that primitive is a workshop,\n                  # then we ARE allowed to move onto it.\n                  if k_idx == primitive_idx and is_workshop:\n                      continue \n                  else:\n                      # Otherwise (e.g., WATER, STONE, or other non-grabbable that isn't the target workshop),\n                      # it's a blocking obstacle for movement.\n                      return False\n      return True\n\n  def is_adjacent_to_kind(r, c, kind_idx):\n      \"\"\"\n      Checks if any cell in the 3x3 neighborhood (including diagonals) around (r, c)\n      contains the specified `kind_idx`. Used for primitives interacted with adjacently.\n      \"\"\"\n      for dr in [-1, 0, 1]:\n          for dc in [-1, 0, 1]:\n              if dr == 0 and dc == 0:\n                  continue # Skip the current cell (r,c) itself\n              nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n              # Check bounds and if the kind is present in the neighboring cell\n              if 0 <= nr < W and 0 <= nc < H and global_grid[nr, nc, kind_idx] == 1:\n                  return True\n      return False\n  \n  # BFS Initialization\n  # queue stores (current_position (r,c), path_so_far (list of actions))\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])])\n  # visited set stores (r, c) tuples to avoid cycles and re-processing\n  visited = {start_pos} \n\n  path_to_target = None       # Stores the sequence of movement actions\n  needs_use_action = False    # Flag to indicate if a USE action is required at the end\n\n  # BFS Loop\n  while queue:\n      (r, c), path_so_far = queue.popleft()\n\n      # Check if the current position meets the collection criteria for the primitive\n      if is_grabbable:\n          # For grabbable items (e.g., WOOD), agent must be ON the cell.\n          if global_grid[r, c, primitive_idx] == 1:\n              path_to_target = path_so_far\n              needs_use_action = True\n              break\n      elif is_workshop:\n          # For workshops (e.g., WORKSHOP0), agent must be ON the cell.\n          # No USE action is typically needed for \"collecting\" a workshop; it's a location.\n          if global_grid[r, c, primitive_idx] == 1:\n              path_to_target = path_so_far\n              needs_use_action = False \n              break\n      elif is_water_or_stone:\n          # For water/stone, agent must be ADJACENT to the primitive.\n          if is_adjacent_to_kind(r, c, primitive_idx):\n              path_to_target = path_so_far\n              needs_use_action = True\n              break\n      # If the primitive is 'BOUNDARY', it will never satisfy any collection condition,\n      # and the BFS will exhaust, resulting in an empty path, which is correct.\n\n      # Explore neighbors: Add valid, unvisited adjacent cells to the queue\n      for action_val, (dr, dc) in move_deltas.items():\n          next_r, next_c = r + dr, c + dc\n          next_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n\n          if is_traversable(next_r, next_c) and next_pos not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_pos)\n              queue.append((next_pos, path_so_far + [action_val]))\n  \n  # Construct the final sequence of actions\n  if path_to_target is not None:\n      if needs_use_action:\n          actions = path_to_target + [USE]\n      else:\n          actions = path_to_target\n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T01:08:54.323652", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # 1. Get necessary information from the environment\n  current_state = env._current_state \n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Get the integer ID of the primitive from the cookbook's index\n  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Get action mappings (integers for UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT, USE)\n  ACTION_MAP = env.action_specs()\n  UP = ACTION_MAP['UP']\n  DOWN = ACTION_MAP['DOWN']\n  LEFT = ACTION_MAP['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = ACTION_MAP['RIGHT']\n  USE = ACTION_MAP['USE']\n\n  # Define movement deltas and their corresponding actions (row, col)\n  DELTAS_AND_ACTIONS = [\n      ((-1, 0), UP),    # Move up (decrease row index)\n      ((1, 0), DOWN),   # Move down (increase row index)\n      ((0, -1), LEFT),  # Move left (decrease col index)\n      ((0, 1), RIGHT)   # Move right (increase col index)\n  ]\n\n  # Early exit: If the specified primitive is not a grabbable item, it cannot be collected.\n  if primitive_id not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  # 2. Immediate Collection Check: If the agent is already adjacent to the primitive\n  # In this case, only a 'USE' action is needed.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_id):\n      return [USE]\n\n  # 3. Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path to an adjacent cell\n  # The queue stores tuples: (current_position (r, c), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here)\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) \n  visited = {start_pos} # Keep track of visited positions to prevent loops and redundant searches\n\n  best_path_actions = []\n  found_path = False\n\n  while q:\n      (curr_r, curr_c), actions_so_far = q.popleft()\n\n      # Create a temporary CraftState object at the current BFS position\n      # This allows us to use the `next_to` method to check for adjacency to the primitive.\n      # The grid and inventory remain constant during pathfinding, only position changes.\n      temp_state_for_check = craft.CraftState(\n          scenario=current_state.scenario,\n          grid=grid,\n          pos=(curr_r, curr_c),\n          dir=current_state.dir, # Direction doesn't influence `next_to` check\n          inventory=current_state.inventory # Inventory doesn't influence `next_to` check\n      )\n\n      # Check if the current position is adjacent to the target primitive\n      if temp_state_for_check.next_to(primitive_id):\n          best_path_actions = actions_so_far\n          found_path = True\n          break # Shortest path to an adjacent cell found, exit BFS\n\n      # Explore valid neighboring cells\n      for (dr, dc), action_val in DELTAS_AND_ACTIONS:\n          next_r, next_c = curr_r + dr, curr_c + dc\n          next_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n\n          # Check 1: Boundary Check - Ensure the new position is within grid limits\n          if not (0 <= next_r < WIDTH and 0 <= next_c < HEIGHT):\n              continue\n\n          # Check 2: Traversability Check - Avoid cells containing non-grabbable obstacles\n          is_traversable = True\n          for i_kind in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n              if grid[next_r, next_c, i_kind] == 1: # If this cell is occupied by an obstacle\n                  is_traversable = False\n                  break\n          if not is_traversable:\n              continue\n\n          # Check 3: Visited Check - Avoid re-visiting already explored cells (for shortest path)\n          if next_pos not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_pos)\n              # Add the new position to the queue with the updated path\n              q.append((next_pos, actions_so_far + [action_val]))\n\n  # 4. Construct the final sequence of actions\n  final_actions = best_path_actions\n\n  # If a path to an adjacent cell was found, append the 'USE' action to collect the primitive.\n  if found_path:\n      final_actions.append(USE)\n  \n  return final_actions", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T01:08:55.481958", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive] # Get the integer ID of the primitive\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment's action_specs\n  ACTION_MAP = env.action_specs()\n  UP = ACTION_MAP['UP']\n  DOWN = ACTION_MAP['DOWN']\n  LEFT = ACTION_MAP['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = ACTION_MAP['RIGHT']\n  USE = ACTION_MAP['USE']\n\n  # Define movement deltas (row_delta, col_delta) mapped to actions\n  DELTAS_AND_ACTIONS = [\n      ((-1, 0), UP),    # Move Up (decrement row)\n      ((1, 0), DOWN),   # Move Down (increment row)\n      ((0, -1), LEFT),  # Move Left (decrement col)\n      ((0, 1), RIGHT)   # Move Right (increment col)\n  ]\n\n  # Pre-check: If the 'primitive' is not actually a primitive resource that can be collected\n  # (e.g., it's a workshop, water, boundary, or a crafted item), return an empty list.\n  if primitive_id not in env.world.cookbook.primitives:\n      return []\n  \n  # Edge Case: If the agent is already next to the primitive and it's grabbable,\n  # a single USE action is sufficient.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_id) and primitive_id in current_state.world.grabbable_indices:\n      return [USE]\n\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) # Queue stores: ((current_row, current_col), [list_of_actions_to_reach_here])\n  visited = {start_pos} # Set to keep track of visited (row, col) positions\n\n  best_path_actions = []\n  found_path = False\n\n  while q:\n      (r, c), path_so_far = q.popleft()\n\n      # Create a temporary CraftState object at the current (r, c) position.\n      # This allows us to use the `next_to` method to check if this hypothetical position\n      # is adjacent to the target primitive, without actually performing steps in the environment.\n      temp_state_for_check = craft.CraftState(\n          scenario=current_state.scenario,\n          grid=grid, # The full grid is needed for `next_to` to identify items\n          pos=(r, c),\n          dir=current_state.dir, # Direction doesn't affect `next_to` check\n          inventory=current_state.inventory # Inventory doesn't affect `next_to` check\n      )\n\n      # Check if the current position (r, c) is adjacent to the target primitive\n      if temp_state_for_check.next_to(primitive_id):\n          best_path_actions = path_so_far\n          found_path = True\n          break # Found the shortest path to be adjacent to the primitive\n\n      # Explore neighboring cells\n      for (dr, dc), action_val in DELTAS_AND_ACTIONS:\n          next_r, next_c = r + dr, c + dc\n          next_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n\n          # 1. Check if the next position is within grid boundaries\n          if not (0 <= next_r < WIDTH and 0 <= next_c < HEIGHT):\n              continue\n\n          # 2. Check traversability: Ensure the next position is not an obstacle.\n          # An obstacle is any cell containing a non-grabbable entity (e.g., water, boundary).\n          is_traversable = True\n          for i_kind in current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n              # If the cell (next_r, next_c) contains this non-grabbable item (grid value is 1)\n              if grid[next_r, next_c, i_kind] == 1:\n                  is_traversable = False\n                  break # This cell is an obstacle, cannot move here\n          \n          if not is_traversable:\n              continue # Skip this neighbor if it's an obstacle\n\n          # 3. If the neighbor has not been visited, add it to the queue\n          if next_pos not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_pos)\n              q.append((next_pos, path_so_far + [action_val]))\n\n  final_actions = best_path_actions\n\n  # If a path to an adjacent cell was found, and the primitive is indeed grabbable,\n  # append the 'USE' action to actually collect it.\n  if found_path and primitive_id in current_state.world.grabbable_indices:\n      final_actions.append(USE)\n\n  return final_actions", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T01:09:49.965198", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions = []\n\n  # 1. Get Action Mappings and Primitive Index\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT, USE = action_map['UP'], action_map['DOWN'], action_map['LEFT'], action_map['RIGHT'], action_map['USE']\n\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Get current state information\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  start_dir = current_state.dir # Initial direction of the agent\n  global_grid = current_state.grid\n  W, H, _ = global_grid.shape\n\n  # Determine the type of primitive for target condition and action logic\n  is_grabbable = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n  is_non_grabbable_resource = (primitive_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices and not is_workshop)\n\n  # Map DMLab action values to (dr, dc) movement deltas AND CraftState.dir values.\n  # CraftState.dir: 0=South (DOWN), 1=North (UP), 2=West (LEFT), 3=East (RIGHT).\n  action_to_move_and_dir = {\n      UP: ((-1, 0), 1),    # Move UP (North), new direction is North (1)\n      DOWN: ((1, 0), 0),   # Move DOWN (South), new direction is South (0)\n      LEFT: ((0, -1), 2),  # Move LEFT (West), new direction is West (2)\n      RIGHT: ((0, 1), 3)   # Move RIGHT (East), new direction is East (3)\n  }\n\n  # Map CraftState.dir values to (dr, dc) deltas for the cell \"in front\" of the agent.\n  # This is crucial for determining where the USE action will apply.\n  dir_to_fwd_delta = {\n      0: (1, 0),  # Facing South (DOWN), cell in front is (row+1, col)\n      1: (-1, 0), # Facing North (UP), cell in front is (row-1, col)\n      2: (0, -1), # Facing West (LEFT), cell in front is (row, col-1)\n      3: (0, 1)   # Facing East (RIGHT), cell in front is (row, col+1)\n  }\n\n  # Define indices that block agent movement.\n  # These are all non-grabbable items *except* workshops, which the agent can step onto.\n  movement_blocking_indices = env.world.non_grabbable_indices - env.world.workshop_indices\n\n  def is_valid_move(r, c):\n      \"\"\"Checks if (r, c) is within grid bounds and doesn't contain any movement-blocking obstacles.\"\"\"\n      if not (0 <= r < W and 0 <= c < H):\n          return False\n      # If any item at (r,c) is in the set of movement-blocking indices, it's not traversable.\n      if any(global_grid[r, c, item_idx] == 1 for item_idx in movement_blocking_indices):\n          return False\n      return True\n  \n  # BFS Queue: Stores tuples of ( (current_position (r,c), current_direction (int)), path_so_far (list of actions) )\n  queue = collections.deque([(((start_pos), start_dir), [])])\n  \n  # Visited set: Stores (position (r,c), direction (int)) tuples to avoid redundant exploration.\n  visited = {(start_pos, start_dir)}\n\n  path_to_target = None # This will store the sequence of actions to reach the target state.\n  \n  while queue:\n      ((r, c), current_dir_val), path_so_far = queue.popleft()\n\n      # Check if the current state (position and direction) satisfies the collection goal.\n      # Goal check logic depends on the type of primitive.\n      if is_grabbable:\n          # For grabbable items (e.g., WOOD, IRON), the agent needs to be ON the same cell\n          # as the primitive to collect it.\n          if global_grid[r, c, primitive_idx] == 1:\n              path_to_target = path_so_far\n              break # Found the shortest path to a cell containing the grabbable item.\n      elif is_workshop:\n          # For workshops (e.g., BENCH), the agent needs to be ON the workshop cell.\n          # No 'USE' action needed as it's a location to use, not an item to pick up.\n          if global_grid[r, c, primitive_idx] == 1:\n              path_to_target = path_so_far\n              break # Found the shortest path to the workshop location.\n      elif is_non_grabbable_resource:\n          # For non-grabbable resources (e.g., STONE, WATER), the agent must be\n          # adjacent to the primitive AND facing it to use the 'USE' action.\n          fwd_dr, fwd_dc = dir_to_fwd_delta[current_dir_val]\n          target_r, target_c = r + fwd_dr, c + fwd_dc\n\n          # Check if the cell directly in front contains the primitive and is within bounds.\n          if 0 <= target_r < W and 0 <= target_c < H and global_grid[target_r, target_c, primitive_idx] == 1:\n              path_to_target = path_so_far\n              break # Found the shortest path ending in the correct position and direction to use the primitive.\n\n      # Explore neighbors by applying movement actions.\n      for action_val, (move_delta, new_dir_val) in action_to_move_and_dir.items():\n          dr, dc = move_delta\n          next_r, next_c = r + dr, c + dc\n          next_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n          next_state_tuple = (next_pos, new_dir_val)\n\n          # Only proceed if the next position is valid (within bounds and not a movement-blocking obstacle)\n          # and this (position, direction) state has not been visited before.\n          if is_valid_move(next_r, next_c) and next_state_tuple not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_state_tuple)\n              queue.append((next_state_tuple, path_so_so_far + [action_val]))\n  \n  if path_to_target:\n      # If a path was found, append the USE action if it's a resource to be \"collected\".\n      # Workshops are locations, not items to be picked up, so they don't need a USE action.\n      if is_grabbable or is_non_grabbable_resource:\n          actions = path_to_target + [USE]\n      else: # It's a workshop\n          actions = path_to_target\n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T01:09:51.221882", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions = []\n\n  # 1. Get Action Mappings and Primitive Index\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT, USE = action_map['UP'], action_map['DOWN'], action_map['LEFT'], action_map['RIGHT'], action_map['USE']\n\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Get current state information\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  start_dir = current_state.dir # Initial direction of the agent\n  global_grid = current_state.grid\n  W, H, _ = global_grid.shape\n\n  # Define categories of primitives for goal checking and traversability\n  is_grabbable_resource = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop_location = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n  \n  # Determine truly impassable obstacles: these are non-grabbable items that *also* block movement.\n  # Workshops are non-grabbable but typically traversable.\n  truly_impassable_indices = env.world.non_grabbable_indices - set(env.world.workshop_indices)\n\n  # Map DMLab action values to (dr, dc) movement deltas AND CraftState.dir values.\n  # CraftState.dir: 0=South (DOWN), 1=North (UP), 2=West (LEFT), 3=East (RIGHT).\n  # The agent's direction updates to match the last movement action.\n  action_to_move_and_dir = {\n      UP: ((-1, 0), 1),    # Move UP, new direction is North (1)\n      DOWN: ((1, 0), 0),   # Move DOWN, new direction is South (0)\n      LEFT: ((0, -1), 2),  # Move LEFT, new direction is West (2)\n      RIGHT: ((0, 1), 3)   # Move RIGHT, new direction is East (3)\n  }\n\n  # Map CraftState.dir values to (dr, dc) deltas for the cell \"in front\" of the agent.\n  # This is crucial for determining where the USE action will apply.\n  dir_to_fwd_delta = {\n      0: (1, 0),  # Facing South (DOWN), cell in front is (row+1, col)\n      1: (-1, 0), # Facing North (UP), cell in front is (row-1, col)\n      2: (0, -1), # Facing West (LEFT), cell in front is (row, col-1)\n      3: (0, 1)   # Facing East (RIGHT), cell in front is (row, col+1)\n  }\n\n  def is_valid_move(r, c):\n      \"\"\"Checks if (r, c) is within grid bounds and doesn't contain any truly impassable obstacles.\"\"\"\n      if not (0 <= r < W and 0 <= c < H):\n          return False\n      # If the cell contains *any* item that is in the truly_impassable_indices set, it's not traversable.\n      if any(global_grid[r, c, idx] == 1 for idx in truly_impassable_indices):\n          return False\n      return True\n  \n  # BFS Queue: Stores tuples of ( ((current_position (r,c)), current_direction (int)), path_so_far (list of actions) )\n  queue = collections.deque([(((start_pos), start_dir), [])])\n  \n  # Visited set: Stores (position (r,c), direction (int)) tuples to avoid redundant exploration.\n  visited = {(start_pos, start_dir)}\n\n  path_to_target = None # This will store the sequence of actions to reach the target state.\n  \n  while queue:\n      ((r, c), current_dir_val), path_so_far = queue.popleft()\n\n      # Check if the current state (position and direction) satisfies the collection goal.\n      \n      # Case 1: Primitive is a grabbable resource (e.g., WOOD, IRON) OR a workshop.\n      # Agent needs to be ON the cell containing the primitive.\n      if is_grabbable_resource or is_workshop_location:\n          if global_grid[r, c, primitive_idx] == 1:\n              path_to_target = path_so_far\n              break # Found the shortest path to the target cell.\n      \n      # Case 2: Primitive is an impassable non-grabbable resource (e.g., STONE, WATER).\n      # Agent needs to be adjacent AND facing the primitive.\n      elif primitive_idx in truly_impassable_indices:\n          fwd_dr, fwd_dc = dir_to_fwd_delta[current_dir_val]\n          target_r, target_c = r + fwd_dr, c + fwd_dc\n\n          # Check if the cell directly in front contains the primitive.\n          if (0 <= target_r < W and 0 <= target_c < H and \n              global_grid[target_r, target_c, primitive_idx] == 1):\n              path_to_target = path_so_far\n              break # Found the shortest path ending in the correct position and direction to use the primitive.\n\n      # Explore neighbors by applying movement actions.\n      for action_val, (move_delta, new_dir_val) in action_to_move_and_dir.items():\n          dr, dc = move_delta\n          next_r, next_c = r + dr, c + dc\n          next_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n          next_state_tuple = (next_pos, new_dir_val)\n\n          # Only proceed if the next position is valid (within bounds and not an obstacle)\n          # and this (position, direction) state has not been visited before.\n          if is_valid_move(next_r, next_c) and next_state_tuple not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_state_tuple)\n              queue.append((next_state_tuple, path_so_far + [action_val]))\n  \n  if path_to_target is not None:\n      # If a path was found, append the USE action at the end to perform the collection.\n      # The DSL's COLLECT_FUNC implies a final USE action for any primitive.\n      actions = path_to_target + [USE]\n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T01:10:55.964029", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T01:10:57.076604", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions_list = []\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  initial_grid = current_state.grid\n  initial_pos = current_state.pos # tuple (r, c)\n  initial_dir = current_state.dir # int (0-3), 0:RIGHT, 1:UP, 2:LEFT, 3:DOWN\n\n  # Get the integer ID for the target primitive from the cookbook index\n  primitive_id = current_state.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = initial_grid.shape\n\n  # Retrieve action mapping from the environment's action specifications\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION = action_map['UP'] # 'UP' in action_specs implies moving forward\n  TURN_LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  TURN_RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Direction mapping: (dr, dc) for agent's facing direction (0:R, 1:U, 2:L, 3:D)\n  # This helps calculate the next position when moving forward\n  DIR_TO_DRDC = {\n      0: (0, 1),   # Facing RIGHT: +1 to column (c)\n      1: (-1, 0),  # Facing UP: -1 to row (r)\n      2: (0, -1),  # Facing LEFT: -1 to column (c)\n      3: (1, 0)    # Facing DOWN: +1 to row (r)\n  }\n\n  # Maps for updating the agent's direction when turning left/right\n  TURN_LEFT_MAP = {0: 1, 1: 2, 2: 3, 3: 0} # R -> U -> L -> D -> R\n  TURN_RIGHT_MAP = {0: 3, 1: 0, 2: 1, 3: 2} # R -> D -> L -> U -> R\n\n  # Identify non-walkable entities (e.g., BOUNDARY, WATER, WORKSHOP_X) that block agent movement\n  non_grabbable_indices = current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # --- Nested Helper Functions for Readability ---\n  def _is_cell_walkable(r, c):\n      \"\"\"Checks if a given grid cell (r, c) is walkable.\"\"\"\n      if not (0 <= r < WIDTH and 0 <= c < HEIGHT):\n          return False  # Out of bounds\n\n      # Check for non-grabbable blocking entities\n      for kind_idx in non_grabbable_indices:\n          if initial_grid[r, c, kind_idx] > 0:\n              return False  # Contains a non-walkable item\n\n      # Ensure the agent does not try to walk onto the primitive itself.\n      # Agent collects from an adjacent cell, not by occupying the same cell.\n      if initial_grid[r, c, primitive_id] > 0:\n          return False\n\n      return True\n\n  def _is_primitive_in_agent_neighborhood(agent_r, agent_c):\n      \"\"\"Checks if the target primitive is in the 3x3 neighborhood of (agent_r, agent_c).\"\"\"\n      for dr_check in [-1, 0, 1]:\n          for dc_check in [-1, 0, 1]:\n              check_r, check_c = agent_r + dr_check, agent_c + dc_check\n              if (0 <= check_r < WIDTH and 0 <= check_c < HEIGHT and\n                  initial_grid[check_r, check_c, primitive_id] > 0):\n                  return True\n      return False\n  # --- End of Nested Helper Functions ---\n\n  # Optimization: If the primitive is already in the 3x3 neighborhood of the agent's current position,\n  # no pathfinding is needed; just use the item.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_id):\n      return [USE_ACTION]\n\n  # Initialize Breadth-First Search (BFS)\n  # Queue stores ( (current_position_tuple, current_direction_int), list_of_actions_to_reach_here )\n  queue = collections.deque([((initial_pos, initial_dir), [])])\n  # Visited set stores (position_tuple, direction_int) to avoid redundant computations and cycles\n  visited = {(initial_pos, initial_dir)}\n\n  target_path = None # This will store the sequence of actions to reach a collectable position\n\n  # BFS Loop\n  while queue:\n      (current_pos, current_dir), path_actions = queue.popleft()\n      r, c = current_pos\n\n      # Check if the current position is a \"goal\" state for collection.\n      # A goal state means the primitive is within the 3x3 neighborhood of the agent's current (r, c).\n      if _is_primitive_in_agent_neighborhood(r, c):\n          target_path = path_actions # Path to reach this collectable position\n          break # Shortest path found, terminate BFS\n\n      # Explore possible next actions from the current state: Move Forward, Turn Left, Turn Right\n\n      # Try Move Forward\n      move_dr, move_dc = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n      next_r, next_c = r + move_dr, c + move_dc\n      next_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n      next_dir = current_dir # Moving forward does not change facing direction\n\n      if _is_cell_walkable(next_r, next_c) and \\\n         (next_pos, next_dir) not in visited:\n          visited.add((next_pos, next_dir))\n          queue.append(((next_pos, next_dir), path_actions + [MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION]))\n\n      # Try Turn Left\n      next_dir_left = TURN_LEFT_MAP[current_dir]\n      if (current_pos, next_dir_left) not in visited:\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_left))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_left), path_actions + [TURN_LEFT_ACTION]))\n\n      # Try Turn Right\n      next_dir_right = TURN_RIGHT_MAP[current_dir]\n      if (current_pos, next_dir_right) not in visited:\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_right))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_right), path_actions + [TURN_RIGHT_ACTION]))\n\n  # If a path to a collectable position was found, append the USE action to perform the collection\n  if target_path is not None:\n      actions_list.extend(target_path)\n      actions_list.append(USE_ACTION)\n\n  return actions_list", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T01:11:59.967789", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions = []\n  \n  # Retrieve the current state of the environment.\n  # This provides access to the grid layout, agent's position, and world configuration.\n  current_state = env._current_state \n  grid = current_state.grid\n  current_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's current (row, column) position\n  \n  # Get the integer ID for the specified primitive string.\n  # The `index.index()` method ensures the primitive is registered and returns its ID.\n  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n\n  # Get grid dimensions for boundary checks during pathfinding.\n  GRID_ROWS, GRID_COLS, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Map action names to their integer values using the environment's action specifications.\n  # This makes the code robust to changes in action mapping.\n  action_specs = env.action_specs()\n  DOWN = action_specs['DOWN']\n  UP = action_specs['UP']\n  LEFT = action_specs['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_specs['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_specs['USE']\n\n  # Define movement deltas for the four cardinal directions (row_change, col_change).\n  # These deltas correspond to the actions for moving UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT.\n  MOVEMENT_DELTAS = {\n      UP: (-1, 0),    # Moving UP decreases the row index\n      DOWN: (1, 0),   # Moving DOWN increases the row index\n      LEFT: (0, -1),  # Moving LEFT decreases the column index\n      RIGHT: (0, 1)   # Moving RIGHT increases the column index\n  }\n\n  # --- Step 1: Check if the agent is already adjacent to the primitive. ---\n  # The `CraftState.next_to()` method checks if the target `primitive_id`\n  # is present in the 3x3 neighborhood around the agent's current position (including the agent's cell itself).\n  # If it is, only a 'USE' action is needed to interact with/collect the primitive.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_id):\n      actions.append(USE)\n      return actions\n\n  # --- Step 2: Locate all occurrences of the primitive on the grid. ---\n  # Iterate through the entire grid to find all cells that contain the target primitive.\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for r in range(GRID_ROWS):\n      for c in range(GRID_COLS):\n          # If the primitive_id layer at (r, c) is 1, it means the primitive is present there.\n          if grid[r, c, primitive_id] == 1:\n              primitive_locations.append((r, c))\n\n  # If no instances of the primitive are found on the grid, it cannot be collected.\n  # Return an empty list of actions.\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      return []\n\n  # --- Step 3: Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path. ---\n  # The goal is to find the shortest sequence of movement actions that lead the agent\n  # to a cell *adjacent* to any of the primitive locations.\n  \n  # The queue for BFS stores tuples: `((current_row, current_col), [list_of_actions_to_reach_here])`.\n  q = collections.deque([(current_pos, [])]) \n  \n  # The `visited` set keeps track of (row, col) positions that have already been\n  # added to the queue, preventing infinite loops and redundant path exploration.\n  visited = {current_pos} \n\n  # This variable will store the shortest path found to an adjacent cell.\n  shortest_path_to_adjacent = None \n\n  # Start the BFS traversal.\n  while q:\n      (r, c), path_so_far = q.popleft()\n\n      # Check if the current cell (r, c) is adjacent to any of the primitive locations.\n      # Adjacency is defined as a Manhattan distance of 1 (directly up, down, left, or right).\n      for pr, pc in primitive_locations:\n          if abs(r - pr) + abs(c - pc) == 1: \n              shortest_path_to_adjacent = path_so_far # Found the path!\n              break # Exit the inner loop, as we've found our target path.\n      \n      # If a path to an adjacent cell was found, we can stop the BFS.\n      if shortest_path_to_adjacent is not None:\n          break \n\n      # Explore valid neighboring cells (up, down, left, right).\n      for action_dir, (dr, dc) in MOVEMENT_DELTAS.items():\n          nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc # Calculate the coordinates of the potential new position.\n\n          # Boundary check: Ensure the new position is within the grid limits.\n          if not (0 <= nr < GRID_ROWS and 0 <= nc < GRID_COLS):\n              continue\n          \n          # Traversability check: Determine if the new cell is walkable.\n          # A cell is considered non-traversable if it contains any item\n          # whose kind index is in the `env.world.non_grabbable_indices` set.\n          # These typically represent obstacles (e.g., `BOUNDARY`, `WATER`, `WORKSHOP` structures).\n          is_traversable = True\n          for kind_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n              # If the new cell `(nr, nc)` contains a non-grabbable item, it's an obstacle.\n              if grid[nr, nc, kind_idx] == 1: \n                  is_traversable = False\n                  break # No need to check other non-grabbable kinds, this cell is blocked.\n          \n          if not is_traversable:\n              continue # Skip this neighbor if it's an obstacle.\n          \n          # If the neighbor is traversable and has not been visited yet, add it to the queue.\n          if (nr, nc) not in visited:\n              visited.add((nr, nc)) # Mark this position as visited.\n              # Extend the path with the action taken to reach this new position.\n              new_path = path_so_far + [action_dir] \n              q.append(((nr, nc), new_path)) # Add the new state to the BFS queue.\n    \n  # --- Step 4: Construct the final action sequence. ---\n  # If a path to an adjacent cell was successfully found during the BFS,\n  # append these movement actions to the `actions` list.\n  if shortest_path_to_adjacent is not None:\n      actions.extend(shortest_path_to_adjacent)\n      # After reaching a cell adjacent to the primitive, perform the 'USE' action.\n      # This typically picks up grabbable items or interacts with non-grabbable structures.\n      actions.append(USE) \n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T01:12:01.169852", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions = []\n  \n  # Get the current state directly for grid and position information\n  current_state = env._current_state \n  grid = current_state.grid\n  current_pos = current_state.pos\n  \n  # Get the integer ID of the primitive from the cookbook index\n  # env.world.cookbook.index provides a mapping from string names to integer IDs.\n  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Retrieve action mapping from the environment for robustness\n  # This ensures the action integers correspond to the environment's current mapping.\n  _action_specs = env.action_specs()\n  DOWN = _action_specs['DOWN']\n  UP = _action_specs['UP']\n  LEFT = _action_specs['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = _action_specs['RIGHT']\n  USE = _action_specs['USE']\n\n  # Define movement deltas (dr, dc) for convenience for the 4 cardinal directions,\n  # mapped to their corresponding action constants.\n  DELTAS = {\n      UP: (-1, 0),    # Moving UP decreases the row index\n      DOWN: (1, 0),   # Moving DOWN increases the row index\n      LEFT: (0, -1),  # Moving LEFT decreases the column index\n      RIGHT: (0, 1)   # Moving RIGHT increases the column index\n  }\n\n  # 1. Check if the agent is already next to the primitive.\n  # The `next_to` method checks if the primitive is in the 3x3 neighborhood\n  # around the agent's current position.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_id):\n      # If adjacent, and the primitive is grabbable, a single 'USE' action is sufficient.\n      if primitive_id in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n          actions.append(USE)\n      return actions\n\n  # 2. Find all locations of the target primitive on the grid.\n  # We iterate through the entire grid to identify all cells where the primitive is present.\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for r in range(WIDTH):\n      for c in range(HEIGHT):\n          # If the primitive_id occupies this cell (indicated by a 1 in its grid layer),\n          # add its coordinates to our list of target locations.\n          if grid[r, c, primitive_id] == 1:\n              primitive_locations.append((r, c))\n\n  # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the grid, it cannot be collected.\n  # In this case, an empty list of actions is returned.\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      return []\n\n  # 3. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path\n  #    to a cell that is adjacent to any of the primitive locations.\n  # The queue stores tuples: ((current_row, current_col), [list_of_actions_to_reach_here]).\n  q = collections.deque([(current_pos, [])]) \n  # The visited set keeps track of positions already explored to avoid cycles and redundant paths,\n  # ensuring we find the shortest path.\n  visited = {current_pos} \n\n  # This variable will store the list of actions forming the shortest path\n  # to a cell adjacent to the target primitive, once it's discovered.\n  target_adj_pos_path = None \n\n  while q:\n      (r, c), path = q.popleft()\n\n      # Check if the current position (r, c) is adjacent to any of the primitive locations.\n      # Adjacency is defined by a Manhattan distance of 1 (horizontally or vertically).\n      # From such a position, the 'USE' action can be applied to interact with the primitive.\n      for pr, pc in primitive_locations:\n          if abs(r - pr) + abs(c - pc) == 1: \n              target_adj_pos_path = path # Found the shortest path to an adjacent cell.\n              break # Break from this inner loop as we've found our primary target path.\n      \n      if target_adj_pos_path is not None:\n          break # Exit the BFS loop once the shortest path to an adjacent cell has been found.\n\n      # Explore valid neighboring cells (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT).\n      for action_dir, (dr, dc) in DELTAS.items():\n          nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc # Calculate the new potential position.\n\n          # Check bounds: Ensure the new position is within the grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= nr < WIDTH and 0 <= nc < HEIGHT):\n              continue\n          \n          # Check traversability:\n          # A cell is considered non-traversable if it contains any item\n          # whose kind index is in the world's `non_grabbable_indices` set.\n          # These typically represent obstacles like 'BOUNDARY', 'WATER', or 'WORKSHOP' structures\n          # that the agent cannot move through.\n          is_traversable = True\n          for i_kind in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n              if grid[nr, nc, i_kind] == 1: # If this cell contains a non-grabbable item.\n                  is_traversable = False\n                  break # This neighbor is an obstacle, so stop checking and mark as not traversable.\n          \n          if not is_traversable:\n              continue # Skip this neighbor if it's an obstacle.\n          \n          # If the neighbor has not been visited, add it to the queue to explore later.\n          # This prevents cycles and ensures the shortest path is found.\n          if (nr, nc) not in visited:\n              visited.add((nr, nc)) # Mark as visited.\n              new_path = path + [action_dir] # Extend the current path with the action taken to reach here.\n              q.append(((nr, nc), new_path)) # Add the new state (position and path) to the queue.\n    \n  # 4. If a path to an adjacent cell was found during BFS,\n  #    extend the actions list with this path and then append a 'USE' action\n  #    if the primitive is actually grabbable.\n  if target_adj_pos_path is not None:\n      actions.extend(target_adj_pos_path)\n      # Only append the 'USE' action if the primitive is listed as a grabbable item\n      # in the CraftWorld configuration. This prevents trying to 'collect' non-grabbable\n      # entities like water or boundaries.\n      if primitive_id in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n          actions.append(USE) \n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 