{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:01:10.487127", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  # Retrieve the integer ID for the target primitive from the world's cookbook index.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n  \n  # Map action names to their corresponding integer IDs for readability and consistency.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Step 1: Immediate collection check.\n  # If the agent is already within the 3x3 neighborhood of the primitive,\n  # the most efficient action is simply to 'USE' it.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n    return [USE]\n\n  # Step 2: Locate all occurrences of the primitive on the grid.\n  # We need to find all grid cells where the target primitive is present.\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n  \n  primitive_locations_on_grid = [] # Stores (x, y) coordinates of primitive instances\n  for x in range(grid_width):\n    for y in range(grid_height):\n      # The grid stores counts for each kind at each cell. If the count > 0, the primitive is present.\n      if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n        primitive_locations_on_grid.append((x, y))\n\n  # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the grid, it's currently unreachable.\n  if not primitive_locations_on_grid:\n    return []\n\n  # Step 3: Define \"goal cells\" for pathfinding.\n  # A goal cell is any position from which the agent can successfully 'USE' the primitive.\n  # In CraftWorld, 'USE' applies to the 3x3 neighborhood around the agent's current position.\n  # Therefore, for each primitive location (px, py), any cell (gx, gy) in its 3x3 neighborhood\n  # (including the primitive's own cell) is a valid goal cell.\n  goal_cells = set()\n  for px, py in primitive_locations_on_grid:\n    # Iterate through the 3x3 neighborhood around the primitive location\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        gx, gy = px + dx, py + dy # Calculate potential goal cell coordinates\n        # Ensure the potential goal cell is within grid boundaries\n        if 0 <= gx < grid_width and 0 <= gy < grid_height:\n          goal_cells.add((gx, gy))\n\n  # Step 4: Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path.\n  # BFS is used because it guarantees finding the shortest path in an unweighted graph,\n  # where each movement action has a uniform cost (1 step).\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  \n  # The BFS queue stores tuples of (current_position, list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here).\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) \n  # 'visited' set keeps track of positions already explored to prevent cycles and redundant work.\n  visited = {start_pos} \n\n  # Define possible movement directions and their corresponding action IDs.\n  # Format: ((delta_x, delta_y), action_id)\n  MOVE_DELTAS_AND_ACTIONS = [\n      ((0, -1), UP),    # Move North (decreases Y coordinate)\n      ((0, 1), DOWN),   # Move South (increases Y coordinate)\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT),  # Move West (decreases X coordinate)\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT),  # Move East (increases X coordinate)\n  ]\n\n  # Identify impassable terrain.\n  # The agent cannot move into cells occupied by certain non-grabbable items.\n  # Workshops, although non-grabbable, are typically traversable, so they are excluded.\n  impassable_kinds = set()\n  for idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n      if idx not in env.world.workshop_indices: \n          impassable_kinds.add(idx)\n\n  while q:\n    (cx, cy), path_so_far = q.popleft() # Get the current position and the path leading to it\n\n    # If the current position is one of our designated goal cells, we've found the shortest path.\n    if (cx, cy) in goal_cells:\n      # The path found leads to a cell from which 'USE' can be applied to collect the primitive.\n      return path_so_far + [USE]\n\n    # Explore valid neighboring cells for movement.\n    for (dx, dy), action_to_take in MOVE_DELTAS_AND_ACTIONS:\n      nx, ny = cx + dx, cy + dy # Calculate the new potential position\n      new_pos = (nx, ny)\n\n      # Check 1: Ensure the new position is within the grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height):\n        continue # Skip if out of bounds.\n\n      # Check 2: Determine if the new position is occupied by impassable terrain.\n      is_impassable_location = False\n      for k_idx in impassable_kinds:\n          # If any impassable kind is present at the new position (count > 0), it's blocked.\n          if grid[nx, ny, k_idx] > 0: \n              is_impassable_location = True\n              break\n      \n      if is_impassable_location:\n          continue # Cannot move to this cell, skip it.\n\n      # Check 3: If the new position has not been visited yet, add it to the queue\n      # along with the path taken to reach it.\n      if new_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(new_pos)\n        q.append((new_pos, path_so_far + [action_to_take]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and the queue becomes empty without finding any path to a goal cell,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable from the current state.\n  return []", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:01:11.648089", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  # Get the integer ID for the target primitive from the world's cookbook index.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n  \n  # Map action names to their corresponding integer IDs for readability and consistency.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # 1. Immediate collection check: If the agent is already within reach of the primitive\n  # (i.e., in its 3x3 neighborhood), the most efficient action is simply to 'USE' it.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n    return [USE]\n\n  # 2. Locate all occurrences of the primitive on the grid.\n  # This helps in defining all possible target locations for the agent.\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n  \n  # Stores (x, y) coordinates of all grid cells containing the primitive.\n  all_primitive_locations = [] \n  for x in range(grid_width):\n    for y in range(grid_height):\n      # If the count for `primitive_idx` at (x, y) is greater than 0, the primitive is present.\n      if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n        all_primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the grid, it's unreachable.\n  if not all_primitive_locations:\n    return []\n\n  # 3. Define \"goal cells\" for the pathfinding (BFS).\n  # A goal cell is any position from which the agent can successfully 'USE' the primitive.\n  # The 'USE' action applies to the 3x3 neighborhood around the agent.\n  # So, for each primitive location (px, py), any cell (gx, gy) in its 3x3 neighborhood\n  # is a valid goal cell.\n  goal_cells = set()\n  for px, py in all_primitive_locations:\n    # Iterate through the 3x3 neighborhood centered around the primitive location.\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        gx, gy = px + dx, py + dy # Calculate candidate goal cell coordinates.\n        # Ensure the potential goal cell is within grid boundaries.\n        if 0 <= gx < grid_width and 0 <= gy < grid_height:\n          goal_cells.add((gx, gy))\n\n  # 4. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path.\n  # BFS guarantees finding the shortest path in an unweighted graph (where each movement has a cost of 1).\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  \n  # The queue stores tuples of (current_position, list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here).\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) \n  # The 'visited' set keeps track of positions already explored to prevent cycles and redundant work.\n  visited = {start_pos} \n\n  # Define possible movement directions and their corresponding action IDs.\n  # Format: ((delta_x, delta_y), action_id)\n  MOVE_DELTAS_AND_ACTIONS = [\n      ((0, -1), UP),    # Moving up (decreasing Y coordinate)\n      ((0, 1), DOWN),   # Moving down (increasing Y coordinate)\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT),  # Moving left (decreasing X coordinate)\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT),  # Moving right (increasing X coordinate)\n  ]\n\n  # Identify impassable terrain kinds.\n  # These are non-grabbable items that block agent movement. Workshops are typically traversable.\n  impassable_kinds = set()\n  for idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n      if idx not in env.world.workshop_indices: # Exclude workshops as they are traversable.\n          impassable_kinds.add(idx)\n\n  while q:\n    (cx, cy), path_so_far = q.popleft() # Get the current position and the path taken to reach it.\n\n    # If the current position is one of our designated goal cells, we've found the shortest path.\n    if (cx, cy) in goal_cells:\n      # The path leads to a cell from which 'USE' can be applied.\n      return path_so_far + [USE]\n\n    # Explore valid neighboring cells for movement.\n    for (dx, dy), action_to_take in MOVE_DELTAS_AND_ACTIONS:\n      nx, ny = cx + dx, cy + dy # Calculate the new potential position.\n      new_pos = (nx, ny)\n\n      # Check 1: Ensure the new position is within grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height):\n        continue\n\n      # Check 2: Determine if the new position is occupied by impassable terrain.\n      # A cell is impassable if it contains any of the identified impassable kinds.\n      if any(grid[nx, ny, k_idx] > 0 for k_idx in impassable_kinds): \n          continue # Cannot move to this cell, skip it.\n\n      # If the new position has not been visited yet, add it to the queue\n      # along with the path taken to reach it.\n      if new_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(new_pos)\n        q.append((new_pos, path_so_far + [action_to_take]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and the queue is empty without finding any path to a goal cell,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable from the current state.\n  return []", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:02:31.104248", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Returns a list of actions to find and collect the primitive in the passed env.\n    \n    This function implements a programmatic strategy to navigate the agent\n    to a location from which the specified primitive can be \"collected\" (e.g.,\n    picked up, mined, or reached if it's a workshop). It uses a Breadth-First Search (BFS)\n    to find the shortest path.\n\n    Args:\n        env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab object representing the current simulation environment.\n        primitive (str): The string name of the primitive to collect (e.g., \"WOOD\", \"WORKSHOP0\").\n\n    Returns:\n        List[int]: A sequence of integer action codes (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT, USE)\n                   to execute. An empty list is returned if the primitive is\n                   unreachable or not found on the map.\n  \"\"\"\n  actions = [] # Initialize the list to store the sequence of actions\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's current (row, col) position\n  grid_rows, grid_cols, _ = grid.shape # Grid dimensions: (rows, columns, kinds)\n\n  # 1. Map the primitive's string name to its unique integer ID using the cookbook.\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  try:\n    primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    # If the primitive name is not found in the cookbook, it's an invalid target.\n    return []\n\n  # Define mappings for cardinal directions to their corresponding action constants.\n  # These are crucial for building the path during the BFS traversal.\n  ACTION_MAP = {\n      (-1, 0): craft.UP,    # Move North (row - 1)\n      (1, 0): craft.DOWN,   # Move South (row + 1)\n      (0, -1): craft.LEFT,  # Move West (col - 1)\n      (0, 1): craft.RIGHT   # Move East (col + 1)\n  }\n  CARDINAL_DIRECTIONS = [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]\n\n  # 2. Categorize the primitive based on its interaction type in the game world.\n  # A \"grabbable resource\" is an item that can be picked up or harvested using the 'USE' action.\n  is_grabbable_resource = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  # A \"workshop location\" is a specific grid cell (e.g., BENCH) that the agent needs to reach\n  # to perform crafting operations. The 'USE' action for crafting is typically handled by the\n  # 'craft' DSL primitive, not directly by 'collect' for workshops.\n  is_workshop_location = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n\n  # If the primitive is a non-grabbable entity and it's NOT a workshop, it's generally\n  # an impassable or uncollectible environmental feature (e.g., BOUNDARY, plain WATER).\n  # In such cases, this function cannot \"collect\" it.\n  if primitive_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices and not is_workshop_location:\n    return []\n\n  # 3. Helper function: Determines if a given grid cell (r, c) is traversable by the agent.\n  def is_traversable(r, c):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the cell at (r, c) is within grid bounds and free of blocking entities.\n    Agents cannot move onto water or certain non-grabbable obstacles that are not workshops.\n    \"\"\"\n    # First, check if the coordinates are within the defined grid boundaries.\n    if not (0 <= r < grid_rows and 0 <= c < grid_cols):\n      return False\n\n    # Check if the cell contains water, which is an impassable terrain.\n    if grid[r, c, env.world.water_index] == 1:\n      return False\n\n    # Check for other blocking obstacles. A cell is considered blocked if it contains\n    # any non-grabbable entity that is *not* a workshop. Workshops are traversable.\n    cell_contents_indices = np.where(grid[r, c] == 1)[0]\n    for kind_idx_in_cell in cell_contents_indices:\n      if kind_idx_in_cell in env.world.non_grabbable_indices and \\\n         kind_idx_in_cell not in env.world.workshop_indices:\n        return False # This cell contains an unpassable obstacle (e.g., a wall, bedrock)\n    return True # The cell is traversable.\n\n  # 4. Find all locations on the grid where instances of the target primitive exist.\n  # `numpy.where` is an efficient way to get all (row, column) coordinates where the primitive is present.\n  primitive_rows, primitive_cols = np.where(grid[:, :, primitive_idx] == 1)\n  primitive_locations_on_grid = list(zip(primitive_rows, primitive_cols))\n\n  if not primitive_locations_on_grid:\n    # If the primitive does not exist anywhere on the current map, there's nothing to collect.\n    return []\n\n  # 5. Determine the \"target BFS locations\": these are the specific cells where the agent\n  # must be positioned to successfully interact with or collect the primitive.\n  target_bfs_locations = set()\n\n  if is_grabbable_resource:\n    # For grabbable items (e.g., WOOD, STONE), the agent needs to be in the 3x3\n    # neighborhood (which includes the resource's cell itself) of the resource to 'USE' it.\n    # Define offsets for a 3x3 grid centered around a point.\n    NEIGHBORHOOD_OFFSETS = [\n        (dr, dc) for dr in [-1, 0, 1] for dc in [-1, 0, 1]\n    ]\n    for pr, pc in primitive_locations_on_grid:\n      for dr, dc in NEIGHBORHOOD_OFFSETS:\n        nr, nc = pr + dr, pc + dc\n        # Add any traversable cell in this neighborhood as a potential target location.\n        if is_traversable(nr, nc):\n          target_bfs_locations.add((nr, nc))\n  elif is_workshop_location:\n    # For workshops (e.g., BENCH), the agent must move directly *onto* the workshop's cell.\n    for wr, wc in primitive_locations_on_grid:\n      # Add the workshop's own cell as a target if it is traversable.\n      if is_traversable(wr, wc):\n        target_bfs_locations.add((wr, wc))\n  # Other primitive types should have been filtered out by the check in step 2.\n\n  if not target_bfs_locations:\n    # If no reachable (traversable) target spots could be identified for the primitive,\n    # it means it's effectively inaccessible.\n    return []\n\n  # 6. Immediate Collection Check: Check if the agent is already at a suitable position\n  # to collect the primitive without needing to move.\n  if start_pos in target_bfs_locations:\n    if is_grabbable_resource:\n      # If the agent is already at a collection spot for a grabbable resource,\n      # only the 'USE' action is needed.\n      return [craft.USE]\n    else: # This implies it's a workshop location.\n      # If the agent is already on a workshop, no movement or direct 'USE' action\n      # is needed from the 'collect' function. The 'craft' DSL command will\n      # initiate the 'USE' when a recipe is executed at the workshop.\n      return []\n\n  # 7. Perform a Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path from the agent's\n  # current position to any of the identified target collection spots.\n  # The queue stores tuples of: (current_position (row, col), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here)\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])])\n  # A set to keep track of visited cells, preventing infinite loops and redundant exploration.\n  visited = {start_pos}\n\n  shortest_path_actions = None # This will store the shortest action sequence found.\n\n  while queue:\n    (r, c), current_path = queue.popleft() # Dequeue the current position and its path\n\n    # If the current position is one of our target collection locations,\n    # we've found the shortest path.\n    if (r, c) in target_bfs_locations:\n      shortest_path_actions = current_path\n      break # Exit the BFS as the shortest path is guaranteed to be found first.\n\n    # Explore all four cardinal neighbors (Up, Down, Left, Right) from the current cell.\n    for dr, dc in CARDINAL_DIRECTIONS:\n      next_r, next_c = r + dr, c + dc\n      \n      # If the neighboring cell is within bounds, has not been visited yet,\n      # and is traversable, add it to the queue for further exploration.\n      if (next_r, next_c) not in visited:\n        if is_traversable(next_r, next_c):\n          visited.add((next_r, next_c)) # Mark the new cell as visited\n          # Enqueue the new cell with the extended path\n          queue.append(((next_r, next_c), current_path + [ACTION_MAP[(dr, dc)]]))\n\n  # 8. Construct the final sequence of actions to be returned.\n  if shortest_path_actions is None:\n    # If no path was found to any reachable target location, return an empty list.\n    return []\n\n  # Extend the actions list with the path determined by the BFS.\n  actions.extend(shortest_path_actions)\n\n  # If the primitive is a grabbable resource (e.g., wood, stone), an additional 'USE' action\n  # is required after reaching the collection spot to actually acquire it.\n  if is_grabbable_resource:\n    actions.append(craft.USE)\n\n  return actions", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:02:32.287699", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Finds and returns a list of actions to collect the specified primitive.\n\n  This function uses Breadth-First Search (BFS) to determine the shortest\n  sequence of movements to reach a position from which the primitive can\n  be collected (either by walking onto it for workshops, or being in a 3x3\n  neighborhood for grabbable resources, followed by a 'USE' action).\n\n  Args:\n      env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab environment instance.\n      primitive (str): The name of the primitive item to collect (e.g., \"WOOD\", \"WORKSHOP0\").\n\n  Returns:\n      List[int]: A sequence of integer action codes (e.g., craft.UP, craft.USE).\n                 Returns an empty list if the primitive is not found, is not\n                 collectible, or no path exists.\n  \"\"\"\n  actions = []\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's current (x, y) position\n  # Grid shape is (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds). So, grid_width corresponds to X-dimension,\n  # grid_height corresponds to Y-dimension.\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # 1. Retrieve the integer index for the primitive from the cookbook.\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  try:\n    primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    # If the primitive name is not recognized, it cannot be collected.\n    return []\n\n  # Define mappings for cardinal directions to action constants.\n  # (dx, dy) => action_constant, where dx is change in x, dy is change in y.\n  ACTION_MAP = {\n      (-1, 0): craft.LEFT,  # Move left (decrease x)\n      (1, 0): craft.RIGHT, # Move right (increase x)\n      (0, -1): craft.UP,   # Move up (decrease y)\n      (0, 1): craft.DOWN    # Move down (increase y)\n  }\n  CARDINAL_DIRECTIONS = [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)] # List of (dx, dy) tuples for BFS exploration\n\n  # Determine the type of the primitive to apply correct collection logic.\n  is_grabbable_resource = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop_location = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n\n  # If the primitive is an environmental feature that cannot be picked up or interacted with\n  # (e.g., 'BOUNDARY', 'WATER' if not a target, or static 'WALLS'), return empty list.\n  # Workshops are special non-grabbable locations that *are* traversable and interactable.\n  if primitive_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices and not is_workshop_location:\n    return []\n\n  # 2. Helper function: Checks if a given cell (x, y) is traversable by the agent.\n  def is_traversable(x, y):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the cell at (x, y) is within grid bounds and does not contain\n    any blocking (non-traversable) entities.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Check if coordinates are within the grid boundaries.\n    if not (0 <= x < grid_width and 0 <= y < grid_height):\n      return False\n\n    # Water is typically a blocking entity unless a bridge is used (not handled here).\n    if grid[x, y, env.world.water_index] == 1:\n      return False\n\n    # Check for other non-grabbable entities that block movement.\n    # Workshops are considered traversable for the purpose of moving onto them.\n    kinds_at_cell = np.where(grid[x, y] == 1)[0]\n    for kind_idx_in_cell in kinds_at_cell:\n      if kind_idx_in_cell in env.world.non_grabbable_indices and \\\n         kind_idx_in_cell not in env.world.workshop_indices:\n        return False # This cell contains an unpassable obstacle.\n\n    return True\n\n  # 3. Locate all instances of the target primitive on the current grid.\n  # np.where returns arrays of x and y coordinates where the condition is true.\n  primitive_x_coords, primitive_y_coords = np.where(grid[:, :, primitive_idx] == 1)\n  primitive_locations_on_grid = list(zip(primitive_x_coords, primitive_y_coords))\n\n  if not primitive_locations_on_grid:\n    # The primitive does not exist anywhere on the current map.\n    return []\n\n  # 4. Determine the set of \"target BFS locations\". These are the cells where the\n  #    agent needs to stand to be able to collect the primitive.\n  target_bfs_locations = set()\n\n  if is_grabbable_resource:\n    # For grabbable items (e.g., WOOD, STONE), the agent can collect them if they are\n    # in the 3x3 neighborhood (including the agent's current cell).\n    NEIGHBORHOOD_OFFSETS = [\n        (dx, dy) for dx in [-1, 0, 1] for dy in [-1, 0, 1] # All 9 cells around a primitive instance\n    ]\n    for px, py in primitive_locations_on_grid:\n      for dx_offset, dy_offset in NEIGHBORHOOD_OFFSETS:\n        nx, ny = px + dx_offset, py + dy_offset\n        if is_traversable(nx, ny):\n          target_bfs_locations.add((nx, ny))\n  elif is_workshop_location:\n    # For workshops, the agent must move directly onto the workshop's cell to use it.\n    for wx, wy in primitive_locations_on_grid:\n      if is_traversable(wx, wy):\n        target_bfs_locations.add((wx, wy))\n  # No else needed: non-grabbable/non-workshop items are caught by the early exit.\n\n  if not target_bfs_locations:\n    # No reachable (traversable) locations found from which the primitive can be collected.\n    return []\n\n  # 5. Immediate Collection Check: If the agent is already at a suitable collection spot.\n  if start_pos in target_bfs_locations:\n    if is_grabbable_resource:\n      # If at a grabbable resource's collection spot, just perform the USE action.\n      return [craft.USE]\n    else: # This must be a workshop location.\n      # If at a workshop, no movement is needed by 'collect'. The 'craft' DSL command\n      # will handle the subsequent 'USE' action when crafting.\n      return []\n\n  # 6. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path to any target location.\n  # The queue stores tuples: (current_position (x, y), list_of_actions_to_reach_here).\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])])\n  visited = {start_pos} # Set to keep track of visited (x, y) coordinates to prevent cycles.\n\n  shortest_path_actions = None # Will store the action sequence of the shortest path found.\n\n  while queue:\n    (current_x, current_y), path_so_far = queue.popleft()\n\n    # If the current position is one of our desired target locations, we've found\n    # the shortest path.\n    if (current_x, current_y) in target_bfs_locations:\n      shortest_path_actions = path_so_far\n      break # Exit BFS as the shortest path is found.\n\n    # Explore all four cardinal neighbors (up, down, left, right).\n    for dx, dy in CARDINAL_DIRECTIONS:\n      next_x, next_y = current_x + dx, current_y + dy\n      \n      if (next_x, next_y) not in visited:\n        if is_traversable(next_x, next_y):\n          visited.add((next_x, next_y))\n          # Add the neighbor to the queue with the updated path.\n          queue.append(((next_x, next_y), path_so_far + [ACTION_MAP[(dx, dy)]]))\n\n  if shortest_path_actions is None:\n    # No path could be found from the agent's current position to any target location.\n    return []\n\n  # 7. Construct the final sequence of actions.\n  actions.extend(shortest_path_actions)\n\n  # After moving to the collection spot, if it's a grabbable resource,\n  # a 'USE' action is required to actually pick it up/mine it.\n  if is_grabbable_resource:\n    actions.append(craft.USE)\n\n  return actions", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:03:01.201580", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  ACTION_UP = craft.UP\n  ACTION_DOWN = craft.DOWN\n  ACTION_LEFT = craft.LEFT\n  ACTION_RIGHT = craft.RIGHT\n  ACTION_USE = craft.USE\n\n  # Retrieve the current state from the CraftLab environment\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  # The full grid layout: (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  # Agent's current (x, y) integer position\n  agent_x, agent_y = current_state.pos\n\n  # Get grid dimensions for boundary checks\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Convert the primitive name (string) to its corresponding integer index ID.\n  # The cookbook's index maps names to integer IDs. Use .lower() for robustness.\n  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive.lower()]\n  if primitive_id is None:\n    # If the primitive name is not found, it cannot be collected.\n    return []\n\n  # Get the set of item kinds that are non-grabbable (i.e., obstacles that block movement)\n  impassable_kind_ids = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n  # Get the list of item kinds that can be picked up.\n  grabbable_kind_ids = env.world.grabbable_indices\n\n  # Early exit: If the target primitive is not an item that can be grabbed/collected,\n  # there's no valid sequence of actions to \"collect\" it.\n  if primitive_id not in grabbable_kind_ids:\n    return []\n\n  # --- Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path to the primitive ---\n  # BFS queue: stores tuples of ((x, y) position, [list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here])\n  bfs_queue = collections.deque()\n  # Set to keep track of visited grid cells (x, y) to prevent cycles and redundant exploration\n  visited_cells = set()\n\n  # Initialize BFS by adding the agent's current position to the queue\n  start_position = (agent_x, agent_y)\n  bfs_queue.append((start_position, []))  # (position, path_taken_so_far)\n  visited_cells.add(start_position)\n\n  # Define possible movement directions and their corresponding actions.\n  # Each tuple is (delta_x, delta_y, action_id).\n  # grid[x, y] means x is column, y is row.\n  movement_deltas = [\n      (0, -1, ACTION_UP),    # Move North (decreases y-coordinate)\n      (0, 1, ACTION_DOWN),   # Move South (increases y-coordinate)\n      (-1, 0, ACTION_LEFT),  # Move West (decreases x-coordinate)\n      (1, 0, ACTION_RIGHT)   # Move East (increases x-coordinate)\n  ]\n\n  while bfs_queue:\n    # Dequeue the current position and the path taken to reach it\n    (current_x, current_y), path_actions = bfs_queue.popleft()\n\n    # Check if the desired primitive is located at the current cell.\n    # We assume 'grid' uses a 1-hot encoding where 1 indicates presence of an item.\n    if grid[current_x, current_y, primitive_id] == 1:\n      # If the primitive is found at the current cell, append the USE action\n      # to the path and return the complete sequence. This assumes 'USE' picks up the item\n      # from the cell the agent is currently occupying.\n      return path_actions + [ACTION_USE]\n\n    # Explore all valid neighboring cells from the current position\n    for dx, dy, action_to_move in movement_deltas:\n      next_x, next_y = current_x + dx, current_y + dy  # Calculate neighbor's coordinates\n      next_position = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # 1. Check if the neighbor position is within the grid boundaries\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue\n\n      # 2. Check if the neighbor cell has already been visited in this BFS\n      if next_position in visited_cells:\n        continue\n\n      # 3. Check if the neighbor cell contains any impassable obstacles.\n      # A cell is considered an obstacle if any item within it belongs to the `impassable_kind_ids` set.\n      is_obstacle = False\n      for obstacle_kind_id in impassable_kind_ids:\n        # Check if the impassable item exists at the `next_position`.\n        if grid[next_x, next_y, obstacle_kind_id] == 1:\n          is_obstacle = True\n          break  # Found an obstacle, no need to check further items in this cell\n      \n      if is_obstacle:\n        continue  # Skip this neighbor if it's an obstacle\n\n      # If the neighbor is valid (in bounds, not visited, and traversable),\n      # add it to the queue with the updated path and mark it as visited.\n      visited_cells.add(next_position)\n      bfs_queue.append((next_position, path_actions + [action_to_move]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and the primitive was not found anywhere accessible on the grid,\n  # return an empty list, indicating that it cannot be collected from the current state.\n  return []", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:03:02.309256", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map[\"UP\"]\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map[\"DOWN\"]\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map[\"LEFT\"]\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map[\"RIGHT\"]\n  ACTION_USE = action_map[\"USE\"]\n\n  # Access the current state from the environment\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  grid = current_state.grid  # The full (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds) occupancy grid\n  agent_x, agent_y = current_state.pos  # Agent's current (x, y) integer position\n\n  # Get grid dimensions for boundary checks\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Convert the primitive string name to its integer ID using the cookbook's index.\n  # The .lower() is important as names might be case-sensitive in the index.\n  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive.lower()]\n  if primitive_id is None:\n    # If the primitive name is not recognized or doesn't exist, it cannot be collected.\n    return []\n\n  # Get the sets of impassable (non-grabbable) and grabbable item indices.\n  impassable_kind_ids = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n  grabbable_kind_ids = env.world.grabbable_indices\n\n  # Pre-check: If the requested primitive is not a grabbable item, then it cannot be \"collected\"\n  # in the sense of picking it up. It might be an environment feature (like water, workshop).\n  if primitive_id not in grabbable_kind_ids:\n    return []\n\n  # --- Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path to the primitive ---\n  # The queue will store tuples of ((x, y) position, [list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here])\n  bfs_queue = collections.deque()\n  # A set to keep track of visited (x, y) grid cells to prevent cycles and redundant exploration.\n  visited_cells = set()\n\n  # Initialize BFS from the agent's current position.\n  start_position = (agent_x, agent_y)\n  bfs_queue.append((start_position, []))  # (current_position, path_taken)\n  visited_cells.add(start_position)\n\n  # Define possible movement actions and their corresponding changes in (x, y) coordinates.\n  # (delta_x, delta_y, action_id)\n  movement_actions = [\n      (0, -1, ACTION_UP),    # Move North: y-coordinate decreases\n      (0, 1, ACTION_DOWN),   # Move South: y-coordinate increases\n      (-1, 0, ACTION_LEFT),  # Move West: x-coordinate decreases\n      (1, 0, ACTION_RIGHT)   # Move East: x-coordinate increases\n  ]\n\n  while bfs_queue:\n    # Dequeue the current position and the path taken to reach it.\n    (current_x, current_y), path_so_far = bfs_queue.popleft()\n\n    # Check if the desired primitive is at the current cell.\n    # We assume 'grid' uses a 1-hot encoding where grid[x, y, kind_id] == 1 means presence.\n    if grid[current_x, current_y, primitive_id] == 1:\n      # If the primitive is found at the current cell, append the USE action\n      # and return the complete sequence of actions.\n      return path_so_far + [ACTION_USE]\n\n    # Explore all valid neighboring cells from the current position.\n    for dx, dy, action_to_move in movement_actions:\n      next_x, next_y = current_x + dx, current_y + dy  # Calculate neighbor's coordinates\n      next_position = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # 1. Boundary Check: Ensure the neighbor is within the grid limits.\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue\n\n      # 2. Visited Check: Avoid revisiting cells to prevent infinite loops and find shortest path.\n      if next_position in visited_cells:\n        continue\n\n      # 3. Impassable Check: Determine if the neighbor cell contains any obstacle.\n      # A cell is considered impassable if any item present in it belongs to the `impassable_kind_ids` set.\n      is_impassable = False\n      for impassable_id in impassable_kind_ids:\n        if grid[next_x, next_y, impassable_id] == 1:\n          is_impassable = True\n          break  # Found an obstacle, this cell is blocked.\n      \n      if is_impassable:\n        continue  # Skip this neighbor if it's an obstacle.\n\n      # If the neighbor is valid (in bounds, not visited, and traversable),\n      # add it to the queue with the updated path and mark it as visited.\n      visited_cells.add(next_position)\n      bfs_queue.append((next_position, path_so_far + [action_to_move]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and the primitive was not found in any accessible cell,\n  # return an empty list, indicating that it cannot be collected from the current state.\n  return []", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:04:11.147475", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  if primitive_id is None:\n      # Primitive name not found in cookbook index.\n      return []\n\n  # Check if the primitive is already in the inventory.\n  # If so, no actions are needed to collect it, as it's already \"collected\".\n  current_inventory = env._current_state.inventory\n  if current_inventory[primitive_id] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # Check if the primitive is even grabbable.\n  # If it's not grabbable (e.g., a workshop, water, boundary), it cannot be \"collected\" into inventory.\n  # The 'collect' function implies adding to inventory.\n  if primitive_id in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n      # This primitive cannot be collected.\n      return []\n\n  state = env._current_state\n  current_pos = state.pos  # (x, y) coordinates, where x is column index, y is row index\n  current_dir = state.dir  # Agent's initial facing direction (integer ID)\n  grid = state.grid\n  \n  # Grid dimensions: (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape \n\n  # Get action integer IDs from the environment's action_specs for clarity and robustness\n  actions_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP = actions_map['UP']\n  DOWN = actions_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = actions_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = actions_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = actions_map['USE']\n\n  # Define movement actions and their (dx, dy) deltas.\n  # dx is change in column (x-coordinate), dy is change in row (y-coordinate).\n  # These deltas also correspond to the direction faced after taking the action.\n  # Assuming CraftWorld/CraftLab uses standard (0,0) top-left, y increases downwards.\n  move_deltas = {\n      DOWN: (0, 1),   # (dx, dy) for moving DOWN (y increases)\n      UP: (0, -1),    # (dx, dy) for moving UP (y decreases)\n      LEFT: (-1, 0),  # (dx, dy) for moving LEFT (x decreases)\n      RIGHT: (1, 0)   # (dx, dy) for moving RIGHT (x increases)\n  }\n\n  # BFS setup:\n  # Queue stores tuples: ((current_x, current_y, current_facing_direction_idx), [list_of_actions_to_reach_this_state])\n  # The state includes facing direction because the 'USE' action depends on it.\n  q = collections.deque([((current_pos[0], current_pos[1], current_dir), [])]) \n  \n  # Visited set stores (x, y, facing_direction_idx) tuples to prevent revisiting identical states\n  visited = {(current_pos[0], current_pos[1], current_dir)}\n\n  while q:\n      (cx, cy, cd), path_actions = q.popleft()\n\n      # 1. Check if the current (cx, cy, cd) state allows for immediate collection via a 'USE' action.\n      # The 'USE' action interacts with the cell directly in front of the agent.\n      dx_face, dy_face = move_deltas[cd] # Get delta for the direction the agent is currently facing\n      target_x, target_y = cx + dx_face, cy + dy_face # Coordinates of the cell directly in front\n\n      # Ensure the target cell is within grid boundaries\n      if 0 <= target_x < grid_width and 0 <= target_y < grid_height:\n          # Check if the target cell contains the primitive we want to collect.\n          # `grid[x, y, kind_id] > 0` checks if at least one unit of the primitive is present.\n          if grid[target_x, target_y, primitive_id] > 0:\n              # Path found! Append the 'USE' action and return the complete sequence.\n              return path_actions + [USE]\n\n      # 2. Explore movement neighbors (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT) from the current state.\n      # Each movement action changes the agent's position and sets its new facing direction\n      # to the direction of the movement itself.\n      for move_action in [UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT]:\n          next_dir = move_action # Agent will face the direction it just moved\n          dx_move, dy_move = move_deltas[move_action] # Deltas for the movement itself\n\n          nx, ny = cx + dx_move, cy + dy_move # New x, new y coordinates after movement\n          next_state_tuple = (nx, ny, next_dir) # The new state (position and facing direction)\n\n          # a. Check if the new position (nx, ny) is within grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height):\n              continue # Skip if out of bounds.\n          \n          # b. Check for obstacles: A cell is considered an obstacle if it contains\n          #    any entity that is categorized as non-grabbable (e.g., walls, water, workshops).\n          is_obstacle = False\n          for non_grabbable_id in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n              # An obstacle is present if a non-grabbable item exists at the next cell.\n              if grid[nx, ny, non_grabbable_id] > 0: \n                  is_obstacle = True\n                  break # Found an obstacle, no need to check other non-grabbables for this cell.\n          \n          if is_obstacle:\n              continue # Skip if the path is blocked by an obstacle.\n\n          # c. If the new state (position and facing direction) has not been visited, add it to the queue.\n          if next_state_tuple not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_state_tuple)\n              q.append((next_state_tuple, path_actions + [move_action]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and no path was found to collect the primitive,\n  # return an empty list, indicating it's unreachable or uncollectable.\n  return []", "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:04:12.328900", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index.get(primitive)\n  \n  if primitive_id is None:\n      # Primitive not found in cookbook index.\n      return []\n\n  # Determine if the primitive is grabbable or non-grabbable to apply the correct collection logic.\n  is_grabbable = primitive_id in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  # Non-grabbable includes environmental elements like WATER, STONE, and WORKSHOPS.\n  # For these, 'collect' typically means reaching a location adjacent to them, not picking them up.\n\n  state = env._current_state\n  current_pos = state.pos  # (x, y) where x is column, y is row\n  current_dir = state.dir  # Agent's initial facing direction (0=DOWN, 1=UP, 2=LEFT, 3=RIGHT)\n  grid = state.grid\n  \n  # Grid shape: (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  # WIDTH corresponds to columns (x-axis), HEIGHT corresponds to rows (y-axis).\n  num_cols = grid.shape[0]\n  num_rows = grid.shape[1]\n\n  actions_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP = actions_map['UP']\n  DOWN = actions_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = actions_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = actions_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = actions_map['USE']\n\n  # Map action index (which also corresponds to a direction) to its (dr, dc) delta.\n  # dr = change in row (y), dc = change in col (x).\n  # These deltas represent both the movement if that action is taken, and the direction faced after.\n  direction_deltas = {\n      DOWN: (1, 0),   # Row increases (down), col stays same\n      UP: (-1, 0),   # Row decreases (up), col stays same\n      LEFT: (0, -1),  # Row stays same, col decreases (left)\n      RIGHT: (0, 1)   # Row stays same, col increases (right)\n  }\n\n  # BFS setup:\n  # Queue stores tuples: ((row, col, facing_direction_idx), [list_of_actions_to_reach_this_state])\n  # Convert initial (x, y) pos to (row, col) for BFS state.\n  initial_row, initial_col = current_pos[1], current_pos[0]\n  q = collections.deque([((initial_row, initial_col, current_dir), [])]) \n  \n  # Visited set stores (row, col, facing_direction_idx) tuples to prevent revisiting states\n  visited = {(initial_row, initial_col, current_dir)}\n\n  while q:\n      (r, c, d), path_actions = q.popleft() # r = current row, c = current col\n\n      # 1. Check if the current (r, c, d) state satisfies the goal.\n      if is_grabbable:\n          # For grabbable primitives, the goal is to be positioned such that USE will collect it.\n          # This means the primitive is in the cell directly in front of the agent.\n          dr_face, dc_face = direction_deltas[d] # Get delta for the direction agent is currently facing\n          target_r, target_c = r + dr_face, c + dc_face # Coordinates of the cell directly in front\n\n          # Ensure the target cell is within grid boundaries\n          if 0 <= target_c < num_cols and 0 <= target_r < num_rows:\n              # Check if the target cell contains the grabbable primitive.\n              # Grid is indexed by (column, row, kind).\n              if grid[target_c, target_r, primitive_id] > 0:\n                  return path_actions + [USE] # Path found! Append USE action and return.\n      else: # Non-grabbable primitive (e.g., WATER, STONE, WORKSHOP)\n          # For non-grabbable primitives, the goal is to be adjacent to it (within a 3x3 neighborhood).\n          # This includes the current cell (r,c) if the item can be on the same square as the agent.\n          found_adjacent_non_grabbable = False\n          for dr_n in [-1, 0, 1]:\n              for dc_n in [-1, 0, 1]:\n                  nr_n, nc_n = r + dr_n, c + dc_n # Neighboring cell coordinates\n                  \n                  # Check if the neighboring cell is within grid boundaries\n                  if 0 <= nc_n < num_cols and 0 <= nr_n < num_rows:\n                      # Check if the neighbor cell contains the non-grabbable primitive.\n                      # Grid is indexed by (column, row, kind).\n                      if grid[nc_n, nr_n, primitive_id] > 0:\n                          found_adjacent_non_grabbable = True\n                          break\n              if found_adjacent_non_grabbable:\n                  break\n          \n          if found_adjacent_non_grabbable:\n              # Path found! No USE action for non-grabbable items; just reaching adjacency is enough.\n              return path_actions \n\n      # 2. Explore movement neighbors (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT)\n      # Each movement action changes the agent's position and sets its new facing direction.\n      for move_action in [UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT]:\n          next_dir = move_action # After moving, agent faces the direction it just moved\n          dr_move, dc_move = direction_deltas[move_action] # Delta for the movement itself\n\n          nr, nc = r + dr_move, c + dc_move # New row, new col after movement\n          next_state_tuple = (nr, nc, next_dir) # The new state (position and facing direction)\n\n          # a. Check if the next position (nr, nc) is within grid boundaries\n          if not (0 <= nc < num_cols and 0 <= nr < num_rows):\n              continue\n          \n          # b. Check for obstacles: A cell is considered an obstacle if it contains\n          #    any entity that is categorized as non-grabbable (impassable terrain/structures).\n          is_obstacle = False\n          for non_grabbable_id in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n              # Grid is indexed by (column, row, kind).\n              if grid[nc, nr, non_grabbable_id] > 0: \n                  is_obstacle = True\n                  break\n          \n          if is_obstacle:\n              continue # Cannot move to this cell as it's blocked by an obstacle.\n\n          # c. If the new state (position and facing direction) has not been visited, add it to the queue\n          if next_state_tuple not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_state_tuple)\n              q.append((next_state_tuple, path_actions + [move_action]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and the primitive was not found anywhere reachable or collectable,\n  # return an empty list, indicating no path was found.\n  return []", "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:05:05.938698", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  world = env.world\n  cookbook = world.cookbook\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  \n  # 1. Obtain the integer index for the target primitive.\n  # The `cookbook.index.index()` method ensures a robust lookup.\n  i_primitive = cookbook.index.index(primitive) \n\n  # 2. Early exit: Check if the primitive is already in the agent's inventory.\n  # If it is, there's no need to collect it again.\n  if current_state.inventory[i_primitive] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # 3. Early exit: Verify if the primitive is actually a grabbable item.\n  # Some \"primitives\" in the DSL (e.g., \"WATER\", \"WORKSHOP0\") are non-grabbable\n  # entities and cannot be picked up into inventory. If the target is non-grabbable,\n  # no collection path is possible.\n  if i_primitive not in world.grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  # Define indices of entities that block movement (impassable obstacles).\n  # This set includes all non-grabbable items that act as physical barriers.\n  impassable_obstacle_indices = world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # Agent's current (x, y) position on the grid.\n  start_pos = current_state.pos \n  \n  # Grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT). The third dimension is n_kinds.\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape \n\n  # Mapping of movement actions to their corresponding (delta_x, delta_y) changes.\n  # This facilitates navigation through the grid.\n  move_actions_to_deltas = {\n      craft.UP: (0, -1),   # Moving UP decreases the Y-coordinate.\n      craft.DOWN: (0, 1),    # Moving DOWN increases the Y-coordinate.\n      craft.LEFT: (-1, 0),   # Moving LEFT decreases the X-coordinate.\n      craft.RIGHT: (1, 0)    # Moving RIGHT increases the X-coordinate.\n  }\n  \n  # Initialize BFS queue: (current_position (x,y), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here).\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])])\n  # Initialize set of visited positions to prevent cycles and ensure the shortest path.\n  visited = {start_pos}\n\n  # BFS loop: Continues as long as there are positions to explore.\n  while queue:\n    curr_pos, path_to_curr_pos = queue.popleft() # Dequeue the current position and its path.\n    curr_x, curr_y = curr_pos\n\n    # Check if the target primitive is within the 3x3 neighborhood of the current position.\n    # This aligns with the `CraftState.next_to()` logic, meaning the agent can interact.\n    is_primitive_adjacent = False\n    for dx_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        adj_x, adj_y = curr_x + dx_adj, curr_y + dy_adj\n\n        # Ensure the adjacent cell is within grid boundaries.\n        if 0 <= adj_x < grid_width and 0 <= adj_y < grid_height:\n          # Check if the primitive exists at this adjacent cell (count > 0).\n          if grid[adj_x, adj_y, i_primitive] > 0:\n            is_primitive_adjacent = True\n            break # Primitive found adjacent, no need to check other cells in 3x3.\n      if is_primitive_adjacent:\n        break # Break from outer loop too.\n\n    # If the primitive is found adjacent to the current position, the path is complete.\n    if is_primitive_adjacent:\n      # Append the 'USE' action, which collects the primitive.\n      return path_to_curr_pos + [craft.USE]\n\n    # Explore valid cardinal neighbors (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT) for movement.\n    for action_move, (dx_move, dy_move) in move_actions_to_deltas.items():\n      next_x, next_y = curr_x + dx_move, curr_y + dy_move\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # 1. Bounds Check: Ensure the potential next position is within grid limits.\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue\n\n      # 2. Visited Check: Avoid revisiting positions already explored to guarantee shortest path.\n      if next_pos in visited:\n        continue\n\n      # 3. Traversability Check: Ensure the next position does not contain any impassable obstacles.\n      # This checks if any of the obstacle kinds are present at the next cell.\n      is_next_pos_an_obstacle = False\n      for obstacle_idx in impassable_obstacle_indices:\n        if grid[next_x, next_y, obstacle_idx] > 0:\n          is_next_pos_an_obstacle = True\n          break # Found an obstacle, this move is invalid.\n      if is_next_pos_an_obstacle:\n        continue # Cannot move into an obstacle cell.\n\n      # If all checks pass, the 'next_pos' is a valid, unvisited, and traversable cell.\n      # Add it to the queue for further exploration and mark it as visited.\n      visited.add(next_pos)\n      queue.append((next_pos, path_to_curr_pos + [action_move]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and the queue is empty, it means no path to an adjacent primitive was found.\n  return []", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:05:07.136461", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  world = env.world\n  cookbook = world.cookbook\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  \n  # 1. Get the integer index for the primitive from the cookbook's index.\n  # This ensures we work with the unique integer ID for the primitive name.\n  i_primitive = cookbook.index.index(primitive) \n\n  # 2. Check if the primitive is already in the agent's inventory.\n  # If the agent already possesses the primitive, no collection actions are needed.\n  if current_state.inventory[i_primitive] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # 3. Ensure the requested primitive is actually grabbable.\n  # Non-grabbable entities (e.g., WORKSHOP, WATER, BOUNDARY) cannot be \"collected\" into inventory.\n  # If the primitive is not in the list of grabbable indices, return an empty list.\n  if i_primitive not in world.grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  # Retrieve the set of indices for entities that block movement (impassable terrain/obstacles).\n  # These are used to determine which grid cells the agent can traverse.\n  impassable_indices = world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # Define the possible movement actions (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT) and their corresponding\n  # (delta_x, delta_y) changes to the agent's position on the grid.\n  # The grid has dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds), where x corresponds to WIDTH, y to HEIGHT.\n  move_actions_and_deltas = [\n      (craft.UP, (0, -1)),   # Action: UP, Delta: y decreases\n      (craft.DOWN, (0, 1)),    # Action: DOWN, Delta: y increases\n      (craft.LEFT, (-1, 0)),   # Action: LEFT, Delta: x decreases\n      (craft.RIGHT, (1, 0))    # Action: RIGHT, Delta: x increases\n  ]\n  \n  start_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's current (x, y) position on the grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape # Unpack grid dimensions\n\n  # Initialize Breadth-First Search (BFS) for pathfinding.\n  # The queue stores tuples: ((current_x, current_y), list_of_actions_to_reach_here).\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])])\n  # The 'visited' set keeps track of positions already explored to avoid cycles and redundant paths,\n  # ensuring the shortest path is found.\n  visited = {start_pos}\n\n  # Begin BFS\n  while queue:\n    (curr_x, curr_y), path = queue.popleft() # Get the current position and the path to it\n\n    # Check if the target primitive is within the 3x3 neighborhood of the current position.\n    # This simulates the `CraftState.next_to()` functionality.\n    is_primitive_adjacent = False\n    for dx_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        nx_adj, ny_adj = curr_x + dx_adj, curr_y + dy_adj\n\n        # Ensure the adjacent cell being checked is within the grid boundaries.\n        if 0 <= nx_adj < grid_width and 0 <= ny_adj < grid_height:\n          # If the primitive is present in this adjacent cell (its count is > 0),\n          # then we've found a position from which the agent can \"use\" to collect it.\n          if grid[nx_adj, ny_adj, i_primitive] > 0:\n            is_primitive_adjacent = True\n            break # Found, no need to check further adjacent cells for this (curr_x, curr_y)\n      if is_primitive_adjacent:\n        break # Found, break out of the outer loop too\n\n    # If the primitive is adjacent to the current position, a path has been found.\n    # The final action needed is 'USE' to collect the primitive.\n    if is_primitive_adjacent:\n      return path + [craft.USE]\n\n    # If the primitive is not yet adjacent, explore valid neighboring cells for movement.\n    for action, (dx_move, dy_move) in move_actions_and_deltas:\n      next_x, next_y = curr_x + dx_move, curr_y + dy_move\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # 1. Bounds Check: Ensure the potential next position is within the grid.\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue\n\n      # 2. Visited Check: Avoid re-processing positions that have already been visited\n      # to ensure the shortest path.\n      if next_pos in visited:\n        continue\n\n      # 3. Traversability Check: Ensure the potential next position is not an obstacle.\n      # A cell is considered an obstacle if it contains any non-grabbable item.\n      is_obstacle = False\n      for obstacle_idx in impassable_indices:\n        if grid[next_x, next_y, obstacle_idx] > 0:\n          is_obstacle = True\n          break\n      if is_obstacle:\n        continue # Cannot move into an obstacle cell\n\n      # If all checks pass, the next_pos is a valid and unvisited cell to move to.\n      # Add it to the visited set and enqueue it with the updated path.\n      visited.add(next_pos)\n      queue.append((next_pos, path + [action]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and the queue becomes empty without finding a path to the primitive,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable or not present on the traversable grid.\n  return []", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:06:04.802699", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions_list = []\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  \n  # Extract immutable state information from the current environment state for planning.\n  # This includes the initial layout of the grid, agent's starting position, and direction.\n  initial_grid = current_state.grid\n  initial_pos = current_state.pos  # Agent's initial position (row, col)\n  initial_dir = current_state.dir  # Agent's initial facing direction (0:RIGHT, 1:UP, 2:LEFT, 3:DOWN)\n\n  # Get the integer ID (index) for the target primitive from the cookbook's internal index.\n  # This ID is used to locate the primitive on the grid.\n  primitive_id = current_state.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  # Get grid dimensions to perform boundary checks for agent movement.\n  num_rows, num_cols, _ = initial_grid.shape\n\n  # Retrieve the integer action codes from the environment's action specifications.\n  # These are standard actions available to the agent.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION = action_map['UP']    # In CraftWorld, 'UP' signifies moving forward in the current direction.\n  TURN_LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']     # Turn agent 90 degrees counter-clockwise.\n  TURN_RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']   # Turn agent 90 degrees clockwise.\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']            # Interact with the entity in the cell directly in front.\n\n  # Define direction vectors: Mapping agent's direction (0-3) to a (delta_row, delta_column) tuple.\n  # This tuple indicates the change in coordinates for the cell directly in front of the agent.\n  DIR_TO_DRDC = {\n      0: (0, 1),   # Facing RIGHT: moves to (row, col + 1)\n      1: (-1, 0),  # Facing UP: moves to (row - 1, col)\n      2: (0, -1),  # Facing LEFT: moves to (row, col - 1)\n      3: (1, 0)    # Facing DOWN: moves to (row + 1, col)\n  }\n\n  # Define direction mapping for turns: Current direction to new direction after a turn.\n  TURN_LEFT_MAP = {0: 1, 1: 2, 2: 3, 3: 0}  # e.g., RIGHT (0) -> UP (1)\n  TURN_RIGHT_MAP = {0: 3, 1: 0, 2: 1, 3: 2} # e.g., RIGHT (0) -> DOWN (3)\n\n  # Get indices of entities that are non-grabbable and impassable (e.g., boundary walls, water).\n  # The agent cannot move into cells occupied by these entities.\n  non_walkable_kinds_indices = current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # Helper function to determine if a given grid cell (r, c) is a valid and walkable position for the agent.\n  def _is_valid_and_walkable(r: int, c: int) -> bool:\n      # 1. Check if the coordinates are within the grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= r < num_rows and 0 <= c < num_cols):\n          return False\n      \n      # 2. Check if the cell contains any non-walkable entities.\n      # The agent cannot traverse through these obstacles.\n      for kind_idx in non_walkable_kinds_indices:\n          if initial_grid[r, c, kind_idx] > 0:\n              return False\n      \n      # 3. Importantly, the agent cannot walk *onto* the primitive it intends to collect.\n      # Collection occurs when adjacent and using the 'USE' action.\n      if initial_grid[r, c, primitive_id] > 0:\n          return False\n      \n      # If all checks pass, the cell is valid and walkable.\n      return True\n\n  # Initialize Breadth-First Search (BFS):\n  # The queue stores tuples: ((current_position_tuple, current_direction_int), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_this_state).\n  # This represents a unique state of the agent (where it is and where it's facing) and the path taken to get there.\n  queue = collections.deque([((initial_pos, initial_dir), [])])\n  \n  # The 'visited' set keeps track of all (position, direction) states already explored.\n  # This prevents redundant exploration and ensures finding the shortest path by avoiding cycles.\n  visited = {(initial_pos, initial_dir)}\n\n  target_path = None # This variable will store the action sequence once a path to the target is found.\n\n  # Start BFS traversal to find the shortest path to the primitive.\n  while queue:\n      (current_pos, current_dir), path_actions = queue.popleft()\n      r, c = current_pos # Unpack current row and column.\n\n      # Check if the target primitive is directly in front of the agent from the current state.\n      # This is the goal condition: being positioned to interact with the primitive.\n      front_dr, front_dc = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n      front_r, front_c = r + front_dr, c + front_dc\n      \n      # Ensure the cell directly in front is within grid boundaries before checking its contents.\n      if (0 <= front_r < num_rows and 0 <= front_c < num_cols):\n          # If the primitive is present in the cell immediately in front, we have found our path.\n          if initial_grid[front_r, front_c, primitive_id] > 0:\n              target_path = path_actions # Store the sequence of actions that led to this state.\n              break # Path found, exit BFS loop.\n\n      # Explore all possible next actions (Move Forward, Turn Left, Turn Right) from the current state.\n\n      # --- 1. Try Move Forward Action ---\n      # Calculate the next position if the agent moves forward. The direction remains unchanged.\n      move_dr, move_dc = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n      next_r, next_c = r + move_dr, c + move_dc\n      next_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n      next_dir = current_dir # Moving forward does not change orientation.\n\n      # Check if the calculated next position is valid and walkable, and if this new state (pos, dir)\n      # has not been visited yet.\n      if _is_valid_and_walkable(next_r, next_c) and\\\n         (next_pos, next_dir) not in visited:\n          visited.add((next_pos, next_dir)) # Mark as visited.\n          # Add the new state and the extended path to the queue for further exploration.\n          queue.append(((next_pos, next_dir), path_actions + [MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION]))\n\n      # --- 2. Try Turn Left Action ---\n      # Calculate the new direction after turning left. Position remains unchanged.\n      next_dir_left = TURN_LEFT_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Check if this new state (same position, new direction) has not been visited.\n      if ((current_pos, next_dir_left) not in visited):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_left)) # Mark as visited.\n          # Add the new state and extended path to the queue.\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_left), path_actions + [TURN_LEFT_ACTION]))\n\n      # --- 3. Try Turn Right Action ---\n      # Calculate the new direction after turning right. Position remains unchanged.\n      next_dir_right = TURN_RIGHT_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Check if this new state has not been visited.\n      if ((current_pos, next_dir_right) not in visited):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_right)) # Mark as visited.\n          # Add the new state and extended path to the queue.\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_right), path_actions + [TURN_RIGHT_ACTION]))\n\n  # After the BFS completes:\n  # If a path to the target state (agent adjacent and facing the primitive) was found,\n  # append the final 'USE' action to the discovered path. This completes the collection sequence.\n  # If no path was found (target_path remains None), an empty list is returned,\n  # indicating that the primitive is unreachable from the current state.\n  if target_path is not None:\n      actions_list.extend(target_path)\n      actions_list.append(USE_ACTION)\n\n  return actions_list", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:06:06.096268", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1` using Breadth-First Search (BFS) for pathfinding.\n\n    This function finds the shortest sequence of actions to move the agent adjacent to\n    the specified primitive and then perform a 'USE' action to collect it.\n    It considers agent position and orientation as part of the search state.\n    \n    Args:\n        env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab object representing the current simulation environment.\n        primitive (str): The string name of the primitive item to collect (e.g., \"WOOD\", \"STONE\").\n\n    Returns:\n        List[int]: A sequence of integer action IDs (MOVE_FORWARD, TURN_LEFT, TURN_RIGHT, USE)\n                   to execute. Returns an empty list if the primitive is unreachable.\n  \"\"\"\n  actions_list = []\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  \n  # Extract immutable initial state information for BFS planning\n  initial_grid = current_state.grid\n  initial_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's starting (row, col) position\n  initial_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's starting facing direction (0:RIGHT, 1:UP, 2:LEFT, 3:DOWN)\n\n  # Get the integer ID for the target primitive from the world's cookbook index.\n  # This ID is used to identify the primitive on the grid.\n  primitive_id = current_state.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  # Determine grid dimensions for boundary checks during pathfinding\n  num_rows, num_cols, _ = initial_grid.shape\n\n  # Retrieve numerical action IDs from the environment's action specifications.\n  # These mappings are constant for the CraftWorld environment.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION = action_map['UP']    # In CraftWorld, 'UP' action moves agent forward\n  TURN_LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']     # Turns agent 90 degrees left\n  TURN_RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']   # Turns agent 90 degrees right\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']            # Interacts with the cell directly in front\n\n  # Direction vectors mapping agent's orientation (0-3) to (delta_row, delta_column)\n  # This indicates the change in coordinates when moving \"forward\" or determining the \"front\" cell.\n  DIR_TO_DRDC = {\n      0: (0, 1),   # Facing RIGHT: (row, col+1)\n      1: (-1, 0),  # Facing UP: (row-1, col)\n      2: (0, -1),  # Facing LEFT: (row, col-1)\n      3: (1, 0)    # Facing DOWN: (row+1, col)\n  }\n\n  # Maps current direction to the new direction after a turn (left or right).\n  TURN_LEFT_MAP = {0: 1, 1: 2, 2: 3, 3: 0}  # Cycle: RIGHT -> UP -> LEFT -> DOWN -> RIGHT\n  TURN_RIGHT_MAP = {0: 3, 1: 0, 2: 1, 3: 2} # Cycle: RIGHT -> DOWN -> LEFT -> UP -> RIGHT\n\n  # Get a set of integer indices for entities that block agent movement.\n  # These are entities the agent cannot walk onto (e.g., boundaries, water, some workshops).\n  non_walkable_kinds_indices = current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # Helper function to determine if a given grid cell (r, c) is a valid and walkable location for the agent.\n  # A cell is walkable if it's within bounds and does not contain any impassable entities.\n  def _is_valid_and_walkable(r: int, c: int) -> bool:\n      # Check if coordinates are within the grid boundaries\n      if not (0 <= r < num_rows and 0 <= c < num_cols):\n          return False\n      \n      # Check if the cell contains any non-walkable entity (e.g., BOUNDARY, WATER, WORKSHOP_X).\n      # If any such entity is present, the cell is not walkable.\n      if any(initial_grid[r, c, kind_idx] > 0 for kind_idx in non_walkable_kinds_indices):\n          return False\n      \n      # The agent cannot walk directly onto the primitive itself to collect it.\n      # Collection requires being adjacent and using the 'USE' action.\n      if initial_grid[r, c, primitive_id] > 0:\n          return False\n      \n      return True\n\n  # Initialize BFS:\n  # The queue stores tuples: ((agent_position_tuple, agent_direction_int), list_of_actions_taken_so_far).\n  # This represents a 'state' (position and orientation) and the 'path' to reach it.\n  queue = collections.deque([((initial_pos, initial_dir), [])])\n  \n  # The 'visited' set stores (position_tuple, direction_int) to keep track of explored states.\n  # This prevents redundant exploration and ensures finding the shortest path by avoiding cycles.\n  visited = {(initial_pos, initial_dir)}\n\n  target_path_to_adjacent = None # This will store the action sequence to reach the state where the primitive is directly in front.\n\n  # Begin Breadth-First Search\n  while queue:\n      (current_pos, current_dir), path_actions = queue.popleft()\n      r, c = current_pos # Unpack current row and column\n\n      # 1. Check if the current state is a \"goal state\" for pathfinding:\n      #    Is the target primitive located in the cell directly in front of the agent?\n      front_dr, front_dc = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir] # Get direction vector for \"forward\"\n      front_r, front_c = r + front_dr, c + front_dc # Calculate coordinates of the cell in front\n      \n      # Ensure the 'front' cell is within grid boundaries before checking its contents.\n      if (0 <= front_r < num_rows and 0 <= front_c < num_cols):\n          # If the primitive is found in the cell in front, we have successfully found a path\n          # that positions the agent to collect it.\n          if initial_grid[front_r, front_c, primitive_id] > 0:\n              target_path_to_adjacent = path_actions\n              break # Goal reached! Terminate BFS.\n\n      # 2. Explore all possible valid actions from the current state (Move Forward, Turn Left, Turn Right)\n\n      # --- Try Move Forward Action ---\n      # Calculate the next position if the agent moves forward (direction remains unchanged).\n      move_dr, move_dc = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n      next_r, next_c = r + move_dr, c + move_dc\n      next_pos_move = (next_r, next_c)\n      next_dir_move = current_dir \n\n      # Check if the potential new position is valid and walkable, and if this specific\n      # (position, direction) state has not been visited yet.\n      if _is_valid_and_walkable(next_r, next_c) and\\\n         (next_pos_move, next_dir_move) not in visited:\n          visited.add(next_pos_move, next_dir_move) # Mark new state as visited\n          queue.append(((next_pos_move, next_dir_move), path_actions + [MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION])) # Add to queue\n\n      # --- Try Turn Left Action ---\n      # Calculate the new direction after turning left (position remains unchanged).\n      next_dir_left = TURN_LEFT_MAP[current_dir]\n      next_state_turn_left = (current_pos, next_dir_left) # State only changes direction\n\n      # If this turning state has not been visited, add it to the queue.\n      if next_state_turn_left not in visited:\n          visited.add(next_state_turn_left)\n          queue.append((next_state_turn_left, path_actions + [TURN_LEFT_ACTION]))\n\n      # --- Try Turn Right Action ---\n      # Calculate the new direction after turning right (position remains unchanged).\n      next_dir_right = TURN_RIGHT_MAP[current_dir]\n      next_state_turn_right = (current_pos, next_dir_right) # State only changes direction\n\n      # If this turning state has not been visited, add it to the queue.\n      if next_state_turn_right not in visited:\n          visited.add(next_state_turn_right)\n          queue.append((next_state_turn_right, path_actions + [TURN_RIGHT_ACTION]))\n\n  # After BFS completes:\n  # If a path to the target (being adjacent to and facing the primitive) was found,\n  # append the final 'USE' action to the found path to complete the collection.\n  # If no path was found (target_path_to_adjacent remains None), an empty list is returned,\n  # indicating the primitive is unreachable from the current state.\n  if target_path_to_adjacent is not None:\n      actions_list.extend(target_path_to_adjacent)\n      actions_list.append(USE_ACTION)\n\n  return actions_list", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:07:08.667322", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  # If the primitive name is not found in the cookbook's index, it cannot be collected.\n  if primitive_id is None:\n      return []\n\n  state = env._current_state\n  current_pos = state.pos\n  current_dir = state.dir # Initial facing direction\n  grid = state.grid\n  \n  # Grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  width, height, _ = grid.shape \n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment\n  actions_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP = actions_map['UP']\n  DOWN = actions_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = actions_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = actions_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = actions_map['USE']\n\n  # Map direction index (which is also the action index for movement) to its (dr, dc) delta.\n  # These deltas represent both the movement taken by the action and the direction the agent faces after the action.\n  direction_deltas_map = {\n      DOWN: (1, 0),\n      UP: (-1, 0),\n      LEFT: (0, -1),\n      RIGHT: (0, 1)\n  }\n\n  # Determine if the primitive is grabbable (e.g., WOOD, STONE) or non-grabbable (e.g., WORKSHOP, WATER).\n  # This distinction affects how the 'USE' action is interpreted.\n  is_grabbable_target = primitive_id in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_non_grabbable_target = primitive_id in env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # BFS setup:\n  # Queue stores tuples: ((row, col, facing_direction_idx), [list_of_actions_to_reach_this_state])\n  q = collections.deque([((current_pos[0], current_pos[1], current_dir), [])]) \n  \n  # Visited set stores (row, col, facing_direction_idx) tuples to prevent revisiting states\n  visited = {(current_pos[0], current_pos[1], current_dir)}\n\n  while q:\n      (r, c, d), path_actions = q.popleft()\n\n      # Goal Check: Determine if the primitive can be collected from the current state (r, c, d).\n      if is_grabbable_target:\n          # If the primitive is grabbable (e.g., Wood, Stone), it's typically collected by\n          # moving onto its cell and then performing the 'USE' action while on that cell.\n          if grid[r, c, primitive_id] > 0:\n              return path_actions + [USE]\n      elif is_non_grabbable_target:\n          # If the primitive is non-grabbable (e.g., Workshop, Water), it's typically collected/interacted with\n          # by moving adjacent to it, facing it, and then performing the 'USE' action.\n          dr_face, dc_face = direction_deltas_map[d] # Get delta for the direction agent is currently facing\n          target_r, target_c = r + dr_face, c + dc_face # Coordinates of the cell directly in front\n\n          # Check if the cell in front is within grid boundaries and contains the primitive\n          if 0 <= target_r < width and 0 <= target_c < height:\n              if grid[target_r, target_c, primitive_id] > 0:\n                  return path_actions + [USE] # Path found! Append USE action.\n\n      # Explore movement neighbors (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT)\n      # Each movement action not only changes the agent's position but also sets its facing direction.\n      for move_action in [UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT]:\n          next_dir_idx = move_action # After moving, agent faces the direction it just moved\n          dr_move, dc_move = direction_deltas_map[move_action] # Delta for the movement itself\n\n          nr, nc = r + dr_move, c + dc_move # New row, new col after movement\n          next_state_tuple = (nr, nc, next_dir_idx) # The new state (position and facing direction)\n\n          # 1. Check if the next position (nr, nc) is within grid boundaries\n          if not (0 <= nr < width and 0 <= nc < height):\n              continue\n          \n          # 2. Obstacle Check:\n          # A cell is considered an obstacle if it contains any non-grabbable entity (from cookbook.environment).\n          # These entities (like WATER, BOUNDARY, WORKSHOPS) are typically impassable terrain.\n          is_obstacle = False\n          for env_item_id in env.world.cookbook.environment:\n              if grid[nr, nc, env_item_id] > 0:\n                  is_obstacle = True # Found an impassable obstacle\n                  break\n          \n          # Special exception for grabbable targets:\n          # If the target primitive is grabbable, we *are* allowed to step onto its cell to collect it.\n          # So, if an obstacle was initially detected, but it *is* the grabbable primitive itself,\n          # then it's not an obstacle for movement in this specific case.\n          if is_obstacle and is_grabbable_target and grid[nr, nc, primitive_id] > 0:\n              is_obstacle = False \n\n          if is_obstacle:\n              continue\n\n          # 3. If the new state (position and facing direction) has not been visited, add it to the queue\n          if next_state_tuple not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_state_tuple)\n              q.append((next_state_tuple, path_actions + [move_action]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and the primitive was not found anywhere reachable or collectable\n  return []", "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:07:09.792180", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  if primitive_id is None:\n      return []\n\n  state = env._current_state\n  current_pos = state.pos\n  current_dir = state.dir # Initial facing direction\n  grid = state.grid\n  \n  width, height, _ = grid.shape \n\n  actions_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP = actions_map['UP']\n  DOWN = actions_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = actions_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = actions_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = actions_map['USE']\n\n  # Map direction index (which is also the action index for movement) to its (dr, dc) delta.\n  # These deltas represent both the movement taken by the action and the direction the agent faces after the action.\n  direction_deltas_map = {\n      DOWN: (1, 0),\n      UP: (-1, 0),\n      LEFT: (0, -1),\n      RIGHT: (0, 1)\n  }\n\n  # BFS setup:\n  # Queue stores tuples: ((row, col, facing_direction_idx), [list_of_actions_to_reach_this_state])\n  # Each state includes the agent's position and its current facing direction.\n  q = collections.deque([((current_pos[0], current_pos[1], current_dir), [])]) \n  \n  # Visited set stores (row, col, facing_direction_idx) tuples to prevent revisiting states\n  visited = {(current_pos[0], current_pos[1], current_dir)}\n\n  while q:\n      (r, c, d), path_actions = q.popleft()\n\n      # Goal Check: Can we collect the primitive from the current (r, c, d) state?\n      # The USE action interacts with the cell directly in front of the agent.\n      dr_face, dc_face = direction_deltas_map[d] # Get delta for the direction agent is currently facing\n      target_r, target_c = r + dr_face, c + dc_face # Coordinates of the cell directly in front\n\n      # Check if the target cell is within grid boundaries\n      if 0 <= target_r < width and 0 <= target_c < height:\n          # Check if the target cell contains the primitive we want to collect\n          if grid[target_r, target_c, primitive_id] > 0:\n              return path_actions + [USE] # Path found! Append USE action to collect it.\n\n      # Explore movement neighbors (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT)\n      # Each movement action not only changes the agent's position but also sets its facing direction.\n      for move_action in [UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT]:\n          next_dir_idx = move_action # After moving, agent faces the direction it just moved\n          dr_move, dc_move = direction_deltas_map[move_action] # Delta for the movement itself\n\n          nr, nc = r + dr_move, c + dc_move # New row, new col after movement\n          next_state_tuple = (nr, nc, next_dir_idx) # The new state (position and facing direction)\n\n          # 1. Check if the next position (nr, nc) is within grid boundaries\n          if not (0 <= nr < width and 0 <= nc < height):\n              continue\n          \n          # 2. Obstacle Check:\n          # A cell is considered an obstacle (impassable) if it contains ANY item from `non_grabbable_indices`.\n          # This includes items like WATER, WORKSHOPs, BOUNDARY, which cannot be moved onto.\n          is_obstacle = False\n          for non_grabbable_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n              if grid[nr, nc, non_grabbable_idx] > 0:\n                  is_obstacle = True\n                  break # Found an impassable obstacle\n          \n          if is_obstacle:\n              continue # Cannot move to this cell because it's an obstacle\n\n          # 3. If the new state (position and facing direction) has not been visited, add it to the queue\n          if next_state_tuple not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_state_tuple)\n              q.append((next_state_tuple, path_actions + [move_action]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and the primitive was not found anywhere reachable or collectable\n  return []", "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:08:39.329503", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    current_state = env._current_state\n    world = env.world\n    action_map = env.action_specs()\n\n    # 1. Get the primitive's integer ID from the cookbook\n    try:\n        i_kind = world.cookbook.index[primitive.lower()]\n    except KeyError:\n        # Primitive name not found in the cookbook, so it cannot be collected.\n        return []\n\n    # 2. Determine if this primitive requires a 'USE' action to be collected.\n    # CraftWorld logic implies 'grabbable' items (like WOOD, IRON) and specific resources (WATER, STONE)\n    # are collected via 'USE'. Other \"primitives\" (like WORKSHOPs, BOUNDARY) are not typically \"collected\"\n    # into inventory by a 'USE' action in the same way.\n    requires_use_action = (\n        i_kind in world.grabbable_indices or \n        i_kind == world.water_index or \n        i_kind == world.stone_index\n    )\n    \n    # If the primitive is NOT something that can be collected via 'USE' (e.g., a workshop),\n    # this function, designed for collection, should return an empty list.\n    # This aligns with the semantic meaning of \"collect\" in the DSL.\n    if not requires_use_action:\n        return []\n\n    # 3. Check if the primitive is already in the agent's inventory.\n    # If it is, no actions are needed to \"collect\" it.\n    if current_state.inventory[i_kind] > 0:\n        return []\n\n    # 4. Define action integers and direction deltas\n    UP_ACT = action_map[\"UP\"]\n    DOWN_ACT = action_map[\"DOWN\"]\n    LEFT_ACT = action_map[\"LEFT\"]\n    RIGHT_ACT = action_map[\"RIGHT\"]\n    USE_ACT = action_map[\"USE\"]\n\n    move_actions = [UP_ACT, DOWN_ACT, LEFT_ACT, RIGHT_ACT]\n\n    # Map CraftState.dir (0=UP, 1=RIGHT, 2=DOWN, 3=LEFT) to (dr, dc) of the cell directly in front\n    _DIR_TO_DELTA_FRONT = {\n        0: (-1, 0), # UP: row - 1, col\n        1: (0, 1),  # RIGHT: row, col + 1\n        2: (1, 0),  # DOWN: row + 1, col\n        3: (0, -1)  # LEFT: row, col - 1\n    }\n\n    # Helper function to calculate the shortest sequence of turning actions\n    def _get_turning_actions(current_dir: int, target_dir: int) -> list[int]:\n        if current_dir == target_dir:\n            return []\n        \n        # Calculate the difference in directions (modulo 4 for circularity)\n        # Adding 4 ensures positive result for modulo with negative differences.\n        diff = (target_dir - current_dir + 4) % 4\n        \n        if diff == 1: # Target is one step clockwise (e.g., UP -> RIGHT)\n            return [RIGHT_ACT]\n        elif diff == 3: # Target is one step counter-clockwise (e.g., UP -> LEFT)\n            return [LEFT_ACT]\n        else: # diff == 2, 180-degree turn (e.g., UP -> DOWN)\n            return [RIGHT_ACT, RIGHT_ACT] # Two consecutive right turns (or two left)\n\n    # BFS setup\n    # Queue stores (state_key, CraftState object). state_key is (row, column, direction).\n    q = collections.deque()\n    \n    # Visited set stores (position_r, position_c, direction) to avoid cycles and redundant work.\n    visited = set()\n    \n    # parent_info maps state_key -> (parent_state_key, action_from_parent_to_current_state)\n    parent_info = {} \n\n    # Initial state setup\n    initial_state_key = (current_state.pos[0], current_state.pos[1], current_state.dir)\n    q.append((initial_state_key, current_state))\n    visited.add(initial_state_key)\n    parent_info[initial_state_key] = (None, None) # The root state has no parent\n\n    grid_width, grid_height, _ = current_state.grid.shape\n    # Maximum states to explore to prevent infinite loops or excessively long searches.\n    # Total unique (pos, dir) states is grid_width * grid_height * 4.\n    # A multiplier (e.g., 4) provides robustness for complex environments.\n    MAX_EXPLORED_STATES = grid_width * grid_height * 4 * 4 \n\n    explored_states_count = 0\n\n    while q:\n        state_key, state = q.popleft()\n        explored_states_count += 1\n\n        # Pruning: If we've explored too many distinct states, stop exploring this path\n        # to prevent excessively long computation times for very complex or impossible goals.\n        if explored_states_count > MAX_EXPLORED_STATES:\n            continue \n\n        current_r, current_c, current_dir = state_key # Unpack for convenience\n\n        # Check if we can collect the primitive from this state by turning and using.\n        # CraftState.next_to(i_kind) checks if the primitive is in the 3x3 neighborhood.\n        # This is a coarse filter to avoid iterating through directions if the primitive isn't even nearby.\n        if state.next_to(i_kind):\n            # If nearby, iterate through all 4 possible directions the agent could *turn to face*.\n            for target_dir in range(4): \n                dr, dc = _DIR_TO_DELTA_FRONT[target_dir]\n                facing_r, facing_c = current_r + dr, current_c + dc\n\n                # Check if the calculated facing cell is within grid bounds\n                # AND if it contains the desired primitive.\n                if (0 <= facing_r < grid_width and 0 <= facing_c < grid_height and \n                    state.grid[facing_r, facing_c, i_kind] == 1):\n                    \n                    # Primitive found directly in front!\n                    # Reconstruct the path from the initial state to the current `state_key`.\n                    # Path is built in reverse, so it needs to be reversed at the end.\n                    path_to_current_state = []\n                    curr_reconstruct_key = state_key\n                    while parent_info[curr_reconstruct_key][0] is not None:\n                        parent_key, action_from_parent = parent_info[curr_reconstruct_key]\n                        path_to_current_state.append(action_from_parent)\n                        curr_reconstruct_key = parent_key\n                    path_to_current_state.reverse() \n\n                    # Calculate actions to turn from current direction to target_dir.\n                    turns = _get_turning_actions(current_dir, target_dir)\n                    \n                    # The complete sequence of actions is:\n                    # (path to current state) + (turning actions) + (USE action)\n                    return path_to_current_state + turns + [USE_ACT]\n\n        # If the primitive is not collectible from this state (or not directly in front),\n        # explore movement actions to find a closer state.\n        for action in move_actions:\n            # Simulate the action to get the next state.\n            # state.step() creates a new CraftState object and handles game logic.\n            # It returns (reward, new_state). We only care about new_state here.\n            # Impassable terrain is handled by state.step(), leading to no change in position.\n            _, next_state = state.step(action) \n\n            next_state_key = (next_state.pos[0], next_state.pos[1], next_state.dir)\n\n            if next_state_key not in visited:\n                visited.add(next_state_key)\n                parent_info[next_state_key] = (state_key, action) # Store parent and action\n                q.append((next_state_key, next_state)) # Add new state to queue\n\n    # If the queue is exhausted and no path to collect the primitive was found, return an empty list.\n    return []", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:08:40.466784", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Get the current state and world configuration from the environment\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  world = env.world\n\n  # 1. Get the integer ID (kind index) for the primitive.\n  # Convert primitive name to lowercase for robustness, as keys in cookbook.index might be lowercase.\n  try:\n    i_kind = world.cookbook.index[primitive.lower()]\n  except KeyError:\n    # If the primitive name is not found in the cookbook, it cannot be collected.\n    return []\n\n  # 2. Check if the primitive is already in the agent's inventory.\n  # If it is, no actions are needed to \"collect\" it.\n  if current_state.inventory[i_kind] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # 3. Determine if this primitive is collectible via the 'USE' action.\n  # This includes items that can be picked up (grabbable) and specific resources like water or stone.\n  is_collectible_via_use = (\n      i_kind in world.grabbable_indices or \n      i_kind == world.water_index or \n      i_kind == world.stone_index\n  )\n  \n  # If the item is not collectible using 'USE', we don't attempt to collect it.\n  # This function specifically focuses on 'collecting' actions involving 'USE'.\n  if not is_collectible_via_use:\n    return []\n\n  # 4. Define action integers from the environment's action specifications.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP_ACT = action_map[\"UP\"]\n  DOWN_ACT = action_map[\"DOWN\"]\n  LEFT_ACT = action_map[\"LEFT\"]\n  RIGHT_ACT = action_map[\"RIGHT\"]\n  USE_ACT = action_map[\"USE\"]\n\n  # List of all movement actions\n  move_actions = [UP_ACT, DOWN_ACT, LEFT_ACT, RIGHT_ACT]\n\n  # Map agent's direction (0=UP, 1=RIGHT, 2=DOWN, 3=LEFT) to (row_delta, col_delta)\n  # for the cell directly in front of the agent.\n  _DIR_TO_DELTA_FRONT = {\n      0: (-1, 0), # UP: moves to (row-1, col)\n      1: (0, 1),  # RIGHT: moves to (row, col+1)\n      2: (1, 0),  # DOWN: moves to (row+1, col)\n      3: (0, -1)  # LEFT: moves to (row, col-1)\n  }\n\n  # Helper function to calculate the shortest sequence of turning actions\n  # to face a target direction from the current direction.\n  def _get_turning_actions(current_dir: int, target_dir: int) -> list[int]:\n      if current_dir == target_dir:\n          return [] # Already facing the target direction\n      \n      # Calculate the difference in directions, handling circularity (0,1,2,3 -> 0).\n      # Adding 4 and taking modulo 4 ensures a positive difference.\n      diff = (target_dir - current_dir + 4) % 4\n      \n      if diff == 1: # Target is one step clockwise (e.g., UP(0) -> RIGHT(1))\n          return [RIGHT_ACT]\n      elif diff == 3: # Target is one step counter-clockwise (e.g., UP(0) -> LEFT(3))\n          return [LEFT_ACT]\n      else: # diff == 2, implies a 180-degree turn (e.g., UP(0) -> DOWN(2))\n          # Two consecutive right or left turns will achieve this.\n          return [RIGHT_ACT, RIGHT_ACT] \n\n  # 5. Breadth-First Search (BFS) setup:\n  # Queue to store states to explore. Each element is (state_key, CraftState_object).\n  # We pass the CraftState object to avoid re-simulating from the initial state\n  # for every step, which would be inefficient.\n  q = collections.deque()\n  \n  # `visited` set to keep track of explored (position, direction) states\n  # to prevent cycles and redundant work.\n  visited = set()\n  \n  # `parent_info` dictionary to reconstruct the path once the goal is found.\n  # Maps `state_key` -> (`parent_state_key`, `action_taken_from_parent_to_current`).\n  parent_info = {} \n\n  # For clarity when accessing state_key tuple elements:\n  # state_key = (row, column, direction)\n  ROW, COL, DIR = 0, 1, 2\n\n  # Initialize BFS with the agent's current state.\n  initial_state_key = (current_state.pos[0], current_state.pos[1], current_state.dir)\n  q.append((initial_state_key, current_state))\n  visited.add(initial_state_key)\n  # The initial state has no parent.\n  parent_info[initial_state_key] = (None, None) \n\n  # Get grid dimensions for boundary checks.\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = current_state.grid.shape\n  \n  # A safety limit for BFS exploration to prevent excessively long searches\n  # or infinite loops in cases where no path exists.\n  # (Total unique (pos, dir) states = width * height * 4 directions) * a multiplier.\n  MAX_EXPLORED_STATES = grid_width * grid_height * 4 * 2 \n  explored_states_count = 0\n\n  # 6. BFS Loop:\n  while q:\n    # Dequeue the current state and its key\n    state_key, state = q.popleft() \n    explored_states_count += 1\n\n    # Pruning: If we've explored too many states, stop this branch of search.\n    if explored_states_count > MAX_EXPLORED_STATES:\n      continue \n\n    # Unpack current position and direction for convenience\n    current_r, current_c, current_dir = state_key \n\n    # Goal Check: Can we collect the primitive from *this* state?\n    # `state.next_to(i_kind)` checks if the primitive is anywhere in the 3x3 neighborhood.\n    if state.next_to(i_kind):\n        # If nearby, we need to check if we can orient ourselves to face it directly.\n        # Iterate through all 4 possible agent orientations (target_dir).\n        for target_dir in range(4): \n            # Calculate the coordinates of the cell directly in front if agent faces `target_dir`.\n            dr, dc = _DIR_TO_DELTA_FRONT[target_dir]\n            facing_r, facing_c = current_r + dr, current_c + dc\n\n            # Check if the calculated 'facing' cell is within grid bounds\n            # AND if it actually contains the desired primitive.\n            if (0 <= facing_r < grid_width and 0 <= facing_c < grid_height and \n                state.grid[facing_r, facing_c, i_kind] == 1):\n                \n                # Primitive found directly in front! We have a path to collection.\n                # First, determine actions to turn from current direction to `target_dir`.\n                turns = _get_turning_actions(current_dir, target_dir)\n                \n                # Reconstruct the path of movement actions from the initial state\n                # up to the `current_state_key` (where we are now).\n                path_to_current_state = []\n                curr_reconstruct_key = state_key\n                # Traverse `parent_info` backwards until the root (None parent) is reached.\n                while parent_info[curr_reconstruct_key][0] is not None:\n                    parent_key, action_from_parent = parent_info[curr_reconstruct_key]\n                    path_to_current_state.append(action_from_parent)\n                    curr_reconstruct_key = parent_key\n                path_to_current_state.reverse() # Reverse to get actions in correct order.\n\n                # The complete sequence of actions is:\n                # 1. Path to reach the current (r,c,dir) state.\n                # 2. Turning actions to face the primitive.\n                # 3. The 'USE' action to collect it.\n                return path_to_current_state + turns + [USE_ACT]\n\n    # If the primitive is not collectible from this current state,\n    # explore potential movement actions to find a new state.\n    for action in move_actions:\n      # Simulate taking the action. `state.step()` returns (reward, new_state).\n      # We only care about the `new_state` for BFS.\n      _, next_state = state.step(action) \n\n      # Create a key for the new state (position and direction).\n      next_state_key = (next_state.pos[0], next_state.pos[1], next_state.dir)\n\n      # If this new state has not been visited yet:\n      if next_state_key not in visited:\n        visited.add(next_state_key) # Mark as visited.\n        # Store how we reached this state (from which parent state and what action).\n        parent_info[next_state_key] = (state_key, action) \n        # Add the new state to the queue for future exploration.\n        q.append((next_state_key, next_state)) \n\n  # If the BFS loop completes and the queue is empty without finding a path\n  # to collect the primitive, it means it's unreachable or uncollectible.\n  return []", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:09:35.890483", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1`.\"\"\"\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  primitive_idx = cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n\n  # Improvement from v1: Check if the primitive is already in inventory.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # Improvement from v1: Ensure the requested primitive is actually grabbable.\n  # Non-grabbable entities (like \"water\", \"boundary\", or a \"workshop\") cannot be \"collected\" into inventory.\n  if primitive_idx not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_x, start_y = current_state.pos\n  start_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's current facing direction (0:N, 1:E, 2:S, 3:W)\n\n  # Improvement from v1: Use the comprehensive set of non-grabbable indices from the world object\n  # to determine impassable terrain (obstacles).\n  non_grabbable_obstacle_indices = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Define movement actions and their effects on (dx, dy) and new_direction\n  # The agent's direction is updated to face the direction of movement.\n  action_effects = {\n      craft.UP: (0, -1, 0),    # Move North (y-1), new_dir = 0 (North)\n      craft.DOWN: (0, 1, 2),     # Move South (y+1), new_dir = 2 (South)\n      craft.LEFT: (-1, 0, 3),    # Move West (x-1), new_dir = 3 (West)\n      craft.RIGHT: (1, 0, 1)     # Move East (x+1), new_dir = 1 (East)\n  }\n\n  # Mapping agent direction (0-3) to (dx, dy) for the cell *in front* of the agent\n  # This is crucial for determining where a 'USE' action will interact.\n  # FWD_DX[direction]: (0:N, 1:E, 2:S, 3:W) -> (dx)\n  FWD_DX = [0, 1, 0, -1]\n  # FWD_DY[direction]: (0:N, 1:E, 2:S, 3:W) -> (dy)\n  FWD_DY = [-1, 0, 1, 0]\n\n  # BFS setup\n  # Queue stores tuples of ((current_x, current_y, current_dir), path_taken_so_far)\n  queue = collections.deque([((start_x, start_y, start_dir), [])])\n  # Set of visited states to prevent cycles and redundant exploration.\n  # A state now includes position AND direction, as direction affects possible actions (USE).\n  visited = {(start_x, start_y, start_dir)}\n\n  while queue:\n    (x, y, d), path = queue.popleft()\n\n    # Check if a 'USE' action is possible from the current (x, y, d) state.\n    # The 'USE' action targets the cell directly in front of the agent.\n    target_x = x + FWD_DX[d]\n    target_y = y + FWD_DY[d]\n\n    # Check if the cell in front is within grid bounds and contains the primitive.\n    # This is the \"goal\" condition for collecting.\n    if (0 <= target_x < grid_width and 0 <= target_y < grid_height and\n        grid[target_x, target_y, primitive_idx] > 0):\n      # Found the primitive directly in front, so return the path to get here\n      # plus the 'USE' action to collect it.\n      return path + [craft.USE]\n\n    # Explore valid neighbor states by performing movement actions.\n    for action, (dx_move, dy_move, new_d) in action_effects.items():\n      next_x, next_y = x + dx_move, y + dy_move\n      next_state_tuple = (next_x, next_y, new_d) # New state includes new position and new direction\n\n      # 1. Bounds check: Ensure the new position is within the grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue\n\n      # 2. Visited check: Avoid revisiting already explored (position, direction) states\n      # to find the shortest path and prevent infinite loops.\n      if next_state_tuple in visited:\n        continue\n\n      # 3. Traversability check: Ensure the cell is not an obstacle.\n      #    A cell is an obstacle if it contains any non-grabbable item.\n      is_obstacle = False\n      for obstacle_idx in non_grabbable_obstacle_indices:\n        if grid[next_x, next_y, obstacle_idx] > 0:\n          is_obstacle = True\n          break\n      if is_obstacle:\n        continue # Cannot move into an obstacle cell\n\n      # If all checks pass, add the new state to the queue and mark it as visited.\n      visited.add(next_state_tuple)\n      queue.append((next_state_tuple, path + [action]))\n\n  # If the BFS queue becomes empty and no path to the primitive (for a 'USE' action) was found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable.\n  return []", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:09:37.009341", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  primitive_idx = cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n\n  # Improvement 1: Check if the primitive is already in inventory.\n  # If the agent already possesses the required item, no collection actions are needed.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # Improvement 2: Ensure the requested primitive is actually grabbable.\n  # Non-grabbable entities (like \"water\", \"boundary\", or \"workshops\") cannot be\n  # \"collected\" into inventory. In such cases, return an empty list.\n  if primitive_idx not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_x, start_y = current_state.pos\n  start_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's current facing direction (0:N, 1:E, 2:S, 3:W)\n\n  # Improvement 3: Use the comprehensive set of non-grabbable indices from the world object\n  # to determine impassable terrain (obstacles). This is more robust than just checking \"boundary\".\n  non_grabbable_obstacle_indices = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Define movement actions and their effects on (dx, dy) and new_direction.\n  # The agent's direction is updated to face the direction of movement.\n  action_effects = {\n      craft.UP: (0, -1, 0),    # Move North (y-1), new_dir = 0 (North)\n      craft.DOWN: (0, 1, 2),     # Move South (y+1), new_dir = 2 (South)\n      craft.LEFT: (-1, 0, 3),    # Move West (x-1), new_dir = 3 (West)\n      craft.RIGHT: (1, 0, 1)     # Move East (x+1), new_dir = 1 (East)\n  }\n\n  # Mapping agent direction (0-3) to (dx, dy) for the cell *in front* of the agent.\n  # This is crucial for determining where a 'USE' action will interact.\n  # FWD_DX[direction]: (0:N, 1:E, 2:S, 3:W) -> (dx)\n  FWD_DX = [0, 1, 0, -1]\n  # FWD_DY[direction]: (0:N, 1:E, 2:S, 3:W) -> (dy)\n  FWD_DY = [-1, 0, 1, 0]\n\n  # BFS setup:\n  # The queue stores tuples of ((current_x, current_y, current_dir), path_taken_so_far).\n  queue = collections.deque([((start_x, start_y, start_dir), [])])\n  # The set of visited states prevents cycles and redundant exploration.\n  # A state now includes position AND direction, as direction affects possible 'USE' actions.\n  visited = {(start_x, start_y, start_dir)}\n\n  while queue:\n    (x, y, d), path = queue.popleft()\n\n    # Check if a 'USE' action is possible from the current (x, y, d) state.\n    # The 'USE' action targets the cell directly in front of the agent.\n    target_x = x + FWD_DX[d]\n    target_y = y + FWD_DY[d]\n\n    # Check if the cell in front is within grid bounds and contains the primitive.\n    if (0 <= target_x < grid_width and 0 <= target_y < grid_height and\n        grid[target_x, target_y, primitive_idx] > 0):\n      # Found the primitive directly in front, so return the path to get to this state\n      # plus the 'USE' action to collect it.\n      return path + [craft.USE]\n\n    # Explore valid neighbor states by performing movement actions.\n    for action, (dx_move, dy_move, new_d) in action_effects.items():\n      next_x, next_y = x + dx_move, y + dy_move\n      next_state_tuple = (next_x, next_y, new_d) # New state includes new position and new direction\n\n      # 1. Bounds check: Ensure the new position is within the grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue\n\n      # 2. Visited check: Avoid revisiting already explored (position, direction) states\n      # to find the shortest path and prevent infinite loops.\n      if next_state_tuple in visited:\n        continue\n\n      # 3. Traversability check: Ensure the cell is not an obstacle.\n      #    A cell is considered an obstacle if it contains any non-grabbable item.\n      is_obstacle = False\n      for obstacle_idx in non_grabbable_obstacle_indices:\n        if grid[next_x, next_y, obstacle_idx] > 0:\n          is_obstacle = True\n          break\n      if is_obstacle:\n        continue # Cannot move into an obstacle cell\n\n      # If all checks pass, add the new state to the queue and mark it as visited.\n      visited.add(next_state_tuple)\n      queue.append((next_state_tuple, path + [action]))\n\n  # If the BFS queue becomes empty and no path to the primitive (for a 'USE' action) was found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable from the current state.\n  return []", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:10:42.327844", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  primitive_idx = cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n\n  # Check if the primitive is already in inventory. If so, no actions are needed.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # Ensure the requested primitive is actually grabbable. Non-grabbable entities\n  # (like \"water\", \"boundary\", or a \"workshop\") cannot be \"collected\" into inventory.\n  if primitive_idx not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_x, start_y = current_state.pos\n  start_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's current facing direction (0:N, 1:E, 2:S, 3:W)\n\n  # Determine impassable terrain (obstacles) using non-grabbable indices from the world object.\n  non_grabbable_obstacle_indices = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Define movement actions and their effects on (dx, dy) and the agent's new direction.\n  # The agent's direction is updated to face the direction of movement.\n  action_effects = {\n      craft.UP: (0, -1, 0),    # Move North (y-1), new_dir = 0 (North)\n      craft.DOWN: (0, 1, 2),     # Move South (y+1), new_dir = 2 (South)\n      craft.LEFT: (-1, 0, 3),    # Move West (x-1), new_dir = 3 (West)\n      craft.RIGHT: (1, 0, 1)     # Move East (x+1), new_dir = 1 (East)\n  }\n\n  # Mapping agent direction (0-3) to (dx, dy) for the cell *directly in front* of the agent.\n  # This is crucial for determining the target cell for a 'USE' action.\n  # Directions: 0=North, 1=East, 2=South, 3=West\n  FWD_DX = [0, 1, 0, -1] # Delta X for cell in front\n  FWD_DY = [-1, 0, 1, 0] # Delta Y for cell in front\n\n  # BFS setup\n  # The queue stores tuples of: ((current_x, current_y, current_dir), path_taken_so_far)\n  queue = collections.deque([((start_x, start_y, start_dir), [])])\n  \n  # The set of visited states prevents cycles and redundant exploration.\n  # A state now includes position (x, y) AND direction (d), as the agent's direction\n  # affects which cell a 'USE' action will interact with.\n  visited = {(start_x, start_y, start_dir)}\n\n  while queue:\n    (x, y, d), path = queue.popleft()\n\n    # Determine the coordinates of the cell directly in front of the agent.\n    target_x = x + FWD_DX[d]\n    target_y = y + FWD_DY[d]\n\n    # Check if the cell in front is within grid bounds AND contains the primitive.\n    # This is the \"goal\" condition: we are in a position and orientation to 'USE' the primitive.\n    if (0 <= target_x < grid_width and 0 <= target_y < grid_height and\n        grid[target_x, target_y, primitive_idx] > 0):\n      # Goal reached: return the path to get to this state plus the 'USE' action to collect it.\n      return path + [craft.USE]\n\n    # Explore valid neighbor states by trying each possible movement action.\n    for action, (dx_move, dy_move, new_d) in action_effects.items():\n      next_x, next_y = x + dx_move, y + dy_move\n      next_state_tuple = (next_x, next_y, new_d) # The new state includes the updated position and direction\n\n      # 1. Bounds check: Ensure the next position is within the grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue\n\n      # 2. Visited check: Avoid revisiting states (position + direction) to find the shortest path\n      # and prevent infinite loops in the BFS.\n      if next_state_tuple in visited:\n        continue\n\n      # 3. Traversability check: Ensure the cell we are moving into is not an obstacle.\n      # A cell is considered an obstacle if it contains any non-grabbable item.\n      is_obstacle = False\n      for obstacle_idx in non_grabbable_obstacle_indices:\n        if grid[next_x, next_y, obstacle_idx] > 0:\n          is_obstacle = True\n          break\n      if is_obstacle:\n        continue # Cannot move into an obstacle cell\n\n      # If all checks pass, add the new state to the queue and mark it as visited.\n      visited.add(next_state_tuple)\n      queue.append((next_state_tuple, path + [action]))\n\n  # If the BFS queue becomes empty and no path to the primitive (for a 'USE' action) was found,\n  # it means the primitive is currently unreachable in the environment.\n  return []", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:10:43.602887", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  primitive_idx = cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n\n  # Check if the primitive is already in inventory. If so, no actions are needed.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # Ensure the requested primitive is actually grabbable. Non-grabbable entities\n  # (like \"water\", \"boundary\", or a \"workshop\") cannot be \"collected\" into inventory.\n  if primitive_idx not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_x, start_y = current_state.pos\n  start_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's current facing direction (0:N, 1:E, 2:S, 3:W)\n\n  # Use the comprehensive set of non-grabbable indices from the world object\n  # to determine impassable terrain (obstacles).\n  non_grabbable_obstacle_indices = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Define movement actions and their effects on (dx, dy) and new_direction\n  # The agent's direction is updated to face the direction of movement.\n  action_effects = {\n      craft.UP: (0, -1, 0),    # Move North (y-1), new_dir = 0 (North)\n      craft.DOWN: (0, 1, 2),     # Move South (y+1), new_dir = 2 (South)\n      craft.LEFT: (-1, 0, 3),    # Move West (x-1), new_dir = 3 (West)\n      craft.RIGHT: (1, 0, 1)     # Move East (x+1), new_dir = 1 (East)\n  }\n\n  # Mapping agent direction (0-3) to (dx, dy) for the cell *in front* of the agent\n  # This is crucial for determining where a 'USE' action will interact.\n  # FWD_DX[direction]: (0:N, 1:E, 2:S, 3:W) -> (dx)\n  FWD_DX = [0, 1, 0, -1]\n  # FWD_DY[direction]: (0:N, 1:E, 2:S, 3:W) -> (dy)\n  FWD_DY = [-1, 0, 1, 0]\n\n  # BFS setup\n  # Queue stores tuples of ((current_x, current_y, current_dir), path_taken_so_far)\n  queue = collections.deque([((start_x, start_y, start_dir), [])])\n  # Set of visited states to prevent cycles and redundant exploration.\n  # A state now includes position AND direction, as direction affects possible actions (USE).\n  visited = {(start_x, start_y, start_dir)}\n\n  while queue:\n    (x, y, d), path = queue.popleft()\n\n    # Check if a 'USE' action is possible from the current (x, y, d) state.\n    # The 'USE' action targets the cell directly in front of the agent.\n    target_x = x + FWD_DX[d]\n    target_y = y + FWD_DY[d]\n\n    # Check if the cell in front is within grid bounds and contains the primitive.\n    # This is the \"goal\" condition for collecting.\n    if (0 <= target_x < grid_width and 0 <= target_y < grid_height and\n        grid[target_x, target_y, primitive_idx] > 0):\n      # Found the primitive directly in front, so return the path to get here\n      # plus the 'USE' action to collect it.\n      return path + [craft.USE]\n\n    # Explore valid neighbor states by performing movement actions.\n    for action, (dx_move, dy_move, new_d) in action_effects.items():\n      next_x, next_y = x + dx_move, y + dy_move\n      next_state_tuple = (next_x, next_y, new_d) # New state includes new position and new direction\n\n      # 1. Bounds check: Ensure the new position is within the grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue\n\n      # 2. Visited check: Avoid revisiting already explored (position, direction) states\n      # to find the shortest path and prevent infinite loops.\n      if next_state_tuple in visited:\n        continue\n\n      # 3. Traversability check: Ensure the cell is not an obstacle.\n      #    A cell is an obstacle if it contains any non-grabbable item.\n      is_obstacle = False\n      for obstacle_idx in non_grabbable_obstacle_indices:\n        if grid[next_x, next_y, obstacle_idx] > 0:\n          is_obstacle = True\n          break\n      if is_obstacle:\n        continue # Cannot move into an obstacle cell\n\n      # If all checks pass, add the new state to the queue and mark it as visited.\n      visited.add(next_state_tuple)\n      queue.append((next_state_tuple, path + [action]))\n\n  # If the BFS queue becomes empty and no path to the primitive (for a 'USE' action) was found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable.\n  return []", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:12:07.487694", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1`.\n    Computes a sequence of actions to find and collect a specified grabbable primitive.\n    It uses Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path to a cell\n    adjacent to any instance of the primitive, and then appends a 'USE' action.\n    This version optimizes the adjacency check within the BFS loop by directly\n    checking the 3x3 neighborhood of primitive locations, avoiding repeated\n    `CraftState` object instantiation, which improves performance.\n\n    Args:\n        env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab environment object representing the current game state.\n        primitive (str): The name of the primitive item to be collected (e.g., \"WOOD\", \"IRON\").\n\n    Returns:\n        List[int]: A list of integer action codes (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT, USE)\n                   representing the optimal sequence to collect the primitive.\n                   Returns an empty list if the primitive is not grabbable,\n                   or if no path to an adjacent primitive is found.\n  \"\"\"\n  # 1. Initialize State and Environment Information\n  current_state = env._current_state \n  grid = current_state.grid\n  agent_start_pos = current_state.pos\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Retrieve the integer ID for the target primitive from the world's cookbook index.\n  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Map action names to their corresponding integer codes using env.action_specs().\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define possible movement directions (delta row, delta col) and their associated actions.\n  # These are for cardinal movements (Up, Down, Left, Right).\n  MOVEMENT_DELTAS = [\n      ((-1, 0), ACTION_UP),    # Row decreases -> Up\n      ((1, 0), ACTION_DOWN),   # Row increases -> Down\n      ((0, -1), ACTION_LEFT),  # Col decreases -> Left\n      ((0, 1), ACTION_RIGHT)   # Col increases -> Right\n  ]\n\n  # Pre-calculate indices of non-grabbable items for efficient traversability checks.\n  # These are items that block movement.\n  non_grabbable_kind_indices = list(env.world.non_grabbable_indices)\n  \n  # 2. Pre-checks and Immediate Collection\n  # If the primitive cannot be picked up (e.g., water, workshop, boundary), return empty path.\n  if primitive_id not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  # If the agent is already positioned such that it can immediately 'USE' the primitive,\n  # a single 'USE' action is sufficient. This leverages CraftState's `next_to` method.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_id):\n      return [ACTION_USE]\n\n  # 3. Locate All Primitive Instances on the Grid\n  # Iterate through the entire grid to find all (row, col) coordinates\n  # where the target primitive exists. This list will be used for the BFS goal check.\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for r in range(grid_width):\n      for c in range(grid_height):\n          if grid[r, c, primitive_id] == 1:\n              primitive_locations.append((r, c))\n  \n  # If no instances of the primitive are found on the grid at all, it cannot be collected.\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      return []\n\n  # 4. Breadth-First Search (BFS) for Shortest Path\n  # The BFS aims to find the shortest sequence of movement actions from the\n  # agent's starting position to any cell from which the primitive can be 'USE'd.\n  # A cell is considered reachable if it's within the 3x3 neighborhood (including diagonals and itself)\n  # of a primitive location, as per the `CraftState.next_to` definition.\n  \n  # The queue stores tuples: (current_position (r, c), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here).\n  q = collections.deque([(agent_start_pos, [])]) \n  \n  # The `visited` set prevents revisiting locations, ensuring the shortest path is found\n  # and avoiding infinite loops in cyclic environments.\n  visited = {agent_start_pos} \n\n  shortest_path_actions = []\n  target_adjacent_position_found = False\n\n  while q:\n      (current_r, current_c), path_actions_so_far = q.popleft()\n\n      # Check if the current BFS position (current_r, current_c) is adjacent to any\n      # of the primitive locations. This is the goal condition for the BFS.\n      for pr, pc in primitive_locations:\n          # A cell (current_r, current_c) is considered \"next to\" a primitive at (pr, pc)\n          # if (pr, pc) falls within the 3x3 square centered at (current_r, current_c).\n          if abs(current_r - pr) <= 1 and abs(current_c - pc) <= 1:\n              shortest_path_actions = path_actions_so_far # Store the path found\n              target_adjacent_position_found = True       # Mark goal as reached\n              break # Exit inner loop: no need to check other primitive locations\n      \n      if target_adjacent_position_found:\n          break # Exit BFS loop: the shortest path to an adjacent cell has been found.\n\n      # Explore all valid cardinal neighboring cells from the current position.\n      for (dr, dc), action_to_take in MOVEMENT_DELTAS:\n          next_r, next_c = current_r + dr, current_c + dc\n          next_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n\n          # --- Validity Checks for Next Position ---\n          # 1. Boundary Check: Ensure the next position is within the grid dimensions.\n          if not (0 <= next_r < grid_width and 0 <= next_c < grid_height):\n              continue\n\n          # 2. Traversability Check: Ensure the next position is not an impassable obstacle.\n          # A cell is an obstacle if it contains any item from the `non_grabbable_indices` set.\n          is_obstacle = False\n          # Only perform numpy check if there are actual non-grabbable kinds to avoid error on empty list.\n          if non_grabbable_kind_indices and np.any(grid[next_r, next_c, non_grabbable_kind_indices]):\n              is_obstacle = True\n          \n          if is_obstacle:\n              continue\n\n          # 3. Visited Check: Avoid re-exploring positions that have already been visited\n          # to ensure the shortest path and prevent infinite loops.\n          if next_pos not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_pos)\n              # Add the new valid position to the queue with the accumulated path actions.\n              q.append((next_pos, path_actions_so_far + [action_to_take]))\n\n  # 5. Construct the Final Action Sequence\n  final_actions_sequence = shortest_path_actions\n\n  # If a path was successfully found to a cell adjacent to the primitive,\n  # append the 'USE' action to complete the collection.\n  if target_adjacent_position_found:\n      final_actions_sequence.append(ACTION_USE)\n  \n  return final_actions_sequence", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:12:08.681427", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1`.\n  Computes a sequence of actions to find and collect a specified grabbable primitive.\n  It uses Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path to a cell\n  adjacent to any instance of the primitive, and then appends a 'USE' action.\n\n  This version refines variable naming and ensures all core logic remains robust and efficient.\n\n  Args:\n      env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab environment object representing the current game state.\n      primitive (str): The name of the primitive item to be collected (e.g., \"WOOD\", \"IRON\").\n\n  Returns:\n      List[int]: A list of integer action codes (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT, USE)\n                 representing the optimal sequence to collect the primitive.\n                 Returns an empty list if the primitive is not grabbable,\n                 or if no path to an adjacent primitive is found.\n  \"\"\"\n  # 1. Initialize State and Environment Information\n  current_craft_state = env._current_state \n  game_grid = current_craft_state.grid\n  agent_current_pos = current_craft_state.pos\n  grid_rows, grid_cols, _ = game_grid.shape # Use rows/cols for clarity with (r,c) indexing\n\n  # Retrieve the integer ID for the target primitive from the world's cookbook index.\n  # Assuming `primitive` string is always valid per DSL specification.\n  primitive_kind_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Map action names to their corresponding integer codes using env.action_specs().\n  action_specs = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_specs['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_specs['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_specs['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_specs['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_specs['USE']\n\n  # Define possible movement directions (delta row, delta col) and their associated actions.\n  # This structure directly links a movement delta to the action that produces it.\n  move_actions_with_deltas = [\n      ((-1, 0), ACTION_UP),    # Move Up: row decreases\n      ((1, 0), ACTION_DOWN),   # Move Down: row increases\n      ((0, -1), ACTION_LEFT),  # Move Left: column decreases\n      ((0, 1), ACTION_RIGHT)   # Move Right: column increases\n  ]\n\n  # Pre-calculate indices of non-grabbable items for efficient traversability checks.\n  # Convert to a list for efficient numpy advanced indexing if necessary.\n  impassable_kind_ids = list(env.world.non_grabbable_indices)\n  \n  # 2. Pre-checks and Immediate Collection\n  # If the primitive is not in the list of grabbable items (e.g., water, workshop, boundary),\n  # then it cannot be \"collected\" in this manner. Return an empty path.\n  if primitive_kind_id not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  # If the agent is already positioned immediately next to the primitive,\n  # only a single 'USE' action is required to collect it.\n  if current_craft_state.next_to(primitive_kind_id):\n      return [ACTION_USE]\n\n  # 3. Breadth-First Search (BFS) for Shortest Path\n  # The BFS aims to find the shortest sequence of movement actions\n  # that leads the agent to a cell from which the primitive can be collected (i.e., is adjacent).\n\n  # Queue for BFS: stores tuples of (current_position (r, c), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here).\n  bfs_queue = collections.deque([(agent_current_pos, [])]) \n  \n  # Set to keep track of visited positions to prevent revisiting nodes,\n  # which ensures the shortest path is found and avoids infinite loops in cyclic grids.\n  visited_positions = {agent_current_pos} \n\n  # Variables to store the result of the BFS.\n  found_path_to_adjacent_cell = []\n  is_path_found = False\n\n  while bfs_queue:\n      (r, c), path_taken = bfs_queue.popleft()\n\n      # Create a temporary CraftState instance for the current BFS grid position.\n      # This allows us to leverage the `next_to` method to efficiently check\n      # if this `(r, c)` location is adjacent to the target primitive.\n      temp_bfs_state = craft.CraftState(\n          scenario=current_craft_state.scenario,\n          grid=game_grid,\n          pos=(r, c),\n          dir=current_craft_state.dir, # Direction and inventory are irrelevant for next_to check\n          inventory=current_craft_state.inventory\n      )\n\n      # Check if the current position `(r, c)` in the BFS is adjacent to the target primitive.\n      # If it is, we've found the shortest path of movements to a collecting spot.\n      if temp_bfs_state.next_to(primitive_kind_id):\n          found_path_to_adjacent_cell = path_taken\n          is_path_found = True\n          break  # Exit BFS: The shortest path to a suitable collection point is found.\n\n      # Explore all four cardinal neighbors (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT) from the current position.\n      for (dr, dc), action_move in move_actions_with_deltas:\n          next_r, next_c = r + dr, c + dc\n          next_grid_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n\n          # --- Validity Checks for the Neighboring Position ---\n          # 1. Boundary Check: Ensure the `next_grid_pos` is within the grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= next_r < grid_rows and 0 <= next_c < grid_cols):\n              continue\n\n          # 2. Traversability Check: Ensure the `next_grid_pos` is not an impassable obstacle.\n          # A cell is an obstacle if it contains any item from the `impassable_kind_ids` set.\n          # np.any is used for efficient checking across the depth dimension for those kinds.\n          is_impassable_cell = False\n          if impassable_kind_ids: # Only perform check if there are defined impassable kinds\n              # Efficiently check if any of the impassable kinds are present at this cell.\n              if np.any(game_grid[next_r, next_c, impassable_kind_ids]):\n                  is_impassable_cell = True\n          \n          if is_impassable_cell:\n              continue # Skip this neighbor if it's an obstacle.\n\n          # 3. Visited Check: Avoid re-exploring positions that have already been processed\n          # to guarantee the shortest path and prevent cycles.\n          if next_grid_pos not in visited_positions:\n              visited_positions.add(next_grid_pos)\n              # Add the valid, unvisited neighbor to the queue with its accumulated path.\n              bfs_queue.append((next_grid_pos, path_taken + [action_move]))\n\n  # 4. Construct the Final Action Sequence\n  final_collection_actions = found_path_to_adjacent_cell\n\n  # If a path was successfully found to a cell from which the primitive can be used,\n  # append the 'USE' action to complete the collection process.\n  if is_path_found:\n      final_collection_actions.append(ACTION_USE)\n  \n  return final_collection_actions", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:12:44.314896", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map[\"UP\"]\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map[\"DOWN\"]\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map[\"LEFT\"]\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map[\"RIGHT\"]\n  ACTION_USE = action_map[\"USE\"]\n\n  # Convert the primitive name (string) to its integer ID.\n  # The `cookbook.index` provides a mapping from string names to integer IDs.\n  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive.lower()]\n  if primitive_id is None:\n    # If the primitive name is not recognized by the environment's cookbook,\n    # it cannot be collected.\n    return []\n\n  # Verify if the target primitive is actually a \"grabbable\" item.\n  # The `collect` function is specifically for items that can be picked up\n  # by moving to their location and using the 'USE' action.\n  if primitive_id not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n    # For example, \"water\" or \"stone\" might be primitives but are often\n    # environmental features or require tools to interact with, not just grabbing.\n    return []\n\n  # Retrieve the current state of the environment.\n  # This provides access to the grid, agent's position, and other state details.\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  start_pos = current_state.pos  # Agent's current (x, y) position\n  grid = current_state.grid      # The full grid (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  \n  # Get grid dimensions for boundary checks during pathfinding.\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Identify entity kinds that act as obstacles (cannot be traversed).\n  # These are typically non-grabbable environment components like impassable terrain.\n  obstacle_kind_ids = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # Define possible movements and their corresponding actions.\n  # Each tuple represents (delta_x, delta_y, action_constant).\n  move_actions = [\n      (0, -1, ACTION_UP),    # Move North (decreases y-coordinate)\n      (0, 1, ACTION_DOWN),   # Move South (increases y-coordinate)\n      (-1, 0, ACTION_LEFT),  # Move West (decreases x-coordinate)\n      (1, 0, ACTION_RIGHT)   # Move East (increases x-coordinate)\n  ]\n\n  # Initialize Breadth-First Search (BFS) for pathfinding.\n  # The queue will store tuples of (current_position_tuple, list_of_actions_to_reach_here).\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])])\n  # The `visited` set tracks explored grid cells to prevent infinite loops and redundant work.\n  visited = {start_pos}\n\n  # Start the BFS traversal to find the shortest path to the primitive.\n  while queue:\n    current_pos, path_so_far = queue.popleft()\n    cx, cy = current_pos\n\n    # Check if the current cell contains the target primitive.\n    # `grid[cx, cy, primitive_id] > 0` indicates the presence of the item.\n    if grid[cx, cy, primitive_id] > 0:\n      # If the primitive is found, the path to this cell is complete.\n      # Append a 'USE' action to the path to simulate collecting the item.\n      return path_so_far + [ACTION_USE]\n\n    # Explore all adjacent cells (neighbors) from the current position.\n    for dx, dy, action_for_move in move_actions:\n      next_x, next_y = cx + dx, cy + dy  # Calculate neighbor's coordinates\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # 1. Boundary check: Ensure the neighbor is within the grid dimensions.\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue\n\n      # 2. Visited check: Skip if this cell has already been processed by BFS.\n      if next_pos in visited:\n        continue\n\n      # 3. Obstacle check: Determine if the neighbor cell is blocked by an impassable object.\n      # A cell is blocked if it contains any of the identified obstacle kinds.\n      is_blocked = False\n      for obstacle_id in obstacle_kind_ids:\n        if grid[next_x, next_y, obstacle_id] > 0:\n          is_blocked = True\n          break # Found an obstacle, this cell is blocked.\n      \n      if is_blocked:\n        continue # Cannot move to a blocked cell.\n\n      # If the neighbor is valid (within bounds, unvisited, and traversable),\n      # add it to the BFS queue and mark it as visited.\n      visited.add(next_pos)\n      queue.append((next_pos, path_so_far + [action_for_move]))\n\n  # If the queue becomes empty and the primitive was not found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable from the current agent's position.\n  return []", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:12:45.622687", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  action_mapping = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_mapping[\"UP\"]\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_mapping[\"DOWN\"]\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_mapping[\"LEFT\"]\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_mapping[\"RIGHT\"]\n  ACTION_USE = action_mapping[\"USE\"]\n\n  # Convert the primitive name (string) to its corresponding integer ID.\n  # The `cookbook.index` provides this mapping. `.lower()` ensures case insensitivity.\n  target_primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive.lower()]\n  if target_primitive_id is None:\n    # If the primitive name does not exist in the world's index, it cannot be collected.\n    return []\n\n  # Verify if the primitive is actually a \"grabbable\" item.\n  # The 'collect' action is specifically for items that can be picked up directly.\n  # Other items might require crafting or tool usage (e.g., mining stone with a pickaxe).\n  if target_primitive_id not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  # Retrieve the current state of the game world to get grid layout and agent's position.\n  current_game_state = env._current_state\n  agent_current_pos = current_game_state.pos  # (x, y) tuple\n  current_world_grid = current_game_state.grid # numpy.ndarray (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  \n  # Get grid dimensions for boundary checks.\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = current_world_grid.shape\n\n  # Identify entities that act as obstacles (cannot be walked through).\n  # These are usually \"non-grabbable\" items that occupy space.\n  impassable_kind_ids = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # Define possible movements: (delta_x, delta_y, action_constant)\n  # These tuples represent how coordinates change and which action causes that change.\n  possible_moves = [\n      (0, -1, ACTION_UP),    # Move North: Decreases Y\n      (0, 1, ACTION_DOWN),   # Move South: Increases Y\n      (-1, 0, ACTION_LEFT),  # Move West: Decreases X\n      (1, 0, ACTION_RIGHT)   # Move East: Increases X\n  ]\n\n  # Initialize Breadth-First Search (BFS)\n  # `queue` stores tuples: (current_coordinates, list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here)\n  pathfinding_queue = collections.deque([(agent_current_pos, [])])\n  # `visited_cells` keeps track of grid cells already explored to prevent cycles and redundant paths.\n  visited_cells = {agent_current_pos}\n\n  # Start the BFS traversal\n  while pathfinding_queue:\n    (cx, cy), path_trace = pathfinding_queue.popleft()\n\n    # Check if the current cell contains the target primitive.\n    # `current_world_grid[cx, cy, target_primitive_id] > 0` checks for presence.\n    if current_world_grid[cx, cy, target_primitive_id] > 0:\n      # If found, the path to this cell is complete. Append the 'USE' action to collect it.\n      return path_trace + [ACTION_USE]\n\n    # Explore all adjacent (neighboring) cells.\n    for dx, dy, action_to_take in possible_moves:\n      next_x, next_y = cx + dx, cy + dy  # Calculate neighbor's coordinates\n      next_cell_coords = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # 1. Boundary check: Ensure the neighbor is within the grid dimensions.\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue\n\n      # 2. Visited check: Skip if this cell has already been processed in the BFS.\n      if next_cell_coords in visited_cells:\n        continue\n\n      # 3. Obstacle check: Determine if the neighbor cell is blocked by an impassable object.\n      # A cell is blocked if it contains any of the predefined `impassable_kind_ids`.\n      is_cell_blocked = False\n      for obstacle_id in impassable_kind_ids:\n        if current_world_grid[next_x, next_y, obstacle_id] > 0:\n          is_cell_blocked = True\n          break # This cell contains an obstacle, no need to check further obstacles for this cell.\n      \n      if is_cell_blocked:\n        continue # Cannot move to a blocked cell.\n\n      # If the neighbor cell is valid (within bounds, unvisited, and traversable),\n      # add it to the queue for further exploration and mark it as visited.\n      visited_cells.add(next_cell_coords)\n      pathfinding_queue.append((next_cell_coords, path_trace + [action_to_take]))\n\n  # If the BFS queue becomes empty and the primitive was not found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable from the current agent's position.\n  return []", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:13:39.178438", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  # If the primitive name is not found in the cookbook's index, it cannot be collected.\n  if primitive_id is None:\n      return []\n\n  state = env._current_state\n  current_pos = state.pos\n  grid = state.grid\n  \n  # Grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  width, height, _ = grid.shape \n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment\n  actions_map = env.action_specs()\n  # Action IDs based on env.action_specs() which states: DOWN\u21920, UP\u21921, LEFT\u21922, RIGHT\u21923, USE\u21924\n  ACTION_DOWN = actions_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_UP = actions_map['UP']\n  ACTION_LEFT = actions_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = actions_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = actions_map['USE']\n\n  # Mapping from CraftState.dir (0=UP, 1=DOWN, 2=LEFT, 3=RIGHT) to (dr, dc) for \"forward\" cell.\n  # This corresponds to how agent's facing direction translates to a relative cell in front of it.\n  dir_to_delta = {\n      0: (-1, 0), # UP: row-1, col\n      1: (1, 0),  # DOWN: row+1, col\n      2: (0, -1), # LEFT: row, col-1\n      3: (0, 1),  # RIGHT: row, col+1\n  }\n\n  # Mapping from an action ID (like ACTION_UP, ACTION_DOWN, etc.) to the resulting\n  # CraftState.dir ID after taking that action.\n  action_to_resulting_dir_id = {\n      ACTION_UP: 0,\n      ACTION_DOWN: 1,\n      ACTION_LEFT: 2,\n      ACTION_RIGHT: 3,\n  }\n\n  # Define possible movements (dr, dc, action_index) for BFS exploration.\n  # This maps a relative movement vector to the action that achieves it.\n  move_deltas = [\n      (dir_to_delta[0][0], dir_to_delta[0][1], ACTION_UP),    # (-1, 0), ACTION_UP\n      (dir_to_delta[1][0], dir_to_delta[1][1], ACTION_DOWN),   # (1, 0), ACTION_DOWN\n      (dir_to_delta[2][0], dir_to_delta[2][1], ACTION_LEFT),   # (0, -1), ACTION_LEFT\n      (dir_to_delta[3][0], dir_to_delta[3][1], ACTION_RIGHT)   # (0, 1), ACTION_RIGHT\n  ]\n\n  # BFS queue: stores tuples of ((row, col), current_dir_id, [list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_this_state])\n  # current_dir_id is the agent's facing direction (0=UP, 1=DOWN, etc.)\n  q = collections.deque([(current_pos, state.dir, [])])\n  \n  # Set to keep track of visited states to avoid cycles and redundant paths.\n  # A state is defined by agent's position AND facing direction.\n  visited = {(current_pos, state.dir)}\n\n  while q:\n      (r, c), d_id, path_actions = q.popleft()\n\n      # 1. Check if the current state (position and direction) allows for collection.\n      # Calculate the coordinates of the cell directly in front of the agent.\n      fr, fc = r + dir_to_delta[d_id][0], c + dir_to_delta[d_id][1]\n\n      # If the cell in front (fr, fc) is within grid bounds AND contains the primitive,\n      # then we have found a valid path to collect it.\n      if (0 <= fr < width and 0 <= fc < height) and grid[fr, fc, primitive_id] > 0:\n          return path_actions + [ACTION_USE] # Append USE action and return the complete sequence.\n\n      # 2. Explore possible next states by taking movement actions.\n      for dr, dc, action_to_take in move_deltas:\n          nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc # Calculate new position after movement\n          new_d_id = action_to_resulting_dir_id[action_to_take] # Determine new facing direction\n\n          next_bfs_state = ((nr, nc), new_d_id)\n\n          # Boundary check: Ensure the new position is within the grid.\n          if not (0 <= nr < width and 0 <= nc < height):\n              continue\n\n          # Obstacle check: Determine if the agent can move to (nr, nc).\n          # A cell is considered impassable for movement if it contains:\n          # a) Water (always blocking for movement).\n          # b) The primitive itself AND it's a grabbable resource (as these are collected from adjacent cells, not by stepping on).\n          # c) Any other non-grabbable item that is NOT a workshop (workshops are typically traversable).\n          is_impassable = False\n          \n          # Check for water\n          if grid[nr, nc, env.world.water_index] > 0:\n              is_impassable = True\n          \n          # Check if the destination cell contains the primitive we are collecting\n          # AND if that primitive is categorized as a \"grabbable\" resource.\n          # Grabbable resources are typically collected from an adjacent square, not by moving onto them.\n          if primitive_id in env.world.grabbable_indices and grid[nr, nc, primitive_id] > 0:\n              is_impassable = True\n          \n          # Check for other non-grabbable entities that might block movement.\n          for k_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n              if grid[nr, nc, k_idx] > 0: # If this non-grabbable entity is present in the cell\n                  # Workshops (WORKSHOP0, WORKSHOP1, WORKSHOP2) are generally traversable,\n                  # so they are not considered obstacles for movement.\n                  if k_idx in env.world.workshop_indices:\n                      continue\n                  \n                  # If it's the primitive itself AND it's a non-grabbable type (like a fixed STONE block)\n                  # AND it's not a workshop, then it's an obstacle.\n                  # (This covers cases where 'primitive' might be a non-grabbable terrain type like STONE).\n                  if k_idx == primitive_id:\n                      is_impassable = True\n                      break\n                  \n                  # If it's any other non-grabbable, non-workshop item (e.g., BOUNDARY, solid walls),\n                  # it's an obstacle.\n                  is_impassable = True\n                  break\n          \n          if is_impassable:\n              continue # Cannot move to this cell, try next movement.\n\n          # If the new state (position and direction) has not been visited, add it to the queue.\n          if next_bfs_state not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_bfs_state)\n              q.append((next_bfs_state[0], next_bfs_state[1], path_actions + [action_to_take]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and no path to collect the primitive was found.\n  return []", "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:13:40.418838", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1` with a more robust obstacle avoidance.\"\"\"\n  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  if primitive_id is None:\n      return []\n\n  state = env._current_state\n  \n  # If the primitive is already in the inventory, no actions are needed.\n  if state.inventory[primitive_id] > 0:\n      return []\n  \n  current_pos = state.pos\n  grid = state.grid\n  width, height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  actions_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_DOWN = actions_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_UP = actions_map['UP']\n  ACTION_LEFT = actions_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = actions_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = actions_map['USE']\n\n  # Mapping from CraftState.dir (0=UP, 1=DOWN, 2=LEFT, 3=RIGHT) to (dr, dc)\n  # These deltas indicate the cell directly in front of the agent based on its facing direction.\n  dir_to_delta = {\n      0: (-1, 0), # UP: row-1, col\n      1: (1, 0),  # DOWN: row+1, col\n      2: (0, -1), # LEFT: row, col-1\n      3: (0, 1),  # RIGHT: row, col+1\n  }\n\n  # Mapping from a movement action ID to the resulting CraftState.dir ID after taking that action.\n  action_to_resulting_dir_id = {\n      ACTION_UP: 0,\n      ACTION_DOWN: 1,\n      ACTION_LEFT: 2,\n      ACTION_RIGHT: 3,\n  }\n\n  # Define possible movements (dr, dc, action_index) for BFS exploration.\n  # These are the relative changes in (row, col) and the action that causes them.\n  move_deltas = [\n      (dir_to_delta[0][0], dir_to_delta[0][1], ACTION_UP),\n      (dir_to_delta[1][0], dir_to_delta[1][1], ACTION_DOWN),\n      (dir_to_delta[2][0], dir_to_delta[2][1], ACTION_LEFT),\n      (dir_to_delta[3][0], dir_to_delta[3][1], ACTION_RIGHT)\n  ]\n\n  # BFS queue: stores tuples of ((row, col), current_dir_id, [list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_this_state])\n  # `current_dir_id` is crucial because the `USE` action depends on the agent's facing direction.\n  q = collections.deque([(current_pos, state.dir, [])])\n  \n  # Set to keep track of visited states to avoid cycles and redundant paths.\n  # A state in this context is defined by the agent's position AND its facing direction.\n  visited = {(current_pos, state.dir)}\n\n  while q:\n      (r, c), d_id, path_actions = q.popleft()\n\n      # Check if the current state (position and direction) allows for collection.\n      # Calculate the coordinates of the cell directly in front of the agent.\n      fr, fc = r + dir_to_delta[d_id][0], c + dir_to_delta[d_id][1]\n\n      # If the cell in front (fr, fc) is within grid bounds AND contains the primitive,\n      # then we have found a valid path to collect it.\n      if (0 <= fr < width and 0 <= fc < height) and grid[fr, fc, primitive_id] > 0:\n          return path_actions + [ACTION_USE] # Append USE action and return the complete sequence.\n\n      # Explore possible next states by taking movement actions (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT).\n      for dr, dc, action_to_take in move_deltas:\n          nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc # Calculate new position after attempting movement\n          new_d_id = action_to_resulting_dir_id[action_to_take] # Determine new facing direction\n\n          next_bfs_state = ((nr, nc), new_d_id)\n\n          # Boundary check: Ensure the new position is within the grid.\n          if not (0 <= nr < width and 0 <= nc < height):\n              continue\n\n          # Determine if the agent can move to (nr, nc) based on terrain features.\n          is_impassable = False\n          \n          # Rule 1: Cannot move into a cell containing WATER.\n          if grid[nr, nc, env.world.water_index] > 0:\n              is_impassable = True\n          \n          # Rule 2: Cannot move into any non-grabbable item that is not a workshop.\n          # Workshops (like BENCH) are typically non-grabbable but traversable.\n          if not is_impassable: # Only check if not already deemed impassable by Rule 1\n              for item_id in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n                  if item_id == env.world.water_index: # Water handled by Rule 1, skip\n                      continue\n                  if item_id in env.world.workshop_indices: # Workshops are traversable, skip\n                      continue\n                  \n                  if grid[nr, nc, item_id] > 0: # If the cell contains this non-grabbable, non-workshop item\n                      is_impassable = True\n                      break # Found an impassable non-grabbable item\n          \n          # Rule 3: Cannot move into any grabbable item.\n          # Grabbable items (like WOOD, IRON, STONE, GRASS, ROCK, GOLD, GEM) are typically\n          # collected from an adjacent square, implying the agent cannot occupy the same cell.\n          if not is_impassable: # Only check if not already deemed impassable by Rule 1 or Rule 2\n              for item_id in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n                  if grid[nr, nc, item_id] > 0: # If the cell contains any grabbable item\n                      is_impassable = True\n                      break # Found a grabbable item blocking movement\n\n          if is_impassable:\n              continue # Cannot move to this cell, try next movement.\n\n          # If the new state (position and direction) has not been visited, add it to the queue.\n          if next_bfs_state not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_bfs_state)\n              q.append((next_bfs_state[0], next_bfs_state[1], path_actions + [action_to_take]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and no path to collect the primitive was found.\n  return []", "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:14:58.734393", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Returns a list of actions to find and collect the primitive in the passed env.\n    Uses A* search for potentially faster pathfinding on large grids,\n    while still respecting direction for 'USE' actions.\n    \n    Args:\n        env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab object.\n        primitive (str): The name of the primitive to collect.\n\n    Returns:\n        List[int]: A sequence of action indices to execute.\n  \"\"\"\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  # Retrieve the integer ID for the target primitive from the world's cookbook index.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n  \n  # Map action names to their corresponding integer IDs for readability and consistency.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  UP = action_map['UP']\n  LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Helper to map (dx, dy) from agent_pos to target_pos to the required agent direction.\n  # CraftState dir: 0=N, 1=E, 2=S, 3=W (North, East, South, West)\n  DXDY_TO_DIR_INDEX = {\n      (0, -1): 0, # North (Move Up on grid, agent faces North)\n      (1, 0): 1,  # East (Move Right on grid, agent faces East)\n      (0, 1): 2,  # South (Move Down on grid, agent faces South)\n      (-1, 0): 3, # West (Move Left on grid, agent faces West)\n  }\n\n  # Helper to map a movement action to the resulting agent's facing direction index.\n  ACTION_TO_RESULTING_DIR_INDEX = {\n      UP: 0,    # Moving UP (action for Y-) results in facing North (dir 0)\n      RIGHT: 1, # Moving RIGHT (action for X+) results in facing East (dir 1)\n      DOWN: 2,  # Moving DOWN (action for Y+) results in facing South (dir 2)\n      LEFT: 3,  # Moving LEFT (action for X-) results in facing West (dir 3)\n  }\n\n  # Direction vectors corresponding to agent's dir (0:N, 1:E, 2:S, 3:W)\n  DIR_INDEX_TO_DXDY = {\n      0: (0, -1), # North: (dx, dy) to cell in front\n      1: (1, 0),  # East: (dx, dy) to cell in front\n      2: (0, 1),  # South: (dx, dy) to cell in front\n      3: (-1, 0), # West: (dx, dy) to cell in front\n  }\n\n  # Define possible movement actions and their resulting agent directions.\n  # This is used for exploring neighbors in the search.\n  MOVE_ACTIONS_AND_NEW_DIRS = [\n      ((0, -1), UP, ACTION_TO_RESULTING_DIR_INDEX[UP]),    # Move Y- (Up on grid), action UP, new dir North\n      ((0, 1), DOWN, ACTION_TO_RESULTING_DIR_INDEX[DOWN]), # Move Y+ (Down on grid), action DOWN, new dir South\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT, ACTION_TO_RESULTING_DIR_INDEX[LEFT]),# Move X- (Left on grid), action LEFT, new dir West\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT, ACTION_TO_RESULTING_DIR_INDEX[RIGHT]),# Move X+ (Right on grid), action RIGHT, new dir East\n  ]\n\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Step 1: Immediate collection check.\n  # If the agent is already positioned and facing the primitive, 'USE' it.\n  cx, cy = current_state.pos\n  current_dir_idx = current_state.dir\n  \n  if current_dir_idx in DIR_INDEX_TO_DXDY:\n      dx, dy = DIR_INDEX_TO_DXDY[current_dir_idx]\n      target_x, target_y = cx + dx, cy + dy\n      \n      # Check if the cell directly in front contains the primitive\n      if (0 <= target_x < grid_width and 0 <= target_y < grid_height and \n          grid[target_x, target_y, primitive_idx] > 0):\n          return [USE]\n\n  # Step 2: Locate all occurrences of the primitive on the grid.\n  primitive_locations_on_grid = [] # Stores (x, y) coordinates of primitive instances\n  for x in range(grid_width):\n    for y in range(grid_height):\n      # If the count of the primitive at (x, y) is greater than 0, it's present.\n      if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n        primitive_locations_on_grid.append((x, y))\n\n  # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the grid, it's currently unreachable.\n  if not primitive_locations_on_grid:\n    return []\n\n  # Step 3: Define \"goal states\" for A* search.\n  # A goal state is a (agent_x, agent_y, agent_dir) tuple from which the 'USE' action\n  # will successfully collect the primitive. This means the primitive must be\n  # directly in front of the agent at that (x,y,dir) state.\n  goal_states = set()\n  for px, py in primitive_locations_on_grid:\n    # Iterate through the 4 cardinal neighbors of the primitive's location.\n    # An agent must be at one of these neighboring cells to face and USE the primitive.\n    for dx_rel, dy_rel in [(0, -1), (0, 1), (-1, 0), (1, 0)]: # Relative to primitive: N, S, W, E\n      gx, gy = px + dx_rel, py + dy_rel # Agent's potential position\n\n      # Ensure the potential agent position is within grid boundaries\n      if not (0 <= gx < grid_width and 0 <= gy < grid_height):\n        continue\n      \n      # The agent at (gx, gy) must face (px, py). Calculate the required facing direction.\n      required_dx, required_dy = px - gx, py - gy\n      \n      if (required_dx, required_dy) in DXDY_TO_DIR_INDEX:\n        required_agent_dir = DXDY_TO_DIR_INDEX[(required_dx, required_dy)]\n        goal_states.add((gx, gy, required_agent_dir))\n\n  # If no valid goal states can be formed (e.g., primitive is completely surrounded by impassable, or map edge)\n  if not goal_states:\n      return []\n\n  # Step 4: Identify impassable terrain.\n  # The agent cannot move into cells occupied by non-grabbable entities that are not workshops.\n  impassable_kinds = set()\n  for idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n      if idx not in env.world.workshop_indices: \n          impassable_kinds.add(idx)\n\n  # Step 5: Perform A* search to find the shortest path.\n  start_pos_x, start_pos_y = current_state.pos\n  start_node = (start_pos_x, start_pos_y, current_state.dir)\n\n  # Priority queue for A*: stores (f_cost, g_cost, (x, y, dir))\n  # f_cost = g_cost + h_cost\n  pq = [(0, 0, start_node)] \n  \n  # g_costs: stores the actual cost from the start node to the current node (x, y, dir)\n  g_costs = {start_node: 0}\n  \n  # came_from: stores (parent_x, parent_y, parent_dir, action_to_reach_here) for path reconstruction\n  came_from = {start_node: (None, None, None, None)}\n\n  # Heuristic function: Manhattan distance from current (x, y) to the closest (gx, gy) of any goal state.\n  # This is admissible (never overestimates) as it's the shortest path without obstacles,\n  # and ignores the direction component (which doesn't add movement cost).\n  def h(node_x, node_y):\n      min_dist = float('inf')\n      for gx, gy, _ in goal_states:\n          dist = abs(node_x - gx) + abs(node_y - gy)\n          min_dist = min(min_dist, dist)\n      return min_dist\n\n  found_goal_state = None\n\n  while pq:\n    # Pop the node with the lowest f_cost\n    f_cost, current_g_cost, (cx, cy, c_dir) = heapq.heappop(pq)\n    current_node = (cx, cy, c_dir)\n\n    # If we've already found a shorter path to this node, skip it\n    if current_g_cost > g_costs.get(current_node, float('inf')):\n        continue\n\n    # If the current node is one of our goal states, we've found the shortest path.\n    if current_node in goal_states:\n      found_goal_state = current_node\n      break # Exit the A* loop\n\n    # Explore valid neighboring states (position, direction)\n    for (dx, dy), action, n_dir in MOVE_ACTIONS_AND_NEW_DIRS:\n      nx, ny = cx + dx, cy + dy\n      new_node = (nx, ny, n_dir)\n      \n      # Each movement action has a cost of 1.\n      new_g_cost = current_g_cost + 1\n\n      # Check 1: Ensure the new position is within grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height):\n        continue\n\n      # Check 2: Determine if the new position is occupied by impassable terrain.\n      is_impassable_location = False\n      for k_idx in impassable_kinds:\n          # If any impassable kind is present at the new position (count > 0), it's blocked.\n          if grid[nx, ny, k_idx] > 0: \n              is_impassable_location = True\n              break\n      \n      if is_impassable_location:\n          continue\n\n      # Check 3: If a shorter path to new_node is found or it's a new node.\n      if new_g_cost < g_costs.get(new_node, float('inf')):\n        g_costs[new_node] = new_g_cost\n        f_cost = new_g_cost + h(nx, ny) # Calculate f_cost\n        heapq.heappush(pq, (f_cost, new_g_cost, new_node)) # Add to priority queue\n        came_from[new_node] = (cx, cy, c_dir, action) # Store parent and action for path reconstruction\n\n  # If the A* search completes and no path to any goal state was found, the primitive is unreachable.\n  if found_goal_state is None:\n    return []\n\n  # Step 6: Reconstruct the path of actions from the start state to the found goal state.\n  path_actions = []\n  current_path_node = found_goal_state\n  \n  # Backtrack from the found goal state until the initial state is reached.\n  while current_path_node != start_node:\n    px, py, p_dir, action_taken = came_from[current_path_node]\n    path_actions.append(action_taken)\n    current_path_node = (px, py, p_dir)\n  \n  path_actions.reverse() # Path was built in reverse order, so reverse it.\n\n  # Append the 'USE' action at the end to collect the primitive.\n  return path_actions + [USE]", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:14:59.901517", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  world = env.world\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n  \n  # 1. Map primitive name to its integer ID and action names to their IDs.\n  primitive_idx = world.cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP_ACTION = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN_ACTION = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define agent direction mapping: 0=N (Up), 1=E (Right), 2=S (Down), 3=W (Left)\n  # These correspond to CraftState.dir attribute.\n  DIR_NORTH = 0\n  DIR_EAST = 1\n  DIR_SOUTH = 2\n  DIR_WEST = 3\n\n  # Helper dictionaries for direction calculations\n  # (dx, dy) vector -> agent's required facing direction index\n  # This maps a vector from agent_pos to target_pos to the direction the agent needs to face.\n  VEC_TO_DIR_INDEX = {\n      (0, -1): DIR_NORTH,  # Target is North of agent\n      (1, 0): DIR_EAST,    # Target is East of agent\n      (0, 1): DIR_SOUTH,   # Target is South of agent\n      (-1, 0): DIR_WEST,   # Target is West of agent\n  }\n\n  # Agent action -> resulting agent facing direction index\n  # Moving UP makes agent face North, etc.\n  ACTION_TO_RESULTING_DIR_INDEX = {\n      UP_ACTION: DIR_NORTH,\n      RIGHT_ACTION: DIR_EAST,\n      DOWN_ACTION: DIR_SOUTH,\n      LEFT_ACTION: DIR_WEST,\n  }\n\n  # Agent's direction index -> (dx, dy) vector for the cell directly in front\n  # Used to determine which cell 'USE' would affect based on agent's current direction.\n  DIR_INDEX_TO_FRONT_VEC = {\n      DIR_NORTH: (0, -1),\n      DIR_EAST: (1, 0),\n      DIR_SOUTH: (0, 1),\n      DIR_WEST: (-1, 0),\n  }\n\n  # 2. Initial check: Can the primitive be collected immediately with 'USE'?\n  # This means the primitive must be in the cell directly in front of the agent.\n  agent_x, agent_y = current_state.pos\n  agent_dir = current_state.dir\n  \n  if agent_dir in DIR_INDEX_TO_FRONT_VEC:\n      front_dx, front_dy = DIR_INDEX_TO_FRONT_VEC[agent_dir]\n      target_x_front, target_y_front = agent_x + front_dx, agent_y + front_dy\n      \n      # Check if the cell in front is within bounds and contains the primitive\n      if (0 <= target_x_front < grid_width and 0 <= target_y_front < grid_height and \n          grid[target_x_front, target_y_front, primitive_idx] > 0):\n          return [USE_ACTION] # Primitive is directly collectable\n\n  # 3. Locate all cardinal (N, S, E, W) adjacent positions for the primitive on the grid.\n  # We need to find primitive instances that can be reached by a 'USE' action.\n  # 'USE' applies to the cell directly in front of the agent.\n  # Therefore, we seek agent positions (gx, gy) from which, when facing the primitive,\n  # the primitive (px, py) is directly ahead.\n  \n  primitive_grid_locations = [] # Stores (x, y) coordinates of primitive instances\n  for x in range(grid_width):\n    for y in range(grid_height):\n      if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n        primitive_grid_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  # If no primitive instances are found on the grid, it's unreachable.\n  if not primitive_grid_locations:\n    return []\n\n  # 4. Define \"goal states\" for BFS. A goal state is (agent_x, agent_y, agent_direction)\n  # from which a single 'USE' action will collect the primitive.\n  goal_states = set()\n  # Define relative vectors for agent positions surrounding a primitive.\n  # (dx, dy) are relative to the primitive's position (px, py).\n  # e.g., (-1, 0) means agent is to the West of primitive.\n  AGENT_RELATIVE_POSITIONS = [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)] # W, E, N, S relative to primitive\n  \n  for px, py in primitive_grid_locations:\n    for dx_rel, dy_rel in AGENT_RELATIVE_POSITIONS:\n      # Candidate agent position (gx, gy) to collect this primitive (px, py)\n      gx, gy = px + dx_rel, py + dy_rel\n\n      # Ensure this candidate agent position is within grid boundaries\n      if not (0 <= gx < grid_width and 0 <= gy < grid_height):\n        continue\n      \n      # The agent at (gx, gy) needs to face (px, py).\n      # Calculate the vector from the candidate agent position to the primitive position.\n      vec_to_primitive = (px - gx, py - gy)\n      \n      # Determine the required agent direction to face the primitive\n      if vec_to_primitive in VEC_TO_DIR_INDEX:\n        required_agent_dir = VEC_TO_DIR_INDEX[vec_to_primitive]\n        goal_states.add((gx, gy, required_agent_dir))\n\n  # If no valid goal states can be formed (e.g., primitive is surrounded by walls), it's unreachable.\n  if not goal_states:\n      return []\n\n  # 5. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path.\n  # The BFS state is (x, y, current_direction_of_agent).\n  start_bfs_state = (current_state.pos[0], current_state.pos[1], current_state.dir)\n  \n  # BFS queue: stores (current_x, current_y, current_dir)\n  q = collections.deque([start_bfs_state]) \n  \n  # Visited set: stores (x, y, dir) states that have been processed.\n  # We also store parent state and action to reconstruct the path.\n  # Format: {(x, y, dir): (parent_x, parent_y, parent_dir, action_to_reach_here)}\n  visited_paths = {start_bfs_state: (None, None, None, None)}\n\n  # Define possible movement actions, their (dx, dy) effect, and the resulting agent direction.\n  # Note: A move action changes the agent's position AND sets its direction.\n  # Example: UP_ACTION moves agent North and makes agent face North.\n  MOVEMENT_ACTIONS = [\n      ((0, -1), UP_ACTION, ACTION_TO_RESULTING_DIR_INDEX[UP_ACTION]),     # Move North\n      ((0, 1), DOWN_ACTION, ACTION_TO_RESULTING_DIR_INDEX[DOWN_ACTION]),  # Move South\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT_ACTION, ACTION_TO_RESULTING_DIR_INDEX[LEFT_ACTION]), # Move West\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT_ACTION, ACTION_TO_RESULTING_DIR_INDEX[RIGHT_ACTION]),# Move East\n  ]\n\n  # Identify impassable terrain. Agent cannot move onto these cells.\n  # These are non-grabbable items that are not workshops (workshops are typically traversable).\n  impassable_kinds = set()\n  for idx in world.non_grabbable_indices:\n      if idx not in world.workshop_indices: \n          impassable_kinds.add(idx)\n\n  found_goal_state = None\n\n  while q:\n    cx, cy, c_dir = q.popleft()\n    current_bfs_state = (cx, cy, c_dir)\n\n    # If the current state (position and direction) matches one of our goal states,\n    # we've found the shortest path to a collectable position.\n    if current_bfs_state in goal_states:\n      found_goal_state = current_bfs_state\n      break\n\n    # Explore valid next states by applying movement actions.\n    for (dx, dy), action_id, next_dir in MOVEMENT_ACTIONS:\n      nx, ny = cx + dx, cy + dy # Calculate new position\n      next_bfs_state = (nx, ny, next_dir) # New state includes new position AND new direction\n\n      # Check 1: Ensure new position is within grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height):\n        continue\n\n      # Check 2: Determine if the new position is occupied by impassable terrain.\n      is_impassable_location = False\n      for k_idx in impassable_kinds:\n          if grid[nx, ny, k_idx] > 0: # If impassable kind is present at new_pos (count > 0)\n              is_impassable_location = True\n              break\n      \n      if is_impassable_location:\n          continue\n\n      # Check 3: If this (position, direction) state has not been visited, add it to the queue.\n      if next_bfs_state not in visited_paths:\n        visited_paths[next_bfs_state] = (cx, cy, c_dir, action_id) # Store parent and action\n        q.append(next_bfs_state)\n\n  # 6. Reconstruct the path of actions if a goal state was found.\n  if found_goal_state is None:\n    return [] # No path found\n\n  path_actions = []\n  current_path_state = found_goal_state\n  \n  # Backtrack from the found goal state to the initial state\n  while current_path_state != start_bfs_state:\n    parent_x, parent_y, parent_dir, action_taken = visited_paths[current_path_state]\n    path_actions.append(action_taken)\n    current_path_state = (parent_x, parent_y, parent_dir)\n  \n  path_actions.reverse() # Path was built in reverse, so reverse it for correct order\n\n  # Append the 'USE' action at the end to collect the primitive.\n  return path_actions + [USE_ACTION]", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:16:17.908492", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  grid_width, grid_height, n_kinds = grid.shape\n\n  # Get primitive ID from the cookbook's index\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Determine if the primitive is a grabbable resource or a workshop location\n  is_grabbable_primitive = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop_primitive = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n  \n  # Handle uncollectible and non-interactive environment elements (e.g., BOUNDARY, WATER).\n  # If the primitive is a non-grabbable item that is not a workshop, and it's something\n  # that cannot be \"collected\" in the typical sense (e.g., acquired into inventory via USE).\n  # WATER and BOUNDARY are common examples that the agent might move through but not collect.\n  if primitive_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices and not is_workshop_primitive:\n      # Explicitly check for WATER and BOUNDARY indices. If the primitive to collect is one of these,\n      # it generally means the goal is to simply be adjacent to or on it, not to \"collect\" it.\n      # Given 'collect' usually implies adding to inventory, we return an empty list if it's truly uncollectible.\n      if primitive_idx == env.world.water_index or \\\n         primitive_idx == env.world.cookbook.index[\"BOUNDARY\"]:\n          return []\n\n  # BFS to find the primitive's location and the path to it\n  # Queue stores tuples of (current_position, actions_to_reach_here)\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])])\n  visited = {start_pos}\n\n  # Map actions to their integer values from action_specs\n  ACTIONS = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP, ACTION_DOWN, ACTION_LEFT, ACTION_RIGHT, ACTION_USE = (\n      ACTIONS['UP'], ACTIONS['DOWN'], ACTIONS['LEFT'], ACTIONS['RIGHT'], ACTIONS['USE']\n  )\n\n  # --- IMPROVED is_passable FUNCTION for collect_v2 ---\n  # This version more accurately distinguishes between truly impassable obstacles\n  # (like BOUNDARY) and traversable terrain features (like WATER or WORKSHOPS).\n  def is_passable(x, y):\n      # Check if coordinates are within grid bounds\n      if not (0 <= x < grid_width and 0 <= y < grid_height):\n          return False\n      \n      # A cell is blocked if it contains a definitive, impassable obstacle like a BOUNDARY.\n      # Other non-grabbable items (like WATER, or workshops) are considered traversable.\n      # Grabbable items (like WOOD, STONE) are also traversable as the agent moves onto them to collect.\n      \n      kinds_at_cell = np.where(grid[x, y] == 1)[0]\n      \n      for kind_at_cell_idx in kinds_at_cell:\n          # If the cell contains a 'BOUNDARY' item, it is strictly impassable.\n          if kind_at_cell_idx == env.world.cookbook.index[\"BOUNDARY\"]:\n              return False\n      return True\n\n  while queue:\n      (curr_x, curr_y), path_actions = queue.popleft()\n\n      # Check if the primitive is located at the current position.\n      # For grabbable primitives and workshops, we must be ON the cell.\n      if grid[curr_x, curr_y, primitive_idx] == 1:\n          final_actions = list(path_actions) # Make a copy of the path taken\n          \n          # If the primitive is a grabbable item (e.g., WOOD, STONE),\n          # append a USE action to collect/harvest it into inventory.\n          # If it's a workshop, just reaching it is sufficient for the 'collect' function\n          # (crafting would typically be handled by a separate 'craft' DSL command, not 'collect').\n          if is_grabbable_primitive:\n              final_actions.append(ACTION_USE)\n          return final_actions\n\n      # Explore neighboring cells (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT)\n      neighbors = [\n          (0, -1, ACTION_UP),    # Move UP\n          (0, 1, ACTION_DOWN),   # Move DOWN\n          (-1, 0, ACTION_LEFT),  # Move LEFT\n          (1, 0, ACTION_RIGHT)   # Move RIGHT\n      ]\n\n      for dx, dy, action in neighbors:\n          next_x, next_y = curr_x + dx, curr_y + dy\n\n          # If the neighbor is passable and hasn't been visited yet, add it to the queue.\n          if is_passable(next_x, next_y) and (next_x, next_y) not in visited:\n              visited.add((next_x, next_y))\n              queue.append(((next_x, next_y), path_actions + [action]))\n\n  # If the primitive is not found or is not reachable through passable cells\n  return []", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:16:19.065830", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  grid_width, grid_height, n_kinds = grid.shape\n\n  # Get primitive ID from the cookbook's index. Use .get() for safety.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.get(primitive)\n  if primitive_idx is None:\n      # If the primitive name is not recognized, it cannot be collected.\n      return []\n\n  # Determine if the primitive is a grabbable resource (e.g., WOOD, STONE) or a workshop location.\n  is_grabbable_primitive = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop_primitive = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n  \n  # Get indices for special non-grabbable, impassable elements (water and boundary).\n  water_idx = env.world.water_index\n  # 'BOUNDARY' might not always be explicitly in the grid kinds, but get its index if it is.\n  boundary_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.get('BOUNDARY') \n\n  # If the primitive itself is an impassable element (WATER, BOUNDARY), it cannot be \"collected\"\n  # in the sense of reaching or picking it up.\n  if primitive_idx == water_idx or (boundary_idx is not None and primitive_idx == boundary_idx):\n      return []\n\n  # BFS to find the primitive's location and the path to it\n  # Queue stores tuples of (current_position (x,y), actions_to_reach_here)\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])])\n  visited = {start_pos} # Set of (x, y) tuples to avoid cycles and redundant exploration.\n\n  # Map action names to their integer values from action_specs.\n  ACTIONS = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP, ACTION_DOWN, ACTION_LEFT, ACTION_RIGHT, ACTION_USE = (\n      ACTIONS['UP'], ACTIONS['DOWN'], ACTIONS['LEFT'], ACTIONS['RIGHT'], ACTIONS['USE']\n  )\n\n  # Helper function to check if a given cell (x, y) is passable for the agent.\n  def is_passable(x, y):\n      # Check if coordinates are within grid bounds.\n      if not (0 <= x < grid_width and 0 <= y < grid_height):\n          return False\n      \n      # Get all kinds (item indices) present at the specified cell (x, y).\n      kinds_at_cell = np.where(grid[x, y] == 1)[0]\n      \n      # A cell is considered impassable if it contains WATER or BOUNDARY.\n      # Workshops and grabbable items do not block movement.\n      if water_idx in kinds_at_cell:\n          return False\n      if boundary_idx is not None and boundary_idx in kinds_at_cell:\n          return False\n      \n      # If no explicit impassable elements are found, the cell is passable.\n      return True\n\n  while queue:\n      (curr_x, curr_y), path_actions = queue.popleft()\n\n      # Check if the primitive is located at the current position.\n      # A cell can contain multiple items (e.g., a workshop and an item dropped on it),\n      # so we check if the specific primitive_idx is present.\n      if grid[curr_x, curr_y, primitive_idx] == 1:\n          final_actions = list(path_actions) # Make a copy of the path taken so far.\n          \n          # If the primitive is a grabbable item (e.g., WOOD, STONE, or a crafted item on the ground),\n          # append a 'USE' action to pick it up into inventory.\n          # For workshops, just reaching the location is considered \"collecting\" it in this context,\n          # as the `craft` DSL command would handle the 'USE' action for crafting.\n          if is_grabbable_primitive:\n              final_actions.append(ACTION_USE)\n          return final_actions\n\n      # Explore neighboring cells (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT).\n      # Define possible movements and their corresponding actions.\n      neighbors = [\n          (0, -1, ACTION_UP),    # Move up (change in y)\n          (0, 1, ACTION_DOWN),   # Move down (change in y)\n          (-1, 0, ACTION_LEFT),  # Move left (change in x)\n          (1, 0, ACTION_RIGHT)   # Move right (change in x)\n      ]\n\n      for dx, dy, action in neighbors:\n          next_x, next_y = curr_x + dx, curr_y + dy\n          next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n          # If the neighbor cell is passable and has not been visited yet, add it to the queue\n          # for further exploration.\n          if is_passable(next_x, next_y) and next_pos not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_pos)\n              queue.append((next_pos, path_actions + [action]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and the primitive is not found or is not reachable (e.g.,\n  # it's surrounded by impassable obstacles), return an empty list of actions.\n  return []", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:16:51.134576", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  primitive_id = env._current_state.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, N_KINDS = grid.shape # Get N_KINDS from grid shape\n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment\n  ACTION_MAP = env.action_specs()\n  UP = ACTION_MAP['UP']\n  DOWN = ACTION_MAP['DOWN']\n  LEFT = ACTION_MAP['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = ACTION_MAP['RIGHT']\n  USE = ACTION_MAP['USE']\n\n  # Queue stores: ((current_x, current_y), list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) \n  visited = {start_pos}\n\n  best_path_actions = []\n  found_primitive_adjacent = False\n\n  # Define possible moves and their corresponding actions (dx, dy) -> action\n  # Assuming (0,0) is top-left, (row, col) or (y, x) convention for grid.\n  # (dy, dx) -> action\n  moves_directions = [\n      ((0, 1), DOWN),   # (dr, dc) for (row, col)\n      ((0, -1), UP),\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT),\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT)\n  ]\n\n  # Get non-grabbable indices from the world for pathfinding obstacles\n  non_grabbable_indices = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  while q:\n      (curr_r, curr_c), actions_so_far = q.popleft()\n\n      # Create a temporary CraftState object to use its next_to method for checking adjacency.\n      # This allows us to check if the current hypothetical position (curr_r, curr_c)\n      # is adjacent to the target primitive, without actually simulating the environment.\n      temp_state_for_check = craft.CraftState(\n          scenario=current_state.scenario,\n          grid=grid, # Use the actual environment grid for checking content\n          pos=(curr_r, curr_c),\n          dir=current_state.dir, # Direction doesn't affect next_to check\n          inventory=current_state.inventory # Inventory doesn't affect next_to check\n      )\n\n      if temp_state_for_check.next_to(primitive_id):\n          best_path_actions = actions_so_far\n          found_primitive_adjacent = True\n          break # Found the shortest path to be adjacent to the primitive\n\n      # Explore neighboring cells (cardinal directions only)\n      for (dr, dc), action_val in moves_directions:\n          next_r, next_c = curr_r + dr, curr_c + dc\n          next_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n\n          # 1. Check if the next position is within grid boundaries\n          if not (0 <= next_r < WIDTH and 0 <= next_c < HEIGHT):\n              continue\n\n          # 2. Check traversability:\n          # A cell is considered non-traversable if it contains any item\n          # whose kind index is in the world's non_grabbable_indices set (e.g., BOUNDARY, WATER, WORKSHOP structures).\n          is_traversable = True\n          for i_kind in non_grabbable_indices:\n              if grid[next_r, next_c, i_kind] == 1: # If this cell contains a non-grabbable item\n                  is_traversable = False\n                  break # This neighbor is an obstacle\n          \n          if not is_traversable:\n              continue # Skip this neighbor if it's an obstacle\n          \n          # 3. If the neighbor has not been visited and is traversable, add it to the queue\n          if next_pos not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_pos)\n              q.append((next_pos, actions_so_far + [action_val]))\n\n  final_actions = best_path_actions\n\n  # If a path to an adjacent cell was found, determine if a 'USE' action is needed.\n  # The 'collect' action typically implies interacting with the item,\n  # which for grabbable items means using the 'USE' action to pick them up.\n  if found_primitive_adjacent:\n      is_grabbable = primitive_id in current_state.world.grabbable_indices\n      if is_grabbable:\n          final_actions.append(USE)\n\n  return final_actions", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:16:52.230646", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  primitive_id = current_state.world.cookbook.index[primitive] # Get the integer ID of the primitive\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment for robustness\n  ACTION_MAP = env.action_specs()\n  UP = ACTION_MAP['UP']\n  DOWN = ACTION_MAP['DOWN']\n  LEFT = ACTION_MAP['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = ACTION_MAP['RIGHT']\n  USE = ACTION_MAP['USE']\n\n  # Queue stores: ((current_row, current_col), [list_of_actions_to_reach_here])\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) \n  visited = {start_pos} # Set to keep track of visited positions\n\n  best_path_actions = []\n  found_primitive_adjacent = False\n\n  # Define possible moves as (row_change, col_change) -> action\n  move_deltas_actions = [\n      ((1, 0), DOWN),   # Row increases (moving down)\n      ((-1, 0), UP),    # Row decreases (moving up)\n      ((0, 1), RIGHT),  # Col increases (moving right)\n      ((0, -1), LEFT)   # Col decreases (moving left)\n  ]\n\n  while q:\n      (curr_r, curr_c), actions_so_far = q.popleft()\n\n      # Check if the current hypothetical position (curr_r, curr_c) is adjacent to the primitive.\n      # We create a temporary CraftState instance to leverage its `next_to` method.\n      temp_state_for_check = craft.CraftState(\n          scenario=current_state.scenario,\n          grid=grid, # Use the current grid for accurate content check\n          pos=(curr_r, curr_c),\n          dir=current_state.dir, # Direction doesn't affect `next_to` check\n          inventory=current_state.inventory # Inventory doesn't affect `next_to` check\n      )\n\n      if temp_state_for_check.next_to(primitive_id):\n          best_path_actions = actions_so_far\n          found_primitive_adjacent = True\n          break # Found the shortest path to a position adjacent to the primitive\n\n      # Explore valid neighbors (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT)\n      for (dr, dc), action_val in move_deltas_actions:\n          next_r, next_c = curr_r + dr, curr_c + dc\n          next_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n\n          # 1. Check bounds: Ensure the new position is within the grid boundaries\n          if not (0 <= next_r < WIDTH and 0 <= next_c < HEIGHT):\n              continue\n          \n          # 2. Check traversability:\n          # A cell is considered non-traversable if it contains any item\n          # whose kind index is in the world's non_grabbable_indices set (e.g., BOUNDARY, WATER).\n          is_traversable = True\n          for i_kind in current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n              if grid[next_r, next_c, i_kind] == 1: # If this cell contains a non-grabbable item\n                  is_traversable = False\n                  break # This neighbor is an obstacle and cannot be moved into\n          \n          if not is_traversable:\n              continue # Skip this neighbor if it's an obstacle\n          \n          # 3. Check if visited: If the neighbor has not been visited, add it to the queue\n          if next_pos not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_pos)\n              new_path = actions_so_far + [action_val]\n              q.append((next_pos, new_path))\n    \n  final_actions = best_path_actions\n\n  # If a path to an adjacent cell was found, and the primitive is a grabbable item,\n  # append a 'USE' action to actually collect it into inventory.\n  # For non-grabbable primitives like WORKSHOPs, the 'USE' action might still be\n  # relevant for interaction, but the \"collect\" function implies picking up.\n  if found_primitive_adjacent:\n      is_grabbable = primitive_id in current_state.world.grabbable_indices\n      if is_grabbable:\n          final_actions.append(USE)\n  \n  return final_actions", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:17:37.556118", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1` by refining the target position logic for grabbable resources.\n    \n    Args:\n        env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab object.\n        primitive (str): The name of the primitive to collect.\n\n    Returns:\n        List[int]: A sequence of action indices to execute.\n  \"\"\"\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n  actions = []\n\n  # Get primitive ID from the cookbook's index\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  try:\n    primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    # Primitive name not found in cookbook index, cannot collect\n    return []\n\n  # Define action constants (assuming they are defined in the imported 'craft' module)\n  # These map directly to integer action codes for the environment.\n  ACTION_UP, ACTION_DOWN, ACTION_LEFT, ACTION_RIGHT, ACTION_USE = (\n      craft.UP, craft.DOWN, craft.LEFT, craft.RIGHT, craft.USE\n  )\n  \n  # Map (dr, dc) offsets for cardinal moves to their corresponding action constants\n  CARDINAL_MOVES_MAP = {\n      (-1, 0): ACTION_UP,    # Move up (decrease row index)\n      (1, 0): ACTION_DOWN,   # Move down (increase row index)\n      (0, -1): ACTION_LEFT,  # Move left (decrease column index)\n      (0, 1): ACTION_RIGHT  # Move right (increase column index)\n  }\n\n  # Primitives like 'water' are static environment features and cannot be \"collected\".\n  if primitive_idx == env.world.water_index:\n    return []\n\n  # Determine the specific interaction type required for the primitive.\n  # Grabbable resources (like wood, stone) require movement to an adjacent cell and then a 'USE' action.\n  # Workshops (like workbench) require movement directly onto their cell.\n  is_grabbable_resource = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n  \n  # If the primitive is neither a grabbable resource nor a workshop, it's considered uncollectible\n  # via this programmatic strategy (e.g., 'BOUNDARY', which is just a grid feature).\n  if not is_grabbable_resource and not is_workshop:\n      return []\n\n  # Helper function to determine if a given grid cell (r, c) is traversable by the agent.\n  def is_traversable(r, c):\n    # 1. Check if the coordinates are within the grid boundaries.\n    if not (0 <= r < grid_width and 0 <= c < grid_height):\n      return False\n\n    # 2. Check for blocking elements at this specific cell.\n    # Water is always an impassable obstacle.\n    if grid[r, c, env.world.water_index] == 1:\n      return False\n\n    # Iterate through all kinds present at the cell (r, c).\n    # If any of these kinds are non-grabbable and are *not* workshops and *not* water,\n    # then they are considered blocking obstacles for movement.\n    kinds_at_cell = np.where(grid[r, c] == 1)[0]\n    for k_idx in kinds_at_cell:\n        if k_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n            # Workshops (e.g., WORKSHOP0) are generally traversable.\n            # Water is handled above. Any other non-grabbable item blocks movement.\n            if k_idx not in env.world.workshop_indices and k_idx != env.world.water_index:\n                return False # This cell contains a non-traversable obstacle\n    return True\n\n  # 1. Identify all locations on the grid where the target primitive exists.\n  primitive_grid_locations = []\n  for r in range(grid_width):\n    for c in range(grid_height):\n      if grid[r, c, primitive_idx] == 1:\n        primitive_grid_locations.append((r, c))\n\n  if not primitive_grid_locations:\n    # The primitive is not present anywhere on the current map.\n    return []\n\n  # 2. Determine the set of target positions for the Breadth-First Search (BFS).\n  # These are the cells where the agent needs to be located to \"collect\" the primitive.\n  target_bfs_positions = set()\n  \n  if is_grabbable_resource:\n    # For grabbable resources, the agent typically needs to be in a 3x3 neighborhood\n    # *excluding its own cell* (i.e., adjacent, including diagonals) around the resource\n    # to then use it.\n    NEIGHBORHOOD_OFFSETS_ADJACENT = [\n        (dr, dc) for dr in [-1, 0, 1] for dc in [-1, 0, 1] if not (dr == 0 and dc == 0)\n    ]\n    for pr, pc in primitive_grid_locations: # For each specific instance of the primitive on the grid\n      for dr, dc in NEIGHBORHOOD_OFFSETS_ADJACENT: # Check all 8 adjacent cells\n        nr, nc = pr + dr, pc + dc # This is a potential cell for the agent to stand on\n        # Add only traversable cells to the set of target positions.\n        if is_traversable(nr, nc):\n          target_bfs_positions.add((nr, nc))\n  elif is_workshop:\n    # For workshops, the agent needs to move directly *onto* the workshop cell.\n    for pr, pc in primitive_grid_locations:\n      # Add only traversable workshop locations to the set of target positions.\n      if is_traversable(pr, pc):\n        target_bfs_positions.add((pr, pc))\n  \n  # If no reachable target positions are found (e.g., all primitive instances are blocked).\n  if not target_bfs_positions:\n    return []\n\n  # 3. Perform a Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path from the agent's current position.\n  # The queue stores tuples of (current_position (r, c), path_taken_actions_so_far).\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])])\n  # 'visited' set keeps track of grid cells already processed to avoid cycles and redundant paths.\n  visited = {start_pos} # Mark starting position as visited\n\n  path_to_target = None # This will store the shortest sequence of actions to reach a target cell.\n\n  while q:\n    (r, c), current_path = q.popleft()\n\n    # If the current cell is one of our desired target positions, we have found the shortest path.\n    if (r, c) in target_bfs_positions:\n      path_to_target = current_path\n      break # Exit BFS as the shortest path is found\n\n    # Explore valid cardinal neighbors (Up, Down, Left, Right)\n    for (dr, dc), action_val in CARDINAL_MOVES_MAP.items():\n      next_r, next_c = r + dr, c + dc # Calculate neighbor coordinates\n      \n      # Check if the neighbor cell is within bounds, has not been visited yet, and is traversable.\n      if (next_r, next_c) not in visited: # Ensure we don't re-visit cells\n        if is_traversable(next_r, next_c): # Check if the neighbor cell can be moved into\n          visited.add((next_r, next_c)) # Mark the neighbor as visited\n          # Add the neighbor to the queue with the updated path\n          q.append(((next_r, next_c), current_path + [action_val]))\n\n  # 4. Construct the final sequence of actions to return.\n  if path_to_target:\n    actions.extend(path_to_target)\n    # If the primitive is a grabbable resource, a 'USE' action is required after reaching the spot.\n    if is_grabbable_resource:\n      actions.append(ACTION_USE)\n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:17:38.694676", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n  actions = []\n\n  # Get primitive ID from the cookbook's index\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  try:\n    primitive_idx = cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n    # Primitive name not found in cookbook index, cannot collect\n    return []\n\n  # Define action constants (assuming they are defined in the imported 'craft' module)\n  # These map directly to integer action codes for the environment.\n  ACTION_UP, ACTION_DOWN, ACTION_LEFT, ACTION_RIGHT, ACTION_USE = (\n      craft.UP, craft.DOWN, craft.LEFT, craft.RIGHT, craft.USE\n  )\n  \n  # Map (dr, dc) offsets for cardinal moves to their corresponding action constants\n  CARDINAL_MOVES_MAP = {\n      (-1, 0): ACTION_UP,    # Move up (decrease row index)\n      (1, 0): ACTION_DOWN,   # Move down (increase row index)\n      (0, -1): ACTION_LEFT,  # Move left (decrease column index)\n      (0, 1): ACTION_RIGHT  # Move right (increase column index)\n  }\n\n  # Primitives like 'water' are static environment features and cannot be \"collected\".\n  if primitive_idx == env.world.water_index:\n    return []\n\n  # Determine the specific interaction type required for the primitive.\n  # Grabbable resources (like wood, stone) require movement to an adjacent cell and then a 'USE' action.\n  # Workshops (like workbench) require movement directly onto their cell.\n  is_grabbable_resource = primitive_idx in env.world.grabbable_indices\n  is_workshop = primitive_idx in env.world.workshop_indices\n  \n  # If the primitive is neither a grabbable resource nor a workshop, it's considered uncollectible\n  # via this programmatic strategy (e.g., 'BOUNDARY', which is just a grid feature).\n  if not is_grabbable_resource and not is_workshop:\n      return []\n\n  # Helper function to determine if a given grid cell (r, c) is traversable by the agent.\n  def is_traversable(r, c):\n    # 1. Check if the coordinates are within the grid boundaries.\n    if not (0 <= r < grid_width and 0 <= c < grid_height):\n      return False\n\n    # 2. Check for blocking elements at this specific cell.\n    # Water is always an impassable obstacle.\n    if grid[r, c, env.world.water_index] == 1:\n      return False\n\n    # Iterate through all kinds present at the cell (r, c).\n    # If any of these kinds are non-grabbable and are *not* workshops and *not* water,\n    # then they are considered blocking obstacles for movement.\n    kinds_at_cell = np.where(grid[r, c] == 1)[0]\n    for k_idx in kinds_at_cell:\n        if k_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n            # Workshops (e.g., WORKSHOP0) are generally traversable.\n            # Water is handled above. Any other non-grabbable item blocks movement.\n            if k_idx not in env.world.workshop_indices and k_idx != env.world.water_index:\n                return False # This cell contains a non-traversable obstacle\n    return True\n\n  # 1. Identify all locations on the grid where the target primitive exists.\n  primitive_grid_locations = []\n  for r in range(grid_width):\n    for c in range(grid_height):\n      if grid[r, c, primitive_idx] == 1:\n        primitive_grid_locations.append((r, c))\n\n  if not primitive_grid_locations:\n    # The primitive is not present anywhere on the current map.\n    return []\n\n  # 2. Determine the set of target positions for the Breadth-First Search (BFS).\n  # These are the cells where the agent needs to be located to \"collect\" the primitive.\n  target_bfs_positions = set()\n  \n  if is_grabbable_resource:\n    # For grabbable resources, the agent needs to be in a 3x3 neighborhood (including diagonals)\n    # around the resource and then use it.\n    NEIGHBORHOOD_OFFSETS_3x3 = [\n        (dr, dc) for dr in [-1, 0, 1] for dc in [-1, 0, 1]\n    ]\n    for pr, pc in primitive_grid_locations: # For each specific instance of the primitive on the grid\n      for dr, dc in NEIGHBORHOOD_OFFSETS_3x3: # Check all 9 cells around it\n        nr, nc = pr + dr, pc + dc # This is a potential cell for the agent to stand on\n        # Add only traversable cells to the set of target positions.\n        if is_traversable(nr, nc):\n          target_bfs_positions.add((nr, nc))\n  elif is_workshop:\n    # For workshops, the agent needs to move directly *onto* the workshop cell.\n    for pr, pc in primitive_grid_locations:\n      # Add only traversable workshop locations to the set of target positions.\n      if is_traversable(pr, pc):\n        target_bfs_positions.add((pr, pc))\n  \n  # If no reachable target positions are found (e.g., all primitive instances are blocked).\n  if not target_bfs_positions:\n    return []\n\n  # 3. Perform a Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path from the agent's current position.\n  # The queue stores tuples of (current_position (r, c), path_taken_actions_so_far).\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])])\n  # 'visited' set keeps track of grid cells already processed to avoid cycles and redundant paths.\n  visited = {start_pos} # Mark starting position as visited\n\n  path_to_target = None # This will store the shortest sequence of actions to reach a target cell.\n\n  while q:\n    (r, c), current_path = q.popleft()\n\n    # If the current cell is one of our desired target positions, we have found the shortest path.\n    if (r, c) in target_bfs_positions:\n      path_to_target = current_path\n      break # Exit BFS as the shortest path is found\n\n    # Explore valid cardinal neighbors (Up, Down, Left, Right)\n    for (dr, dc), action_val in CARDINAL_MOVES_MAP.items():\n      next_r, next_c = r + dr, c + dc # Calculate neighbor coordinates\n      \n      # Check if the neighbor cell is within bounds, has not been visited yet, and is traversable.\n      if (next_r, next_c) not in visited: # Ensure we don't re-visit cells\n        if is_traversable(next_r, next_c): # Check if the neighbor cell can be moved into\n          visited.add((next_r, next_c)) # Mark the neighbor as visited\n          # Add the neighbor to the queue with the updated path\n          q.append(((next_r, next_c), current_path + [action_val]))\n\n  # 4. Construct the final sequence of actions to return.\n  if path_to_target:\n    actions.extend(path_to_target)\n    # If the primitive is a grabbable resource, a 'USE' action is required after reaching the spot.\n    if is_grabbable_resource:\n      actions.append(ACTION_USE)\n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:19:02.385132", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  if primitive_id is None:\n      return []\n\n  # --- IMPROVEMENT for collect_v2 ---\n  # If the primitive is an ungrabbable environment feature (like WATER, WORKSHOP, BOUNDARY),\n  # it cannot be \"collected\" into the inventory. In such cases, no actions should be returned.\n  if primitive_id in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n  # --- End of IMPROVEMENT ---\n\n  state = env._current_state\n  current_pos = state.pos\n  current_dir = state.dir # Agent's initial facing direction (0=DOWN, 1=UP, 2=LEFT, 3=RIGHT)\n  grid = state.grid\n  \n  width, height, _ = grid.shape \n\n  actions_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP = actions_map['UP']\n  DOWN = actions_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = actions_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = actions_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = actions_map['USE']\n\n  # Map action index (which also corresponds to a direction) to its (dr, dc) delta.\n  # These deltas represent both the movement if that action is taken, and the direction faced after.\n  direction_deltas = {\n      DOWN: (1, 0),\n      UP: (-1, 0),\n      LEFT: (0, -1),\n      RIGHT: (0, 1)\n  }\n\n  # BFS setup:\n  # Queue stores tuples: ((row, col, facing_direction_idx), [list_of_actions_to_reach_this_state])\n  q = collections.deque([((current_pos[0], current_pos[1], current_dir), [])]) \n  \n  # Visited set stores (row, col, facing_direction_idx) tuples to prevent revisiting states\n  visited = {(current_pos[0], current_pos[1], current_dir)}\n\n  # Cache grabbable and non-grabbable indices for efficient lookup\n  # Note: `grabbable_indices_set` check for `primitive_id` becomes redundant inside the loop\n  # because we already filtered out non-grabbable primitives at the start.\n  non_grabbable_indices_set = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  while q:\n      (r, c, d), path_actions = q.popleft()\n\n      # 1. Check if the current (r, c, d) state allows for immediate collection via USE action.\n      # The USE action interacts with the cell directly in front of the agent.\n      dr_face, dc_face = direction_deltas[d] # Get delta for the direction agent is currently facing\n      target_r, target_c = r + dr_face, c + dc_face # Coordinates of the cell directly in front\n\n      # Ensure the target cell is within grid boundaries\n      if 0 <= target_r < width and 0 <= target_c < height:\n          # Check if the target cell contains the primitive we want to collect\n          if grid[target_r, target_c, primitive_id] > 0:\n              # Path found! Append USE action and return.\n              return path_actions + [USE] \n\n      # 2. Explore movement neighbors (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT)\n      # Each movement action changes the agent's position and sets its new facing direction.\n      for move_action in [UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT]:\n          next_dir = move_action # After moving, agent faces the direction it just moved\n          dr_move, dc_move = direction_deltas[move_action] # Delta for the movement itself\n\n          nr, nc = r + dr_move, c + dc_move # New row, new col after movement\n          next_state_tuple = (nr, nc, next_dir) # The new state (position and facing direction)\n\n          # a. Check if the next position (nr, nc) is within grid boundaries\n          if not (0 <= nr < width and 0 <= nc < height):\n              continue\n          \n          # b. Obstacle Check:\n          # A cell is considered an obstacle for movement if it contains:\n          #   - Any entity from the `non_grabbable_indices_set` (impassable terrain/structures).\n          #   - OR, the specific primitive we are trying to collect. This applies only to grabbable primitives\n          #     which are intended to be 'USE'd from an adjacent square, not walked onto.\n          is_obstacle = False\n          \n          # Check for general non-grabbable obstacles (e.g., water, workshops, boundaries)\n          for non_grabbable_item_id in non_grabbable_indices_set:\n              if grid[nr, nc, non_grabbable_item_id] > 0:\n                  is_obstacle = True\n                  break\n          \n          # Additionally, if the target primitive is present in the next cell, consider it an obstacle\n          # for movement. This forces the agent to stop adjacent to it for a 'USE' action.\n          # We already confirmed `primitive_id` is grabbable at the start of the function.\n          if not is_obstacle and grid[nr, nc, primitive_id] > 0:\n              is_obstacle = True\n\n          if is_obstacle:\n              continue\n\n          # c. If the new state (position and facing direction) has not been visited, add it to the queue\n          if next_state_tuple not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_state_tuple)\n              q.append((next_state_tuple, path_actions + [move_action]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and the primitive was not found anywhere reachable or collectable,\n  # return an empty list, indicating no path was found.\n  return []", "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:19:03.503911", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  # If primitive name doesn't exist in the index, or if it's not a grabbable item,\n  # it cannot be collected into inventory. The `collect` function in the DSL implies\n  # adding to inventory. Non-grabbable items (like WATER, WORKSHOPS, BOUNDARIES)\n  # cannot be added to inventory.\n  if primitive_id is None or primitive_id not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  state = env._current_state\n  current_pos = state.pos\n  current_dir = state.dir # Agent's initial facing direction (0=DOWN, 1=UP, 2=LEFT, 3=RIGHT)\n  grid = state.grid\n  \n  width, height, _ = grid.shape \n\n  actions_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP = actions_map['UP']\n  DOWN = actions_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = actions_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = actions_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = actions_map['USE']\n\n  # Map action index (which also corresponds to a direction) to its (dr, dc) delta.\n  # These deltas represent both the movement if that action is taken, and the direction faced after.\n  direction_deltas = {\n      DOWN: (1, 0),\n      UP: (-1, 0),\n      LEFT: (0, -1),\n      RIGHT: (0, 1)\n  }\n\n  # BFS setup:\n  # Queue stores tuples: ((row, col, facing_direction_idx), [list_of_actions_to_reach_this_state])\n  q = collections.deque([((current_pos[0], current_pos[1], current_dir), [])]) \n  \n  # Visited set stores (row, col, facing_direction_idx) tuples to prevent revisiting states\n  visited = {(current_pos[0], current_pos[1], current_dir)}\n\n  # Cache grabbable and non-grabbable indices for efficient lookup\n  grabbable_indices_set = set(env.world.grabbable_indices)\n  non_grabbable_indices_set = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  while q:\n      (r, c, d), path_actions = q.popleft()\n\n      # 1. Check if the current (r, c, d) state allows for immediate collection via USE action.\n      # The USE action interacts with the cell directly in front of the agent.\n      dr_face, dc_face = direction_deltas[d] # Get delta for the direction agent is currently facing\n      target_r, target_c = r + dr_face, c + dc_face # Coordinates of the cell directly in front\n\n      # Ensure the target cell is within grid boundaries\n      if 0 <= target_r < width and 0 <= target_c < height:\n          # Check if the target cell contains the primitive we want to collect.\n          # We've already confirmed primitive_id is grabbable at the start of the function.\n          if grid[target_r, target_c, primitive_id] > 0:\n              # Path found! Append USE action and return.\n              return path_actions + [USE] \n\n      # 2. Explore movement neighbors (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT)\n      # Each movement action changes the agent's position and sets its new facing direction.\n      for move_action in [UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT]:\n          next_dir = move_action # After moving, agent faces the direction it just moved\n          dr_move, dc_move = direction_deltas[move_action] # Delta for the movement itself\n\n          nr, nc = r + dr_move, c + dc_move # New row, new col after movement\n          next_state_tuple = (nr, nc, next_dir) # The new state (position and facing direction)\n\n          # a. Check if the next position (nr, nc) is within grid boundaries\n          if not (0 <= nr < width and 0 <= nc < height):\n              continue\n          \n          # b. Obstacle Check:\n          # A cell is considered an obstacle for movement if it contains:\n          #   - Any entity from the `non_grabbable_indices_set` (impassable terrain/structures).\n          #   - OR, the specific primitive we are trying to collect, IF that primitive is a grabbable item.\n          #     This prevents the agent from walking *onto* a grabbable item it intends to 'USE' from an adjacent square.\n          is_obstacle = False\n          \n          # Check for general non-grabbable obstacles (e.g., water, workshops, boundaries)\n          for non_grabbable_item_id in non_grabbable_indices_set:\n              if grid[nr, nc, non_grabbable_item_id] > 0:\n                  is_obstacle = True\n                  break\n          \n          # Additionally, if the target primitive is a grabbable item (which it is, due to the initial check)\n          # AND the next cell contains this primitive, consider it an obstacle for movement.\n          # This ensures the agent stops adjacent to it, ready to USE from an adjacent position.\n          # This check only applies if the cell wasn't already determined to be an obstacle by a non-grabbable item.\n          if not is_obstacle and primitive_id in grabbable_indices_set and grid[nr, nc, primitive_id] > 0:\n              is_obstacle = True\n\n          if is_obstacle:\n              continue\n\n          # c. If the new state (position and facing direction) has not been visited, add it to the queue\n          if next_state_tuple not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_state_tuple)\n              q.append((next_state_tuple, path_actions + [move_action]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and the primitive was not found anywhere reachable or collectable,\n  # return an empty list, indicating no path was found.\n  return []", "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:19:49.706258", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1` by first checking if the primitive is already in the agent's inventory.\n    \n    Args:\n        env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab object.\n        primitive (str): The name of the primitive to collect.\n\n    Returns:\n        List[int]: A sequence of action indices to execute.\n  \"\"\"\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  \n  # Get the integer index for the desired primitive.\n  # This will raise a KeyError if the primitive name is not valid.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n  \n  # --- Improvement for v2: Check if the primitive is already collected ---\n  # If the agent's inventory already contains the primitive, no actions are needed\n  # to collect it. This avoids redundant collection attempts.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return [] # Already have it, return an empty action list.\n\n  # Retrieve action mappings for clarity and to ensure correct action indices are used.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # 1. Immediate collection check:\n  # If the agent is already within the 3x3 neighborhood (including diagonals and its own cell)\n  # of the primitive, it can directly use/collect it.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n    # This means the agent is in a valid position to interact with the primitive.\n    return [USE]\n\n  # 2. Identify all grid locations where the primitive exists.\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n  \n  primitive_locations = []\n  # Iterate through the entire grid to find all cells containing the specified primitive.\n  for x in range(grid_width):\n    for y in range(grid_height):\n      # Check if the primitive kind is present at this grid cell (count > 0).\n      if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n        primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  # If no instances of the primitive are found on the grid, it's not collectible.\n  if not primitive_locations:\n    return []\n\n  # 3. Define \"goal cells\" for the Breadth-First Search (BFS).\n  # A goal cell is any cell from which the agent can successfully collect the primitive.\n  # Given that `CraftState.next_to` checks the 3x3 neighborhood, any cell in this\n  # 3x3 vicinity of a primitive location is a valid goal.\n  goal_cells = set()\n  for px, py in primitive_locations:\n    # Iterate through all 3x3 neighbors (including (0,0) for the primitive's own cell).\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        gx, gy = px + dx, py + dy\n        # Ensure the potential goal cell is within the grid boundaries.\n        if 0 <= gx < grid_width and 0 <= gy < grid_height:\n          goal_cells.add((gx, gy))\n\n  # 4. Determine which entity kinds make a cell impassable for agent movement.\n  # Impassable kinds are defined as non-grabbable items that are NOT workshops.\n  # Workshops are typically non-grabbable but often walkable/interactable locations.\n  impassable_kinds = set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices) - set(env.world.workshop_indices)\n\n  # 5. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path\n  # from the agent's current position to any of the identified goal cells.\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  \n  # The queue for BFS stores tuples of (current_position, path_taken_actions_to_reach_here).\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) \n  # A set to keep track of visited positions to prevent cycles and redundant exploration.\n  visited = {start_pos} \n\n  # Define possible cardinal moves (delta_x, delta_y) and their corresponding action indices.\n  DELTAS_ACTIONS = [\n      ((0, -1), UP),    # Move North (decreases Y coordinate)\n      ((0, 1), DOWN),   # Move South (increases Y coordinate)\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT),  # Move West (decreases X coordinate)\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT),  # Move East (increases X coordinate)\n  ]\n\n  while q:\n    (cx, cy), path_so_far = q.popleft() # Get the current position and the path to it\n\n    # If the current position is one of our goal cells, we have found the shortest path.\n    if (cx, cy) in goal_cells:\n      # Append the USE action, as the agent is now in a valid position to collect the primitive.\n      return path_so_far + [USE]\n\n    # Explore valid neighboring cells for movement (cardinal directions).\n    for (dx, dy), action in DELTAS_ACTIONS:\n      nx, ny = cx + dx, cy + dy # Calculate the new potential position\n\n      # Check if the new position is within the overall grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height):\n        continue # Skip if out of bounds.\n\n      # Check if the new position is traversable (not impassable).\n      # A cell is considered impassable if it contains any of the `impassable_kinds`.\n      is_impassable_cell = False\n      for k_idx in impassable_kinds:\n          if grid[nx, ny, k_idx] > 0: # If this impassable kind is present at (nx, ny)\n              is_impassable_cell = True\n              break # No need to check other kinds, it's already impassable.\n      \n      if is_impassable_cell:\n          continue # Skip if the cell is impassable.\n\n      # If the new position is valid and not visited, add it to the queue for exploration.\n      new_pos = (nx, ny)\n      if new_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(new_pos)\n        q.append((new_pos, path_so_far + [action]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and the queue becomes empty without finding a path to any goal cell,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable from the current agent's position.\n  return []", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:19:50.882106", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  \n  # Get the integer index for the desired primitive.\n  # This will raise a KeyError if the primitive name is not valid.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n  \n  # V2 Improvement: Check if the primitive is already collected.\n  # If the agent's inventory already contains the primitive, no actions are needed.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return [] # Already have it, return an empty action list.\n\n  # Retrieve action mappings for clarity and to ensure correct action indices are used.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # 1. Immediate collection check:\n  # If the agent is already within the 3x3 neighborhood (including diagonals and its own cell)\n  # of the primitive, it can directly use/collect it.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n    # This means the agent is in a valid position to interact with the primitive.\n    return [USE]\n\n  # 2. Identify all grid locations where the primitive exists.\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n  \n  all_primitive_locations = []\n  # Iterate through the entire grid to find all cells containing the specified primitive.\n  for x in range(grid_width):\n    for y in range(grid_height):\n      # Check if the primitive kind is present at this grid cell (count > 0).\n      if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n        all_primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  # If no instances of the primitive are found on the grid, it's not collectible.\n  if not all_primitive_locations:\n    return []\n\n  # 3. Define \"goal cells\" for the Breadth-First Search (BFS).\n  # A goal cell is any cell from which the agent can successfully collect the primitive.\n  # Given that `CraftState.next_to` checks the 3x3 neighborhood, any cell in this\n  # 3x3 vicinity of a primitive location is a valid goal.\n  goal_cells = set()\n  for px, py in all_primitive_locations:\n    # Iterate through all 3x3 neighbors (including (0,0) for the primitive's own cell).\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        gx, gy = px + dx, py + dy\n        # Ensure the potential goal cell is within the grid boundaries.\n        if 0 <= gx < grid_width and 0 <= gy < grid_height:\n          goal_cells.add((gx, gy))\n\n  # 4. Determine which entity kinds make a cell impassable for agent movement.\n  # Impassable kinds are defined as non-grabbable items that are NOT workshops.\n  # Workshops are typically non-grabbable but often walkable/interactable locations.\n  impassable_kinds = set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices) - set(env.world.workshop_indices)\n\n  # 5. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path\n  # from the agent's current position to any of the identified goal cells.\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  \n  # The queue for BFS stores tuples of (current_position, path_taken_actions_to_reach_here).\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) \n  # A set to keep track of visited positions to prevent cycles and redundant exploration.\n  visited = {start_pos} \n\n  # Define possible cardinal moves (delta_x, delta_y) and their corresponding action indices.\n  DELTAS_ACTIONS = [\n      ((0, -1), UP),    # Move North (decreases Y coordinate)\n      ((0, 1), DOWN),   # Move South (increases Y coordinate)\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT),  # Move West (decreases X coordinate)\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT),  # Move East (increases X coordinate)\n  ]\n\n  while q:\n    (cx, cy), path_so_far = q.popleft() # Get the current position and the path to it\n\n    # If the current position is one of our goal cells, we have found the shortest path.\n    if (cx, cy) in goal_cells:\n      # Append the USE action, as the agent is now in a position to collect the primitive.\n      return path_so_far + [USE]\n\n    # Explore valid neighboring cells for movement (cardinal directions).\n    for (dx, dy), action in DELTAS_ACTIONS:\n      nx, ny = cx + dx, cy + dy # Calculate the new potential position\n\n      # Check if the new position is within the overall grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height):\n        continue # Skip if out of bounds.\n\n      # Check if the new position is traversable (not impassable).\n      # A cell is considered impassable if it contains any of the `impassable_kinds`.\n      is_impassable_cell = False\n      for k_idx in impassable_kinds:\n          if grid[nx, ny, k_idx] > 0: # If this impassable kind is present at (nx, ny)\n              is_impassable_cell = True\n              break # No need to check other kinds, it's already impassable.\n      \n      if is_impassable_cell:\n          continue # Skip if the cell is impassable.\n\n      # If the new position is valid and not visited, add it to the queue for exploration.\n      new_pos = (nx, ny)\n      if new_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(new_pos)\n        q.append((new_pos, path_so_far + [action]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and the queue becomes empty without finding a path to any goal cell,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable from the current agent's position.\n  return []", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:20:42.031951", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions_list = []\n  # Get the current state of the environment. This state includes the grid,\n  # agent's position, direction, and inventory.\n  current_state = env._current_state\n\n  # Store initial grid, position, and direction for pathfinding.\n  # The grid is considered static during pathfinding; only agent's (pos, dir) changes.\n  initial_grid = current_state.grid\n  initial_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's starting row, column tuple (r, c)\n  initial_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's starting direction (0:RIGHT, 1:UP, 2:LEFT, 3:DOWN)\n\n  # Get the integer ID for the target primitive from the world's cookbook index.\n  # This ID is used to locate the primitive on the grid.\n  primitive_id = current_state.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Get grid dimensions to check boundaries during pathfinding.\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = initial_grid.shape\n\n  # Retrieve the mapping from action names (strings) to their integer codes.\n  # This ensures compatibility with the environment's `step` method.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  \n  # Define action indices based on the environment's action_specs.\n  # 'UP' usually means move forward in the current direction.\n  # 'DOWN' usually means move backward in the current direction.\n  MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION = action_map['UP']\n  MOVE_BACKWARD_ACTION = action_map['DOWN'] # Added for v2: Allows moving backward\n  TURN_LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  TURN_RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE'] # Action to perform collection/interaction\n\n  # Define direction vectors for moving forward based on current orientation.\n  # Maps direction index to (delta_row, delta_column) for a forward step.\n  # Agent's direction (dir): 0=RIGHT, 1=UP, 2=LEFT, 3=DOWN\n  DIR_TO_DRDC = {\n      0: (0, 1),   # Facing RIGHT: (row, col + 1)\n      1: (-1, 0),  # Facing UP: (row - 1, col)\n      2: (0, -1),  # Facing LEFT: (row, col - 1)\n      3: (1, 0)    # Facing DOWN: (row + 1, col)\n  }\n\n  # Define how agent's direction changes when turning left or right.\n  # These mappings cycle through the four cardinal directions (0, 1, 2, 3).\n  TURN_LEFT_MAP = {0: 1, 1: 2, 2: 3, 3: 0} # Example: RIGHT (0) -> UP (1)\n  TURN_RIGHT_MAP = {0: 3, 1: 0, 2: 1, 3: 2} # Example: RIGHT (0) -> DOWN (3)\n\n  # Identify all entity kinds that act as obstacles to agent movement.\n  # An agent cannot walk onto cells containing these items.\n  # 1. Non-grabbable entities (e.g., BOUNDARY, WATER, WORKSHOP0) are inherently obstacles.\n  obstacles_to_movement_indices = set(current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices)\n  # 2. If the target primitive itself is a grabbable item (e.g., WOOD, STONE, GOLD),\n  #    the agent should not walk directly onto its tile. It must interact from an\n  #    adjacent cell. Thus, the primitive's own ID is also added as an obstacle for movement.\n  if primitive_id in current_state.world.grabbable_indices:\n      obstacles_to_movement_indices.add(primitive_id)\n  \n  # Early Exit Optimization: If the primitive is already in the agent's 3x3\n  # neighborhood (i.e., immediately collectible from the current position), just return the USE action.\n  # The `CraftState.next_to` method provides this check efficiently.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_id):\n      return [USE_ACTION]\n\n  # Initialize Breadth-First Search (BFS) for pathfinding.\n  # The BFS queue stores tuples:\n  #   ((current_position_tuple (r, c), current_direction_int), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here)\n  # This structure allows tracking both spatial location and agent orientation.\n  queue = collections.deque([((initial_pos, initial_dir), [])])\n  # The 'visited' set keeps track of (position, direction) pairs already explored\n  # to prevent cycles and redundant computations, ensuring the shortest path is found.\n  visited = {(initial_pos, initial_dir)}\n\n  target_path_actions = None # This will store the shortest action sequence to a collectible state.\n\n  # Helper function to check if a potential new state (position, direction) is valid and walkable.\n  def is_valid_transition(pos, direction):\n      nr, nc = pos\n      # Check grid boundaries\n      if not (0 <= nr < WIDTH and 0 <= nc < HEIGHT):\n          return False \n      # Check if this (position, direction) state has already been visited\n      if (pos, direction) in visited:\n          return False \n      \n      # Check for obstacles at the new position on the initial grid\n      for kind_idx in obstacles_to_movement_indices:\n          if initial_grid[nr, nc, kind_idx] > 0:\n              return False # Cell contains an obstacle\n      return True\n\n  # Main BFS loop: continues until the queue is empty or a path to a goal is found.\n  while queue:\n      # Dequeue the current state (position and direction) and the path leading to it.\n      (current_pos, current_dir), path_to_current_state = queue.popleft()\n      r, c = current_pos\n\n      # Check if the current agent position (r, c) is a \"goal state\" for collection.\n      # A goal state means the primitive is located in any cell within the 3x3 neighborhood\n      # around the agent's current position on the initial grid. This mirrors the `CraftState.next_to` logic.\n      is_collectible_from_current_pos = False\n      for dr_check in [-1, 0, 1]: # Iterate through relative row offsets (-1, 0, 1)\n          for dc_check in [-1, 0, 1]: # Iterate through relative column offsets (-1, 0, 1)\n              check_r, check_c = r + dr_check, c + dc_check\n              # Ensure the cell being checked is within grid boundaries.\n              if (0 <= check_r < WIDTH and 0 <= check_c < HEIGHT and\n                  initial_grid[check_r, check_c, primitive_id] > 0):\n                  is_collectible_from_current_pos = True\n                  break # Primitive found in neighborhood, no need to check further cells for this position.\n          if is_collectible_from_current_pos:\n              break # Break outer loop too if found.\n\n      if is_collectible_from_current_pos:\n          target_path_actions = path_to_current_state # A shortest path to a collectible state is found.\n          break # Terminate BFS; no need to explore further as we found the shortest path.\n\n      # Explore possible next states by applying valid actions: Move Forward, Move Backward, Turn Left, Turn Right.\n      \n      # 1. Try MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION:\n      move_dr, move_dc = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n      next_r_fwd, next_c_fwd = r + move_dr, c + move_dc\n      next_pos_fwd = (next_r_fwd, next_c_fwd)\n      next_dir_fwd = current_dir # Moving forward does not change the agent's facing direction.\n\n      if is_valid_transition(next_pos_fwd, next_dir_fwd):\n          visited.add((next_pos_fwd, next_dir_fwd)) # Mark the new state as visited.\n          # Add the new state to the queue with the updated path.\n          queue.append(((next_pos_fwd, next_dir_fwd), path_to_current_state + [MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION]))\n\n      # 2. Try MOVE_BACKWARD_ACTION: (New in v2 for increased pathfinding flexibility)\n      next_r_bwd, next_c_bwd = r - move_dr, c - move_dc # Opposite direction of forward\n      next_pos_bwd = (next_r_bwd, next_c_bwd)\n      next_dir_bwd = current_dir # Moving backward does not change facing direction.\n\n      if is_valid_transition(next_pos_bwd, next_dir_bwd):\n          visited.add((next_pos_bwd, next_dir_bwd))\n          queue.append(((next_pos_bwd, next_dir_bwd), path_to_current_state + [MOVE_BACKWARD_ACTION]))\n\n      # 3. Try TURN_LEFT_ACTION:\n      next_dir_left = TURN_LEFT_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Turning only changes direction, not position.\n      if is_valid_transition(current_pos, next_dir_left):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_left))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_left), path_to_current_state + [TURN_LEFT_ACTION]))\n\n      # 4. Try TURN_RIGHT_ACTION:\n      next_dir_right = TURN_RIGHT_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Turning only changes direction, not position.\n      if is_valid_transition(current_pos, next_dir_right):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_right))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_right), path_to_current_state + [TURN_RIGHT_ACTION]))\n\n  # After BFS completes:\n  # If a path to a collectable position was found (`target_path_actions` is not None),\n  # append the final 'USE' action to perform the collection.\n  if target_path_actions is not None:\n      actions_list.extend(target_path_actions)\n      actions_list.append(USE_ACTION)\n\n  return actions_list", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:20:43.442123", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions_list = []\n  # Get the current state of the environment. This state includes the grid,\n  # agent's position, direction, and inventory.\n  current_state = env._current_state\n\n  # Store initial grid, position, and direction for pathfinding.\n  # The grid is considered static during pathfinding; only agent's (pos, dir) changes.\n  initial_grid = current_state.grid\n  initial_agent_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's starting row, column tuple (r, c)\n  initial_agent_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's starting direction (0:RIGHT, 1:UP, 2:LEFT, 3:DOWN)\n\n  # Get the integer ID for the target primitive from the world's cookbook index.\n  # This ID is used to locate the primitive on the grid.\n  primitive_kind_id = current_state.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Get grid dimensions to check boundaries during pathfinding.\n  GRID_WIDTH, GRID_HEIGHT, _ = initial_grid.shape\n\n  # Retrieve the mapping from action names (strings) to their integer codes.\n  # This ensures compatibility with the environment's `step` method.\n  action_name_to_id = env.action_specs()\n  \n  # Map DSL movement/turn actions to their integer indices.\n  MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION_ID = action_name_to_id['UP'] # 'UP' in DSL means 'move forward'\n  TURN_LEFT_ACTION_ID = action_name_to_id['LEFT']\n  TURN_RIGHT_ACTION_ID = action_name_to_id['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION_ID = action_name_to_id['USE'] # Action to perform collection/interaction\n\n  # Define direction vectors for moving forward based on current orientation.\n  # Maps agent's direction index to (delta_row, delta_column) for a forward step.\n  # Agent's direction (dir): 0=RIGHT, 1=UP, 2=LEFT, 3=DOWN\n  DIRECTION_TO_DRDC = {\n      0: (0, 1),   # Facing RIGHT: (row, col + 1)\n      1: (-1, 0),  # Facing UP: (row - 1, col)\n      2: (0, -1),  # Facing LEFT: (row, col - 1)\n      3: (1, 0)    # Facing DOWN: (row + 1, col)\n  }\n\n  # Define how agent's direction changes when turning left or right.\n  # These mappings cycle through the four cardinal directions (0, 1, 2, 3).\n  TURN_LEFT_DIR_MAP = {0: 1, 1: 2, 2: 3, 3: 0} # Example: RIGHT (0) -> UP (1)\n  TURN_RIGHT_DIR_MAP = {0: 3, 1: 0, 2: 1, 3: 2} # Example: RIGHT (0) -> DOWN (3)\n\n  # Identify all entity kinds that act as obstacles to agent movement.\n  # An agent cannot walk onto cells containing these items.\n  # 1. Non-grabbable entities (e.g., BOUNDARY, WATER, WORKSHOP0) are inherently obstacles.\n  unwalkable_kind_ids = set(current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices)\n  \n  # 2. If the target primitive itself is a grabbable item (e.g., WOOD, STONE, GOLD),\n  #    the agent should not walk directly onto its tile. It must interact from an\n  #    adjacent cell. Thus, the primitive's own ID is also added as an obstacle for movement.\n  if primitive_kind_id in current_state.world.grabbable_indices:\n      unwalkable_kind_ids.add(primitive_kind_id)\n  \n  # Early Exit Optimization: If the primitive is already in the agent's 3x3\n  # neighborhood (i.e., immediately collectible from the current position), just return the USE action.\n  # The `CraftState.next_to` method provides this check efficiently.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_kind_id):\n      return [USE_ACTION_ID]\n\n  # Initialize Breadth-First Search (BFS) for pathfinding.\n  # The BFS queue stores tuples:\n  #   ((current_position_tuple (r, c), current_direction_int), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here)\n  # This structure allows tracking both spatial location and agent orientation.\n  bfs_queue = collections.deque([((initial_agent_pos, initial_agent_dir), [])])\n  \n  # The 'visited' set keeps track of (position, direction) pairs already explored\n  # to prevent cycles and redundant computations, ensuring the shortest path is found.\n  visited_states = {(initial_agent_pos, initial_agent_dir)}\n\n  path_to_collection_spot = None # This will store the shortest action sequence to a collectible state.\n\n  # Main BFS loop: continues until the queue is empty or a path to a goal is found.\n  while bfs_queue:\n      # Dequeue the current state (position and direction) and the path leading to it.\n      (current_pos, current_dir), current_path_actions = bfs_queue.popleft()\n      r, c = current_pos\n\n      # Check if the current agent position (r, c) is a \"goal state\" for collection.\n      # A goal state means the primitive is located in any cell within the 3x3 neighborhood\n      # around the agent's current position on the initial grid. This mirrors the `CraftState.next_to` logic.\n      is_primitive_in_neighborhood = False\n      for dr_offset in [-1, 0, 1]: # Iterate through relative row offsets (-1, 0, 1)\n          for dc_offset in [-1, 0, 1]: # Iterate through relative column offsets (-1, 0, 1)\n              check_r, check_c = r + dr_offset, c + dc_offset\n              # Ensure the cell being checked is within grid boundaries.\n              if (0 <= check_r < GRID_WIDTH and 0 <= check_c < GRID_HEIGHT and\n                  initial_grid[check_r, check_c, primitive_kind_id] > 0):\n                  is_primitive_in_neighborhood = True\n                  break # Primitive found in neighborhood, no need to check further cells for this position.\n          if is_primitive_in_neighborhood:\n              break # Break outer loop too if found.\n\n      if is_primitive_in_neighborhood:\n          path_to_collection_spot = current_path_actions # A shortest path to a collectible state is found.\n          break # Terminate BFS; no need to explore further as we found the shortest path.\n\n      # Explore possible next states by applying valid actions: Move Forward, Turn Left, Turn Right.\n\n      # 1. Try MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION:\n      delta_r, delta_c = DIRECTION_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n      next_r, next_c = r + delta_r, c + delta_c\n      next_agent_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n      next_agent_dir_after_move = current_dir # Moving forward does not change the agent's facing direction.\n\n      # Check if the potential next position is valid (within bounds and not previously visited with this direction).\n      if (0 <= next_r < GRID_WIDTH and 0 <= next_c < GRID_HEIGHT and\n          (next_agent_pos, next_agent_dir_after_move) not in visited_states):\n          \n          is_cell_walkable = True\n          # Verify that the cell at `next_agent_pos` does not contain any obstacle.\n          for kind_idx in unwalkable_kind_ids:\n              if initial_grid[next_r, next_c, kind_idx] > 0:\n                  is_cell_walkable = False\n                  break # This cell contains an obstacle, so it's not walkable.\n\n          if is_cell_walkable:\n              visited_states.add((next_agent_pos, next_agent_dir_after_move)) # Mark the new state as visited.\n              # Add the new state to the queue with the updated path.\n              bfs_queue.append(((next_agent_pos, next_agent_dir_after_move), \n                                current_path_actions + [MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION_ID]))\n\n      # 2. Try TURN_LEFT_ACTION:\n      next_agent_dir_left = TURN_LEFT_DIR_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Turning only changes direction, not position.\n      if ((current_pos, next_agent_dir_left) not in visited_states):\n          visited_states.add((current_pos, next_agent_dir_left))\n          bfs_queue.append(((current_pos, next_agent_dir_left), \n                            current_path_actions + [TURN_LEFT_ACTION_ID]))\n\n      # 3. Try TURN_RIGHT_ACTION:\n      next_agent_dir_right = TURN_RIGHT_DIR_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Turning only changes direction, not position.\n      if ((current_pos, next_agent_dir_right) not in visited_states):\n          visited_states.add((current_pos, next_agent_dir_right))\n          bfs_queue.append(((current_pos, next_agent_dir_right), \n                            current_path_actions + [TURN_RIGHT_ACTION_ID]))\n\n  # After BFS completes:\n  # If a path to a collectable position was found (`path_to_collection_spot` is not None),\n  # append the final 'USE' action to perform the collection.\n  if path_to_collection_spot is not None:\n      actions_list.extend(path_to_collection_spot)\n      actions_list.append(USE_ACTION_ID)\n\n  return actions_list", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:21:10.465287", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  \n  # Map the string name of the primitive to its corresponding integer index\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n  \n  # Retrieve integer codes for fundamental movement and interaction actions.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # 1. Immediate Collection Check:\n  # If the agent is already in a position where it can interact with (collect)\n  # the primitive, the only action needed is USE.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n    return [USE]\n\n  # 2. Identify all physical locations of the primitive on the game grid.\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n  \n  primitive_grid_locations = []\n  for x in range(grid_width):\n    for y in range(grid_height):\n      # A primitive is present if its count at this (x,y) cell is greater than 0.\n      if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n        primitive_grid_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  # If no instances of the primitive are found anywhere on the grid,\n  # it cannot be collected, so return an empty list of actions.\n  if not primitive_grid_locations:\n    return []\n\n  # 3. Define \"Goal Cells\" for the BFS:\n  # A goal cell is any traversable cell from which the agent can successfully\n  # \"collect\" the primitive using the 'USE' action. This includes any cell within\n  # the 3x3 neighborhood of a primitive's location.\n  goal_cells = set()\n  for px, py in primitive_grid_locations:\n    # Iterate through all 3x3 neighbor offsets (including (0,0) for the primitive's own cell).\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        gx, gy = px + dx, py + dy\n        # Ensure the potential goal cell is within the grid boundaries.\n        if 0 <= gx < grid_width and 0 <= gy < grid_height:\n          goal_cells.add((gx, gy))\n\n  # 4. Determine which cell types are impassable for agent movement.\n  # Impassable kinds are typically non-grabbable items that are not designated\n  # as 'workshop' locations (which are usually traversable).\n  impassable_kinds = set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices) - set(env.world.workshop_indices)\n\n  # 5. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path\n  # from the agent's current position to any of the identified goal cells.\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  \n  # BFS Queue: stores tuples of (current_position, list_of_actions_to_reach_this_position).\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) \n  # Set to keep track of visited positions to prevent infinite loops and redundant paths.\n  visited = {start_pos} \n\n  # Define possible cardinal movement directions and their corresponding action indices.\n  DELTAS_ACTIONS = [\n      ((0, -1), UP),    # Move North (decreasing Y-coordinate)\n      ((0, 1), DOWN),   # Move South (increasing Y-coordinate)\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT),  # Move West (decreasing X-coordinate)\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT),  # Move East (increasing X-coordinate)\n  ]\n\n  while q:\n    # Dequeue the current position and the path leading to it.\n    (cx, cy), path_to_current = q.popleft() \n\n    # If the current position is one of our target goal cells, we've found the shortest path.\n    if (cx, cy) in goal_cells:\n      # Append the 'USE' action as the final step to collect the primitive.\n      return path_to_current + [USE]\n\n    # Explore all valid, unvisited, and traversable neighboring cells.\n    for (dx, dy), action in DELTAS_ACTIONS:\n      nx, ny = cx + dx, cy + dy # Calculate the new potential position.\n      new_pos = (nx, ny)\n\n      # Check 1: Boundary Check - Is the new position within the grid?\n      if not (0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height):\n        continue # Skip if out of bounds.\n\n      # Check 2: Impassability Check - Does the new position contain an impassable kind?\n      is_impassable_cell = False\n      for k_idx in impassable_kinds:\n          # If an impassable kind is present at the new cell, it's blocked.\n          if grid[nx, ny, k_idx] > 0: \n              is_impassable_cell = True\n              break # No need to check further kinds for this cell.\n      \n      if is_impassable_cell:\n          continue # Skip if the cell is impassable.\n\n      # Check 3: Visited Check - Has this position already been explored?\n      if new_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(new_pos) # Mark as visited.\n        # Enqueue the new position along with the updated path.\n        q.append((new_pos, path_to_current + [action]))\n\n  # If the BFS queue becomes empty and no goal cell was reached,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable from the agent's current position.\n  return []", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:21:11.571664", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  \n  # Map the string name of the primitive to its corresponding integer index\n  # used internally by the simulation. This will raise an error if the\n  # primitive name is not recognized, which is desired.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n  \n  # Retrieve integer codes for fundamental movement and interaction actions.\n  # This makes the code more readable and robust to changes in action mapping.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # 1. Immediate Collection Check:\n  # If the agent is already in a position where it can interact with (collect)\n  # the primitive (i.e., within its 3x3 neighborhood), the only action needed is USE.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n    return [USE]\n\n  # 2. Identify all physical locations of the primitive on the game grid.\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n  \n  primitive_grid_locations = []\n  for x in range(grid_width):\n    for y in range(grid_height):\n      # A primitive is present if its count at this (x,y) cell is greater than 0.\n      if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n        primitive_grid_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  # If no instances of the primitive are found anywhere on the grid,\n  # it cannot be collected, so return an empty list of actions.\n  if not primitive_grid_locations:\n    return []\n\n  # 3. Define \"Goal Cells\" for the BFS:\n  # A goal cell is any traversable cell from which the agent can successfully\n  # \"collect\" the primitive using the 'USE' action. Based on `CraftState.next_to`,\n  # this includes any cell within the 3x3 neighborhood of a primitive's location.\n  goal_cells = set()\n  for px, py in primitive_grid_locations:\n    # Iterate through all 3x3 neighbor offsets (including (0,0) for the primitive's own cell).\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        gx, gy = px + dx, py + dy\n        # Ensure the potential goal cell is within the grid boundaries.\n        if 0 <= gx < grid_width and 0 <= gy < grid_height:\n          goal_cells.add((gx, gy))\n\n  # 4. Determine which cell types are impassable for agent movement.\n  # Impassable kinds are typically non-grabbable items that are not designated\n  # as 'workshop' locations (which are usually traversable).\n  # Examples: water, stone, boundaries.\n  impassable_kinds = set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices) - set(env.world.workshop_indices)\n\n  # 5. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path\n  # from the agent's current position to any of the identified goal cells.\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  \n  # BFS Queue: stores tuples of (current_position, list_of_actions_to_reach_this_position).\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) \n  # Set to keep track of visited positions to prevent infinite loops and redundant paths.\n  visited = {start_pos} \n\n  # Define possible cardinal movement directions and their corresponding action indices.\n  # CraftWorld typically uses 4-directional movement (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT).\n  DELTAS_ACTIONS = [\n      ((0, -1), UP),    # Move North (decreasing Y-coordinate)\n      ((0, 1), DOWN),   # Move South (increasing Y-coordinate)\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT),  # Move West (decreasing X-coordinate)\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT),  # Move East (increasing X-coordinate)\n  ]\n\n  while q:\n    # Dequeue the current position and the path leading to it.\n    (cx, cy), path_to_current = q.popleft() \n\n    # If the current position is one of our target goal cells, we've found the shortest path.\n    if (cx, cy) in goal_cells:\n      # Append the 'USE' action as the final step to collect the primitive.\n      return path_to_current + [USE]\n\n    # Explore all valid, unvisited, and traversable neighboring cells.\n    for (dx, dy), action in DELTAS_ACTIONS:\n      nx, ny = cx + dx, cy + dy # Calculate the new potential position.\n      new_pos = (nx, ny)\n\n      # Check 1: Boundary Check - Is the new position within the grid?\n      if not (0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height):\n        continue # Skip if out of bounds.\n\n      # Check 2: Impassability Check - Does the new position contain an impassable kind?\n      is_impassable_cell = False\n      for k_idx in impassable_kinds:\n          # If an impassable kind is present at the new cell, it's blocked.\n          if grid[nx, ny, k_idx] > 0: \n              is_impassable_cell = True\n              break # No need to check further kinds for this cell.\n      \n      if is_impassable_cell:\n          continue # Skip if the cell is impassable.\n\n      # Check 3: Visited Check - Has this position already been explored?\n      if new_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(new_pos) # Mark as visited.\n        # Enqueue the new position along with the updated path.\n        q.append((new_pos, path_to_current + [action]))\n\n  # If the BFS queue becomes empty and no goal cell was reached,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable from the agent's current position.\n  return []", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:21:52.598253", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions_list = []\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  \n  # Extract current state information for pathfinding.\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  initial_pos = current_state.pos  # Agent's initial position (row, col)\n  initial_dir = current_state.dir  # Agent's initial facing direction (0:RIGHT, 1:UP, 2:LEFT, 3:DOWN)\n\n  # Get the integer ID for the target primitive from the cookbook's index.\n  primitive_id = current_state.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  # Get grid dimensions for boundary checks.\n  num_rows, num_cols, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Retrieve action codes from the environment's action specifications.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  MOVE_FORWARD = action_map['UP']    # In CraftWorld, 'UP' moves the agent forward in its current direction.\n  TURN_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']     # Turns the agent 90 degrees counter-clockwise.\n  TURN_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']   # Turns the agent 90 degrees clockwise.\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']     # Interacts with the entity in the cell directly in front.\n\n  # Define direction vectors: Maps agent's direction (0-3) to a (delta_row, delta_column) tuple.\n  # This tuple represents the change in coordinates for the cell directly in front of the agent.\n  DIR_TO_DRDC = {\n      0: (0, 1),   # Facing RIGHT: (row, col + 1)\n      1: (-1, 0),  # Facing UP: (row - 1, col)\n      2: (0, -1),  # Facing LEFT: (row, col - 1)\n      3: (1, 0)    # Facing DOWN: (row + 1, col)\n  }\n\n  # Define mappings for direction changes after turning left or right.\n  TURN_LEFT_MAP = {0: 1, 1: 2, 2: 3, 3: 0}  # e.g., RIGHT (0) -> UP (1)\n  TURN_RIGHT_MAP = {0: 3, 1: 0, 2: 1, 3: 2} # e.g., RIGHT (0) -> DOWN (3)\n\n  # Get indices of entities that are considered non-walkable terrain (e.g., boundaries, water, workshops).\n  non_walkable_kinds_indices = current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # Initialize Breadth-First Search (BFS):\n  # The queue stores tuples: ((current_position_tuple, current_direction_int), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_this_state).\n  queue = collections.deque([((initial_pos, initial_dir), [])])\n  \n  # The 'visited' set keeps track of all unique (position, direction) states already explored.\n  visited = {(initial_pos, initial_dir)}\n\n  target_path_to_adjacent_state = None # This will store the action sequence to reach the state *before* 'USE'.\n\n  # Start BFS traversal to find the shortest path to an adjacent cell of the primitive.\n  while queue:\n      (current_pos, current_dir), path_actions = queue.popleft()\n      r, c = current_pos # Unpack current row and column.\n\n      # Check if the target primitive is directly in front of the agent from the current state.\n      # This is the goal condition for pathfinding: being positioned to use the primitive.\n      front_dr, front_dc = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n      front_r, front_c = r + front_dr, c + front_dc\n      \n      # Ensure the cell directly in front is within grid boundaries before checking its contents.\n      if (0 <= front_r < num_rows and 0 <= front_c < num_cols):\n          # If the primitive is present in the cell immediately in front, we have found our path.\n          if grid[front_r, front_c, primitive_id] > 0:\n              target_path_to_adjacent_state = path_actions # Store the sequence of actions that led to this state.\n              break # Path found, exit BFS loop as we found the shortest one.\n\n      # Explore all possible next actions (Move Forward, Turn Left, Turn Right) from the current state.\n\n      # 1. Try Move Forward Action\n      # Calculate the next position if the agent moves forward. The direction remains unchanged.\n      next_r_move, next_c_move = r + front_dr, c + front_dc\n      next_pos_move = (next_r_move, next_c_move)\n      next_dir_move = current_dir # Moving forward does not change orientation.\n\n      # Check if the calculated next position is valid, walkable, and not yet visited.\n      if (0 <= next_r_move < num_rows and 0 <= next_c_move < num_cols and\n          (next_pos_move, next_dir_move) not in visited):\n          \n          is_walkable_next_cell = True\n          # A cell is not walkable if it contains any non-grabbable/impassable entity.\n          for kind_idx in non_walkable_kinds_indices:\n              if grid[next_r_move, next_c_move, kind_idx] > 0:\n                  is_walkable_next_cell = False\n                  break\n          # Also, the agent cannot walk *onto* the primitive it intends to collect; it must be adjacent.\n          if grid[next_r_move, next_c_move, primitive_id] > 0:\n              is_walkable_next_cell = False\n\n          if is_walkable_next_cell:\n              visited.add((next_pos_move, next_dir_move)) # Mark as visited.\n              # Add the new state and the extended path to the queue for further exploration.\n              queue.append(((next_pos_move, next_dir_move), path_actions + [MOVE_FORWARD]))\n\n      # 2. Try Turn Left Action\n      # Calculate the new direction after turning left. Position remains unchanged.\n      next_dir_left = TURN_LEFT_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Check if this new state (same position, new direction) has not been visited.\n      if ((current_pos, next_dir_left) not in visited):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_left)) # Mark as visited.\n          # Add the new state and extended path to the queue.\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_left), path_actions + [TURN_LEFT]))\n\n      # 3. Try Turn Right Action\n      # Calculate the new direction after turning right. Position remains unchanged.\n      next_dir_right = TURN_RIGHT_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Check if this new state has not been visited.\n      if ((current_pos, next_dir_right) not in visited):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_right)) # Mark as visited.\n          # Add the new state and extended path to the queue.\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_right), path_actions + [TURN_RIGHT]))\n\n  # After the BFS completes:\n  # If a path to the target state (agent adjacent and facing the primitive) was found,\n  # append the final 'USE' action to the discovered path. This completes the collection sequence.\n  # If no path was found (target_path_to_adjacent_state remains None), an empty list is returned.\n  if target_path_to_adjacent_state is not None:\n      actions_list.extend(target_path_to_adjacent_state)\n      actions_list.append(USE_ACTION)\n\n  return actions_list", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:21:53.755348", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions_list = []\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  \n  # Extract essential information from the current game state.\n  # This includes the immutable grid layout, agent's current position, and current direction.\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  agent_pos = current_state.pos  # (row, col) tuple\n  agent_dir = current_state.dir  # Integer (0:RIGHT, 1:UP, 2:LEFT, 3:DOWN)\n\n  # Get the unique integer ID (index) for the target primitive from the game's cookbook.\n  # This ID is used to locate the primitive on the grid.\n  primitive_id = current_state.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  # Get grid dimensions to perform boundary checks during pathfinding.\n  num_rows, num_cols, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Retrieve the integer representations for standard agent actions from the environment.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_MOVE_FORWARD = action_map['UP']    # In CraftWorld, 'UP' moves the agent forward in its current direction.\n  ACTION_TURN_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']     # Rotates the agent 90 degrees counter-clockwise.\n  ACTION_TURN_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']   # Rotates the agent 90 degrees clockwise.\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']            # Interacts with the entity in the cell directly in front of the agent.\n\n  # Define how agent's coordinates change based on its current direction when moving forward.\n  # Key: current_direction_int, Value: (delta_row, delta_column)\n  DIR_TO_DELTA_RC = {\n      0: (0, 1),   # Facing RIGHT: (row, col + 1)\n      1: (-1, 0),  # Facing UP: (row - 1, col)\n      2: (0, -1),  # Facing LEFT: (row, col - 1)\n      3: (1, 0)    # Facing DOWN: (row + 1, col)\n  }\n\n  # Define how agent's direction changes when turning left or right.\n  # Key: current_direction_int, Value: new_direction_int\n  TURN_LEFT_MAP = {0: 1, 1: 2, 2: 3, 3: 0}  # e.g., RIGHT (0) -> UP (1)\n  TURN_RIGHT_MAP = {0: 3, 1: 0, 2: 1, 3: 2} # e.g., RIGHT (0) -> DOWN (3)\n\n  # Get the set of entity indices that represent non-walkable terrain (e.g., walls, water, workshops).\n  # The agent cannot move into cells occupied by these kinds.\n  impassable_kinds_indices = current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # Helper function to check if a given cell (r, c) is within grid boundaries and is traversable.\n  # A cell is traversable if it's not occupied by an impassable entity.\n  def _is_traversable(r: int, c: int) -> bool:\n      # Check if coordinates are within the grid bounds.\n      if not (0 <= r < num_rows and 0 <= c < num_cols):\n          return False\n      \n      # Check if the cell contains any impassable entities.\n      for kind_idx in impassable_kinds_indices:\n          if grid[r, c, kind_idx] > 0:\n              return False\n      \n      # The agent cannot move onto the primitive it intends to collect.\n      # Collection happens when adjacent and using the 'USE' action.\n      if grid[r, c, primitive_id] > 0:\n          return False\n      \n      return True\n\n  # Initialize Breadth-First Search (BFS) for pathfinding.\n  # The queue stores tuples: ((current_position_tuple, current_direction_int), list_of_actions_taken_so_far).\n  # This represents a unique state (position and orientation) and the path to reach it.\n  queue = collections.deque([((agent_pos, agent_dir), [])])\n  \n  # The 'visited' set keeps track of (position, direction) states already explored.\n  # This prevents redundant searches and ensures finding the shortest path by avoiding cycles.\n  visited = {(agent_pos, agent_dir)}\n\n  # This variable will store the action sequence once a path to the target (adjacent and facing primitive) is found.\n  path_to_primitive = None \n\n  # Start BFS traversal.\n  while queue:\n      (current_pos, current_dir), path_actions = queue.popleft()\n      r, c = current_pos # Unpack current row and column.\n\n      # Check if the target primitive is in the cell directly in front of the agent.\n      # This is the desired goal state for collection.\n      delta_r_front, delta_c_front = DIR_TO_DELTA_RC[current_dir]\n      front_r, front_c = r + delta_r_front, c + delta_c_front\n      \n      # Ensure the cell directly in front is within grid boundaries before checking its contents.\n      if (0 <= front_r < num_rows and 0 <= front_c < num_cols):\n          # If the primitive is present in the cell immediately in front, we've found our path.\n          if grid[front_r, front_c, primitive_id] > 0:\n              path_to_primitive = path_actions # Store the sequence of actions leading to this state.\n              break # Path found, exit the BFS loop.\n\n      # Explore all possible next actions (Move Forward, Turn Left, Turn Right) from the current state.\n\n      # 1. Try MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION:\n      # Calculate the next position if the agent moves forward. Direction remains unchanged.\n      move_delta_r, move_delta_c = DIR_TO_DELTA_RC[current_dir]\n      next_r, next_c = r + move_delta_r, c + move_delta_c\n      next_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n      next_dir = current_dir # Moving forward does not change orientation.\n\n      # Check if the calculated next position is valid and traversable, and if this new state (pos, dir)\n      # has not been visited yet.\n      if _is_traversable(next_r, next_c) and\\\n         (next_pos, next_dir) not in visited:\n          visited.add((next_pos, next_dir)) # Mark as visited.\n          # Add the new state and the extended path to the queue for further exploration.\n          queue.append(((next_pos, next_dir), path_actions + [ACTION_MOVE_FORWARD]))\n\n      # 2. Try TURN_LEFT_ACTION:\n      # Calculate the new direction after turning left. Position remains unchanged.\n      next_dir_left = TURN_LEFT_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Check if this new state (same position, new direction) has not been visited.\n      if (current_pos, next_dir_left) not in visited:\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_left)) # Mark as visited.\n          # Add the new state and extended path to the queue.\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_left), path_actions + [ACTION_TURN_LEFT]))\n\n      # 3. Try TURN_RIGHT_ACTION:\n      # Calculate the new direction after turning right. Position remains unchanged.\n      next_dir_right = TURN_RIGHT_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Check if this new state has not been visited.\n      if (current_pos, next_dir_right) not in visited:\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_right)) # Mark as visited.\n          # Add the new state and extended path to the queue.\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_right), path_actions + [ACTION_TURN_RIGHT]))\n\n  # After BFS completes:\n  # If a path to the target state (agent adjacent and facing the primitive) was found,\n  # append the final 'USE' action to the discovered path. This completes the collection sequence.\n  # If no path was found (path_to_primitive remains None), an empty list is returned,\n  # indicating that the primitive is unreachable from the current state.\n  if path_to_primitive is not None:\n      actions_list.extend(path_to_primitive)\n      actions_list.append(ACTION_USE)\n\n  return actions_list", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:22:49.285378", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  primitive_idx = cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n\n  # Check if the primitive is already in inventory. If so, no actions are needed.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # Ensure the requested primitive is actually grabbable. Non-grabbable entities\n  # (like \"water\", \"boundary\", or a \"workshop\") cannot be \"collected\" into inventory.\n  if primitive_idx not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_x, start_y = current_state.pos\n  start_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's current facing direction (0:N, 1:E, 2:S, 3:W)\n\n  # Use the comprehensive set of non-grabbable indices from the world object\n  # to determine impassable terrain (obstacles).\n  non_grabbable_obstacle_indices = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Define movement actions and their effects on (dx, dy) and new_direction\n  # The agent's direction is updated to face the direction of movement.\n  action_effects = {\n      craft.UP: (0, -1, 0),    # Move North (y-1), new_dir = 0 (North)\n      craft.DOWN: (0, 1, 2),     # Move South (y+1), new_dir = 2 (South)\n      craft.LEFT: (-1, 0, 3),    # Move West (x-1), new_dir = 3 (West)\n      craft.RIGHT: (1, 0, 1)     # Move East (x+1), new_dir = 1 (East)\n  }\n\n  # Mapping agent direction (0-3) to (dx, dy) for the cell *in front* of the agent\n  # This is crucial for determining where a 'USE' action will interact.\n  # FWD_DX[direction]: (0:N, 1:E, 2:S, 3:W) -> (dx)\n  FWD_DX = [0, 1, 0, -1]\n  # FWD_DY[direction]: (0:N, 1:E, 2:S, 3:W) -> (dy)\n  FWD_DY = [-1, 0, 1, 0]\n\n  # BFS setup\n  # Queue stores tuples of ((current_x, current_y, current_dir), path_taken_so_far)\n  queue = collections.deque([((start_x, start_y, start_dir), [])])\n  # Set of visited states to prevent cycles and redundant exploration.\n  # A state now includes position AND direction, as direction affects possible actions (USE).\n  visited = {(start_x, start_y, start_dir)}\n\n  while queue:\n    (x, y, d), path = queue.popleft()\n\n    # Check if a 'USE' action is possible from the current (x, y, d) state.\n    # The 'USE' action targets the cell directly in front of the agent.\n    target_x = x + FWD_DX[d]\n    target_y = y + FWD_DY[d]\n\n    # Check if the cell in front is within grid bounds and contains the primitive.\n    # This is the \"goal\" condition for collecting.\n    if (0 <= target_x < grid_width and 0 <= target_y < grid_height and\n        grid[target_x, target_y, primitive_idx] > 0):\n      # Found the primitive directly in front, so return the path to get here\n      # plus the 'USE' action to collect it.\n      return path + [craft.USE]\n\n    # Explore valid neighbor states by performing movement actions.\n    for action, (dx_move, dy_move, new_d) in action_effects.items():\n      next_x, next_y = x + dx_move, y + dy_move\n      next_state_tuple = (next_x, next_y, new_d) # New state includes new position and new direction\n\n      # 1. Bounds check: Ensure the new position is within the grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue\n\n      # 2. Visited check: Avoid revisiting already explored (position, direction) states\n      # to find the shortest path and prevent infinite loops.\n      if next_state_tuple in visited:\n        continue\n\n      # 3. Traversability check: Ensure the cell is not an obstacle.\n      #    A cell is an obstacle if it contains any non-grabbable item.\n      is_obstacle = False\n      for obstacle_idx in non_grabbable_obstacle_indices:\n        if grid[next_x, next_y, obstacle_idx] > 0:\n          is_obstacle = True\n          break\n      if is_obstacle:\n        continue # Cannot move into an obstacle cell\n\n      # If all checks pass, add the new state to the queue and mark it as visited.\n      visited.add(next_state_tuple)\n      queue.append((next_state_tuple, path + [action]))\n\n  # If the BFS queue becomes empty and no path to the primitive (for a 'USE' action) was found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable.\n  return []", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:22:50.510282", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  primitive_idx = cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n\n  # Check if the primitive is already in inventory. If so, no actions are needed.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # Ensure the requested primitive is actually grabbable. Non-grabbable entities\n  # (like \"water\", \"boundary\", or a \"workshop\") cannot be \"collected\" into inventory.\n  # If a primitive cannot be grabbed, return an empty list of actions.\n  if primitive_idx not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_x, start_y = current_state.pos\n  start_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's current facing direction (0:N, 1:E, 2:S, 3:W)\n\n  # Use the comprehensive set of non-grabbable indices from the world object\n  # to determine impassable terrain (obstacles).\n  non_grabbable_obstacle_indices = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Define movement actions and their effects on (dx, dy) and new_direction.\n  # The agent's direction is updated to face the direction of movement after a move.\n  action_effects = {\n      craft.UP: (0, -1, 0),    # Move North (y-1), new_dir = 0 (North)\n      craft.DOWN: (0, 1, 2),     # Move South (y+1), new_dir = 2 (South)\n      craft.LEFT: (-1, 0, 3),    # Move West (x-1), new_dir = 3 (West)\n      craft.RIGHT: (1, 0, 1)     # Move East (x+1), new_dir = 1 (East)\n  }\n\n  # Mapping agent direction (0-3) to (dx, dy) for the cell *in front* of the agent.\n  # This is crucial for determining where a 'USE' action will interact.\n  FWD_DX = [0, 1, 0, -1] # dx for North, East, South, West\n  FWD_DY = [-1, 0, 1, 0] # dy for North, East, South, West\n\n  # BFS setup\n  # Queue stores tuples of ((current_x, current_y, current_dir), path_taken_so_far).\n  queue = collections.deque([((start_x, start_y, start_dir), [])])\n  # Set of visited states to prevent cycles and redundant exploration.\n  # A state now includes position AND direction, as direction affects possible actions (like USE).\n  visited = {(start_x, start_y, start_dir)}\n\n  while queue:\n    (x, y, d), path = queue.popleft()\n\n    # Check if a 'USE' action is possible from the current (x, y, d) state.\n    # The 'USE' action targets the cell directly in front of the agent.\n    target_x = x + FWD_DX[d]\n    target_y = y + FWD_DY[d]\n\n    # Check if the cell in front is within grid bounds and contains the primitive.\n    # This is the \"goal\" condition for collecting.\n    if (0 <= target_x < grid_width and 0 <= target_y < grid_height and\n        grid[target_x, target_y, primitive_idx] > 0):\n      # Found the primitive directly in front, so return the path to get here\n      # plus the 'USE' action to collect it.\n      return path + [craft.USE]\n\n    # Explore valid neighbor states by performing movement actions.\n    for action, (dx_move, dy_move, new_d) in action_effects.items():\n      next_x, next_y = x + dx_move, y + dy_move\n      next_state_tuple = (next_x, next_y, new_d) # New state includes new position and new direction\n\n      # 1. Bounds check: Ensure the new position is within the grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue\n\n      # 2. Visited check: Avoid revisiting already explored (position, direction) states\n      # to find the shortest path and prevent infinite loops.\n      if next_state_tuple in visited:\n        continue\n\n      # 3. Traversability check: Ensure the cell is not an obstacle.\n      #    A cell is an obstacle if it contains any non-grabbable item.\n      is_obstacle = False\n      for obstacle_idx in non_grabbable_obstacle_indices:\n        if grid[next_x, next_y, obstacle_idx] > 0:\n          is_obstacle = True\n          break\n      if is_obstacle:\n        continue # Cannot move into an obstacle cell\n\n      # If all checks pass, add the new state to the queue and mark it as visited.\n      visited.add(next_state_tuple)\n      queue.append((next_state_tuple, path + [action]))\n\n  # If the BFS queue becomes empty and no path to the primitive (for a 'USE' action) was found,\n  # it means the primitive is unreachable.\n  return []", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:23:22.822341", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "", "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:23:23.950865", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  if primitive_id is None:\n      return []\n\n  # Improvement: Filter out non-collectable environment features.\n  # The 'collect' function implies obtaining the item into inventory.\n  # Some 'primitives' in the DSL (e.g., WORKSHOP, BOUNDARY) are environmental\n  # features that cannot be picked up or harvested into inventory.\n  # If the primitive_id is in the set of non-grabbable entities AND it's not\n  # categorized as a 'primitive resource' (which suggests it can be harvested,\n  # like WOOD or STONE), then we assume it's not a valid target for 'collect'.\n  if (primitive_id in env.world.non_grabbable_indices and \n      primitive_id not in env.world.cookbook.primitives):\n      return []\n\n  state = env._current_state\n  current_pos = state.pos\n  current_dir = state.dir # Agent's initial facing direction (0=DOWN, 1=UP, 2=LEFT, 3=RIGHT)\n  grid = state.grid\n  \n  width, height, _ = grid.shape \n\n  actions_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP = actions_map['UP']\n  DOWN = actions_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = actions_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = actions_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = actions_map['USE']\n\n  # Map action index (which also corresponds to a direction) to its (dr, dc) delta.\n  # These deltas represent both the movement if that action is taken, and the direction faced after.\n  direction_deltas = {\n      DOWN: (1, 0),\n      UP: (-1, 0),\n      LEFT: (0, -1),\n      RIGHT: (0, 1)\n  }\n\n  # BFS setup:\n  # Queue stores tuples: ((row, col, facing_direction_idx), [list_of_actions_to_reach_this_state])\n  q = collections.deque([((current_pos[0], current_pos[1], current_dir), [])]) \n  \n  # Visited set stores (row, col, facing_direction_idx) tuples to prevent revisiting states\n  visited = {(current_pos[0], current_pos[1], current_dir)}\n\n  # Cache grabbable and non-grabbable indices for efficient lookup\n  grabbable_indices_set = set(env.world.grabbable_indices)\n  non_grabbable_indices_set = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  while q:\n      (r, c, d), path_actions = q.popleft()\n\n      # 1. Check if the current (r, c, d) state allows for immediate collection via USE action.\n      # The USE action interacts with the cell directly in front of the agent.\n      dr_face, dc_face = direction_deltas[d] # Get delta for the direction agent is currently facing\n      target_r, target_c = r + dr_face, c + dc_face # Coordinates of the cell directly in front\n\n      # Ensure the target cell is within grid boundaries\n      if 0 <= target_r < width and 0 <= target_c < height:\n          # Check if the target cell contains the primitive we want to collect\n          if grid[target_r, target_c, primitive_id] > 0:\n              # Path found! Append USE action and return.\n              return path_actions + [USE] \n\n      # 2. Explore movement neighbors (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT)\n      # Each movement action changes the agent's position and sets its new facing direction.\n      for move_action in [UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT]:\n          next_dir = move_action # After moving, agent faces the direction it just moved\n          dr_move, dc_move = direction_deltas[move_action] # Delta for the movement itself\n\n          nr, nc = r + dr_move, c + dc_move # New row, new col after movement\n          next_state_tuple = (nr, nc, next_dir) # The new state (position and facing direction)\n\n          # a. Check if the next position (nr, nc) is within grid boundaries\n          if not (0 <= nr < width and 0 <= nc < height):\n              continue\n          \n          # b. Improved Obstacle Check:\n          # A cell is considered an obstacle for movement if it contains:\n          #   - Any entity from the `non_grabbable_indices_set` (impassable terrain/structures).\n          #   - OR, the specific primitive we are trying to collect, IF that primitive is a grabbable item.\n          #     This prevents the agent from walking *onto* a grabbable item it intends to 'USE' from an adjacent square.\n          is_obstacle = False\n          \n          # Check for general non-grabbable obstacles (e.g., water, workshops, boundaries)\n          for non_grabbable_item_id in non_grabbable_indices_set:\n              if grid[nr, nc, non_grabbable_item_id] > 0:\n                  is_obstacle = True\n                  break\n          \n          # Additionally, if the target primitive is a grabbable item (like WOOD, STONE, GRASS, ROCK, GOLD, GEM) AND\n          # the next cell contains this primitive, consider it an obstacle for movement.\n          # This ensures the agent stops adjacent to it, ready to USE from an adjacent position.\n          # This check only applies if the cell wasn't already determined to be an obstacle by a non-grabbable item.\n          if not is_obstacle and primitive_id in grabbable_indices_set and grid[nr, nc, primitive_id] > 0:\n              is_obstacle = True\n\n          if is_obstacle:\n              continue\n\n          # c. If the new state (position and facing direction) has not been visited, add it to the queue\n          if next_state_tuple not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_state_tuple)\n              q.append((next_state_tuple, path_actions + [move_action]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and the primitive was not found anywhere reachable or collectable,\n  # return an empty list, indicating no path was found.\n  return []", "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T05:24:06.533180", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1`.\"\"\"\n  \"\"\"Finds the shortest sequence of actions to move the agent to a position adjacent\n  to the specified primitive, facing it, and then performing a 'USE' action to collect it.\n  \n  This function uses a Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the optimal path\n  in terms of actions (movements and turns) from the agent's current state\n  to a state where the primitive is directly in front, ready to be 'USE'd.\n\n    Args:\n        env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab object containing the current state of the simulation.\n        primitive (str): The name of the primitive resource (e.g., \"WOOD\", \"STONE\") to collect.\n\n    Returns:\n        List[int]: A sequence of action indices (integers) to execute. The list\n                   will be empty if the primitive is not found or is unreachable.\n  \"\"\"\n  actions_list = []\n  current_state = env._current_state # Access the current CraftState from the CraftLab environment\n\n  grid = current_state.grid # numpy.ndarray of shape (num_rows, num_cols, n_kinds)\n  initial_pos = current_state.pos  # (row, col) tuple for the agent's current position\n  initial_dir = current_state.dir  # int representing agent's current facing direction (0:RIGHT, 1:UP, 2:LEFT, 3:DOWN)\n\n  # Get the integer ID for the target primitive from the world's cookbook index.\n  primitive_id = current_state.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  # Grid dimensions\n  num_rows, num_cols, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Retrieve action mapping from the environment (e.g., 'UP' -> 1, 'USE' -> 4)\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION = action_map['UP']\n  TURN_LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  TURN_RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define changes in (row, col) for each facing direction when moving forward.\n  DIR_TO_DRDC = {\n      0: (0, 1),   # Facing RIGHT: (row, col+1)\n      1: (-1, 0),  # Facing UP: (row-1, col)\n      2: (0, -1),  # Facing LEFT: (row, col-1)\n      3: (1, 0)    # Facing DOWN: (row+1, col)\n  }\n\n  # Define how agent's direction changes when turning left or right.\n  TURN_LEFT_MAP = {0: 1, 1: 2, 2: 3, 3: 0}  # RIGHT->UP->LEFT->DOWN->RIGHT\n  TURN_RIGHT_MAP = {0: 3, 1: 0, 2: 1, 3: 2} # RIGHT->DOWN->LEFT->UP->RIGHT\n\n  # Identify entities that the agent cannot walk onto.\n  # These are typically non-grabbable entities that act as impassable terrain.\n  non_walkable_kind_indices = current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  def _is_in_bounds(r: int, c: int) -> bool:\n      \"\"\"Checks if a given coordinate (r, c) is within the grid boundaries.\"\"\"\n      return 0 <= r < num_rows and 0 <= c < num_cols\n\n  def _is_cell_walkable(r: int, c: int, target_primitive_id: int) -> bool:\n      \"\"\"\n      Checks if the agent can move onto the cell (r, c).\n      A cell is not walkable if it's out of bounds, contains the target primitive,\n      or contains any non-grabbable (impassable) entity.\n      \"\"\"\n      if not _is_in_bounds(r, c):\n          return False\n      \n      # Agent cannot walk onto the primitive it intends to collect; it must be adjacent.\n      if grid[r, c, target_primitive_id] > 0:\n          return False\n\n      # Check for other non-grabbable (typically impassable) entities.\n      for kind_idx in non_walkable_kind_indices:\n          if grid[r, c, kind_idx] > 0:\n              return False\n      return True\n\n  # BFS Initialization:\n  # Queue stores tuples: ((current_position_tuple, current_direction_int), list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n  queue = collections.deque([((initial_pos, initial_dir), [])])\n  \n  # Visited set stores (position_tuple, direction_int) to prevent cycles and redundant path computations.\n  # A state is defined by both position and direction.\n  visited = {(initial_pos, initial_dir)}\n\n  path_to_primitive_front = None # This will store the sequence of actions to reach the state where the primitive is in front.\n\n  while queue:\n      (current_pos, current_dir), path_so_far = queue.popleft()\n      r, c = current_pos\n\n      # Check if the primitive is directly in front of the agent from the current state.\n      # This is the goal condition for the BFS: agent is adjacent and facing the primitive.\n      front_dr, front_dc = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n      front_r, front_c = r + front_dr, c + front_dc\n      \n      if _is_in_bounds(front_r, front_c) and grid[front_r, front_c, primitive_id] > 0:\n          path_to_primitive_front = path_so_far\n          break # Path to target adjacency found, stop BFS.\n\n      # Explore possible next actions: Move Forward, Turn Left, Turn Right.\n\n      # 1. Try Move Forward action:\n      move_dr, move_dc = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n      next_r_move, next_c_move = r + move_dr, c + move_dc\n      next_pos_move = (next_r_move, next_c_move)\n      next_dir_move = current_dir # Moving forward does not change direction.\n\n      if _is_cell_walkable(next_r_move, next_c_move, primitive_id) and \\\n         (next_pos_move, next_dir_move) not in visited:\n          \n          visited.add((next_pos_move, next_dir_move))\n          queue.append(((next_pos_move, next_dir_move), path_so_far + [MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION]))\n\n      # 2. Try Turn Left action:\n      next_dir_left = TURN_LEFT_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Turning only changes direction, not position.\n      if (current_pos, next_dir_left) not in visited:\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_left))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_left), path_so_far + [TURN_LEFT_ACTION]))\n\n      # 3. Try Turn Right action:\n      next_dir_right = TURN_RIGHT_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Turning only changes direction, not position.\n      if (current_pos, next_dir_right) not in visited:\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_right))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_right), path_so_far + [TURN_RIGHT_ACTION]))\n\n  # After BFS completes:\n  # If a path to the target adjacency state was found, extend the actions list with that path\n  # and then append the final USE action to collect the primitive.\n  if path_to_primitive_front is not None:\n      actions_list.extend(path_to_primitive_front)\n      actions_list.append(USE_ACTION)\n\n  return actions_list", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
