{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T06:38:44.289597", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  \n  # Get the integer index for the desired primitive from the world's cookbook.\n  # Using __getitem__ (env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]) which returns None if the\n  # primitive name is not found. This makes the function robust against unknown primitive names.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  if primitive_idx is None:\n    # If the primitive name is not found in the cookbook's index, it's an invalid target.\n    # Return an empty list as no actions can be taken.\n    return []\n  \n  # Optimization: If the agent already has at least one of the primitive in its inventory,\n  # no further collection actions are needed.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return [] # Already have it, return an empty action list.\n\n  # Retrieve action mappings from the environment's action_specs for clarity and to ensure\n  # correct action indices are used for movement and interaction.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # 1. Immediate collection check:\n  # Determine if the agent is currently positioned within the 3x3 neighborhood (Moore neighborhood)\n  # of the primitive. This neighborhood includes the agent's current cell itself.\n  # If so, a single 'USE' action is sufficient to collect it.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n    # The agent is in a valid position to interact with and collect the primitive.\n    return [USE]\n\n  # 2. Identify all grid locations where instances of the primitive exist.\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n  \n  primitive_locations = []\n  # Utilize numpy.where for an efficient vectorized search of all cells in the grid\n  # where the count of the primitive is greater than zero.\n  primitive_x_coords, primitive_y_coords = np.where(grid[:, :, primitive_idx] > 0)\n  for x, y in zip(primitive_x_coords, primitive_y_coords):\n      primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  # If no instances of the primitive are found anywhere on the grid, it cannot be collected.\n  if not primitive_locations:\n    return []\n\n  # 3. Define \"goal cells\" for the Breadth-First Search (BFS).\n  # A goal cell is any cell from which the agent can successfully collect the primitive.\n  # Since CraftState.next_to checks the 3x3 neighborhood, any cell in this vicinity\n  # of a primitive location is a valid goal to move to before using 'USE'.\n  goal_cells = set()\n  for px, py in primitive_locations:\n    # Iterate through all 3x3 relative offsets (dx, dy) including (0,0) for the primitive's own cell.\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        gx, gy = px + dx, py + dy\n        # Ensure the calculated potential goal cell (gx, gy) is within the grid boundaries.\n        if 0 <= gx < grid_width and 0 <= gy < grid_height:\n          goal_cells.add((gx, gy))\n\n  # 4. Determine which entity kinds make a cell impassable for agent movement.\n  # Impassable kinds are typically non-grabbable items (e.g., water, boundary) that the agent\n  # cannot walk over. Workshop locations, though non-grabbable, are usually traversable,\n  # so they are explicitly excluded from the impassable list.\n  # Convert the resulting set difference to a list for efficient NumPy indexing.\n  impassable_kinds = list(set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices) - set(env.world.workshop_indices))\n\n  # 5. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest sequence of movement actions\n  # from the agent's current position to any of the identified goal cells.\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  \n  # The queue for BFS stores tuples of (current_position, path_taken_actions_to_reach_here).\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) \n  # A set to keep track of visited positions to prevent revisiting cells and ensure the\n  # shortest path is found by exploring layer by layer.\n  visited = {start_pos} \n\n  # Define possible cardinal moves (delta_x, delta_y) and their corresponding action indices.\n  DELTAS_ACTIONS = [\n      ((0, -1), UP),    # Move North (decreases Y coordinate)\n      ((0, 1), DOWN),   # Move South (increases Y coordinate)\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT),  # Move West (decreases X coordinate)\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT),  # Move East (increases X coordinate)\n  ]\n\n  while q:\n    (cx, cy), path_so_far = q.popleft() # Dequeue the current position and the path leading to it.\n\n    # If the current position is one of our designated goal cells, the shortest path has been found.\n    if (cx, cy) in goal_cells:\n      # Append the 'USE' action to the path, as the agent is now in position to collect.\n      return path_so_far + [USE]\n\n    # Explore all valid neighboring cells reachable by cardinal movement.\n    for (dx, dy), action in DELTAS_ACTIONS:\n      nx, ny = cx + dx, cy + dy # Calculate the new potential position.\n\n      # Check if the new position is within the overall grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height):\n        continue # Skip if out of bounds.\n\n      # Check if the new position is traversable (i.e., it does not contain any impassable kind).\n      # Using NumPy's `any` for efficient checking if any impassable item exists at (nx, ny).\n      is_impassable_cell = False\n      if impassable_kinds: # Only perform the check if there are actual impassable kinds defined.\n          is_impassable_cell = np.any(grid[nx, ny, impassable_kinds] > 0)\n      \n      if is_impassable_cell:\n          continue # Skip this cell if it's impassable.\n\n      # If the new position is valid and has not been visited yet, add it to the queue for exploration.\n      new_pos = (nx, ny)\n      if new_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(new_pos)\n        q.append((new_pos, path_so_far + [action]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and the queue becomes empty without finding a path to any goal cell,\n  # it implies that the primitive is unreachable from the agent's current position.\n  return []", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T06:39:29.989175", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions_list = []\n  current_state = env._current_state # Access the underlying CraftState for detailed info\n\n  initial_grid = current_state.grid # (rows, columns, kinds) numpy array\n  initial_agent_pos = current_state.pos  # Agent's starting position (row, col)\n  initial_agent_dir = current_state.dir  # Agent's starting facing direction (0:RIGHT, 1:UP, 2:LEFT, 3:DOWN)\n\n  # Get the integer ID for the target primitive from the cookbook's index\n  primitive_id = current_state.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  # Determine grid dimensions for boundary checks\n  grid_rows, grid_cols, _ = initial_grid.shape\n\n  # Retrieve integer action IDs from the environment's action specifications\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION = action_map['UP']\n  TURN_LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  TURN_RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Direction vectors (dr, dc) for agent's facing direction.\n  # Mapping: 0:RIGHT, 1:UP, 2:LEFT, 3:DOWN\n  DIR_TO_DRDC = {\n      0: (0, 1),   # Facing RIGHT\n      1: (-1, 0),  # Facing UP\n      2: (0, -1),  # Facing LEFT\n      3: (1, 0)    # Facing DOWN\n  }\n\n  # Mapping for updating agent's direction when turning left or right.\n  TURN_LEFT_DIR_MAP = {0: 1, 1: 2, 2: 3, 3: 0}\n  TURN_RIGHT_DIR_MAP = {0: 3, 1: 0, 2: 1, 3: 2}\n\n  # Get indices of entities that block agent movement (e.g., BOUNDARY, WATER, WORKSHOP_X).\n  non_walkable_kinds_indices = current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices\n  # Convert to list once for efficient NumPy array indexing, as it's a set.\n  non_walkable_kinds_list = list(non_walkable_kinds_indices)\n\n\n  # Helper function to check if a cell is within grid boundaries\n  def is_in_bounds(r: int, c: int) -> bool:\n      return 0 <= r < grid_rows and 0 <= c < grid_cols\n\n  # Helper function to check if an agent can walk onto a specific cell.\n  # A cell is not walkable if it's out of bounds, contains a non-grabbable entity,\n  # or contains the primitive itself (agent must stand adjacent to primitive).\n  def is_cell_walkable(r: int, c: int, target_primitive_id: int) -> bool:\n      if not is_in_bounds(r, c):\n          return False\n      \n      # Agent cannot walk onto the primitive it wants to collect.\n      if initial_grid[r, c, target_primitive_id] > 0:\n          return False\n\n      # Check if the cell contains any non-walkable (non-grabbable) entity.\n      if non_walkable_kinds_list and np.any(initial_grid[r, c, non_walkable_kinds_list] > 0):\n          return False\n          \n      return True\n\n  # BFS Initialization:\n  # The queue stores tuples: ((current_position_tuple, current_direction_int), list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n  queue = collections.deque([((initial_agent_pos, initial_agent_dir), [])])\n  \n  # The visited set stores (position_tuple, direction_int) to avoid redundant computations and cycles.\n  visited = {(initial_agent_pos, initial_agent_dir)}\n\n  path_to_primitive_adjacency = None # This will store the sequence of actions.\n\n  while queue:\n      (current_pos, current_dir), path_taken = queue.popleft()\n      current_row, current_col = current_pos\n\n      # 1. Check if the primitive is directly in front of the agent from the current state.\n      front_dr, front_dc = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n      front_cell_row, front_cell_col = current_row + front_dr, current_col + front_dc\n      \n      if is_in_bounds(front_cell_row, front_cell_col):\n          # If the primitive is present in the cell directly in front, we found our target.\n          if initial_grid[front_cell_row, front_cell_col, primitive_id] > 0:\n              path_to_primitive_adjacency = path_taken\n              break # Target state found, stop BFS.\n\n      # 2. Explore possible next actions: Move Forward, Turn Left, Turn Right.\n\n      # Try Move Forward action:\n      move_dr, move_dc = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n      next_row, next_col = current_row + move_dr, current_col + move_dc\n      next_pos = (next_row, next_col)\n      next_dir = current_dir # Moving forward does not change facing direction\n\n      # If the next position is walkable and this state hasn't been visited, add it to the queue.\n      if ((next_pos, next_dir) not in visited and \n          is_cell_walkable(next_row, next_col, primitive_id)):\n          \n          visited.add((next_pos, next_dir))\n          queue.append(((next_pos, next_dir), path_taken + [MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION]))\n\n      # Try Turn Left action:\n      next_dir_left = TURN_LEFT_DIR_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Turning only changes direction, not position.\n      if ((current_pos, next_dir_left) not in visited):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_left))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_left), path_taken + [TURN_LEFT_ACTION]))\n\n      # Try Turn Right action:\n      next_dir_right = TURN_RIGHT_DIR_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Turning only changes direction, not position.\n      if ((current_pos, next_dir_right) not in visited):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_right))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_right), path_taken + [TURN_RIGHT_ACTION]))\n\n  # After BFS completes (either target found or queue empty):\n  # If a path to the target adjacency state was found, append the USE action to complete the collection.\n  if path_to_primitive_adjacency is not None:\n      actions_list.extend(path_to_primitive_adjacency)\n      actions_list.append(USE_ACTION)\n\n  return actions_list", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T06:39:31.124881", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T06:40:43.022719", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v0`.\n\n    This function uses a Breadth-First Search (BFS) algorithm to find the shortest\n    sequence of actions (moves and turns) to position the agent directly in front\n    of the specified primitive. Once the agent is in this \"ready-to-use\" position,\n    a 'USE' action is appended to the sequence.\n\n    The pathfinding considers the grid layout at the time the function is called,\n    identifying walkable cells and avoiding obstacles or walking onto the primitive itself.\n\n    Args:\n        env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab environment object representing the current game state.\n        primitive (str): The name of the primitive item or object to find and collect/use.\n\n    Returns:\n        List[int]: A sequence of action indices to execute (e.g., [MOVE_FORWARD, TURN_LEFT, USE]).\n                   Returns an empty list if the primitive is unreachable or not found.\n  \"\"\"\n  # Initialize the list to store the sequence of actions that will be returned.\n  actions_list = []\n\n  # Get the current state of the environment. This is the starting point for our pathfinding.\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  \n  # Snapshot the initial grid, agent's position, and direction from the current state.\n  # These are used as constants for the BFS search space.\n  grid_snapshot = current_state.grid\n  start_pos = current_state.pos  # Agent's starting position (row, col tuple)\n  start_dir = current_state.dir  # Agent's starting direction (0:RIGHT, 1:UP, 2:LEFT, 3:DOWN)\n\n  # Resolve the primitive's string name to its unique integer ID, as used in the grid and inventory.\n  primitive_id = current_state.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  # Get the dimensions of the grid for boundary checks during pathfinding.\n  GRID_ROWS, GRID_COLS, _ = grid_snapshot.shape\n\n  # Retrieve integer action codes from the environment's action specifications.\n  # These are used to construct the action sequence.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION = action_map['UP']    # In CraftWorld, 'UP' typically moves the agent forward.\n  TURN_LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']     # Changes agent's facing direction counter-clockwise.\n  TURN_RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']   # Changes agent's facing direction clockwise.\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']            # Interacts with the cell directly in front of the agent.\n\n  # Define how agent's position changes for each facing direction when moving forward.\n  # (delta_row, delta_column)\n  DIR_TO_DRDC = {\n      0: (0, 1),   # Facing RIGHT: moves to (row, col + 1)\n      1: (-1, 0),  # Facing UP: moves to (row - 1, col)\n      2: (0, -1),  # Facing LEFT: moves to (row, col - 1)\n      3: (1, 0)    # Facing DOWN: moves to (row + 1, col)\n  }\n\n  # Define how agent's direction changes when turning left or right.\n  TURN_LEFT_MAP = {0: 1, 1: 2, 2: 3, 3: 0}   # E.g., RIGHT (0) turns to UP (1)\n  TURN_RIGHT_MAP = {0: 3, 1: 0, 2: 1, 3: 2}  # E.g., RIGHT (0) turns to DOWN (3)\n\n  # Get the set of entity indices that are considered non-grabbable and block movement.\n  # The agent cannot move into cells occupied by these kinds.\n  blocking_kind_indices = current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # Initialize the BFS queue. Each element is a tuple:\n  # ((current_position_tuple, current_direction_int), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_this_state).\n  queue = collections.deque([((start_pos, start_dir), [])])\n  \n  # Initialize the set of visited states to prevent cycles and redundant exploration.\n  # A state is defined by (position, direction).\n  visited = {(start_pos, start_dir)}\n\n  # This variable will store the shortest sequence of actions to reach the specific state\n  # where the agent is correctly positioned and oriented to 'USE' the primitive.\n  path_to_primitive_use_state = None\n\n  # Start the Breadth-First Search.\n  while queue:\n      # Dequeue the next state to explore.\n      (current_pos, current_dir), path_so_far = queue.popleft()\n      current_r, current_c = current_pos # Unpack current row and column.\n\n      # 1. Check if the current state is the goal state: agent is adjacent to and facing the primitive.\n      dr_front, dc_front = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir] # Get deltas for the cell directly in front.\n      front_r, front_c = current_r + dr_front, current_c + dc_front # Calculate coords of cell in front.\n      \n      # Check if the cell in front is within grid boundaries.\n      if (0 <= front_r < GRID_ROWS and 0 <= front_c < GRID_COLS):\n          # If the primitive is found in the cell directly in front, we've found the target.\n          if grid_snapshot[front_r, front_c, primitive_id] > 0:\n              path_to_primitive_use_state = path_so_far\n              break # Found the shortest path, no need to explore further.\n\n      # 2. Explore possible next actions from the current state: Move Forward, Turn Left, Turn Right.\n\n      # A. Try moving Forward (using the 'UP' action)\n      move_dr, move_dc = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir] # Deltas for moving forward.\n      next_r_move, next_c_move = current_r + move_dr, current_c + move_dc\n      next_pos_move = (next_r_move, next_c_move)\n      next_dir_move = current_dir # Direction doesn't change when moving forward.\n\n      # Check if the potential next position is valid (within bounds and not previously visited with this direction).\n      if (0 <= next_r_move < GRID_ROWS and 0 <= next_c_move < GRID_COLS and\n          (next_pos_move, next_dir_move) not in visited):\n          \n          # Check if the target cell for movement is walkable.\n          # It's not walkable if it contains a blocking entity or is the primitive itself (cannot walk onto items to collect them).\n          is_walkable_cell = True\n          # Check for non-grabbable blocking entities (like boundaries, water, workshops).\n          for kind_idx in blocking_kind_indices:\n              if grid_snapshot[next_r_move, next_c_move, kind_idx] > 0:\n                  is_walkable_cell = False\n                  break # This cell contains a blocking obstacle.\n          \n          # Crucially, prevent walking onto the primitive itself, even if it's grabbable.\n          # The agent needs to stand *next to* it to 'USE'/'collect' it.\n          if grid_snapshot[next_r_move, next_c_move, primitive_id] > 0:\n              is_walkable_cell = False # Cannot walk onto the item we intend to collect.\n\n          if is_walkable_cell:\n              visited.add((next_pos_move, next_dir_move))\n              queue.append(((next_pos_move, next_dir_move), path_so_far + [MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION]))\n\n      # B. Try turning Left (using the 'LEFT' action)\n      next_dir_turn_left = TURN_LEFT_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Position remains unchanged when turning, only direction changes.\n      if ((current_pos, next_dir_turn_left) not in visited):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_turn_left))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_turn_left), path_so_far + [TURN_LEFT_ACTION]))\n\n      # C. Try turning Right (using the 'RIGHT' action)\n      next_dir_turn_right = TURN_RIGHT_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Position remains unchanged when turning, only direction changes.\n      if ((current_pos, next_dir_turn_right) not in visited):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_turn_right))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_turn_right), path_so_far + [TURN_RIGHT_ACTION]))\n\n  # After the BFS concludes:\n  # If a path was successfully found to a state ready for interaction, append the final 'USE' action.\n  if path_to_primitive_use_state is not None:\n      actions_list.extend(path_to_primitive_use_state)\n      actions_list.append(USE_ACTION)\n  \n  # Return the complete sequence of actions. If no path was found, `actions_list` will be empty.\n  return actions_list", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T06:40:44.246980", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions_list = []\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  initial_grid = current_state.grid\n  initial_pos = current_state.pos # tuple (row, col)\n  initial_dir = current_state.dir # int (0-3), 0:RIGHT, 1:UP, 2:LEFT, 3:D\n\n  primitive_id = current_state.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  GRID_ROWS, GRID_COLS, _ = initial_grid.shape # Grid dimensions (rows, columns)\n\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION = action_map['UP'] # 'UP' usually means moving forward relative to agent's facing direction\n  TURN_LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  TURN_RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Direction mapping: (dr, dc) for agent's facing direction (0:R, 1:U, 2:L, 3:D)\n  DIR_TO_DRDC = {\n      0: (0, 1),   # Facing RIGHT: (row, col + 1)\n      1: (-1, 0),  # Facing UP: (row - 1, col)\n      2: (0, -1),  # Facing LEFT: (row, col - 1)\n      3: (1, 0)    # Facing DOWN: (row + 1, col)\n  }\n\n  # Map for updating the agent's direction when turning left or right.\n  TURN_LEFT_MAP = {0: 1, 1: 2, 2: 3, 3: 0}\n  TURN_RIGHT_MAP = {0: 3, 1: 0, 2: 1, 3: 2}\n\n  # Get indices of entities that inherently block movement (e.g., BOUNDARY, WATER, WORKSHOP_X).\n  blocking_kind_indices = current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # --- Improvement for collect_v1: Check if already in position to use the primitive ---\n  # Calculate the cell directly in front of the agent based on its current position and direction.\n  r_curr, c_curr = initial_pos\n  dr_front, dc_front = DIR_TO_DRDC[initial_dir]\n  r_front, c_front = r_curr + dr_front, c_curr + dc_front\n\n  # If the cell in front is within bounds and contains the primitive, the agent can use it immediately.\n  if (0 <= r_front < GRID_ROWS and 0 <= c_front < GRID_COLS and\n      initial_grid[r_front, c_front, primitive_id] > 0):\n      return [USE_ACTION]\n  # --- End of improvement ---\n\n  # BFS state representation: ((current_pos_tuple, current_dir_int), list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n  queue = collections.deque([((initial_pos, initial_dir), [])])\n  visited = {(initial_pos, initial_dir)} # Track (position, direction) pairs to avoid cycles and redundant paths.\n\n  target_path_actions = None # Stores the shortest sequence of actions to reach the \"ready to use\" state.\n\n  while queue:\n      (current_pos, current_dir), path_so_far = queue.popleft()\n      r, c = current_pos\n\n      # Check if the primitive is directly in front of the agent at the *current* state in BFS.\n      # This is the goal condition for the BFS: find a path to a cell *adjacent* to the primitive,\n      # with the agent facing the primitive.\n      dr_front, dc_front = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n      r_front, c_front = r + dr_front, c + dc_front\n      \n      if (0 <= r_front < GRID_ROWS and 0 <= c_front < GRID_COLS):\n          if initial_grid[r_front, c_front, primitive_id] > 0:\n              target_path_actions = path_so_far\n              break # Shortest path found, terminate BFS.\n\n      # Explore possible next actions from the current state: Move Forward, Turn Left, Turn Right.\n      \n      # 1. Try moving Forward\n      dr_move, dc_move = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n      next_r, next_c = r + dr_move, c + dc_move\n      next_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n      next_dir = current_dir # Moving forward does not change facing direction.\n\n      # Check if the next position is within grid bounds.\n      if (0 <= next_r < GRID_ROWS and 0 <= next_c < GRID_COLS):\n          # Check if this (position, direction) state has already been visited.\n          if (next_pos, next_dir) not in visited:\n              # Determine if the 'next_pos' cell is walkable.\n              # A cell is not walkable if it contains any 'blocking_kind' (e.g., boundaries, water).\n              # Also, the agent cannot walk *onto* the primitive itself; it must stand *adjacent* to it.\n              is_walkable = True\n              for kind_idx in blocking_kind_indices:\n                  if initial_grid[next_r, next_c, kind_idx] > 0:\n                      is_walkable = False\n                      break\n              \n              if is_walkable and initial_grid[next_r, next_c, primitive_id] > 0:\n                  is_walkable = False # Cannot walk onto the target primitive\n\n              if is_walkable:\n                  visited.add((next_pos, next_dir))\n                  queue.append(((next_pos, next_dir), path_so_far + [MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION]))\n\n      # 2. Try turning Left\n      next_dir_left = TURN_LEFT_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Turning does not change position, only direction.\n      if ((current_pos, next_dir_left) not in visited):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_left))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_left), path_so_far + [TURN_LEFT_ACTION]))\n\n      # 3. Try turning Right\n      next_dir_right = TURN_RIGHT_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Turning does not change position, only direction.\n      if ((current_pos, next_dir_right) not in visited):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_right))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_right), path_so_far + [TURN_RIGHT_ACTION]))\n\n  # If a path was found to the \"ready to use\" state, append the final USE action.\n  if target_path_actions is not None:\n      actions_list.extend(target_path_actions)\n      actions_list.append(USE_ACTION)\n\n  return actions_list", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T06:41:38.242050", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1`.\n  This function determines the shortest sequence of actions (movements and 'USE')\n  required to collect a specified primitive item in the CraftWorld environment.\n  It leverages Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the optimal path.\n\n  Args:\n      env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab environment instance.\n      primitive (str): The string name of the primitive item to collect (e.g., \"WOOD\", \"STONE\").\n\n  Returns:\n      List[int]: A list of integer action codes (e.g., UP, DOWN, USE) to achieve the collection.\n                 Returns an empty list if the primitive is already in inventory, not found on the map,\n                 or unreachable.\n  \"\"\"\n  current_state = env._current_state\n\n  # --- 1. Map Item Name to Index and Action Names to Codes ---\n  # Get the integer index for the primitive from the cookbook.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n\n  # Get numerical action codes from the environment's action specifications.\n  action_codes = env.action_specs()\n  UP = action_codes['UP']\n  DOWN = action_codes['DOWN']\n  LEFT = action_codes['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_codes['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_codes['USE']\n\n  # --- 2. Early Exit: Check if the primitive is already in the agent's inventory ---\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return [] # Primitive is already collected, no actions needed.\n\n  # --- 3. Immediate Collection Check: Agent is already adjacent to the primitive ---\n  # The `next_to` method checks if the primitive is in the 3x3 neighborhood of the agent.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n    return [USE] # Agent is in position, just use the item.\n\n  # --- 4. Identify Physical Locations of the Primitive on the Grid ---\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n  \n  primitive_locations_on_grid = []\n  for x in range(grid_width):\n    for y in range(grid_height):\n      # Check if the primitive kind exists at this (x, y) cell location.\n      if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n        primitive_locations_on_grid.append((x, y))\n\n  # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the current grid, it's unreachable.\n  if not primitive_locations_on_grid:\n    return [] # Primitive is not present in the environment.\n\n  # --- 5. Define \"Goal Cells\" for Agent Movement ---\n  # A \"goal cell\" is any grid cell from which the agent can perform the 'USE' action\n  # to collect the primitive. This implies any cell in the 3x3 neighborhood\n  # (including the cell itself) of a primitive's location.\n  collectible_agent_positions = set()\n  for px, py in primitive_locations_on_grid:\n    # Iterate through the 3x3 area around the primitive's location (px, py).\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        ax, ay = px + dx, py + dy # Candidate agent position.\n        # Ensure the candidate agent position is within grid boundaries.\n        if 0 <= ax < grid_width and 0 <= ay < grid_height:\n          collectible_agent_positions.add((ax, ay))\n\n  # --- 6. Pre-calculate Impassable Terrain Kinds for Pathfinding ---\n  # These are entities that block agent movement. In CraftWorld, these are typically\n  # non-grabbable items that are *not* workshops (which are usually traversable).\n  # This set will be used to determine if a grid cell is blocked for movement.\n  impassable_terrain_kinds = set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices) - set(env.world.workshop_indices)\n\n  # --- 7. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to Find the Shortest Path ---\n  start_position = current_state.pos # Agent's current (x, y) position.\n  \n  # BFS queue: Stores tuples of (current_position (x,y), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here).\n  bfs_queue = collections.deque([(start_position, [])]) \n  \n  # Set to keep track of visited grid positions to prevent redundant exploration and cycles.\n  visited_positions = {start_position} \n\n  # Define possible movement deltas (dx, dy) and their corresponding action codes.\n  # This mapping simplifies iterating through neighbors.\n  MOVE_DELTAS_AND_ACTIONS = [\n      ((0, -1), UP),    # Move North (decreases Y coordinate)\n      ((0, 1), DOWN),   # Move South (increases Y coordinate)\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT),  # Move West (decreases X coordinate)\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT),  # Move East (increases X coordinate)\n  ]\n\n  while bfs_queue:\n    (current_x, current_y), path_actions_so_far = bfs_queue.popleft() # Dequeue the current state.\n\n    # If the current agent position is one of the desired \"goal cells\",\n    # we have found the shortest path to a location from which collection is possible.\n    if (current_x, current_y) in collectible_agent_positions:\n      return path_actions_so_far + [USE] # Return the path followed by the 'USE' action.\n\n    # Explore all four valid neighboring cells for potential movement.\n    for (dx, dy), action_to_take in MOVE_DELTAS_AND_ACTIONS:\n      next_x, next_y = current_x + dx, current_y + dy # Calculate the new potential position.\n      next_position = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # Check if the new position is within the grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue # Out of bounds, skip this neighbor.\n\n      # Check if the new position is traversable (not blocked by impassable terrain).\n      # It's impassable if any of the defined impassable_terrain_kinds are present there.\n      is_impassable_at_next_pos = any(grid[next_x, next_y, k_idx] > 0 for k_idx in impassable_terrain_kinds)\n      \n      if is_impassable_at_next_pos:\n          continue # Cannot move to this cell, skip.\n\n      # If the new position is valid (within bounds, traversable) and has not been visited yet,\n      # add it to the BFS queue for further exploration.\n      if next_position not in visited_positions:\n        visited_positions.add(next_position) # Mark as visited.\n        bfs_queue.append((next_position, path_actions_so_far + [action_to_take]))\n\n  # --- 8. No Path Found ---\n  # If the BFS completes and the queue becomes empty without finding any goal cell,\n  # it means no path to a collectible location exists from the current agent state.\n  return [] # Primitive is unreachable on the current map.", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T06:41:39.438926", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  \n  # --- 1. Initialize Action Map and Primitive ID ---\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n  \n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # --- 2. Immediate Collection Check (Agent already adjacent) ---\n  # If the agent is already in a position to collect the primitive (i.e., it's within\n  # the 3x3 neighborhood based on `current_state.next_to`), simply use it.\n  # This assumes the 'USE' action is non-directional and acts upon any item\n  # in the 3x3 neighborhood of the agent, consistent with `CraftState.next_to`.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n    return [USE]\n\n  # --- 3. Identify all physical locations of the primitive on the grid ---\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n  \n  primitive_locations_on_grid = [] \n  for x in range(grid_width):\n    for y in range(grid_height):\n      if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0: # Check if the primitive kind exists at this cell\n        primitive_locations_on_grid.append((x, y))\n\n  # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the grid, it's currently unreachable.\n  if not primitive_locations_on_grid:\n    return []\n\n  # --- 4. Determine \"Goal Cells\" for BFS ---\n  # A \"goal cell\" for the agent's movement is any grid cell from which the 'USE'\n  # action can successfully collect the primitive. Since `USE` works if the primitive\n  # is in the agent's 3x3 neighborhood (`next_to` function implies this), any cell\n  # adjacent to (or on top of) a primitive's location is a valid goal cell for the\n  # agent's position.\n  collectible_agent_positions = set()\n  for px, py in primitive_locations_on_grid:\n    # Iterate through the 3x3 neighborhood around the primitive's location (px, py)\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        ax, ay = px + dx, py + dy # Candidate agent position\n        # Ensure the candidate agent position is within grid boundaries\n        if 0 <= ax < grid_width and 0 <= ay < grid_height:\n          collectible_agent_positions.add((ax, ay))\n\n  # --- 5. Pre-calculate Impassable Terrain Kinds ---\n  # These are entities that block agent movement. In CraftWorld, these are generally\n  # non-grabbable items that are not designated workshops (which are traversable).\n  impassable_terrain_kinds = set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices) - set(env.world.workshop_indices)\n\n  # --- 6. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) for the shortest path ---\n  start_position = current_state.pos\n  \n  # BFS queue: stores tuples of (current_position (x,y), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here).\n  bfs_queue = collections.deque([(start_position, [])]) \n  \n  # Set to keep track of visited grid positions to prevent cycles and redundant exploration.\n  visited_positions = {start_position} \n\n  # Define possible movement deltas (dx, dy) and their corresponding action indices.\n  MOVE_ACTIONS = [\n      ((0, -1), UP),    # North (decreases Y)\n      ((0, 1), DOWN),   # South (increases Y)\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT),  # West (decreases X)\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT),  # East (increases X)\n  ]\n\n  while bfs_queue:\n    (current_x, current_y), path_actions = bfs_queue.popleft() # Dequeue current state\n\n    # Check if the current agent position is one of the desired \"goal cells\".\n    # If so, we've found the shortest path to a location from which 'USE' can collect.\n    if (current_x, current_y) in collectible_agent_positions:\n      return path_actions + [USE]\n\n    # Explore all valid neighboring cells for movement.\n    for (dx, dy), action_to_take in MOVE_ACTIONS:\n      next_x, next_y = current_x + dx, current_y + dy # Calculate the new potential position\n      next_position = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # Check if the new position is within the grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue # Out of bounds, skip\n\n      # Check if the new position is traversable (not blocked by impassable terrain).\n      # A cell is impassable if it contains any kind from `impassable_terrain_kinds`.\n      is_impassable_location = any(grid[next_x, next_y, k_idx] > 0 for k_idx in impassable_terrain_kinds)\n      \n      if is_impassable_location:\n          continue # Cannot move to this cell, skip\n\n      # If the new position is valid and has not been visited yet, add it to the queue.\n      if next_position not in visited_positions:\n        visited_positions.add(next_position)\n        bfs_queue.append((next_position, path_actions + [action_to_take]))\n\n  # --- 7. No Path Found ---\n  # If the BFS completes and the queue is empty, it means no path to a collectible\n  # location was found from the current agent state.\n  return []", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T06:42:54.451794", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Returns a list of actions to find and collect the primitive in the passed env.\n    \n    This version implements a Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest\n    sequence of actions (movements and turns) to bring the agent adjacent to\n    the specified primitive and facing it, followed by a 'USE' action.\n\n    Args:\n        env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab object.\n        primitive (str): The name of the primitive to collect.\n\n    Returns:\n        List[int]: A sequence of action indices to execute. Returns an empty\n                   list if the primitive is not found or reachable.\n  \"\"\"\n  actions_list = []\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  initial_grid = current_state.grid\n  initial_pos = current_state.pos  # Agent's (row, col) tuple\n  initial_dir = current_state.dir  # Agent's facing direction (0:R, 1:U, 2:L, 3:D)\n\n  # Get the integer ID for the target primitive from the cookbook index\n  primitive_id = current_state.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  # Get grid dimensions for boundary checks\n  GRID_WIDTH, GRID_HEIGHT, _ = initial_grid.shape\n\n  # Map DSL movement/turn actions to their integer indices from env.action_specs()\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION = action_map['UP'] # 'UP' is typically used for 'move forward' in DMLab-style\n  TURN_LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  TURN_RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define changes in (row, col) for each direction when moving forward.\n  # Direction mapping: 0:RIGHT, 1:UP, 2:LEFT, 3:DOWN\n  DIR_TO_DRDC = {\n      0: (0, 1),   # Facing RIGHT: (row, col + 1)\n      1: (-1, 0),  # Facing UP: (row - 1, col)\n      2: (0, -1),  # Facing LEFT: (row, col - 1)\n      3: (1, 0)    # Facing DOWN: (row + 1, col)\n  }\n\n  # Define how the agent's direction changes when turning left/right.\n  TURN_LEFT_MAP = {0: 1, 1: 2, 2: 3, 3: 0}   # R -> U -> L -> D -> R (Counter-clockwise)\n  TURN_RIGHT_MAP = {0: 3, 1: 0, 2: 1, 3: 2}  # R -> D -> L -> U -> R (Clockwise)\n\n  # Compile a set of entity kinds that block agent movement.\n  # This includes non-grabbable items like boundaries, water, workshops.\n  # Crucially, the primitive itself is added here, as the agent must stop *adjacent* to it,\n  # not step onto its square, before using it.\n  non_walkable_kind_ids = current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices.copy()\n  non_walkable_kind_ids.add(primitive_id) # Agent cannot walk ONTO the primitive\n\n  # BFS state is represented by ( (row, col), direction ).\n  # The queue stores tuples: ( (current_position, current_direction), list_of_actions_to_reach_here ).\n  queue = collections.deque([((initial_pos, initial_dir), [])])\n  # The visited set stores (position, direction) tuples to prevent revisiting states and infinite loops.\n  visited = {(initial_pos, initial_dir)}\n\n  target_path = None # This will store the sequence of actions once the goal state is found.\n\n  while queue:\n      (current_pos, current_dir), path_so_far = queue.popleft()\n      r, c = current_pos\n\n      # 1. Check if the agent is in the \"goal state\": adjacent to and facing the primitive.\n      # Calculate the coordinates of the cell directly in front of the agent.\n      dr_front, dc_front = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n      front_r, front_c = r + dr_front, c + dc_front\n      \n      # Check if the cell in front is within grid bounds.\n      if (0 <= front_r < GRID_WIDTH and 0 <= front_c < GRID_HEIGHT):\n          # If the cell in front contains the target primitive, we've found our path.\n          if initial_grid[front_r, front_c, primitive_id] > 0:\n              target_path = path_so_far # The path to reach this state\n              break # Shortest path found, exit BFS.\n\n      # 2. Explore possible next actions (Move Forward, Turn Left, Turn Right) from the current state.\n      \n      # --- Try Move Forward ---\n      move_dr, move_dc = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n      next_r, next_c = r + move_dr, c + move_dc\n      next_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n      next_dir = current_dir # Moving forward does not change the agent's facing direction.\n\n      # Check if the next position is within bounds and if this (pos, dir) state hasn't been visited.\n      if (0 <= next_r < GRID_WIDTH and 0 <= next_c < GRID_HEIGHT and\n          (next_pos, next_dir) not in visited):\n          \n          # Check if the next position is walkable (i.e., it does not contain any obstacle kind).\n          is_walkable_cell = True\n          for kind_idx in non_walkable_kind_ids:\n              if initial_grid[next_r, next_c, kind_idx] > 0:\n                  is_walkable_cell = False\n                  break\n          \n          if is_walkable_cell:\n              visited.add((next_pos, next_dir))\n              queue.append(((next_pos, next_dir), path_so_far + [MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION]))\n\n      # --- Try Turn Left ---\n      next_dir_left = TURN_LEFT_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Turning changes only direction, not position.\n      if ((current_pos, next_dir_left) not in visited):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_left))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_left), path_so_far + [TURN_LEFT_ACTION]))\n\n      # --- Try Turn Right ---\n      next_dir_right = TURN_RIGHT_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Turning changes only direction, not position.\n      if ((current_pos, next_dir_right) not in visited):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_right))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_right), path_so_far + [TURN_RIGHT_ACTION]))\n\n  # If a path to the goal state (adjacent and facing primitive) was found, append the USE action.\n  if target_path is not None:\n      actions_list.extend(target_path)\n      actions_list.append(USE_ACTION)\n\n  return actions_list", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T06:42:55.633949", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions_list = []\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  initial_grid = current_state.grid\n  initial_pos = current_state.pos # (row, col)\n  initial_dir = current_state.dir # int (0:RIGHT, 1:UP, 2:LEFT, 3:DOWN)\n\n  primitive_id = current_state.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = initial_grid.shape\n\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION = action_map['UP'] # Assuming 'UP' means move forward\n  TURN_LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  TURN_RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Direction mapping: (dr, dc) for agent's facing direction (0:R, 1:U, 2:L, 3:D)\n  DIR_TO_DRDC = {\n      0: (0, 1),   # Facing RIGHT, move positive column\n      1: (-1, 0),  # Facing UP, move negative row\n      2: (0, -1),  # Facing LEFT, move negative column\n      3: (1, 0)    # Facing DOWN, move positive row\n  }\n\n  # Map for turning left/right, updating the agent's direction (0-3)\n  TURN_LEFT_MAP = {0: 1, 1: 2, 2: 3, 3: 0}  # R->U->L->D->R\n  TURN_RIGHT_MAP = {0: 3, 1: 0, 2: 1, 3: 2} # R->D->L->U->R\n\n  # Get indices of non-grabbable items that block movement\n  non_walkable_kinds_indices = current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # Nested helper function for clarity and encapsulation of walkability logic\n  def _is_cell_valid_and_walkable(r_coord, c_coord):\n    # Check grid boundaries\n    if not (0 <= r_coord < WIDTH and 0 <= c_coord < HEIGHT):\n      return False\n\n    # Check if cell contains any entity that blocks movement\n    for kind_idx in non_walkable_kinds_indices:\n      if initial_grid[r_coord, c_coord, kind_idx] > 0:\n        return False\n\n    # Agent cannot walk onto the primitive itself; it must be adjacent to use it.\n    if initial_grid[r_coord, c_coord, primitive_id] > 0:\n      return False\n    \n    return True\n\n  # BFS queue: stores ( (row, col), direction, list_of_actions_to_reach_here )\n  queue = collections.deque([((initial_pos, initial_dir), [])])\n  # Visited set: stores ( (row, col), direction ) to avoid redundant exploration\n  visited = {(initial_pos, initial_dir)}\n\n  target_actions_path = None # Stores the action list to reach the state where primitive is in front\n\n  while queue:\n      (current_pos, current_dir), path_so_far = queue.popleft()\n      r, c = current_pos\n\n      # Check if the primitive is in the cell directly in front of the agent\n      front_dr, front_dc = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n      front_r, front_c = r + front_dr, c + front_dc\n      \n      # If the cell in front is within grid bounds and contains the primitive,\n      # we have found a path to be adjacent and facing the target.\n      if (0 <= front_r < WIDTH and 0 <= front_c < HEIGHT):\n          if initial_grid[front_r, front_c, primitive_id] > 0:\n              target_actions_path = path_so_far\n              break # Shortest path found, exit BFS\n\n      # Explore possible next actions: Move Forward, Turn Left, Turn Right\n\n      # Option 1: Move Forward\n      next_r_move, next_c_move = r + DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir][0], c + DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir][1]\n      next_pos_move = (next_r_move, next_c_move)\n      next_dir_move = current_dir # Direction does not change on move\n\n      if _is_cell_valid_and_walkable(next_r_move, next_c_move):\n          if (next_pos_move, next_dir_move) not in visited:\n              visited.add((next_pos_move, next_dir_move))\n              queue.append(((next_pos_move, next_dir_move), path_so_far + [MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION]))\n\n      # Option 2: Turn Left\n      next_dir_left = TURN_LEFT_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Position does not change on turn\n      if (current_pos, next_dir_left) not in visited:\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_left))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_left), path_so_far + [TURN_LEFT_ACTION]))\n\n      # Option 3: Turn Right\n      next_dir_right = TURN_RIGHT_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Position does not change on turn\n      if (current_pos, next_dir_right) not in visited:\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_right))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_right), path_so_far + [TURN_RIGHT_ACTION]))\n\n  # If a path to the target (adjacent and facing) was found, append the USE action\n  if target_actions_path is not None:\n      actions_list.extend(target_actions_path)\n      actions_list.append(USE_ACTION)\n\n  return actions_list", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T06:43:31.222695", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions = []\n  \n  # 1. Get current state and primitive ID.\n  current_state = env._current_state \n  grid = current_state.grid\n  current_pos = current_state.pos\n  \n  # Robustly get the integer ID of the primitive from the cookbook index.\n  try:\n      primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n      # If the primitive name is unknown (not in the cookbook's index), it cannot be collected.\n      return []\n\n  # 2. Check if the primitive is grabbable.\n  # If the primitive is not in the set of grabbable indices, it cannot be picked up\n  # into the inventory, so an empty list of actions is returned.\n  if primitive_id not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Retrieve action mapping from the environment for robustness.\n  _action_specs = env.action_specs()\n  DOWN = _action_specs['DOWN']\n  UP = _action_specs['UP']\n  LEFT = _action_specs['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = _action_specs['RIGHT']\n  USE = _action_specs['USE']\n\n  # Define movement deltas for convenience for the 4 cardinal directions.\n  DELTAS = {\n      UP: (-1, 0),\n      DOWN: (1, 0),\n      LEFT: (0, -1),\n      RIGHT: (0, 1)\n  }\n\n  # 3. Optimization: Check if the agent is already next to the primitive.\n  # If `current_state.next_to(primitive_id)` is True, a single 'USE' action is sufficient\n  # to collect it, avoiding unnecessary pathfinding.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_id):\n      actions.append(USE)\n      return actions\n\n  # 4. Find all locations of the target primitive on the grid.\n  # We collect all (row, col) coordinates where the primitive is located.\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for r in range(WIDTH):\n      for c in range(HEIGHT):\n          # Check if the primitive_id occupies this cell (value is 1 in the one-hot encoding).\n          if grid[r, c, primitive_id] == 1:\n              primitive_locations.append((r, c))\n\n  # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the grid, it cannot be collected.\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      return []\n\n  # 5. Pre-compute all valid \"target use positions\".\n  # A \"target use position\" is a grid cell from which the agent can apply 'USE'\n  # to collect the desired primitive. This cell must satisfy two conditions:\n  #   a) It must be adjacent to at least one primitive location.\n  #   b) It must be traversable by the agent (i.e., not an obstacle).\n  target_use_positions = set()\n  for pr, pc in primitive_locations:\n      for dr, dc in DELTAS.values(): # Iterate through all 4 cardinal directions (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT)\n          adj_r, adj_c = pr + dr, pc + dc\n\n          # Ensure the adjacent cell is within grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= adj_r < WIDTH and 0 <= adj_c < HEIGHT):\n              continue\n\n          # Ensure the adjacent cell is traversable.\n          # A cell is considered non-traversable if it contains any item whose kind index\n          # is in the `env.world.non_grabbable_indices` set (e.g., BOUNDARY, WATER, WORKSHOPS).\n          is_traversable = True\n          for i_kind in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n              if grid[adj_r, adj_c, i_kind] == 1: # If this cell contains a non-grabbable item\n                  is_traversable = False\n                  break # This neighbor is an obstacle, so it's not traversable\n          \n          if is_traversable:\n              target_use_positions.add((adj_r, adj_c))\n    \n  # If there are no traversable spots from which to use the primitive, it's uncollectable.\n  if not target_use_positions:\n      return []\n\n  # 6. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path\n  #    from the agent's current position to any of the pre-computed `target_use_positions`.\n  # The BFS queue stores tuples: ((current_row, current_col), [list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here]).\n  q = collections.deque([(current_pos, [])]) \n  visited = {current_pos} # Set to keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles and redundant paths.\n\n  target_adj_pos_path = None # This variable will store the shortest path found to an adjacent cell.\n\n  while q:\n      (r, c), path = q.popleft()\n\n      # If the current BFS node (r, c) is one of our pre-computed target positions,\n      # we've found the shortest path to a valid 'use' location.\n      if (r, c) in target_use_positions:\n          target_adj_pos_path = path \n          break # Exit BFS, as the shortest path to an 'usable' position has been found.\n\n      # Explore valid neighboring cells from the current position (r, c).\n      for action_dir, (dr, dc) in DELTAS.items():\n          nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc # Calculate the coordinates of the potential new position.\n\n          # Check 1: Ensure the new position is within the grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= nr < WIDTH and 0 <= nc < HEIGHT):\n              continue\n          \n          # Check 2: Ensure the new position is traversable (not an obstacle).\n          is_traversable = True\n          for i_kind in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n              if grid[nr, nc, i_kind] == 1: # If this cell contains a non-grabbable item.\n                  is_traversable = False\n                  break # This neighbor is an obstacle, so it's not traversable.\n          \n          if not is_traversable:\n              continue # Skip this neighbor if it's an obstacle.\n          \n          # Check 3: If this neighbor has not been visited yet, add it to the queue.\n          if (nr, nc) not in visited:\n              visited.add((nr, nc))\n              # Extend the current path with the action taken to reach this new neighbor.\n              q.append(((nr, nc), path + [action_dir]))\n    \n  # 7. Construct the final sequence of actions.\n  # If a path to an adjacent traversable cell was found (`target_adj_pos_path` is not None),\n  # extend the actions list with this path and then append a 'USE' action to actually collect the primitive.\n  if target_adj_pos_path is not None:\n      actions.extend(target_adj_pos_path)\n      actions.append(USE) # Once adjacent, perform the 'USE' action to collect the primitive.\n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T06:43:32.334728", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions = []\n\n  # Robustness: Get primitive ID, handling potential KeyError if name is invalid.\n  try:\n      primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  except KeyError:\n      return []\n\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  current_pos = current_state.pos\n\n  # Essential check: If the primitive is not grabbable, it cannot be collected into inventory.\n  if primitive_id not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Retrieve action mapping from the environment for robustness\n  _action_specs = env.action_specs()\n  DOWN = _action_specs['DOWN']\n  UP = _action_specs['UP']\n  LEFT = _action_specs['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = _action_specs['RIGHT']\n  USE = _action_specs['USE']\n\n  # Define movement deltas for convenience for the 4 cardinal directions\n  DELTAS = {\n      UP: (-1, 0),\n      DOWN: (1, 0),\n      LEFT: (0, -1),\n      RIGHT: (0, 1)\n  }\n\n  # 1. Optimization: Check if the agent is already next to the primitive.\n  # If so, a single 'USE' action is sufficient.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_id):\n      actions.append(USE)\n      return actions\n\n  # 2. Find all locations of the target primitive on the grid.\n  # We collect all (row, col) coordinates where the primitive is located.\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for r in range(WIDTH):\n      for c in range(HEIGHT):\n          # Check if the primitive_id occupies this cell (value is 1)\n          if grid[r, c, primitive_id] == 1:\n              primitive_locations.append((r, c))\n\n  # Early exit: If the primitive is not found anywhere on the grid, it cannot be collected.\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      return []\n\n  # 3. Pre-compute all valid \"target use positions\".\n  # A \"target use position\" is a traversable grid cell from which the agent can apply 'USE'\n  # to collect the desired primitive. This cell must be adjacent to a primitive location.\n  target_use_positions = set()\n  for pr, pc in primitive_locations:\n      for dr, dc in DELTAS.values(): # Iterate through all 4 cardinal directions\n          adj_r, adj_c = pr + dr, pc + dc\n\n          # Ensure the adjacent cell is within grid boundaries\n          if not (0 <= adj_r < WIDTH and 0 <= adj_c < HEIGHT):\n              continue\n\n          # Ensure the adjacent cell is traversable (not an obstacle).\n          # An agent must be able to stand on this cell.\n          is_traversable = True\n          for i_kind in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n              if grid[adj_r, adj_c, i_kind] == 1: # If this cell contains a non-grabbable item\n                  is_traversable = False\n                  break # This neighbor is an obstacle\n          \n          if is_traversable:\n              target_use_positions.add((adj_r, adj_c))\n    \n  # If there are no traversable spots from which to use the primitive, it's uncollectable.\n  if not target_use_positions:\n      return []\n\n  # 4. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path\n  #    to any of the pre-computed `target_use_positions`.\n  # The queue stores tuples: ((current_row, current_col), [list_of_actions_to_reach_here])\n  q = collections.deque([(current_pos, [])]) \n  visited = {current_pos} # Set to keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles and redundant paths\n\n  target_path = None # This will store the shortest path found to a usable cell\n\n  while q:\n      (r, c), path = q.popleft()\n\n      # Check if the current BFS node (r, c) is one of our pre-computed target positions.\n      if (r, c) in target_use_positions:\n          target_path = path # Found the shortest path to this usable cell\n          break # Exit BFS, the shortest path to an 'usable' position is found\n\n      # Explore valid neighboring cells from the current position (r, c).\n      for action_dir, (dr, dc) in DELTAS.items():\n          nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc # Calculate the coordinates of the potential new position\n\n          # Check 1: Ensure the new position is within the grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= nr < WIDTH and 0 <= nc < HEIGHT):\n              continue\n          \n          # Check 2: Ensure the new position is traversable (not an obstacle).\n          is_traversable = True\n          for i_kind in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n              if grid[nr, nc, i_kind] == 1: # If this cell contains a non-grabbable item\n                  is_traversable = False\n                  break # This neighbor is an obstacle\n          \n          if not is_traversable:\n              continue # Skip this neighbor if it's an obstacle\n          \n          # Check 3: If this neighbor has not been visited yet, add it to the queue.\n          if (nr, nc) not in visited:\n              visited.add((nr, nc))\n              # Extend the current path with the action taken to reach this new neighbor.\n              q.append(((nr, nc), path + [action_dir]))\n    \n  # 5. Construct the final sequence of actions.\n  # If a path to an adjacent cell was found, extend the actions list with this path\n  # and then append a 'USE' action to actually collect the primitive.\n  if target_path is not None:\n      actions.extend(target_path)\n      actions.append(USE) # Once adjacent, perform the 'USE' action to collect the primitive.\n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
