{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T08:19:31.305586", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Returns a list of actions to find and collect the specified primitive in the environment.\n    \n  This version uses a Breadth-First Search (BFS) for pathfinding, optimized for\n  memory by reconstructing the path using parent pointers, and includes an initial\n  check for already collected items.\n\n  Args:\n      env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab object representing the current simulation state.\n      primitive (str): The string name of the primitive to collect (e.g., \"WOOD\", \"STONE\").\n\n  Returns:\n      List[int]: A sequence of action indices (e.g., UP, DOWN, USE) to execute.\n                 Returns an empty list if the primitive is already collected,\n                 not found on the grid, or unreachable.\n  \"\"\"\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  \n  # --- 1. Initialize Essential Data & Pre-Checks ---\n  # Get the integer ID for the target primitive from the cookbook's index.\n  # Using .index() will add it if it doesn't exist, but it's assumed to be a known primitive.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n  \n  # Optimization: If the primitive is already in inventory, no need to collect it.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # Map action names to their integer representations.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Grid dimensions and agent's current position.\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n  agent_start_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's current (x, y) position.\n\n  # --- 2. Immediate Collection Check (Adjacent) ---\n  # If the agent is already adjacent to the primitive (within its 3x3 neighborhood),\n  # the most efficient action is simply to 'USE' it.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n    return [ACTION_USE]\n\n  # --- 3. Locate All Primitive Instances on the Grid ---\n  # Find all (x, y) coordinates where the primitive currently exists.\n  primitive_locations_on_grid = [] \n  for x in range(grid_width):\n    for y in range(grid_height):\n      # If the primitive's layer at (x, y) has a value greater than 0, it exists there.\n      if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n        primitive_locations_on_grid.append((x, y))\n\n  # If no instances of the primitive are found on the map, it's unreachable.\n  if not primitive_locations_on_grid:\n    return []\n\n  # --- 4. Determine \"Goal Cells\" for BFS ---\n  # A \"goal cell\" is any grid location from which the agent can apply the 'USE' action\n  # to collect the target primitive. 'USE' affects a 3x3 area around the agent.\n  target_goal_cells = set()\n  for px, py in primitive_locations_on_grid:\n    # Iterate through the 3x3 neighborhood around each primitive instance.\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        gx, gy = px + dx, py + dy \n        # Ensure the potential goal cell (gx, gy) is within the grid boundaries.\n        if 0 <= gx < grid_width and 0 <= gy < grid_height:\n          target_goal_cells.add((gx, gy))\n\n  # --- 5. Identify Impassable Terrain Kinds ---\n  # These are entities the agent cannot move onto. Non-grabbable items that are\n  # NOT workshops typically block movement.\n  impassable_entity_indices = set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices) - set(env.world.workshop_indices)\n\n  # --- 6. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) ---\n  # BFS queue: Stores only grid positions to visit.\n  bfs_queue = collections.deque([agent_start_pos])\n  # Visited dictionary: Stores {current_pos: (parent_pos, action_to_reach_current_from_parent)}\n  # This allows reconstructing the path efficiently by backtracking from the found goal.\n  visited = {agent_start_pos: (None, None)} # (parent_position, action_to_get_here_from_parent)\n\n  # Define all possible movement directions (delta X, delta Y) and their corresponding action indices.\n  cardinal_moves = [\n      ((0, -1), ACTION_UP),    # Move North (decreases Y-coordinate)\n      ((0, 1), ACTION_DOWN),   # Move South (increases Y-coordinate)\n      ((-1, 0), ACTION_LEFT),  # Move West (decreases X-coordinate)\n      ((1, 0), ACTION_RIGHT),  # Move East (increases X-coordinate)\n  ]\n\n  found_goal_pos = None # To store the specific goal cell reached\n\n  while bfs_queue:\n    cx, cy = bfs_queue.popleft()\n    current_pos = (cx, cy)\n\n    # If the current position is one of our target goal cells, we've found the shortest path.\n    if current_pos in target_goal_cells:\n      found_goal_pos = current_pos\n      break # Exit BFS, as the shortest path to *any* goal cell is found.\n\n    # Explore all valid, unvisited, and traversable neighboring cells from the current position.\n    for (dx, dy), action_to_take in cardinal_moves:\n      next_x, next_y = cx + dx, cy + dy # Calculate the coordinates of the next potential position.\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # 1. Boundary Check: Ensure the new position is within the grid dimensions.\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue # Skip if the new position is out of bounds.\n\n      # 2. Impassability Check: Determine if the new position contains any impassable entity.\n      is_next_cell_impassable = False\n      for k_idx in impassable_entity_indices:\n          # If an impassable kind is present at (next_x, next_y) with a count > 0, the cell is blocked.\n          if grid[next_x, next_y, k_idx] > 0: \n              is_next_cell_impassable = True\n              break # No need to check other impassable kinds for this cell.\n      \n      if is_next_cell_impassable:\n          continue # Skip this move if the cell is impassable.\n\n      # 3. Visited Check: If the new position has not been visited yet during this BFS.\n      if next_pos not in visited:\n        visited[next_pos] = (current_pos, action_to_take) # Store parent and the action to reach next_pos\n        bfs_queue.append(next_pos)\n\n  # --- 7. Reconstruct Path if Goal Found ---\n  if found_goal_pos is None:\n    # If BFS completed (queue became empty) and no path to a goal cell was found,\n    # it means the primitive is currently unreachable from the agent's starting position.\n    return []\n\n  path_actions = []\n  current_path_reconstruction_pos = found_goal_pos\n  # Backtrack from the found goal position to the start position using the 'visited' dictionary.\n  while current_path_reconstruction_pos != agent_start_pos:\n    parent_pos, action_to_reach_current = visited[current_path_reconstruction_pos]\n    path_actions.append(action_to_reach_current)\n    current_path_reconstruction_pos = parent_pos\n  \n  # The path was built in reverse order (from goal to start), so reverse it.\n  path_actions.reverse() \n\n  # Append the 'USE' action at the end to actually collect the primitive.\n  return path_actions + [ACTION_USE]", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T08:19:32.532012", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  \n  # --- 1. Initialize Essential Data & Validate Primitive ---\n  # Get the integer ID for the target primitive from the cookbook's index.\n  # Using `cookbook.index[primitive]` (which calls `Index.__getitem__`)\n  # returns the integer ID if the primitive name exists, or `None` if it does not.\n  # This is preferred over `Index.index(primitive)` which would *add* the primitive\n  # to the index if it's new, which is not desired for collection logic.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  if primitive_idx is None:\n    # If the primitive is not recognized in the environment's cookbook, it's impossible to collect.\n    return []\n\n  # Map action names to their integer representations as defined by the environment's action_specs.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n  ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Get grid dimensions and the agent's current position for navigation logic.\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n  agent_start_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's current (x, y) position.\n\n  # --- 2. Early Exit: Primitive Already Collected or Adjacent ---\n  # If the agent's inventory already contains the primitive, there's no need to collect more.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # If the agent is already within collection range (adjacent) of the primitive,\n  # the most efficient action is simply to 'USE' it. No movement is required.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n    return [ACTION_USE]\n\n  # --- 3. Locate All Instances of the Primitive on the Grid ---\n  # Iterate through the grid to find all (x, y) coordinates where the primitive\n  # currently exists (i.e., its layer has a count greater than 0).\n  primitive_locations_on_grid = []\n  for x in range(grid_width):\n    for y in range(grid_height):\n      if grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0: \n        primitive_locations_on_grid.append((x, y))\n\n  # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the map, it's currently unreachable.\n  if not primitive_locations_on_grid:\n    return []\n\n  # --- 4. Define \"Goal Cells\" for Pathfinding ---\n  # A \"goal cell\" is any grid location from which the agent can apply the 'USE' action\n  # to collect the target primitive. The 'USE' action affects a 3x3 area around the agent.\n  target_goal_cells = set()\n  for px, py in primitive_locations_on_grid:\n    # Consider the 3x3 neighborhood around each primitive instance.\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        gx, gy = px + dx, py + dy \n        # Ensure the potential goal cell (gx, gy) is within the grid boundaries.\n        if 0 <= gx < grid_width and 0 <= gy < grid_height:\n          target_goal_cells.add((gx, gy))\n\n  # --- 5. Identify Impassable Terrain Kinds ---\n  # These are entities that the agent cannot move onto. In CraftWorld, non-grabbable items\n  # (like 'BOUNDARY', 'WATER', 'STONE') are generally impassable, with the exception\n  # of 'WORKSHOP' types which are often traversable interaction points.\n  impassable_entity_indices = set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices) - set(env.world.workshop_indices)\n\n  # --- 6. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) for the Shortest Path ---\n  # BFS queue: Stores tuples of (current_position (x, y), list_of_actions_to_reach_here).\n  bfs_queue = collections.deque([(agent_start_pos, [])]) \n  # Set to keep track of visited positions to prevent cycles and redundant exploration,\n  # guaranteeing the shortest path is found first.\n  visited_positions = {agent_start_pos} \n\n  # Define possible cardinal movements (delta_x, delta_y) and their corresponding action indices.\n  cardinal_moves = [\n      ((0, -1), ACTION_UP),    # Move North (decreases Y coordinate)\n      ((0, 1), ACTION_DOWN),   # Move South (increases Y coordinate)\n      ((-1, 0), ACTION_LEFT),  # Move West (decreases X coordinate)\n      ((1, 0), ACTION_RIGHT),  # Move East (increases X coordinate)\n  ]\n\n  while bfs_queue:\n    current_pos, path_so_far = bfs_queue.popleft() \n    cx, cy = current_pos\n\n    # If the current position is one of the target goal cells, we've found the shortest path.\n    if current_pos in target_goal_cells:\n      # Append the 'USE' action as the final step to actually collect the primitive.\n      return path_so_far + [ACTION_USE]\n\n    # Explore all valid, unvisited, and traversable neighboring cells from the current position.\n    for (dx, dy), action_to_take in cardinal_moves:\n      next_x, next_y = cx + dx, cy + dy # Calculate the coordinates of the next potential position.\n      next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n      # Check 1: Boundary Check - Ensure the new position is within the grid dimensions.\n      if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height):\n        continue # Skip if the new position is out of bounds.\n\n      # Check 2: Impassability Check - Determine if the new position contains any impassable entity.\n      # A cell is impassable if any of the `impassable_entity_indices` are present at that cell.\n      is_next_cell_impassable = False\n      for k_idx in impassable_entity_indices:\n          if grid[next_x, next_y, k_idx] > 0: # If this specific impassable kind is present.\n              is_next_cell_impassable = True\n              break # No need to check other impassable kinds for this cell.\n      \n      if is_next_cell_impassable:\n          continue # Skip this move if the cell is blocked.\n\n      # Check 3: Visited Check - If the new position has not been visited yet during this BFS.\n      if next_pos not in visited_positions:\n        visited_positions.add(next_pos) # Mark the new position as visited.\n        # Enqueue the new position along with the updated path of actions.\n        bfs_queue.append((next_pos, path_so_far + [action_to_take]))\n\n  # If the BFS queue becomes empty and no path to any goal cell was found,\n  # it means the primitive is currently unreachable from the agent's starting position.\n  return []", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T08:20:16.852171", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  \n  # 1. Get the integer index for the primitive from the world's cookbook.\n  # Using env.world.cookbook.index[primitive] directly handles cases where the\n  # primitive name might not exist by returning None, making the function robust.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  if primitive_idx is None:\n    # If the primitive name is not found in the cookbook's index, it's an invalid target.\n    # Return an empty list, as no actions can be taken.\n    return []\n  \n  # 2. Optimization: If the agent already possesses at least one of the primitive\n  # in its inventory, no further collection actions are necessary.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return [] # Already have it, return an empty action list.\n\n  # 3. Retrieve action mappings from the environment's action_specs.\n  # This ensures correct action indices are used for movement and interaction,\n  # improving readability and maintainability.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # 4. Immediate collection check:\n  # Determine if the agent is currently positioned within the 3x3 neighborhood\n  # (Moore neighborhood) of the primitive. If so, a single 'USE' action is sufficient.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n    # The agent is in a valid position to interact with and collect the primitive.\n    return [USE]\n\n  # 5. Identify all grid locations where instances of the primitive exist.\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n  \n  primitive_locations = []\n  # Utilize numpy.where for an efficient, vectorized search of all cells in the grid\n  # where the count of the primitive (at primitive_idx layer) is greater than zero.\n  primitive_x_coords, primitive_y_coords = np.where(grid[:, :, primitive_idx] > 0)\n  for x, y in zip(primitive_x_coords, primitive_y_coords):\n      primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  # If no instances of the primitive are found anywhere on the grid, it cannot be collected.\n  if not primitive_locations:\n    return []\n\n  # 6. Define \"goal cells\" for the Breadth-First Search (BFS).\n  # A goal cell is any cell from which the agent can successfully collect the primitive.\n  # Since CraftState.next_to checks the 3x3 neighborhood, any cell within this vicinity\n  # of a primitive location is a valid target to move to before using 'USE'.\n  goal_cells = set()\n  for px, py in primitive_locations:\n    # Iterate through all 3x3 relative offsets (dx, dy), including (0,0) for the primitive's own cell.\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        gx, gy = px + dx, py + dy\n        # Ensure the calculated potential goal cell (gx, gy) is within the grid boundaries.\n        if 0 <= gx < grid_width and 0 <= gy < grid_height:\n          goal_cells.add((gx, gy))\n\n  # 7. Determine which entity kinds make a cell impassable for agent movement.\n  # Impassable kinds are typically non-grabbable items (e.g., water, boundary) that the agent\n  # cannot walk over. Workshop locations, though non-grabbable, are usually traversable,\n  # so they are explicitly excluded from the impassable list.\n  # Convert the resulting set difference to a list for efficient NumPy indexing.\n  impassable_kinds_indices = list(set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices) - set(env.world.workshop_indices))\n\n  # 8. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest sequence of movement actions\n  # from the agent's current position to any of the identified goal cells.\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  \n  # The queue for BFS stores tuples of (current_position, path_taken_actions_to_reach_here).\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) \n  # A set to keep track of visited positions to prevent revisiting cells and ensure the\n  # shortest path is found by exploring layer by layer.\n  visited = {start_pos} \n\n  # Define possible cardinal moves (delta_x, delta_y) and their corresponding action indices.\n  MOVE_DELTAS_AND_ACTIONS = [\n      ((0, -1), UP),    # Move North (decreases Y coordinate)\n      ((0, 1), DOWN),   # Move South (increases Y coordinate)\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT),  # Move West (decreases X coordinate)\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT),  # Move East (increases X coordinate)\n  ]\n\n  while q:\n    (cx, cy), path_so_far = q.popleft() # Dequeue the current position and the path leading to it.\n\n    # If the current position is one of our designated goal cells, the shortest path has been found.\n    if (cx, cy) in goal_cells:\n      # Append the 'USE' action to the path, as the agent is now in position to collect.\n      return path_so_far + [USE]\n\n    # Explore all valid neighboring cells reachable by cardinal movement.\n    for (dx, dy), action in MOVE_DELTAS_AND_ACTIONS:\n      nx, ny = cx + dx, cy + dy # Calculate the new potential position.\n      new_pos = (nx, ny)\n\n      # Check if the new position is within the overall grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height):\n        continue # Skip if out of bounds.\n\n      # Check if the new position is traversable (i.e., it does not contain any impassable kind).\n      # Using NumPy's `any` for efficient checking if any impassable item exists at (nx, ny).\n      is_impassable_cell = False\n      if impassable_kinds_indices: # Only perform the check if there are actual impassable kinds defined.\n          if np.any(grid[nx, ny, impassable_kinds_indices] > 0):\n              is_impassable_cell = True\n      \n      if is_impassable_cell:\n          continue # Skip this cell if it's impassable.\n\n      # If the new position is valid and has not been visited yet, add it to the queue for exploration.\n      if new_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(new_pos)\n        q.append((new_pos, path_so_far + [action]))\n\n  # 9. If the BFS completes and the queue becomes empty without finding a path to any goal cell,\n  # it implies that the primitive is unreachable from the agent's current position.\n  return []", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T08:20:18.014092", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1` using numpy and robust indexing.\"\"\"\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  \n  # 1. Get the integer index for the desired primitive.\n  # Using __getitem__ (env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]) which returns None if the\n  # primitive name is not found. This makes the function robust against unknown primitive names.\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  if primitive_idx is None:\n    # If the primitive name is not found in the cookbook's index, it's an invalid target.\n    # Return an empty list as no actions can be taken.\n    return []\n\n  # 2. Early exit: If the agent already has at least one of the primitive in its inventory,\n  # no further collection actions are needed.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    return [] # Already have it, return an empty action list.\n\n  # 3. Retrieve action mappings from the environment's action_specs for clarity and to ensure\n  # correct action indices are used for movement and interaction.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE = action_map['USE']\n\n  # 4. Immediate collection check:\n  # Determine if the agent is currently positioned within the 3x3 neighborhood (Moore neighborhood)\n  # of the primitive. This neighborhood includes the agent's current cell itself.\n  # If so, a single 'USE' action is sufficient to collect it.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_idx):\n    # The agent is in a valid position to interact with and collect the primitive.\n    return [USE]\n\n  # 5. Identify all grid locations where instances of the primitive exist.\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n  \n  primitive_locations = []\n  # Utilize numpy.where for an efficient vectorized search of all cells in the grid\n  # where the count of the primitive is greater than zero.\n  primitive_x_coords, primitive_y_coords = np.where(grid[:, :, primitive_idx] > 0)\n  for x, y in zip(primitive_x_coords, primitive_y_coords):\n      primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  # If no instances of the primitive are found anywhere on the grid, it cannot be collected.\n  if not primitive_locations:\n    return []\n\n  # 6. Define \"goal cells\" for the Breadth-First Search (BFS).\n  # A goal cell is any cell from which the agent can successfully collect the primitive.\n  # Since CraftState.next_to checks the 3\u00d73 neighborhood, any cell in this vicinity\n  # of a primitive location is a valid goal to move to before using 'USE'.\n  goal_cells = set()\n  for px, py in primitive_locations:\n    # Iterate through all 3x3 relative offsets (dx, dy) including (0,0) for the primitive's own cell.\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        gx, gy = px + dx, py + dy\n        # Ensure the calculated potential goal cell (gx, gy) is within the grid boundaries.\n        if 0 <= gx < grid_width and 0 <= gy < grid_height:\n          goal_cells.add((gx, gy))\n\n  # 7. Determine which entity kinds make a cell impassable for agent movement.\n  # Impassable kinds are typically non-grabbable items (e.g., water, boundary) that the agent\n  # cannot walk over. Workshop locations, though non-grabbable, are usually traversable,\n  # so they are explicitly excluded from the impassable list.\n  # Convert the resulting set difference to a list for efficient NumPy indexing.\n  impassable_kind_indices = list(set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices) - set(env.world.workshop_indices))\n\n  # 8. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest sequence of movement actions\n  # from the agent's current position to any of the identified goal cells.\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  \n  # The queue for BFS stores tuples of (current_position, path_taken_actions_to_reach_here).\n  q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) \n  # A set to keep track of visited positions to prevent revisiting cells and ensure the\n  # shortest path is found by exploring layer by layer.\n  visited = {start_pos} \n\n  # Define possible cardinal moves (delta_x, delta_y) and their corresponding action indices.\n  DELTAS_ACTIONS = [\n      ((0, -1), UP),    # Move North (decreases Y coordinate)\n      ((0, 1), DOWN),   # Move South (increases Y coordinate)\n      ((-1, 0), LEFT),  # Move West (decreases X coordinate)\n      ((1, 0), RIGHT),  # Move East (increases X coordinate)\n  ]\n\n  while q:\n    (cx, cy), path_so_far = q.popleft() # Dequeue the current position and the path leading to it.\n\n    # If the current position is one of our designated goal cells, the shortest path has been found.\n    if (cx, cy) in goal_cells:\n      # Append the 'USE' action to the path, as the agent is now in position to collect.\n      return path_so_far + [USE]\n\n    # Explore all valid neighboring cells reachable by cardinal movement.\n    for (dx, dy), action in DELTAS_ACTIONS:\n      nx, ny = cx + dx, cy + dy # Calculate the new potential position.\n\n      # Check if the new position is within the overall grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height):\n        continue # Skip if out of bounds.\n\n      # Check if the new position is traversable (i.e., it does not contain any impassable kind).\n      # Using NumPy's `any` for efficient checking if any impassable item exists at (nx, ny).\n      is_impassable_cell = False\n      if impassable_kind_indices: # Only perform the check if there are actual impassable kinds defined.\n          is_impassable_cell = np.any(grid[nx, ny, impassable_kind_indices] > 0)\n      \n      if is_impassable_cell:\n          continue # Skip this cell if it's impassable.\n\n      # If the new position is valid and has not been visited yet, add it to the queue for exploration.\n      new_pos = (nx, ny)\n      if new_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(new_pos)\n        q.append((new_pos, path_so_far + [action]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and the queue becomes empty without finding a path to any goal cell,\n  # it implies that the primitive is unreachable from the agent's current position.\n  return []", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T08:21:42.016629", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T08:21:43.136205", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1`. Finds the shortest sequence of actions to\n  navigate to a specified primitive and collect it using the 'USE' action.\n  \n  This function implements a Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the optimal\n  sequence of movements and turns that places the agent directly in front of\n  the target primitive, followed by a 'USE' action to collect it.\n  \n  The improvement over `collect_v1` lies in pre-computing a boolean map of\n  blocked cells, making the walkability check more efficient during the BFS.\n  \n  Args:\n      env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab object representing the current simulation state.\n      primitive (str): The string name of the primitive item to be collected (e.g., \"WOOD\", \"STONE\", \"GRASS\").\n\n  Returns:\n      List[int]: A list of integer action codes (e.g., UP, LEFT, USE) that, when executed,\n                 will lead to the collection of the primitive. Returns an empty list\n                 if the primitive is unreachable from the current state.\n  \"\"\"\n  # --- 1. Initial State and Environment Setup ---\n  actions_list = []\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  initial_grid = current_state.grid\n  initial_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's starting position (row, col)\n  initial_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's initial facing direction (0:RIGHT, 1:UP, 2:LEFT, 3:DOWN)\n\n  # Resolve the string name of the primitive to its integer ID using the cookbook's index.\n  primitive_id = current_state.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  # Get grid dimensions: num_rows corresponds to grid.shape[0], num_cols to grid.shape[1].\n  num_rows, num_cols, _ = initial_grid.shape\n\n  # Retrieve numerical action codes from the environment's action_specs.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION = action_map['UP'] # 'UP' in action_specs maps to agent moving forward\n  TURN_LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  TURN_RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Define constants for agent directions (standardized for clarity)\n  DIR_RIGHT = 0\n  DIR_UP = 1\n  DIR_LEFT = 2\n  DIR_DOWN = 3\n\n  # Define how movement changes row/column based on the agent's current direction.\n  DIR_TO_DELTA = {\n      DIR_RIGHT: (0, 1),   # Facing RIGHT: moves to (row, col+1)\n      DIR_UP: (-1, 0),     # Facing UP: moves to (row-1, col)\n      DIR_LEFT: (0, -1),   # Facing LEFT: moves to (row, col-1)\n      DIR_DOWN: (1, 0)     # Facing DOWN: moves to (row+1, col)\n  }\n\n  # Define how turns update the agent's direction (clockwise order for turns).\n  TURN_LEFT_MAP = {\n      DIR_RIGHT: DIR_UP,\n      DIR_UP: DIR_LEFT,\n      DIR_LEFT: DIR_DOWN,\n      DIR_DOWN: DIR_RIGHT\n  }\n  TURN_RIGHT_MAP = {\n      DIR_RIGHT: DIR_DOWN,\n      DIR_UP: DIR_RIGHT,\n      DIR_LEFT: DIR_UP,\n      DIR_DOWN: DIR_LEFT\n  }\n\n  # --- 2. Pre-computation of Blocked Cells Map ---\n  # A cell is considered \"blocked\" if the agent cannot move into it. This includes:\n  # 1. The cell containing the target primitive itself (agent must be adjacent).\n  # 2. Cells containing any non-grabbable environment entities (e.g., boundaries, water, some workshops).\n  blocked_cells = np.zeros((num_rows, num_cols), dtype=bool)\n\n  # Mark cells containing the target primitive as blocked for agent movement.\n  blocked_cells |= (initial_grid[:, :, primitive_id] > 0)\n\n  # Mark cells containing any non-grabbable (non-walkable) entities as blocked.\n  non_grabbable_indices_list = list(current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices)\n  if non_grabbable_indices_list:\n      # Use numpy's advanced indexing to select slices for all non-grabbable kinds,\n      # then `np.any` to check if any of these kinds are present in a cell.\n      blocked_cells |= np.any(initial_grid[:, :, non_grabbable_indices_list] > 0, axis=2)\n\n  # --- 3. Helper Function for Walkability Check (uses pre-computed map) ---\n  def _is_walkable_for_agent(r: int, c: int) -> bool:\n      \"\"\"Checks if a given grid cell (r, c) is walkable for the agent.\n      This version uses the pre-computed `blocked_cells` map for efficiency.\n      \"\"\"\n      # Check if coordinates are within the grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= r < num_rows and 0 <= c < num_cols):\n          return False\n      \n      # Direct lookup in the pre-computed blocked_cells map.\n      return not blocked_cells[r, c]\n\n  # --- 4. Breadth-First Search (BFS) Implementation ---\n  # The queue stores tuples: ((agent_position_tuple, agent_direction_int), list_of_actions_taken_so_far).\n  queue = collections.deque([((initial_pos, initial_dir), [])])\n  # The visited set stores (agent_position_tuple, agent_direction_int) tuples to prevent\n  # re-exploring states already visited, ensuring the shortest path is found.\n  visited = {(initial_pos, initial_dir)}\n\n  target_path = None # This will store the optimal action sequence to reach the pre-collection state.\n\n  while queue:\n      (current_pos, current_dir), path_actions = queue.popleft()\n      r, c = current_pos\n\n      # 4.1. Goal Check: Determine if the primitive is directly in front of the agent.\n      # This is the target condition: being adjacent to and facing the primitive, ready to 'USE'.\n      front_dr, front_dc = DIR_TO_DELTA[current_dir]\n      front_r, front_c = r + front_dr, c + front_dc\n      \n      # Ensure the cell in front is within grid boundaries before checking its contents.\n      if (0 <= front_r < num_rows and 0 <= front_c < num_cols):\n          # If the primitive is present in the cell directly in front, we have found our target state.\n          # Note: We specifically check for the primitive's presence here. The `blocked_cells` map\n          # marks this cell as non-walkable for agent *movement*, but it's the target for *interaction*.\n          if initial_grid[front_r, front_c, primitive_id] > 0:\n              target_path = path_actions\n              break # Shortest path found, exit the BFS loop.\n\n      # 4.2. Explore possible next actions: Move Forward, Turn Left, Turn Right.\n\n      # Try Moving Forward (Action: MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION)\n      move_dr, move_dc = DIR_TO_DELTA[current_dir]\n      next_r, next_c = r + move_dr, c + move_dc\n      next_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n      next_dir = current_dir # Direction remains unchanged when moving forward.\n\n      # If the next cell is walkable (using the pre-computed map) and this specific\n      # (position, direction) state has not been visited, add it to the queue.\n      if _is_walkable_for_agent(next_r, next_c) and (next_pos, next_dir) not in visited:\n          visited.add((next_pos, next_dir))\n          queue.append(((next_pos, next_dir), path_actions + [MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION]))\n\n      # Try Turning Left (Action: TURN_LEFT_ACTION)\n      next_dir_left = TURN_LEFT_MAP[current_dir]\n      next_pos_left = current_pos # Position does not change when turning.\n\n      # If this (position, new_direction) state has not been visited, add it to the queue.\n      if (next_pos_left, next_dir_left) not in visited:\n          visited.add((next_pos_left, next_dir_left))\n          queue.append(((next_pos_left, next_dir_left), path_actions + [TURN_LEFT_ACTION]))\n\n      # Try Turning Right (Action: TURN_RIGHT_ACTION)\n      next_dir_right = TURN_RIGHT_MAP[current_dir]\n      next_pos_right = current_pos # Position does not change when turning.\n\n      # If this (position, new_direction) state has not been visited, add it to the queue.\n      if (next_pos_right, next_dir_right) not in visited:\n          visited.add((next_pos_right, next_dir_right))\n          queue.append(((next_pos_right, next_dir_right), path_actions + [TURN_RIGHT_ACTION]))\n\n  # --- 5. Final Action Sequence Construction ---\n  # If a path to the target pre-collection state was found (i.e., target_path is not None),\n  # append the final 'USE' action to complete the collection process.\n  if target_path is not None:\n      actions_list.extend(target_path)\n      actions_list.append(USE_ACTION) # Add the crucial 'USE' action to collect the primitive.\n\n  return actions_list", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T08:22:55.230775", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1`.\n    \n    This version includes an explicit check for grabbable primitives and\n    maintains clear helper functions for readability and correctness.\n    It performs a Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest sequence\n    of movement and turn actions to position the agent adjacent to the\n    specified primitive, followed by a 'USE' action to collect it.\n\n    Args:\n        env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab object containing the current state.\n        primitive (str): The name of the primitive item to collect.\n\n    Returns:\n        List[int]: A sequence of action indices to execute (e.g., [UP, LEFT, USE]).\n                   Returns an empty list if the primitive is not grabbable,\n                   not found, or no path exists.\n  \"\"\"\n  actions_list = []\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  initial_grid = current_state.grid # Static grid state for pathfinding\n  initial_pos = current_state.pos    # Agent's starting (row, col)\n  initial_dir = current_state.dir    # Agent's starting direction (0:R, 1:U, 2:L, 3:D)\n\n  # Get the integer ID for the target primitive.\n  primitive_id = current_state.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  # Early exit: If primitive ID is invalid (e.g., name not found in cookbook)\n  # or if the primitive is not a grabbable item (e.g., water, workshop, or boundary),\n  # then it cannot be collected using the 'USE' action.\n  if primitive_id is None or primitive_id not in current_state.world.grabbable_indices: \n      return []\n\n  # Get grid dimensions: initial_grid.shape is (rows, columns, kinds).\n  # Assuming standard (row, col) indexing for position, so shape[0] is number of rows\n  # and shape[1] is number of columns.\n  NUM_ROWS, NUM_COLS, _ = initial_grid.shape \n\n  # Map string action names to their corresponding integer IDs using the environment's specs.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION = action_map['UP']\n  TURN_LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  TURN_RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Direction vectors: (delta_row, delta_col) for each agent direction.\n  # These define how the agent's (row, col) position changes when moving \"forward\"\n  # based on its current direction.\n  # 0:RIGHT (+col), 1:UP (-row), 2:LEFT (-col), 3:DOWN (+row)\n  DIR_TO_DRDC = {\n      0: (0, 1),   # Facing RIGHT: (row, col+1)\n      1: (-1, 0),  # Facing UP: (row-1, col)\n      2: (0, -1),  # Facing LEFT: (row, col-1)\n      3: (1, 0)    # Facing DOWN: (row+1, col)\n  }\n\n  # Maps for calculating the agent's new direction after turning left or right.\n  # Turns cycle through directions (0, 1, 2, 3).\n  TURN_LEFT_MAP = {0: 1, 1: 2, 2: 3, 3: 0}   # e.g., RIGHT (0) -> UP (1)\n  TURN_RIGHT_MAP = {0: 3, 1: 0, 2: 1, 3: 2} # e.g., RIGHT (0) -> DOWN (3)\n\n  # Get the set of entity indices that the agent cannot walk through.\n  non_walkable_entities = current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  def _is_target_state(pos, current_dir):\n      \"\"\"Checks if the target primitive is located in the cell directly in front\n      of the agent's current position and facing direction. This is the state\n      immediately before the 'USE' action.\n      \"\"\"\n      r, c = pos\n      front_dr, front_dc = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n      front_r, front_c = r + front_dr, c + front_dc\n\n      # Ensure the 'front' cell is within grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= front_r < NUM_ROWS and 0 <= front_c < NUM_COLS):\n          return False\n      \n      # Return True if the primitive is present in the cell directly in front.\n      return initial_grid[front_r, front_c, primitive_id] > 0\n\n  def _is_walkable_cell(pos):\n      \"\"\"Checks if the given cell (row, col) is traversable by the agent.\n      A cell is not walkable if it's:\n      1. Out of grid boundaries.\n      2. Contains any non-walkable entity (e.g., water, walls, workshops).\n      3. Contains the primitive itself (the agent must stop adjacent to,\n         not on top of, the item to 'USE' it).\n      \"\"\"\n      r, c = pos\n      if not (0 <= r < NUM_ROWS and 0 <= c < NUM_COLS):\n          return False # Cell is out of bounds\n      \n      # Check if the cell contains any non-walkable entities.\n      for kind_idx in non_walkable_entities:\n          if initial_grid[r, c, kind_idx] > 0:\n              return False # Cell contains a non-walkable item\n      \n      # Crucially, prevent walking directly onto the primitive itself.\n      if initial_grid[r, c, primitive_id] > 0:\n          return False \n          \n      return True\n  \n  # BFS setup:\n  # The queue stores tuples: ((agent_position_tuple, agent_direction_int), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_this_state).\n  queue = collections.deque([((initial_pos, initial_dir), [])])\n  \n  # The visited set stores (agent_position_tuple, agent_direction_int) pairs\n  # to prevent revisiting states and finding suboptimal paths (guaranteed shortest by BFS).\n  visited = {(initial_pos, initial_dir)}\n\n  target_path = None # This variable will store the action sequence to reach the pre-collection state.\n\n  # Optimization: Check if the agent is already in a state where it can immediately collect the item.\n  if _is_target_state(initial_pos, initial_dir):\n      target_path = [] # No preceding movement actions needed; just the 'USE' action.\n\n  # If not immediately at the target, perform a Breadth-First Search to find the shortest path.\n  if target_path is None:\n      while queue:\n          (current_pos, current_dir), path_actions = queue.popleft()\n          \n          # Explore all possible valid actions from the current state:\n\n          # 1. Try Moving Forward (UP action in CraftLab)\n          move_dr, move_dc = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n          next_r_fwd, next_c_fwd = current_pos[0] + move_dr, current_pos[1] + move_dc\n          next_pos_fwd = (next_r_fwd, next_c_fwd)\n          next_dir_fwd = current_dir # Direction does not change when moving forward.\n\n          # Check if the potential next cell is walkable and the resulting state hasn't been visited.\n          if _is_walkable_cell(next_pos_fwd):\n              new_state_fwd = (next_pos_fwd, next_dir_fwd)\n              if new_state_fwd not in visited:\n                  visited.add(new_state_fwd)\n                  new_path_fwd = path_actions + [MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION]\n                  \n                  # If this new state allows immediate collection, we've found the shortest path.\n                  if _is_target_state(next_pos_fwd, next_dir_fwd):\n                      target_path = new_path_fwd\n                      break # Exit BFS, as shortest path is found.\n                  \n                  queue.append((new_state_fwd, new_path_fwd))\n\n          # 2. Try Turning Left\n          next_dir_left = TURN_LEFT_MAP[current_dir]\n          new_state_left = (current_pos, next_dir_left) # Position remains the same.\n\n          # Check if the resulting state (new direction, same position) hasn't been visited.\n          if new_state_left not in visited:\n              visited.add(new_state_left)\n              new_path_left = path_actions + [TURN_LEFT_ACTION]\n              \n              # If turning left results in a state ready for collection, it's a shortest path.\n              if _is_target_state(current_pos, next_dir_left):\n                  target_path = new_path_left\n                  break # Exit BFS.\n              \n              queue.append((new_state_left, new_path_left))\n\n          # 3. Try Turning Right\n          next_dir_right = TURN_RIGHT_MAP[current_dir]\n          new_state_right = (current_pos, next_dir_right) # Position remains the same.\n\n          # Check if the resulting state (new direction, same position) hasn't been visited.\n          if new_state_right not in visited:\n              visited.add(new_state_right)\n              new_path_right = path_actions + [TURN_RIGHT_ACTION]\n              \n              # If turning right results in a state ready for collection, it's a shortest path.\n              if _is_target_state(current_pos, next_dir_right):\n                  target_path = new_path_right\n                  break # Exit BFS.\n              \n              queue.append((new_state_right, new_path_right))\n\n  # After the BFS completes:\n  # If a valid path to the pre-collection state was found, append the 'USE' action\n  # to the sequence of movement/turn actions.\n  if target_path is not None:\n      actions_list.extend(target_path)\n      actions_list.append(USE_ACTION)\n\n  return actions_list", "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T08:22:56.566456", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Improved version of `collect_v1`.\n    This version reintroduces the crucial check for grabbable primitives and\n    ensures proper early exit for non-collectable items, preventing attempts to\n    'collect' environmental features or workshops.\n    \n    Args:\n        env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab object.\n        primitive (str): The name of the primitive to collect.\n\n    Returns:\n        List[int]: A sequence of action indices to execute.\n  \"\"\"\n  actions_list = []\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  initial_grid = current_state.grid\n  initial_pos = current_state.pos\n  initial_dir = current_state.dir\n\n  primitive_id = current_state.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  # IMPORTANT IMPROVEMENT (from collect_v0):\n  # If the primitive name is not valid (not in the index) OR\n  # if it's not a grabbable item (e.g., a workshop, boundary, or water which are\n  # part of the 'primitive' DSL token but are non-collectable),\n  # we cannot 'collect' it using the 'USE' action. Return an empty list.\n  if primitive_id is None or primitive_id not in current_state.world.grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  # Retrieve grid dimensions\n  GRID_ROWS, GRID_COLS, _ = initial_grid.shape\n\n  # Map string action names to their corresponding integer IDs.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION = action_map['UP']    # 'UP' typically moves the agent forward.\n  TURN_LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  TURN_RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']            # Action to collect the item in front.\n\n  # Define changes in (row, col) for each direction when moving forward.\n  # (dir: (delta_row, delta_col))\n  DIRECTION_VECTORS = {\n      0: (0, 1),   # Facing RIGHT: (row, col+1)\n      1: (-1, 0),  # Facing UP: (row-1, col)\n      2: (0, -1),  # Facing LEFT: (row, col-1)\n      3: (1, 0)    # Facing DOWN: (row+1, col)\n  }\n\n  # Define how the agent's direction changes when turning left or right.\n  # (current_dir: new_dir_after_turn)\n  TURN_LEFT_MAP = {0: 1, 1: 2, 2: 3, 3: 0}\n  TURN_RIGHT_MAP = {0: 3, 1: 0, 2: 1, 3: 2}\n\n  # Get the set of entity indices that the agent cannot walk through.\n  non_walkable_kinds_indices = current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  def _is_target_state(pos, current_dir):\n      \"\"\"Checks if the given position and direction combination places the\n      primitive directly in front of the agent.\n      \"\"\"\n      r, c = pos\n      front_dr, front_dc = DIRECTION_VECTORS[current_dir]\n      front_r, front_c = r + front_dr, c + front_dc\n      \n      # Ensure the 'front' cell is within grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= front_r < GRID_ROWS and 0 <= front_c < GRID_COLS):\n          return False\n      \n      # Check if the target primitive is found in the cell directly in front.\n      return initial_grid[front_r, front_c, primitive_id] > 0\n\n  def _is_walkable_cell(pos):\n      \"\"\"Checks if the given cell is walkable by the agent.\"\"\"\n      r, c = pos\n      # Ensure the cell itself is within grid boundaries.\n      if not (0 <= r < GRID_ROWS and 0 <= c < GRID_COLS):\n          return False\n      \n      # A cell is not walkable if it contains any non-walkable entity.\n      for kind_idx in non_walkable_kinds_indices:\n          if initial_grid[r, c, kind_idx] > 0:\n              return False\n      \n      # Crucially, prevent walking directly *onto* the primitive itself.\n      # The 'USE' action requires the agent to be adjacent, not on top of, the item.\n      if initial_grid[r, c, primitive_id] > 0:\n          return False\n          \n      return True\n  \n  # BFS setup:\n  # Queue stores tuples: ( (agent_position_tuple, agent_direction_int), list_of_actions_to_reach_this_state )\n  queue = collections.deque([((initial_pos, initial_dir), [])])\n  \n  # Visited set stores (agent_position_tuple, agent_direction_int) to avoid cycles and redundant exploration.\n  visited = {(initial_pos, initial_dir)}\n\n  target_path = None # This variable will store the final sequence of actions if a path is found.\n\n  # 1. Immediate Goal Check:\n  # Check if the agent is already in a position to collect the primitive.\n  if _is_target_state(initial_pos, initial_dir):\n      target_path = [] # No preceding movement actions needed.\n\n  # 2. If not immediately at target, perform BFS to find the shortest path.\n  if target_path is None:\n      while queue:\n          (current_pos, current_dir), path_actions = queue.popleft()\n          \n          # Explore possible next actions from the current state:\n          \n          # --- Action: Move Forward (MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION) ---\n          move_dr, move_dc = DIRECTION_VECTORS[current_dir]\n          next_r_fwd, next_c_fwd = current_pos[0] + move_dr, current_pos[1] + move_dc\n          next_pos_fwd = (next_r_fwd, next_c_fwd)\n          next_dir_fwd = current_dir # Direction remains unchanged.\n\n          # Check if the potential next position is walkable and the new state hasn't been visited.\n          if _is_walkable_cell(next_pos_fwd):\n              new_state_fwd = (next_pos_fwd, next_dir_fwd)\n              if new_state_fwd not in visited:\n                  visited.add(new_state_fwd)\n                  new_path_fwd = path_actions + [MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION]\n                  # After moving to next_pos_fwd, check if this new state is a target state.\n                  if _is_target_state(next_pos_fwd, next_dir_fwd):\n                      target_path = new_path_fwd\n                      break # Shortest path found, exit BFS.\n                  queue.append((new_state_fwd, new_path_fwd))\n\n          # --- Action: Turn Left (TURN_LEFT_ACTION) ---\n          next_dir_left = TURN_LEFT_MAP[current_dir]\n          new_state_left = (current_pos, next_dir_left) # Position remains unchanged.\n          # Check if the new state (same position, new direction) has not been visited.\n          if new_state_left not in visited:\n              visited.add(new_state_left)\n              new_path_left = path_actions + [TURN_LEFT_ACTION]\n              # After turning, check if this new state is a target state.\n              if _is_target_state(current_pos, next_dir_left):\n                  target_path = new_path_left\n                  break # Shortest path found, exit BFS.\n              queue.append((new_state_left, new_path_left))\n\n          # --- Action: Turn Right (TURN_RIGHT_ACTION) ---\n          next_dir_right = TURN_RIGHT_MAP[current_dir]\n          new_state_right = (current_pos, next_dir_right) # Position remains unchanged.\n          # Check if the new state (same position, new direction) has not been visited.\n          if new_state_right not in visited:\n              visited.add(new_state_right)\n              new_path_right = path_actions + [TURN_RIGHT_ACTION]\n              # After turning, check if this new state is a target state.\n              if _is_target_state(current_pos, next_dir_right):\n                  target_path = new_path_right\n                  break # Shortest path found, exit BFS.\n              queue.append((new_state_right, new_path_right))\n\n  # After BFS completes (either found path or exhausted all states):\n  # If a valid path to a collection point was found, append the 'USE' action.\n  if target_path is not None:\n      actions_list.extend(target_path)\n      actions_list.append(USE_ACTION)\n\n  return actions_list", "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T08:23:48.353606", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions_list = []\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  \n  primitive_id = current_state.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Improvement: If the primitive is already in inventory, no actions are needed.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_id] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  initial_grid = current_state.grid\n  initial_pos = current_state.pos # tuple (r, c)\n  initial_dir = current_state.dir # int (0-3), 0:RIGHT, 1:UP, 2:LEFT, 3:DOWN\n\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = initial_grid.shape\n\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION = action_map['UP']\n  TURN_LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  TURN_RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # Direction mapping: (dr, dc) for agent's facing direction (0:R, 1:U, 2:L, 3:D)\n  DIR_TO_DRDC = {\n      0: (0, 1),   # Facing RIGHT, move in positive column direction (positive X)\n      1: (-1, 0),  # Facing UP, move in negative row direction (negative Y)\n      2: (0, -1),  # Facing LEFT, move in negative column direction (negative X)\n      3: (1, 0)    # Facing DOWN, move in positive row direction (positive Y)\n  }\n\n  # Map for turning left/right, updating the agent's direction (0-3)\n  TURN_LEFT_MAP = {0: 1, 1: 2, 2: 3, 3: 0}  # Right -> Up -> Left -> Down -> Right\n  TURN_RIGHT_MAP = {0: 3, 1: 0, 2: 1, 3: 2} # Right -> Down -> Left -> Up -> Right\n\n  # Define all item kinds that block movement.\n  # This includes inherently non-grabbable entities (like boundaries, water, workshops)\n  # AND the specific primitive we are trying to collect (agent should stand *next to* it, not *on* it).\n  blocking_kind_ids_set = set(current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices)\n  blocking_kind_ids_set.add(primitive_id) # Agent cannot step on the primitive itself.\n  # Convert to numpy array for efficient indexing in the grid check within the loop\n  blocking_kind_indices_np = np.array(list(blocking_kind_ids_set), dtype=int)\n\n  # BFS state: ((row, col), direction), path_actions\n  # Queue stores ( (current_pos_tuple, current_dir_int), list_of_actions_to_reach_here )\n  queue = collections.deque([((initial_pos, initial_dir), [])])\n  # Visited set stores (current_pos_tuple, current_dir_int) to avoid cycles and redundant paths\n  visited = {(initial_pos, initial_dir)}\n\n  target_path = None # Stores the action list to reach the target state\n\n  while queue:\n      (current_pos, current_dir), path_actions = queue.popleft()\n      r, c = current_pos\n\n      # 1. Check if the primitive is directly in front of the agent at current state.\n      # If so, this is the pre-collection state, and we've found our path.\n      # Calculate the coordinates of the cell directly in front\n      front_dr, front_dc = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n      front_r, front_c = r + front_dr, c + front_dc\n      \n      # Check if front_cell is within grid bounds\n      if (0 <= front_r < WIDTH and 0 <= front_c < HEIGHT):\n          # Check if the front_cell contains the primitive\n          if initial_grid[front_r, front_c, primitive_id] > 0:\n              target_path = path_actions\n              break # Path to target found (agent is adjacent and facing the primitive)\n\n      # 2. Explore possible next actions: Move Forward, Turn Left, Turn Right\n      \n      # Try Move Forward\n      move_dr, move_dc = DIR_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n      next_r, next_c = r + move_dr, c + move_dc\n      next_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n      next_dir = current_dir # Moving forward does not change facing direction\n\n      # Check if next_pos is within bounds and this (position, direction) state hasn't been visited\n      if (0 <= next_r < WIDTH and 0 <= next_c < HEIGHT and\n          (next_pos, next_dir) not in visited):\n          \n          # Check if the next_pos contains any blocking kind using the pre-computed numpy array.\n          if not np.any(initial_grid[next_r, next_c, blocking_kind_indices_np] > 0):\n              # If all checks pass, it's a valid move. Add to queue.\n              visited.add((next_pos, next_dir))\n              queue.append(((next_pos, next_dir), path_actions + [MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION]))\n\n      # Try Turn Left\n      next_dir_left = TURN_LEFT_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Turning does not change position, only direction.\n      if ((current_pos, next_dir_left) not in visited):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_left))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_left), path_actions + [TURN_LEFT_ACTION]))\n\n      # Try Turn Right\n      next_dir_right = TURN_RIGHT_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Turning does not change position, only direction.\n      if ((current_pos, next_dir_right) not in visited):\n          visited.add((current_pos, next_dir_right))\n          queue.append(((current_pos, next_dir_right), path_actions + [TURN_RIGHT_ACTION]))\n\n  # If a path was found (to be adjacent and facing the primitive), append the USE action to the sequence\n  if target_path is not None:\n      actions_list.extend(target_path)\n      actions_list.append(USE_ACTION)\n\n  return actions_list", "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T08:23:49.537388", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "", "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-01T08:24:33.970913", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions_list = []\n  # Get the current state of the environment. This state includes the grid,\n  # agent's position, direction, and inventory.\n  current_state = env._current_state\n\n  # Store initial grid, position, and direction for pathfinding.\n  # The grid is considered static during pathfinding; only agent's (pos, dir) changes.\n  initial_grid = current_state.grid\n  initial_agent_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's starting row, column tuple (r, c)\n  initial_agent_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's starting direction (0:RIGHT, 1:UP, 2:LEFT, 3:DOWN)\n\n  # Get the integer ID for the target primitive from the world's cookbook index.\n  # This ID is used to locate the primitive on the grid.\n  primitive_kind_id = current_state.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # *** IMPROVEMENT FOR V2: Handle non-grabbable primitives ***\n  # The 'collect' action implies picking up an item into inventory.\n  # If the specified primitive cannot be grabbed (e.g., WORKSHOP, WATER, BOUNDARY),\n  # then it cannot be 'collected'. In such cases, return an empty list immediately\n  # as no sequence of actions will achieve the goal of collecting it.\n  if primitive_kind_id not in current_state.world.grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  # Get grid dimensions to check boundaries during pathfinding.\n  GRID_WIDTH, GRID_HEIGHT, _ = initial_grid.shape\n\n  # Retrieve the mapping from action names (strings) to their integer codes.\n  # This ensures compatibility with the environment's `step` method.\n  action_name_to_id = env.action_specs()\n  \n  # Map DSL movement/turn actions to their integer indices.\n  MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION_ID = action_name_to_id['UP'] # 'UP' in DSL means 'move forward'\n  TURN_LEFT_ACTION_ID = action_name_to_id['LEFT']\n  TURN_RIGHT_ACTION_ID = action_name_to_id['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION_ID = action_name_to_id['USE'] # Action to perform collection/interaction\n\n  # Define direction vectors for moving forward based on current orientation.\n  # Maps agent's direction index to (delta_row, delta_column) for a forward step.\n  # Agent's direction (dir): 0=RIGHT, 1=UP, 2=LEFT, 3=DOWN\n  DIRECTION_TO_DRDC = {\n      0: (0, 1),   # Facing RIGHT: (row, col + 1)\n      1: (-1, 0),  # Facing UP: (row - 1, col)\n      2: (0, -1),  # Facing LEFT: (row, col - 1)\n      3: (1, 0)    # Facing DOWN: (row + 1, col)\n  }\n\n  # Define how agent's direction changes when turning left or right.\n  # These mappings cycle through the four cardinal directions (0, 1, 2, 3).\n  TURN_LEFT_DIR_MAP = {0: 1, 1: 2, 2: 3, 3: 0} # Example: RIGHT (0) -> UP (1)\n  TURN_RIGHT_DIR_MAP = {0: 3, 1: 0, 2: 1, 3: 2} # Example: RIGHT (0) -> DOWN (3)\n\n  # Identify all entity kinds that act as obstacles to agent movement.\n  # An agent cannot walk onto cells containing these items.\n  # 1. Non-grabbable entities (e.g., BOUNDARY, WATER, WORKSHOP0) are inherently obstacles.\n  unwalkable_kind_ids = set(current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices)\n  \n  # 2. If the target primitive itself is a grabbable item (e.g., WOOD, STONE, GOLD),\n  #    the agent should not walk directly onto its tile. It must interact from an\n  #    adjacent cell. Thus, the primitive's own ID is also added as an obstacle for movement.\n  unwalkable_kind_ids.add(primitive_kind_id)\n  \n  # Early Exit Optimization: If the primitive is already in the agent's 3x3\n  # neighborhood (i.e., immediately collectible from the current position), just return the USE action.\n  # The `CraftState.next_to` method provides this check efficiently.\n  if current_state.next_to(primitive_kind_id):\n      return [USE_ACTION_ID]\n\n  # Initialize Breadth-First Search (BFS) for pathfinding.\n  # The BFS queue stores tuples:\n  #   ((current_position_tuple (r, c), current_direction_int), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here)\n  # This structure allows tracking both spatial location and agent orientation.\n  bfs_queue = collections.deque([((initial_agent_pos, initial_agent_dir), [])])\n  \n  # The 'visited' set keeps track of (position, direction) pairs already explored\n  # to prevent cycles and redundant computations, ensuring the shortest path is found.\n  visited_states = {(initial_agent_pos, initial_agent_dir)}\n\n  path_to_collection_spot = None # This will store the shortest action sequence to a collectible state.\n\n  # Main BFS loop: continues until the queue is empty or a path to a goal is found.\n  while bfs_queue:\n      # Dequeue the current state (position and direction) and the path leading to it.\n      (current_pos, current_dir), current_path_actions = bfs_queue.popleft()\n      r, c = current_pos\n\n      # Check if the current agent position (r, c) is a \"goal state\" for collection.\n      # A goal state means the primitive is located in any cell within the 3x3 neighborhood\n      # around the agent's current position on the initial grid. This mirrors the `CraftState.next_to` logic.\n      is_primitive_in_neighborhood = False\n      for dr_offset in [-1, 0, 1]: # Iterate through relative row offsets (-1, 0, 1)\n          for dc_offset in [-1, 0, 1]: # Iterate through relative column offsets (-1, 0, 1)\n              check_r, check_c = r + dr_offset, c + dc_offset\n              # Ensure the cell being checked is within grid boundaries.\n              if (0 <= check_r < GRID_WIDTH and 0 <= check_c < GRID_HEIGHT and\n                  initial_grid[check_r, check_c, primitive_kind_id] > 0):\n                  is_primitive_in_neighborhood = True\n                  break # Primitive found in neighborhood, no need to check further cells for this position.\n          if is_primitive_in_neighborhood:\n              break # Break outer loop too if found.\n\n      if is_primitive_in_neighborhood:\n          path_to_collection_spot = current_path_actions # A shortest path to a collectible state is found.\n          break # Terminate BFS; no need to explore further as we found the shortest path.\n\n      # Explore possible next states by applying valid actions: Move Forward, Turn Left, Turn Right.\n\n      # 1. Try MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION:\n      delta_r, delta_c = DIRECTION_TO_DRDC[current_dir]\n      next_r, next_c = r + delta_r, c + delta_c\n      next_agent_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n      next_agent_dir_after_move = current_dir # Moving forward does not change the agent's facing direction.\n\n      # Check if the potential next position is valid (within bounds and not previously visited with this direction).\n      if (0 <= next_r < GRID_WIDTH and 0 <= next_c < GRID_HEIGHT and\n          (next_agent_pos, next_agent_dir_after_move) not in visited_states):\n          \n          is_cell_walkable = True\n          # Verify that the cell at `next_agent_pos` does not contain any obstacle.\n          for kind_idx in unwalkable_kind_ids:\n              if initial_grid[next_r, next_c, kind_idx] > 0:\n                  is_cell_walkable = False\n                  break # This cell contains an obstacle, so it's not walkable.\n\n          if is_cell_walkable:\n              visited_states.add((next_agent_pos, next_agent_dir_after_move)) # Mark the new state as visited.\n              # Add the new state to the queue with the updated path.\n              bfs_queue.append(((next_agent_pos, next_agent_dir_after_move), \n                                current_path_actions + [MOVE_FORWARD_ACTION_ID]))\n\n      # 2. Try TURN_LEFT_ACTION:\n      next_agent_dir_left = TURN_LEFT_DIR_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Turning only changes direction, not position.\n      if ((current_pos, next_agent_dir_left) not in visited_states):\n          visited_states.add((current_pos, next_agent_dir_left))\n          bfs_queue.append(((current_pos, next_agent_dir_left), \n                            current_path_actions + [TURN_LEFT_ACTION_ID]))\n\n      # 3. Try TURN_RIGHT_ACTION:\n      next_agent_dir_right = TURN_RIGHT_DIR_MAP[current_dir]\n      # Turning only changes direction, not position.\n      if ((current_pos, next_agent_dir_right) not in visited_states):\n          visited_states.add((current_pos, next_agent_dir_right))\n          bfs_queue.append(((current_pos, next_agent_dir_right), \n                            current_path_actions + [TURN_RIGHT_ACTION_ID]))\n\n  # After BFS completes:\n  # If a path to a collectable position was found (`path_to_collection_spot` is not None),\n  # append the final 'USE' action to perform the collection.\n  if path_to_collection_spot is not None:\n      actions_list.extend(path_to_collection_spot)\n      actions_list.append(USE_ACTION_ID)\n\n  return actions_list", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
